wiki/Machapuchare\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mt. Machhapuchare</a> ‘the Fish Tail”.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Adventure Sports for your delight and thrills:</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Ultra Light Aircraft:</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nUltra-light aircraft take off from Pokhara and offer spectacular views of the lakes, Annapurna, Dhaulagiri Mountains, Lamjung Himal, and Manaslu including the towering Machhapuchare peak against the rolling green hills and villages. This is an ideal way to see life from a new perspective. The flights take place from sunrise to 11 a.m. and from 3 p.m. to sunset every day during these months.\\r\\n\\r\\n<b>Paragliding</b><strong> :\\r\\n</strong>\\r\\nThe main area for paragliding is from Pokhara Valley at the top of Sarangkot Hill with commanding views of 3 of the world’s 8000m peaks with friendly and constant conditions for your paragliding holiday, Paragliding from morning till afternoon depending upon the wind current and weather conditions.\\r\\n\\r\\nThere are more than 30 Paragliding operators in Nepal to book for, and the interesting one is gliding with a hawk.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Sky Dive:\\r\\n</strong>\\r\\nOut of various adventures in Nepal, sky diving is another sport that’s gaining popularity every year, even though it’s an expensive adventure to do, it is a mind-blowing experience in the very nose of the high giant peaks of Mt. Everest and its surrounding majestic peaks. It involves flying in a small plane near Everest and then jumping with the parachute depending upon the weather conditions.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Zip Flyer Nepal: </strong><strong><em>Dream it-Dare it-Do it</em></strong><strong>!</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nIt’s official, the world’s most extreme zip line:\\r\\n\\r\\n1800 meters long 2000 ft. Vertical drop and 120 km. per hour speed with 02 minutes ride time. If you are looking for a true adrenalin rush then Sky Zip is for you. Unlike anything you’ve seen before the Sky Zip zip line by High Ground Adventures is truly an experience not to be missed.\\r\\n\\r\\nParticipants must be between 35 and 125 kgs (75 and 275 pounds) and be comfortable with heights. This ride is not recommended for individuals with back or neck problems, or those who are pregnant.", "trip_type_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "meta_description": "Multi Adventure Sports in Nepal attract travelers with diverse ranges such as Paragliding, Ultra Light, Aircraft, Zip Flyers, and many more.", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "", "best_season": "", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": ""}}	2024-01-11 15:56:29+00	2024-02-07 05:13:14+00
132	{"faq": [{"answer": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "question": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "question": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "question": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "question": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "question": "5. What to expect on tours?"}], "cost": "", "slug": "2-days-kathmandu-city-tour", "tags": [], "title": "2 Days Kathmandu City Tour", "rating": "Excellent", "duration": "2 Days", "itinerary": [{"id": "4c6e8f5e-65fd-4452-b853-af43bb1b6bde", "day": 1, "meal": "", "order": 1, "title": "Tour of Durbar Square, Swoyambhunath, Pashupatinath & Bouddhanath Stupa.", "images": [], "richText": "A captivating morning tour with Everest Vacation, our city, and a cultural guide will receive you from the hotel in the first hour of the day. You will then start the day with a guided tour of <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathmandu_Durbar_Square\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"><strong>Kathmandu Durbar Square</strong></a>. A place with a stockpile of old history and rich culture, visiting old Royal Durbar Square is experiencing medieval Nepal as a whole.\\r\\n\\r\\nOne of the major attractions here was Kasthamandap Temple (where Kathmandu was named) a temple built from the wood of a single tree. Sadly, the temple with a couple of other monuments was destroyed by the earthquake of 2015. However, you can still visit the ruins of these temples. Then you will have a tour of Kumari Goddess Temple (The only living goddess in Nepal). The Divine Goddess is here from a tender age, and she remains in the position until her puberty period. The priests then select the next Goddess to replace her.\\r\\n\\r\\nWalk around the world-famous <strong>freak street,</strong> A popular destination in Kathmandu in the early 1960s to ’80s for budget tourists and hippies before Thamel was established as a tourist center.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom here you will travel towards the western delight of the Valley. Located on the hilltop <strong>Swoyambhu</strong><strong> Stupa</strong> is the oldest shrine of this nation. Attended by Hindus and Buddhists alike this place is an excellent destination for a quick hike and some fresh air.\\r\\n\\r\\nAbout 2500 years old, Swoyambhunath is also the oldest <strong>UNESCO Heritage</strong> site in Nepal. An environment with positive vibes and abundant pilgrims circumambulating the area, you can just feel the atmosphere all day long. The white dome at the top of the hill is the main structure here. With the abundant population of monkeys residing in the Temple, the Swoyambhunath area is also popular as ‘The Monkey Temple.’ From the hilltop, you can enjoy the panoramic view of most parts of Kathmandu and the hills that surround the city. In clear weather, you can also view multiple mountain ranges in the far North.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter your lunch, take a short rest and be ready to experience the most significant <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/travel-info/about-hinduisms/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Hindu</a> temple of Nepal, you head towards the north of the city towards the holy temple of <a href=\\"https://pashupatinathtemple.org/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"><strong>Pashupatinath Temple</strong></a> in the late afternoon. As non-Hindu tourists and personnel can’t enter the main temple area, you can explore the other monuments and shrines under the vast field of Pashupatinath. Extending on both sides of the <strong>Holy Bagmati</strong> River the temple complex has more than 518 temples in a 264-hectare area.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom Pashupatinath, you drive further north-east to reach the <a href=\\"https://wikitravel.org/en/Boudhanath\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"><strong>Boudhanath Stupa</strong></a>. This stupa is the biggest in Nepal and is also listed on the UNESCO World Heritage list. Boudhanath is the center of Tibetan Buddhism in Nepal. The majestic architecture of the dome is balanced with the Buddhist vibe going all around it. You can spend some time here Taking sips of Tibetan tea and enjoying the view from one of the rooftops here. You will also get a chance to shop for your souvenirs in the shops surrounding the Stupa.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter the nice refreshing tour of the Heritage and religious sites, return to your hotel and get some rest and refreshments.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "1400m", "activities": [], "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"id": "2ae847a1-d847-4213-aa49-d0ae6b01605f", "day": 2, "meal": "Breakfast", "order": 2, "title": "Tour of Bhaktapur & Patan Durbar Square", "images": [], "richText": "Your morning starts with some hot beverages, and you move to the third major city of <strong>Bhaktapur</strong>. Also known as Bhadgaon(the land of rice), Bhaktapur offers you the less disturbed cultural places in the Valley. Walking through the stone patched streets here you can admire the art form and architecture in every corner. The area is famous for beautiful pottery as well as wood and stone carvings. The significant places not to miss on your visit are The <a href=\\"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/nepal/around-the-kathmandu-valley/bhaktapur\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"><strong>Bhaktapur Durbar Square</strong></a>, Nyatapola Temple Square with surrounding temples, Bhaktapur National Art Gallery, and the 55 Windows Palace.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter your trip, Bhaktapur has lunch and proceeds towards the city of arts,<strong> Patan</strong>. Also known as Lalitpur, this city is the second largest city in the valley. A quieter neighborhood than the capital, Patan is a living cultural destination in your trip. You’ll have a visit to the <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patan_Durbar_Square\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Patan Durbar Square</a>, where full of architectural brilliance and art-packed streets waiting for you. Explore the Krishna Temple, One of the most eye-catching and religiously essential sculptures of the square. People believe that this vast temple was carved into a single enormous stone. After your experience rich visit, return to your hotel.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "1400m", "activities": [], "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmandu-durbar-square.jpg", "title": "kathmandu-durbar-square", "altText": "kathmandu-durbar-square", "caption": "kathmandu-durbar-square", "variants": {}}, "tour_type": "Challenging", "meta_title": "2 Days Kathmandu City Tour", "trip_meals": "", "descriptions": "<p><br></p>", "imageGallary": [{"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmandu-durbar-square.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/2-days-kathmandu-tour-by-turkey-people.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmandu-cultural-tour.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmandu-trip-1.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bhaktapur-tour-nepal.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bouddhanath-stupa.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/view-of-Kathmandu-valley-from-top-of-chandragiri.jpeg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/swyambhunath-kathmandu.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Thanka-of-Buddha.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/pashupatinath.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/kathmandu-city-tour.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bouddha-nath-kathmandu.jpeg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bouddha-market.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/swyambhunath-monkey-temple.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}, {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bagalamukhi-temple.jpg", "title": "", "altText": "", "mediaId": null, "variants": {}}], "overviewImage": null, "customSections": [{"id": 1, "note": "", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Extended Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">1 day Kathmandu sightseeing Tour - 4-8 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">1 day Kathmandu sightseeing Tour - 4-8 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": 2, "note": "", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Alternate Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": "overview-1", "note": "", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Highlights", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kathmandu Durbar Square, Hanuman Dhaka, Kumari (A living Goddess), Kasthamandap, Basantapur, Freak-street</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Swoyambhunath Stupa, Monkey Temple, Swoyambhu Temple, Maha Chaitya</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pashupatinath Temple, Hindu Temple, Open crimination center, Evening Aarti at opposite of Pashupati temple</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Boudhanath Stupa, One of the biggest stupas in Asia, the Big Buddha stupa</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Patan Durbar Square, Krishna Temple, Patan Museum, Wooden architecture factory</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bhaktapur Durbar Square, Pottery making, Wood carving, Changunarayan temple</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Or, choose your preferred places to see and let us know, and we will operate your choices. You may add an Everest mountain flight or helicopter flight to Everest on the same day.</li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kathmandu Durbar Square, Hanuman Dhaka, Kumari (A living Goddess), Kasthamandap, Basantapur, Freak-street</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Swoyambhunath Stupa, Monkey Temple, Swoyambhu Temple, Maha Chaitya</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pashupatinath Temple, Hindu Temple, Open crimination center, Evening Aarti at opposite of Pashupati temple</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Boudhanath Stupa, One of the biggest stupas in Asia, the Big Buddha stupa</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Patan Durbar Square, Krishna Temple, Patan Museum, Wooden architecture factory</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bhaktapur Durbar Square, Pottery making, Wood carving, Changunarayan temple</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Or, choose your preferred places to see and let us know, and we will operate your choices. You may add an Everest mountain flight or helicopter flight to Everest on the same day.</li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": [], "description": "<ul><li>Fully private trip (even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.</li><li>Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).</li><li>Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.</li><li>English speaking cultural city tour guide.</li><li>Drinking Water.</li></ul>"}], "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "showBookingForm": false, "sub_description": "7 UNESCO world heritage sites in Kathmandu, Patan & Bhaktapur", "trip_highlights": "<p>If you're short on time but eager to explore the essential monuments of Kathmandu, this guided city tour of Kathmandu Valley, including Patan and Bhaktapur, is the perfect way to do it. This cultural day tour offers a glimpse into the rich heritage of the world heritage sites in the area. Don't miss out on the chance to experience the best of Kathmandu!</p>", "trip_type_level": "Private Tour", "meta_description": "Explore the cultural and historical wonders such as ancient temples, landmarks, and vibrant markets in 2 days Kathmandu City Tour.", "trip_attractions": "Boudhanath, Pashupatinath, Swoyambhunath, Basantapur, Patan Durbar Square & Bhaktapur Durbar Square", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "faq_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "overviewImageSize": 100, "overviewImageAlign": "center", "trip_accommodation": "", "trip_max_elevation": "", "packageSectionOrder": ["itinerary", "includeExclude", "travelInfo", "faq", "additionalInfo:1", "additionalInfo:2", "additionalInfo:overview-1"], "trip_transportations": "Private AC Vehicle", "trip_highlights_title": "2 days Kathmandu City tour with World Heritage Sites in Kathmandu Valley; Kathmandu, Bhaktapur & Patan", "trip_highlights_description": "<p>If you're short on time but eager to explore the essential monuments of Kathmandu, this guided city tour of Kathmandu Valley, including Patan and Bhaktapur, is the perfect way to do it. This cultural day tour offers a glimpse into the rich heritage of the world heritage sites in the area. Don't miss out on the chance to experience the best of Kathmandu!</p>"}	2023-11-30 04:37:56+00	2026-02-27 18:03:02.684+00
283	{"faq": [{"answer": "It’s a special trip that takes you to three amazing countries: Nepal, Tibet, and Bhutan. You’ll see beautiful places, experience different cultures, and explore famous landmarks in each country.", "question": "What is the Nepal-Tibet-Bhutan Tour with Everest Vacation?"}, {"answer": "The tour usually lasts 20 days or 2-3 weeks. This gives you enough time to enjoy the important places in Nepal, Tibet, and Bhutan without feeling rushed.", "question": "How long is the tour?"}, {"answer": "You’ll see many famous sites like:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"666\\" data-end=\\"719\\">The UNESCO World Heritage sites in Kathmandu, Nepal</li>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"722\\" data-end=\\"757\\">The Potala Palace in Lhasa, Tibet</li>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"760\\" data-end=\\"864\\">The famous Paro Taktsang (Tiger’s Nest) in Bhutan<br data-start=\\"809\\" data-end=\\"812\\" />There are many other exciting places included too!</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "question": "What are the main places I’ll visit on the Nepal-Tibet-Bhutan Tour?"}, {"answer": "The best time for Nepal and Bhutan is spring (March to May) and autumn (September to November). For Tibet, it’s best to visit between April and October.", "question": "When is the best time to go on Nepal, Tibet, and Bhutan tour?"}, {"answer": "Don’t worry! Everest Vacation takes care of all visa paperwork. The Nepal visa is usually easy to get when you arrive. We handle the permits for Tibet and Bhutan as part of your tour package.", "question": "What about visas for Nepal, Tibet, and Bhutan?"}, {"answer": "The price usually covers:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"1398\\" data-end=\\"1425\\">Hotels and accommodations</li>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"1428\\" data-end=\\"1454\\">Guided sightseeing tours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"1457\\" data-end=\\"1469\\">Some meals</li>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"1472\\" data-end=\\"1555\\">Transportation by car, bus, and flights (like Kathmandu-Lhasa and Kathmandu-Paro)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"1558\\" data-end=\\"1582\\">Permits and entry fees</li>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"1585\\" data-end=\\"1629\\">Bhutan’s Sustainable Development Fee (SDF)</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "question": "What is included in the tour package price?"}, {"answer": "You will need to pay for:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"1711\\" data-end=\\"1757\\">Your international flights to and from Nepal</li>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"1760\\" data-end=\\"1808\\">Personal spending (like souvenirs and laundry)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"1811\\" data-end=\\"1829\\">Travel insurance</li>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"1832\\" data-end=\\"1884\\">Some meals (so you can try different local dishes)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li data-start=\\"1887\\" data-end=\\"1916\\">Tips for guides and drivers</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "question": "What costs are not included in the price?"}, {"answer": "Everest Vacation seamlessly manages all inter-country travel. This usually involves flights (e.g., Kathmandu to Lhasa, Kathmandu to Paro) and, where appropriate, pre-arranged overland transfers, ensuring smooth transitions throughout your journey.", "question": "How do I travel between Nepal, Tibet, and Bhutan?"}, {"answer": "A medium level of fitness is helpful. You’ll do sightseeing walks and may feel the effects of high altitude in Tibet. In Bhutan, the hike to Tiger’s Nest is optional, so you can decide whether to do it or not.", "question": "What level of physical fitness is required for the Nepal-Tibet-Bhutan Tour?"}, {"answer": "Booking is easy! You can contact us on our website, by email, or by phone. Our friendly team will guide you through the whole process.", "question": "How can I book Nepal, Tibet, and Bhutan tour?"}, {"answer": "Absolutely! As we specialize in private (personal) tours, we offer extensive customization. We can tailor the itinerary to perfectly match your interests, preferred travel duration, and budget. Please discuss your ideal trip with us!", "question": "Can I customize the Nepal, Tibet, and Bhutan tour?"}, {"answer": "We have lots of experience with tours in this region, handle all the details, provide personal service, and support responsible tourism. We make sure your trip is smooth, safe, and unforgettable!", "question": "Why should I choose Everest Vacation for this tour?"}], "cost": "", "slug": "nepal-bhutan-tibet-tour-package", "tags": [], "title": "Nepal, Bhutan, Tibet Tour Package", "rating": "Excellent", "duration": "20 Days", "itinerary": [{"id": "f7b4f2e7-21d2-4923-a5c2-a84b149268b7", "day": 1, "meal": "", "order": 1, "title": "Arrival in Kathmandu and transfer to your hotel.", "images": [], "richText": "Airport transfer, collect your original passport and photographs and request to fill up Tibet group visa form.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "ea9fe4d4-4118-4265-a6ad-e474c0036f02", "day": 2, "meal": "", "order": 2, "title": "Kathmandu Tour", "images": [], "richText": "Apply Tibet visa and Tour continue: Boudhanath Stupa, Pashupatinath Temple, Patan Durbar Square.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "83203307-79a4-446d-abd8-78bdfda10e89", "day": 3, "meal": "", "order": 3, "title": "Kathmandu to Pokhara", "images": [], "richText": "Flight/drive to Pokhara and Phewa lake boating, enjoy around lakeside.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "51f85c7e-168c-4f06-a6ce-be75c6990908", "day": 4, "meal": "", "order": 4, "title": "Pokhara Tour", "images": [], "richText": "Activities: Sarangkot sunrise tour, Bindabasini Temple, Gupteshwor Mahadev Cave, Davis Fall, Mountain Museum.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "06b21bfa-33e8-4551-860b-bd840c7d7ab4", "day": 5, "meal": "", "order": 5, "title": "Pokhara – Chitwan", "images": [], "richText": "Flight/drive to Chitwan National Park, Village tour, Riverside sunset view, Tharu Cultural dance with dinner.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "9e64cd64-fe34-4e03-8fa9-ef18e8031231", "day": 6, "meal": "", "order": 6, "title": "National Park Tour", "images": [], "richText": "Jeep Safari, Canoeing Ride, Jungle walk, and  elephant Breeding Center.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "fbb6e694-8a71-48a5-8f66-eb55cd965b9e", "day": 7, "meal": "", "order": 7, "title": "Chitwan – Kathmandu", "images": [], "richText": "Early morning Bird watching tour, flight/drive to Kathmandu, leisure time / shopping time if you prefer. Collect Tibet visa today.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "e5ee5183-813d-485e-99a6-b247a2875388", "day": 8, "meal": "", "order": 8, "title": "Flight to Paro(Bhutan), drive to Thimphu and Thimphu Sightseeing", "images": [], "richText": "<i>W</i>elcome to Bhutan. Pickup from Paro airport and drive to Thimphu\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>- Thimphu Sightseeing </strong><em>(*If time does not allow, we will do it the next day)</em>\\r\\n- Tachogang Lhakhang,\\r\\n- Visit Buddha Dordenma,\\r\\n- Bhutan Postal Museum, Memorial Chorten\\r\\n<strong>Driving Distance: </strong>1.30 hours’ drive", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "0fb0e059-53f4-4a08-a1b5-8336e503c593", "day": 9, "meal": "", "order": 9, "title": "Punakha Sightseeing", "images": [], "richText": "Drive from Thimphu to Punakha via Dochu La Pass\\r\\n- Dochula Pass\\r\\n- Punakha Dzong\\r\\n- Suspension Bridge\\r\\n- Chimi Lhakhang, Temple of fertility\\r\\n<strong>Distance:</strong> 2.5 hours drive", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "f3fe6ffe-8c3e-4b98-8f67-fe168d92f161", "day": 10, "meal": "", "order": 10, "title": "Punakha to Paro", "images": [], "richText": "After breakfast, drive back to Paro and<strong> Paro valley tour.</strong>\\r\\n<strong>Distance</strong>: 3-4 hours drive", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "f8929a2a-3d6a-4742-ba86-8c6f3bb55a0d", "day": 11, "meal": "", "order": 11, "title": "Taktsang Lhakhang (Tiger’s Nest) Hike/Trek", "images": [], "richText": "Drive to hiking base point.\\r\\n- Hike to Taktsang Lhakhang (Tiger’s Nest)\\r\\n- Visit Kyichu Lhakhang and back to hotel.\\r\\n<strong>Distance: </strong>4-6 hours hike depend on you.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "11d2e0a5-de1b-4879-a3a7-9d045e4a5a48", "day": 12, "meal": "", "order": 12, "title": "Flight from Paro, Bhutan to Kathmandu, Nepal - Kathmandu Sightseeing", "images": [], "richText": "- Drop you at Paro airport before 3 hours of your flight time as per airport rule.\\r\\n\\r\\nWelcome in Kathmandu. Our guide and driver will meet you outside of airport and drop you to your hotel.  After refreshment, start Kathmandu sightseeing\\r\\n- Swoyambhu Monkey Temple\\r\\n- Kathmandu Durbar Square and Ason local market", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "0a1f803f-7af0-4d54-8463-443addca1feb", "day": 13, "meal": "", "order": 13, "title": "Kathmandu to Tibet flight and rest at Tsedang to adjust high elevation.", "images": [], "richText": "Welcome in Lhasa (Tibet) airport and transfer to Tsedang city. Rest today for high-altitude acclimatization. (Tsedang Altitude: 3100m)", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "activities": [], "accommodation": ""}, {"id": "a0b1b7d6-92de-4c88-aa7f-50b3f8f6d792", "day": 14, "meal": "", "order": 14, "title": "Visit Samye Monstaery and Afternoon Visit Yumbu Lhakang .", "images": [], "richText": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"s