n class=\\"ql-ui\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\"></span>Shigatse &amp; Gyantse Sightseeing (Gyantse Kumbum, Pelkor Chöde Monastery, Tashilhunpo Monastery)</li><li data-list=\\"bullet\\"><span class=\\"ql-ui\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\"></span>Visit the freshwater sacred Yamdrok Tso Lake</li><li data-list=\\"bullet\\"><span class=\\"ql-ui\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\"></span>UNESCO-listed Norbulingka Palace and Royal Museum Potala Palace</li><li data-list=\\"bullet\\"><span class=\\"ql-ui\\" contenteditable=\\"false\\"></span>Holy Barkhor Street and Spiritual Buddhist Sacred Jokhang Temple</li></ol>"}	2024-08-20 09:16:48+01	2026-02-27 18:30:29.021+00
156	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "Combination of culture and scenic tour including Nagarkot Sunrise", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "4", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour"}, "faq": [{"answer": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "question": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "question": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "question": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "question": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "question": "5. What to expect on tours?"}], "meta": {"_edit_last": "2", "_edit_lock": "1715929408:2", "_dp_original": "510", "_thumbnail_id": "603", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "Combination of culture and scenic tour including Nagarkot Sunrise", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "4", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "4 Days Kathmandu City with Nagarkot Hill Tour", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "4 Days Kathmandu City with Nagarkot Hill Tour", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "44", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "4 Days Kathmandu City with Nagarkot Hill Tour is very popular offering diversity of culture and scenery coupled with adventure.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour", "tags": [], "title": "4 Days Kathmandu City with Nagarkot Hill Tour", "duration": "4 Days", "overview": {"title": "Highlights", "description": "4 days in <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/kathmandu-pokhara-chitwan-short-tour/\\">Kathmandu</a> and <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagarkot\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Nagarkot</a> with a diversity of culture and scenery. If you are interested, this itinerary will help you to get the most out of this magical yet hectic place aside from the valley with Historical, Cultural, Newari People local lifestyle, and Farming activities.\\r\\n<h4>Outline Itinerary</h4>\\r\\nDay 01: Tour of Kathmandu Durbar Square Swayambhunath, Pashupatinath and Bouddhanath\\r\\nDay 02: Tour of Patan Durbar Square &amp; Bhaktapur\\r\\nDay 03: Tour of Changu Narayan &amp; Nagarkot hill top\\r\\nDay 04: Nagarkot Sunrise Tour and Return back to Kathmandu by drive or hiking with drive."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Tour of Kathmandu Durbar Square Swayambhunath, Pashupatinath and Bouddhanath", "richText": "Morning 09 a.m. departure from the hotel for guided sightseeing tour of historical and cultural tour with delightful scenery around Kathmandu city with Everest Vacation, a short ride to Kathmandu Durbar Square, visit of places with old history and rich culture of old king’s durbar square and Hanuman Dhoka (palace) visit of ancient Kastamandap Temple (where Kathmandu name derived from) this temple built of wood from a single tree, tour of Kumari Goddess (living virgin goddess) Kumari a very young girl, after teenage years phase replaced by another young Kumari, from here a short drive to west of the city at Swayambhunath Stupa located on a hill top, with panorama view of Kathmandu city, surrounding green hills with snow capped mountains in the north.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis old Stupa of Swayambhunath, the oldest historical monument listed as World Heritage Sites with over 2, 5000 years old Buddhist religion area with huge dome shape stupa overlooking four cardinal eyes of Buddha around North, South, East and West directions. Here visiting monastery and chapels, Sywambhunath is guarded with lovely woodland with a many monkeys around, this place is also named as “Monkey Temple”.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom here another tour leads to Pashupatinath Temple, where non Hindu are not permitted inside the main temple entrance, where visitors can have a look of the temple surrounding from above the Bagmati river, this famous Shiva temple decorated with golden tier roofs with silver doors around each corner, this place close to green woodland with lots of monkeys around. Pashupatinath is full of pilgrims in special day on Shiva Ratri (birth anniversary of lord Shiva).\\r\\n\\r\\nNearby on the side of the river funeral and cremation are held for all Hindus, from here return back to your hotels at leisure for the rest of afternoon.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "1400m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 2, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Tour of Bhaktapur & Patan Durbar Square", "richText": "Starting the morning with a short drive towards Patan city located south of Kathmandu at mere distance across the bridge, on reaching Patan also known as Lalitpur meaning “city of arts” visit the old Palace complex, courtyard (Durbar) with tall terracotta palace, impressive window carvings, and a tall Krishna Temple with Garuda pillar, a vehicle of Lord Vishnu and Lord Krishna, from here a pleasant ride to valley 03rd biggest city, this old looking city at one time Nepal capital during Malla period in 12th to 15th century.\\r\\n\\r\\nBhaktapur famous for arts and crafts like woodcarving and pottery, tour of unique Durbar Square with golden gate of 55 windows palace, interesting wooden peacock window, continue tour of Bhaktapur visiting another Durbar Square with famed Nytapola Temple, Bhaktapur National Art Gallery, and Bhairavnath Temple.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter a lovely and interesting day return back to hotel with afternoon free at leisure.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "1400m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 3, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Tour of Changu Narayan & Nagarkot hill top", "richText": "Morning depart hotel for a scenic and interesting drive towards east North East of Kathmandu on the Nepal / Tibet, China Friendship highway, drive leaves past the outer rim of Bhaktapur with uphill reaching at a small medieval Newari village at Changu-Narayan, visit Nepal oldest temple, listed in World Heritage Site, a 05th century old adorned with full artistic work on metals and wood. Inscription dates back 464 AD the first ever epigraphicevidences of Nepalese history, from here carry on drive high above to Nagarkot, located 30 km east of Kathmandu, a favorite weekend gateway for Himalayan mountain views and serenity. From Nagarkot, witness the striking mountain panorama extending from Dhaulagiri in the west towards east of Mt. Everest. Nagarkot at 2,175 meters high visiting the top hill and climb to a observatory tower with beautiful forest surrounding offering a grandstand panorama of the Himalaya with five world’s highest mountains with Everest (8,848m.), Lhotse (8,516m.), Cho Oyu (8,201m.), Makalu (8,463m.) and other lesser peak. Nagarkot famous for sunrise and sunset views over chain of Himalayan snow peaks.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "2175m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 4, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Nagarkot Sunrise Tour and Return back to Kathmandu by drive or hiking with drive.", "richText": "Early morning, you will enjoy amazing sunrise and return back to Kathmandu by drive or hiking with drive.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter a wonderful exciting tour of Kathmandu city historical, cultural places with scenic Mountain View point’s return back to Kathmandu after completing the tour with Everest Vacation.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "2175m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/sunrise-tour-nagarkot.jpg", "title": "sunrise-tour-nagarkot", "altText": "sunrise-tour, nagarkot", "caption": "sunrise-tour, nagarkot", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["542", "602", "4349", "4333", "4304", "4297", "4041", "3960", "3955", "3920", "781", "527", "525", "3969"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "ws_trip_faqs_lists": 5, "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists": "field_63ede38e351c7", "ws_block_attractions": "Boudhanath, Pashupatinath, Swoyambhunath, Basantapur, Patan, Bhaktapur, Changu Narayan & Nagarkot", "ws_block_best_season": "Any Season", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "2", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-light", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "2175 meters", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": "Highlights", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc6695edb31", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_block_transportation": "Private AC Vehicle", "ws_trip_galleries_title": "Photo/Visual Gallery", "_ws_block_transportation": "field_63eeee74072de", "_ws_trip_galleries_title": "field_63ec89128acaa", "starter_kit_padding_type": "p-mediu