s been for the past many centuries. These settlements take you towards the <strong>Changu Narayan</strong> area. A short walk on steps passing many small souvenir shops and restaurants leads into an old temple complex of the temple. <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changu_Narayan_Temple\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\"><strong>Changu Narayan temple</strong> </a>is a unique ancient temple, one of the oldest in Nepal with a history that dates back to the Lichhavi period.\\r\\n\\r\\nChangu Narayan temple, perched on a hill is also in the <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/discover-nepals-rich-cultural-and-natural-heritage-at-world-heritage-sites/\\"><strong>UNESCO World Cultural Heritage Sites</strong></a> list. A scenic spot situated at an altitude of about 1,700 meters, just north of Bhaktapur. The temple is believed to be the oldest of all the temples in Nepal. It is said to have been built by King Hari Datta Verma in 323 A.D., And the most authentic inscription is located in Changu Narayan and dates back to 464 AD. The Changu Narayan temple is endorsed by King Lichhavi and King Mandeva. The wood and stone carvings in the temple are also sublime, and one can analyze the level of artwork of the most exceptional artists of that time. After a wonderful time here and a nice <strong>hike from Nagarkot to Changu Narayan Temple</strong>, drive back to Kathmandu the same day with an optional tour of Bhaktapur.", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "Nagarkot to Changunarayan Temple day hike from Kathmandu ", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "5. What to expect on tours?", "_ws_trip_fact_short_description": "field_63ec73a69d305", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "01", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "Nagarkot Sunrise Tour Day Hiking", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "Extended Tours", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title": "Alternate Tours", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pickup from your hotel at 4:30AM in the morning.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive 32KM from Kathmandu to Nagarkot Hill (2175m.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Sunrise views with panoramic mountain</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Take you at restaurant for Breakfast.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Start hiking from Nagarkot Village</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Complete hike through the pine forest and small Newari villages.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Observe Changunarayan Temple (UNESCO World Heritage Monument)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Take a lunch and drive back to Kathmandu</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630"}, "categoryId": null, "meta_title": "Nagarkot Sunrise Tour Day Hiking", "blogContent": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Nagarkot to Changunarayan Temple day hike from Kathmandu \\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNagarkot sunrise tour with day hiking to Changunarayan Temple is a specially designed package for nature loving travelers. This Nagarkot hike from Kathmandu is one of the most exciting and popular day tours with fabulous mountain view. The Himalayan sunrise and beautiful walk through the pristine forest of rhododendron, pines, and oaks are the major attractions of this tour. The snow-capped mountain views and Newari villages will give you a precious memory that will stay in your heart for a long time to come.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"2175 meters\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Nagarkot Sunrise, UNESCO World Cultural Heritage Sites\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"Everest Vacation provides\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Nagarkot Sunrise Tour Day hiking\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e in a serene and wonderful environment outside the valley rim. A day hike of 3-4 hours to the famous tourist spot at \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNagarkot\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e with an elevation of 2,175 meters high. From the top of Nagarkot, where stands the view and observatory tower you can enjoy the majestic scenic views to your fullest.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe start with a short drive from Kathmandu leading North East on the pristine road passing the exciting villages and towns of Thimi and Bhaktapur. Then we head for a climb with tremendous views of Bhaktapur city and Kathmandu valley’s green farmlands and spread out farm villages. After an hour of a rise on the narrow winding road, we reach a famous viewpoint of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNagarkot\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. One of the great destinations near the valley that is great for day-hike and sunrise.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNagarkot is situated at 2,175 meters of elevation, and this ramp provides you with a grandstand panorama of the Himalayas. You can see five of the world’s tallest mountains – Everest (8,848m.), Lhotse (8,516m.), Cho Oyu (8,201m.), Makalu (8,463m.) along with their ranges of numerous small peaks. The snow peaks look striking and fabulous at both sunset and sunrise. Nagarkot: surrounded by terraced hillsides and picturesque farmhouses is a piece of the Zion in the earth.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom Nagarkot start walking downhill passing through several rural farmlands with terraces and then you will reach a nice area with a temple of Shiva. This spot is also in a peaceful environment and a perfect setting for your short rest here. Continue to walk to Telkot, a roadside village, and then leave the main motorable road onto the dirt tracks through the pristine forest of rhododendrons, pines, and oaks. The view of the snow-capped mountain towards the north distance wherever you set your foot.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter a nice pleasant walk, reach a small medieval period Newari village where you can experience village life. Life here is unchallenged and unchanged from modernization as it has been for the past many centuries. These settlements take you towards the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eChangu Narayan\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e area. A short walk on steps passing many small souvenir shops and restaurants leads into an old temple complex of the temple. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changu_Narayan_Temple\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eChangu Narayan temple\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e \\\\u003c/a\\\\u003eis a unique ancient temple, one of the oldest in Nepal with a history that dates back to the Lichhavi period.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nChangu Narayan temple, perched on a hill is also in the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/discover-nepals-rich-cultural-and-natural-heritage-at-world-heritage-sites/\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUNESCO World Cultural Heritage Sites\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e list. A scenic spot situated at an altitude of about 1,700 meters, just north of Bhaktapur. The temple is believed to be the oldest of all the temples in Nepal. It is said to have been built by King Hari Datta Verma in 323 A.D., And the most authentic inscription is located in Changu Narayan and dates back to 464 AD. The Changu Narayan temple is endorsed by King Lichhavi and King Mandeva. The wood and stone carvings in the temple are also sublime, and one can analyze the level of artwork of the most exceptional artists of that time. After a wonderful time here and a nice \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ehike from Nagarkot to Changu Narayan Temple\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, drive back to Kathmandu the same day with an optional tour of Bhaktapur.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"781\\",\\"779\\",\\"778\\",\\"777\\",\\"776\\",\\"775\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Nagarkot Sunrise Tour Day Hiking\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePickup from your hotel at 4:30AM in the morning.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrive 32KM from Kathmandu to Nagarkot Hill (2175m.)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSunrise views with panoramic mountain\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTake you at restaurant for Breakfast.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eStart hiking from Nagarkot Village\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eComplete hike through the pine forest and small Newari villages.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eObserve Changunarayan Temple (UNESCO World Heritage Monument)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTake a lunch and drive back to Kathmandu\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":1,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation from Kathmandu to Nagarkot and Changunarayan Temple to your hotel Kathmandu by private car and driver.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast and Lunch with tea/ coffee or soft drinks.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eChangunarayan entrance fee (it is world heritage site by UNESCO).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eOne experience hiking guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGuide salary and his meals.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDriver salary and his meals\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour - 2 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Nagarkot to Changunarayan Temple day hike from Kathmandu \\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNagarkot sunrise tour with day hiking to Changunarayan Temple is a specially designed package for nature loving travelers. This Nagarkot hike from Kathmandu is one of the most exciting and popular day tours with fabulous mountain view. The Himalayan sunrise and beautiful walk through the pristine forest of rhododendron, pines, and oaks are the major attractions of this tour. The snow-capped mountain views and Newari villages will give you a precious memory that will stay in your heart for a long time to come.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"2175 meters\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Nagarkot Sunrise, UNESCO World Cultural Heritage Sites\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"Everest Vacation provides\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Nagarkot Sunrise Tour Day hiking\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e in a serene and wonderful environment outside the valley rim. A day hike of 3-4 hours to the famous tourist spot at \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNagarkot\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e with an elevation of 2,175 meters high. From the top of Nagarkot, where stands the view and observatory tower you can enjoy the majestic scenic views to your fullest.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe start with a short drive from Kathmandu leading North East on the pristine road passing the exciting villages and towns of Thimi and Bhaktapur. Then we head for a climb with tremendous views of Bhaktapur city and Kathmandu valley’s green farmlands and spread out farm villages. After an hour of a rise on the narrow winding road, we reach a famous viewpoint of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNagarkot\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. One of the great destinations near the valley that is great for day-hike and sunrise.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNagarkot is situated at 2,175 meters of elevation, and this ramp provides you with a grandstand panorama of the Himalayas. You can see five of the world’s tallest mountains – Everest (8,848m.), Lhotse (8,516m.), Cho Oyu (8,201m.), Makalu (8,463m.) along with their ranges of numerous small peaks. The snow peaks look striking and fabulous at both sunset and sunrise. Nagarkot: surrounded by terraced hillsides and picturesque farmhouses is a piece of the Zion in the earth.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom Nagarkot start walking downhill passing through several rural farmlands with terraces and then you will reach a nice area with a temple of Shiva. This spot is also in a peaceful environment and a perfect setting for your short rest here. Continue to walk to Telkot, a roadside village, and then leave the main motorable road onto the dirt tracks through the pristine forest of rhododendrons, pines, and oaks. The view of the snow-capped mountain towards the north distance wherever you set your foot.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter a nice pleasant walk, reach a small medieval period Newari village where you can experience village life. Life here is unchallenged and unchanged from modernization as it has been for the past many centuries. These settlements take you towards the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eChangu Narayan\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e area. A short walk on steps passing many small souvenir shops and restaurants leads into an old temple complex of the temple. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changu_Narayan_Temple\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eChangu Narayan temple\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e \\\\u003c/a\\\\u003eis a unique ancient temple, one of the oldest in Nepal with a history that dates back to the Lichhavi period.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nChangu Narayan temple, perched on a hill is also in the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/discover-nepals-rich-cultural-and-natural-heritage-at-world-heritage-sites/\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUNESCO World Cultural Heritage Sites\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e list. A scenic spot situated at an altitude of about 1,700 meters, just north of Bhaktapur. The temple is believed to be the oldest of all the temples in Nepal. It is said to have been built by King Hari Datta Verma in 323 A.D., And the most authentic inscription is located in Changu Narayan and dates back to 464 AD. The Changu Narayan temple is endorsed by King Lichhavi and King Mandeva. The wood and stone carvings in the temple are also sublime, and one can analyze the level of artwork of the most exceptional artists of that time. After a wonderful time here and a nice \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ehike from Nagarkot to Changu Narayan Temple\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, drive back to Kathmandu the same day with an optional tour of Bhaktapur.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"781\\",\\"779\\",\\"778\\",\\"777\\",\\"776\\",\\"775\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Nagarkot Sunrise Tour Day Hiking\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePickup from your hotel at 4:30AM in the morning.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrive 32KM from Kathmandu to Nagarkot Hill (2175m.)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSunrise views with panoramic mountain\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTake you at restaurant for Breakfast.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eStart hiking from Nagarkot Village\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eComplete hike through the pine forest and small Newari villages.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eObserve Changunarayan Temple (UNESCO World Heritage Monument)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTake a lunch and drive back to Kathmandu\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":1,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation from Kathmandu to Nagarkot and Changunarayan Temple to your hotel Kathmandu by private car and driver.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast and Lunch with tea/ coffee or soft drinks.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eChangunarayan entrance fee (it is world heritage site by UNESCO).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eOne experience hiking guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGuide salary and his meals.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDriver salary and his meals\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour - 2 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/sunrise-view.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/changunarayan-temple.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/local-peoples.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/mountain-view-from-nagarkot.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/sunrise.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/hiking-way.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/nala-farming.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=791", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "791", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-04 05:41:37", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-04 05:41:37", "post_modified": "2024-01-24 02:09:37", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-01-24 02:09:37"}}, "customSections": [{"id": 1, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Extended Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": 2, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Alternate Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["Everest Vacation provides<strong> Nagarkot Sunrise Tour Day hiking</strong> in a serene and wonderful environment outside the valley rim. A day hike of 3-4 hours to the famous tourist spot at <strong>Nagarkot</strong> with an elevation of 2,175 meters high. From the top of Nagarkot, where stands the view and observatory tower you can enjoy the majestic scenic views to your fullest.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe start with a short drive from Kathmandu leading North East on the pristine road passing the exciting villages and towns of Thimi and Bhaktapur. Then we head for a climb with tremendous views of Bhaktapur city and Kathmandu valley’s green farmlands and spread out farm villages. After an hour of a rise on the narrow winding road, we reach a famous viewpoint of <strong>Nagarkot</strong>. One of the great destinations near the valley that is great for day-hike and sunrise.\\r\\n\\r\\nNagarkot is situated at 2,175 meters of elevation, and this ramp provides you with a grandstand panorama of the Himalayas. You can see five of the world’s tallest mountains – Everest (8,848m.), Lhotse (8,516m.), Cho Oyu (8,201m.), Makalu (8,463m.) along with their ranges of numerous small peaks. The snow peaks look striking and fabulous at both sunset and sunrise. Nagarkot: surrounded by terraced hillsides and picturesque farmhouses is a piece of the Zion in the earth.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom Nagarkot start walking downhill passing through several rural farmlands with terraces and then you will reach a nice area with a temple of Shiva. This spot is also in a peaceful environment and a perfect setting for your short rest here. Continue to walk to Telkot, a roadside village, and then leave the main motorable road onto the dirt tracks through the pristine forest of rhododendrons, pines, and oaks. The view of the snow-capped mountain towards the north distance wherever you set your foot.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter a nice pleasant walk, reach a small medieval period Newari village where you can experience village life. Life here is unchallenged and unchanged from modernization as it has been for the past many centuries. These settlements take you towards the <strong>Changu Narayan</strong> area. A short walk on steps passing many small souvenir shops and restaurants leads into an old temple complex of the temple. <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changu_Narayan_Temple\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\"><strong>Changu Narayan temple</strong> </a>is a unique ancient temple, one of the oldest in Nepal with a history that dates back to the Lichhavi period.\\r\\n\\r\\nChangu Narayan temple, perched on a hill is also in the <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/discover-nepals-rich-cultural-and-natural-heritage-at-world-heritage-sites/\\"><strong>UNESCO World Cultural Heritage Sites</strong></a> list. A scenic spot situated at an altitude of about 1,700 meters, just north of Bhaktapur. The temple is believed to be the oldest of all the temples in Nepal. It is said to have been built by King Hari Datta Verma in 323 A.D., And the most authentic inscription is located in Changu Narayan and dates back to 464 AD. The Changu Narayan temple is endorsed by King Lichhavi and King Mandeva. The wood and stone carvings in the temple are also sublime, and one can analyze the level of artwork of the most exceptional artists of that time. After a wonderful time here and a nice <strong>hike from Nagarkot to Changu Narayan Temple</strong>, drive back to Kathmandu the same day with an optional tour of Bhaktapur."], "description": "Everest Vacation provides<strong> Nagarkot Sunrise Tour Day hiking</strong> in a serene and wonderful environment outside the valley rim. A day hike of 3-4 hours to the famous tourist spot at <strong>Nagarkot</strong> with an elevation of 2,175 meters high. From the top of Nagarkot, where stands the view and observatory tower you can enjoy the majestic scenic views to your fullest.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe start with a short drive from Kathmandu leading North East on the pristine road passing the exciting villages and towns of Thimi and Bhaktapur. Then we head for a climb with tremendous views of Bhaktapur city and Kathmandu valley’s green farmlands and spread out farm villages. After an hour of a rise on the narrow winding road, we reach a famous viewpoint of <strong>Nagarkot</strong>. One of the great destinations near the valley that is great for day-hike and sunrise.\\r\\n\\r\\nNagarkot is situated at 2,175 meters of elevation, and this ramp provides you with a grandstand panorama of the Himalayas. You can see five of the world’s tallest mountains – Everest (8,848m.), Lhotse (8,516m.), Cho Oyu (8,201m.), Makalu (8,463m.) along with their ranges of numerous small peaks. The snow peaks look striking and fabulous at both sunset and sunrise. Nagarkot: surrounded by terraced hillsides and picturesque farmhouses is a piece of the Zion in the earth.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom Nagarkot start walking downhill passing through several rural farmlands with terraces and then you will reach a nice area with a temple of Shiva. This spot is also in a peaceful environment and a perfect setting for your short rest here. Continue to walk to Telkot, a roadside village, and then leave the main motorable road onto the dirt tracks through the pristine forest of rhododendrons, pines, and oaks. The view of the snow-capped mountain towards the north distance wherever you set your foot.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter a nice pleasant walk, reach a small medieval period Newari village where you can experience village life. Life here is unchallenged and unchanged from modernization as it has been for the past many centuries. These settlements take you towards the <strong>Changu Narayan</strong> area. A short walk on steps passing many small souvenir shops and restaurants leads into an old temple complex of the temple. <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changu_Narayan_Temple\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\"><strong>Changu Narayan temple</strong> </a>is a unique ancient temple, one of the oldest in Nepal with a history that dates back to the Lichhavi period.\\r\\n\\r\\nChangu Narayan temple, perched on a hill is also in the <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/discover-nepals-rich-cultural-and-natural-heritage-at-world-heritage-sites/\\"><strong>UNESCO World Cultural Heritage Sites</strong></a> list. A scenic spot situated at an altitude of about 1,700 meters, just north of Bhaktapur. The temple is believed to be the oldest of all the temples in Nepal. It is said to have been built by King Hari Datta Verma in 323 A.D., And the most authentic inscription is located in Changu Narayan and dates back to 464 AD. The Changu Narayan temple is endorsed by King Lichhavi and King Mandeva. The wood and stone carvings in the temple are also sublime, and one can analyze the level of artwork of the most exceptional artists of that time. After a wonderful time here and a nice <strong>hike from Nagarkot to Changu Narayan Temple</strong>, drive back to Kathmandu the same day with an optional tour of Bhaktapur."}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Transportation from Kathmandu to Nagarkot and Changunarayan Temple to your hotel Kathmandu by private car and driver.", "Breakfast and Lunch with tea/ coffee or soft drinks.", "Changunarayan entrance fee (it is world heritage site by UNESCO).", "One experience hiking guide.", "Guide salary and his meals.", "Driver salary and his meals"], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Transportation from Kathmandu to Nagarkot and Changunarayan Temple to your hotel Kathmandu by private car and driver.", "Breakfast and Lunch with tea/ coffee or soft drinks.", "Changunarayan entrance fee (it is world heritage site by UNESCO).", "One experience hiking guide.", "Guide salary and his meals.", "Driver salary and his meals"], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "Explore Nagarkot Sunrise Tour Day Hiking with Everest Vacation.", "trip_highlights": "<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nNagarkot sunrise tour with day hiking to Changunarayan Temple is a specially designed package for nature loving travelers. This Nagarkot hike from Kathmandu is one of the most exciting and popular day tours with fabulous mountain view. The Himalayan sunrise and beautiful walk through the pristine forest of rhododendron, pines, and oaks are the major attractions of this tour. The snow-capped mountain views and Newari villages will give you a precious memory that will stay in your heart for a long time to come.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>", "trip_type_level": "Easy", "meta_description": "Everest Vacation provides Nagarkot Sunrise Tour Day hiking in a serene and wonderful environment outside the valley rim.", "trip_attractions": "Nagarkot Sunrise, UNESCO World Cultural Heritage Sites", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "faq_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "Nagarkot Sunrise, UNESCO World Cultural Heritage Sites", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "2175 meters", "transportation": ""}, "trip_max_elevation": "2175 meters", "trip_highlights_title": "Nagarkot to Changunarayan Temple day hike from Kathmandu"}	2023-12-04 05:41:37+00	2024-01-24 02:09:37+00
169	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "6", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy"}, "faq": [{"answer": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "question": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "question": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "question": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "question": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "question": "5. What to expect on tours?"}], "meta": {"_edit_last": "5", "_edit_lock": "1706865786:5", "_dp_original": "538", "_thumbnail_id": "798", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "6", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Luxury Helicopter tour in the Himalayas Nepal", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "44", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Luxury Helicopter tour in the Himalayas Nepal gives the best scenic view of Everest, Manaslu, and Jomsom with Upper Mustang and Annapurna.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "luxury-helicopter-tour-himalayas-nepal", "tags": [], "title": "Luxury Helicopter tour in the Himalayas Nepal", "duration": "6 Days", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "When it comes to a Luxury vacation in Asia few come close to what the <strong>Luxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas</strong> <strong>Nepal</strong> can offer. This tour is proven time and again to give the best scenic view of the Everest, Manaslu, Jomsom with Upper Mustang and Annapurna.\\r\\n\\r\\nWith the major delights of Everest Base Camp <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kala_Patthar\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kalapatthar</a>, Manaslu Base Camp, Annapurna Base Camp, Jomsom, Lo Manthang, Pokhara, and Dhulikhel, the best of Nepal are off the charts of anyone’s expectation. All these and more are bound professionally with exquisite hotels, luxury transportation, and the best guides to make sure the trip is exemplary.\\r\\n<h4><strong>Luxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas</strong> <strong>Nepal</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\">Everest Region</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Annapurna Region (Jomsom with Upper Mustang)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Manaslu Region</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Outline Itinerary</h3>\\r\\nDay 01: Arrival at Kathmandu, heritage Tour of the Valley\\r\\n<span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 02: Helicopter tour in the Everest region (Everest Base Camp, Kalapatthar, and Hotel Everest View overnight)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 03: Helicopter flight to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu, and to Pokhara\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 04: Heli flight tour of Annapurna Base Camp, Muktinath temple, Jomsom, and Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 05: Flight by Heli from Jomsom to Pokhara to Dhulikhel (Dwarikas Resort)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 06: Drive to Kathmandu via Bhaktapur tour, Departure</span>"}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Arrival at Kathmandu, heritage Tour of the Valley", "richText": "You will be escorted to the hotel in Thamel after landing at the airport in Kathmandu. After some rest and refreshment, you will take a brief tour of the valley in a luxury vehicle.\\r\\n<h4>About Kathmandu</h4>\\r\\nKathmandu is a cauldron mixing culture and commerce in the lap of Himalayas. Thousands of years of history and art of different eras define this city. Kathmandu is the primary spot to enter Nepal through the air as well. This city oozes culture and architecture which has been there for hundreds of years.\\r\\n\\r\\nLegends say that this valley once was a giant lake cut open for the residents by the Buddhist Deity Manjushree. The local people here are Newars. Newars are known for their traditional way of living and business. These people are also known for their artistic decoration on houses, wooden beams, sculptures and more in the valley.\\r\\n\\r\\nWith seven UNESCO world heritage sites in the valley, travelers can find a pristine repository of history, art, and culture in the valley. Pashupatinath, the monkey temple of Swayambhunath, Boudhanath with other main palaces of medieval Malla Kings defines the city. A small tour of these sites treats visitors with wonderful experiences.\\r\\n\\r\\nCompleting the brief introductory tour of the valley, we will drive you back to the hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at Dwarikas Hotel, Kathmandu <a href=\\"https://www.dwarikas.com/home/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.dwarikas.com/home/</a>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 2, "meal": "", "title": "Heli tour in the Everest region (Everest Base Camp, Kalapatthar, and Hotel Everest View)", "richText": "After a hearty breakfast in the hotel, you will prepare to embrace the Everest. Our guide will escort you to the TIA for your flight. Passing by the green hills and scenic landscape, eye-catching mountain views, rural villages and local communities, we will enter Lukla.\\r\\n<h4>About Lukla</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Heli flight approx Time from Kathmandu to Lukla: </strong>45 minutes helicopter ride from Kathmandu (140 km/87 miles)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Lukla Elevation: </strong>2,845 meters / 9,334 feet above sea level\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Weather/Temperature of Lukla: </strong>The month of July (Warmest Month), with an average temperature of 14.7 °C | 58.5 °F. The month of January (Coldest Month), with temperatures averaging 2.8 °C | 37.0 °F.\\r\\n\\r\\nLukla is an iconic town in Khumbu with the most significant airstrip for travelers to Everest. Also sated as the Gateway to Everest, Lukla is a link to the higher Khumbu region and the Himalayas. At an elevation of 9380 ft. most flights here are in the morning for clear weather. One can get the first glance of Sherpa culture at Lukla.\\r\\n\\r\\nA quick refill-stop here and we are up over the Everest Base Camp and landing at Kalapatther.\\r\\n<blockquote>Helicopter ride start from Lukla to Syangboche to Kalapatthar and land there. Landing time around 10 minutes as the high elevation reason (Helicopter engine will not stop during your landing experience because of high elevation and coldness) and back to Everest View Hotel via Gokyo lake overfly.</blockquote>\\r\\n<em>Note: A helicopter can lift only 3 person at a time in Everest base camp due to high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Pheriche or Shyangboche.</em>\\r\\n<h4>About Everest Base Camp (EBC)</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time to Everest Base Camp / Kalapatthar from Lukla: </strong>25 minutes\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Lukla to EBC: </strong>22.65 miles / 36.46 kilometers\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>EBC Elevation: 5,380 m (17,600 ft) above sea level</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Kalapatther Elevation: 5,643 m (18,514 ft) above sea level</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nEverest Base Camp is about 6 days trek or 25 minutes flight from Lukla. At an elevation of over 17,600 ft., the Southern Base Camp is the starting point of the climb for mountaineers climbing to the Summit from the Nepali side. Once here one can have an unobstructed view of the massive south face of the Everest alongside the other mountains. We can view the base camps with orange tents beside the massive Khumbu glacier flying over it.\\r\\n<h4>About Kalapatther/ Kala Patthar (Black Stone)</h4>\\r\\nKalapatther is one of the most popular and gifted spots to view the massive Everest Massif in its full glory in the Himalayas. It is one of the popular day hiking destinations from the Everest Base Camp as well. This ridge at an elevation of 18500 ft.<a name=\\"_GoBack\\"></a>, this wonderful peak lies before the Everest. Landing here one can have a fantastic view of Mt. Everest (8848 m), Mt.Lhotse (8516 m), Nuptse (7861 m ) and many more. This Panoramic spot is one of the most picturesque places to be in the Everest region.\\r\\n\\r\\nLanding at an elevation as high as Kalapatther, you will have some 15 minutes of ground time due to thin air. After some wonderful memories and pictures from the Kalapatther, we will take off from there.\\r\\n\\r\\nEnjoy the serenity of being close to Everest at Kalapatther and we will continue the Heli Flight to Everest view Hotel. Midway in the flight is the beautiful Gokyo lake complex.\\r\\n<h4>About Gokyo Lake</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time from Kalapatthar/EBC to Hotel Everest View via Gokyo Lake:</strong> 25 minutes\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance: </strong>15.47 miles / 24.90 kilometers\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Gokyo Lakes are the glacial lake complex in the Gokyo valley at an elevation of 4700-5000 m. There are five major lakes and hundreds of others fed by the Ngozumpa glacier. The view of Everest and Cho Oyu is pristine from the valley. These lakes are also considered holy by both Hindu and Buddhist pilgrims. Near the Tibetan border, you can see the ranges on both Nepalese and Tibetan sides touching the horizon.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor our overnight stay, we will land ad rest in the luxurious Hotel Everest View in Syangboche.\\r\\n<h4>About Everest View Hotel</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Syangboche / Hotel Everest View Elevation: </strong>3880 meters (12,730 ft.) above sea level\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Everest View Hotel in Syangboche is a hotel located in one of the highest altitudes in the world. This hotel was listed as the world's highest hotel by the Guinness book of world records in 2004 AD. It is located near the top of the ridge in Syangboche. As the name suggests from the premises of the hotel one can have a breathtaking view of Everest and beyond. Luxury is what best explains the hotel and you can get the best of the Everest here.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at Hotel Everest View, Syangboche. <a href=\\"https://hoteleverestview.com/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://hoteleverestview.com</a>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 3, "meal": "", "title": "Helicopter flight to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu, and to Pokhara", "richText": "<strong>Approx Time:</strong> 1 hours from Shangboche to Kathmandu\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Hotel Everest View to Kathmandu:</strong> 86.12 miles / 138.60 kilometers\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom the Everest View Hotel, view the best of the Sunrise views and breakfast. Leaving the Hotel, we will take a flight back to Kathmandu. Following a brief check and refueling at TIA, we will leave for the Manaslu Base Camp.\\r\\n<h4>About Manaslu Base Camp and Samagaun</h4>\\r\\n<blockquote>Helicopter continue flight from Syangboche to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu (At Manaslu Base Camp, helicopter engine will not stop due to the high elevation), 10-15 minutes landing experiences to take photos, videos or eye catching view of mountains and flying to Pokhara.</blockquote>\\r\\n<em>A helicopter can lift only 3 person at a time in Manaslu base camp due to high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Sama Gaun.</em>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time:</strong> 50 minutes from Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp:</strong> 75.27 miles / 121.13 kilometers\\r\\n\\r\\nManaslu is the eighth highest mountain in the world located in the northern ends of the Gorkha District. Standing 8,163 meters tall this beautiful peak is translated as the 'Mountain of Spirit' in Sanskrit. The base of the mountain is about 5 hours trek or 15 minutes flight from Samagaon village. Manaslu Base Camp is one of the best places to view the Manaslu and Ganesh range.\\r\\n\\r\\nSamagaon is the last major settlement near the Manaslu Base Camp. This Tibetan village is one of the major attractions of the Manaslu Base Camp region. As Manaslu base camp is in a high elevation, you will have a similar brief stop as Kalapatther.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf you are in a group of more than three you will take a shuttle from Samagaun. After leaving the Manaslu Base Camp we will fly to Pokhara. After landing at the airport in Pokhara, we will escort you to the hotel. You will explore the major attractions of the city.\\r\\n<h4>About Pokhara</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Manaslu BC to Pokhara</strong>: 45.55 miles , 73.31 kilometers (km)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time</strong>: 40 minutes from Manaslu Base Camp to Pokhara\\r\\n\\r\\nPokhara is the adventure capital of Nepal. For visitors, this city has everything from viewpoints, to natural sites and religious monuments. Pokhara is also the city of lakes. The Phewa, Rupa, and Begnas lakes are three of the most beautiful ones here. The Tal Barahi (an island temple) in Phewa and Bindabashini temples are the most significant temples of the Pokhara valley. You can involve in paragliding, bungee, kayaking, rock climbing, and other outdoor activities as well in the Pokhara city. The nightlife of Pokhara is also one not to miss while you are here.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at Hotel Tiger Mountain Pokhara. <a href=\\"https://www.tigermountainpokhara.com/\\">https://www.tigermountainpokhara.com</a>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 4, "meal": "", "title": "Heli flight tour of Annapurna Base Camp, Muktinath temple, Jomsom and Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang)", "richText": "After breakfast today you will experience the best of the Annapurna region. Often considered as one of the best destinations of the Himalayas, the tour begins with a flight to the base camp.\\r\\n<h4>About Annapurna Base Camp</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Time:</strong> 25 minutes from Pokhara to Annapurna Base Camp\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Pokhara:</strong> 23.24 miles , 37.40 kilometers (km)\\r\\n<strong>ABC Elevation:</strong> 4130m/13549ft from sea level\\r\\n\\r\\nAnnapurna base Cap is one of the best-selected trekking destinations in Nepal. Located at an elevation of over 4000 meters, it faces the majestic Annapurna Massif. Once in the base camp, you can have a 360° view of the Annapurna, Machhapuchhre (fishtail), and Dhaulagiri mountains. Considered as one of the most difficult peaks to climb of the 8 thousanders, Annapurna is beautiful. The base camp is gifted with scenery and views like no other place in the Himalayas.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter the pristine view of snow-capped mountains and landscape, we will leave the base camp and head towards Muktinath via Pokhara.\\r\\n<h4>About Muktinath</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time</strong>: 55 minutes from Pokhara to Muktinath Temple\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance</strong>: Pokhara and Muktinath is 67 KM (kilometers) and 119.89 meters. The mile based measurement distance is 41.7 miles\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Muktinath Elevation: </strong>World's highest temples (altitude 3,800 m) above sea level\\r\\n<blockquote>Pokhara to Annapurna base camp, after refreshment there will return Pokhara for fueling and flight to Muktinath Temple. And 10 minutes flight to Jomsom and continue flight to Lo Manthang (Upper MUstang) and back to Jomsom for overnight.</blockquote>\\r\\nMuktinath is one of the most significant shrines in the Himalayas of Nepal. This temple is visited by hundreds of thousand Buddhist and Hindu pilgrims alike from different Asian countries. Located at the Mustang district, trekkers doing the Annapurna Circuit do the Thorung La Pass (5416 m) from Manang to reach here. Muktinath is also amongst the highest Hindu shrines around the world. Pilgrims believe that a visit here and a bath can wash away the sins of the past and present life. The Landscape surrounding the temple is also wonderful.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter a spiritual tour of Muktinath, we will head to Jomsom (10 minutes flight) for refueling.\\r\\n<h4>About Jomsom</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Jomsom Elevation: </strong>Altitude 2700 m above sea level\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time:</strong> 10 minutes from Muktinath to Jomsom.\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Muktinath:</strong> 8.61 miles , 13.86 kilometers (km)\\r\\n\\r\\nJomsom is an iconic town in the Mustang District also acting as its administrative headquarters. The Airstrip here is one of the busiest in the Annapurna region and easily accessible from the Pokhara airport. Jomsom is also one of the best places to start the trekking to different destinations of the region.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will fly from Jomsom to Lo Manthang next. As a restricted area, we will need permits and a legend officer will accompany you to Lo Manthang.\\r\\n<h4>About Lo Manthang</h4>\\r\\n<blockquote>As a Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang) is a restricted area, a legend officer flying with you to Lo Manthang from Jomsom.</blockquote>\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time</strong>: 20 minutes from Jomsom to Lomanthang\\r\\n<strong>Distance: </strong>30.75 miles / 49.49 kilometers (km) from Jomsom\\r\\n<strong>Lo-Manthang Elevation</strong>: 3,840 m (12,600 ft)<strong> </strong>above sea level\\r\\nLanding time: around 1 Hour in Lo-Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\r\\n\\r\\nLo Manthang in Upper Mustang was the ancient capital of the Kingdom of Lho. This walled city in the heart of Mustang is a repository of culture and traditional art of the local people here. The monasteries, Chhortens, houses and Mani walls of the city reflect the constituents of Tibetan Buddhism. in the center of the city is the ancient palace of the king of Lho. Visiting the region gives one an opportunity to embrace and discover the lifestyle, history, and culture of the locals here. Lo Manthang is one of the major destinations of the upper Mustang tour.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter the tour of Lo Manthang, we will fly back to a lodge in Thasang near Jomsom and rest for the day.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at Thasang Village Lodge, Jomsom. <a href=\\"http://lodgethasangvillage.com/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">http://lodgethasangvillage.com</a>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 5, "meal": "", "title": "Flight by Heli from Jomsom to Pokhara to Dhulikhel (Dwarika Resort)", "richText": "After breakfast at Jomsom, we will fly to Pokhara. Here we will have a brief stop and fly to Dhulikhel city near Kathmandu.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Time from Jomsom to Pokhara</strong>: 45 minutes; Distance: 42.72 miles , 68.76 kilometers\\r\\n<strong>Time from Pokhara to Dhulikhel</strong>: 1 hour via Kathmandu\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Pokhara to Dhulikhel</strong>: 103.70 miles / 166.89 kilometers\\r\\n<strong>Dhulikhel Elevation</strong>: 1550 m above sea level\\r\\n<h4>About Dhulikhel</h4>\\r\\nDhulikhel is a cultural city just outside the Kathmandu valley in the Kabhrepalanchowk district. Popular for the wood arts, monuments, and traditions, Dhulikhel also offers some fantastic views of hills and Himalayas. The temples, houses, and streets here reflect the well-preserved culture of the local Newari people here. You can visit some of the nearby viewpoints and dive into the scenic nature during the Dhulikhel tour.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will return to the Dwarika resort for the night known for authentic royal services and luxury throughout Nepal.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at Dwarika's Resort Dhulikhel. <a href=\\"https://dwarikas-dhulikhel.com/home\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://dwarikas-dhulikhel.com/home</a>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 6, "meal": "", "title": "Drive to Kathmandu via Bhaktapur tour, Departure", "richText": "<div id=\\"collapse-6\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-6\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will drive you back to Kathmandu in a luxury vehicle after breakfast. You have an option to visit the Bhaktapur city midway of the drive from Dhulikhel.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Driving distance:</strong> 18.96 miles , 30.52 kilometers (km) from Dhulikhel to Kathmandu TIA airport\\r\\n<h4>About Bhaktapur</h4>\\r\\nBhaktapur is the most preserved of the main three cities in Kathmandu. Locals still follow their traditional lifestyle here. You can try some of the best Newari cuisines here. Bhaktapur is also home to two of the UNESCO world heritage sites the Bhaktapur Durbar Square and Changunarayan Temple. Apart from these, there are many temples, squares, monuments, and shrines worth visiting in the city.\\r\\n\\r\\nOur guides will escort you back to the airport before the flight. You can also do some souvenir shopping accompanied by our guides in Thamel. Return with some magnificent memories and moments from the luxury helicopter tour of Nepal.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Helicopter-at-Everest-View-Hotel-Syangboche.jpg", "title": "Helicopter-at-Everest-View-Hotel-Syangboche", "altText": "Helicopter-at-Everest-View-Hotel-Syangboche", "caption": "Helicopter-at-Everest-View-Hotel-Syangboche", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["543", "596", "599", "586", "688", "798", "799"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "ws_trip_faqs_lists": 5, "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists": "field_63ede38e351c7", "ws_block_attractions": "Heli Tour Kathmandu, Everest, Manaslu, Pokhara, Annapurna, Muktinath, Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang) & Dhulikhel", "ws_block_best_season": "", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-light", "ws_block_accommodation": "Luxury Hotels/Resorts", "ws_block_max_elevation": "", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": "Overview", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc6695edb31", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_block_transportation": "Helicopter", "ws_trip_galleries_title": "Photo/Visual Gallery", "_ws_block_transportation": "field_63eeee74072de", "_ws_trip_galleries_title": "field_63ec89128acaa", "starter_kit_padding_type": "p-medium", "ws_trip_block_highlights": "Only Helicopter Tour - Luxury Trip with Luxury Accommodation, Luxury vehicle from Hotel to Helipad/Airport, Hotels with Helipad, Kathmandu to Everest Helicopter, Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp Heli, Manaslu Base Camp to Pokhara Heli Services, Pokhara to Annapurna Base Camp, Pokhara to Jomsom Muktinath Heli ride, Jomsom to Lo Manthang Helicopter, Jomsom to Pokhara and to Dhulikhel Helicopter Tour", "ws_trip_information_list": 2, "_starter_kit_padding_type": "field_5f8584c998bc2", "_ws_trip_block_highlights": "field_63ec73a6a0d8f", "_ws_trip_information_list": "field_63ec90a574f02", "starter_kit_section_title": "Day by Day Activities", "_starter_kit_section_title": "field_63ec948c94a16", "starter_kit_enable_section": "1", "ws_trip_faqs_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "_starter_kit_enable_section": "field_63edeb1c7635c", "_ws_trip_faqs_section_title": "field_63ede33e5b304", "starter_kit_section_padding": "", "ws_trip_include_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>The price (cost) for this helicopter tour </strong>might vary with the number of travelers, accommodation type, meals, tour duration, travel season (travel date), routes and activities being the major factors. You can customize these find your ideal package which might not be same with cheaper deals elsewhere. Rest assured, make your visit worth every bit with us.\\r\\n\\r\\nPlease, send your tentative tour plan with interested region (Everest, Annapurna, Manaslu etc.) by submitting our right (below) side form.</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_starter_kit_section_padding": "field_5f3e0f86a2634", "_ws_trip_include_description": "field_63edd6a337cd0", "ws_trip_overview_description": "When it comes to a Luxury vacation in Asia few come close to what the <strong>Luxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas</strong> <strong>Nepal</strong> can offer. This tour is proven time and again to give the best scenic view of the Everest, Manaslu, Jomsom with Upper Mustang and Annapurna.\\r\\n\\r\\nWith the major delights of Everest Base Camp <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kala_Patthar\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kalapatthar</a>, Manaslu Base Camp, Annapurna Base Camp, Jomsom, Lo Manthang, Pokhara, and Dhulikhel, the best of Nepal are off the charts of anyone’s expectation. All these and more are bound professionally with exquisite hotels, luxury transportation, and the best guides to make sure the trip is exemplary.\\r\\n<h4><strong>Luxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas</strong> <strong>Nepal</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\">Everest Region</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Annapurna Region (Jomsom with Upper Mustang)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Manaslu Region</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Outline Itinerary</h3>\\r\\nDay 01: Arrival at Kathmandu, heritage Tour of the Valley\\r\\n<span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 02: Helicopter tour in the Everest region (Everest Base Camp, Kalapatthar, and Hotel Everest View overnight)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 03: Helicopter flight to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu, and to Pokhara\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 04: Heli flight tour of Annapurna Base Camp, Muktinath temple, Jomsom, and Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 05: Flight by Heli from Jomsom to Pokhara to Dhulikhel (Dwarikas Resort)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 06: Drive to Kathmandu via Bhaktapur tour, Departure</span>", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "EXPENSIVE TOUR: Luxury Helicopter Tours with Luxury Accommodation in Nepal Himalayas including Everest and Annapurna Region", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "5. What to expect on tours?", "_ws_trip_fact_short_description": "field_63ec73a69d305", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "01", "ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "02", "ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "03", "ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "04", "ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "05", "ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days": "06", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "Arrival at Kathmandu, heritage Tour of the Valley", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "Heli tour in the Everest region (Everest Base Camp, Kalapatthar, and Hotel Everest View)", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "Helicopter flight to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu, and to Pokhara", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "Heli flight tour of Annapurna Base Camp, Muktinath temple, Jomsom and Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang)", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title": "Flight by Heli from Jomsom to Pokhara to Dhulikhel (Dwarika Resort)", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title": "Drive to Kathmandu via Bhaktapur tour, Departure", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "Extended Tours", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title": "Alternate Tours", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "You will be escorted to the hotel in Thamel after landing at the airport in Kathmandu. After some rest and refreshment, you will take a brief tour of the valley in a luxury vehicle.\\r\\n<h4>About Kathmandu</h4>\\r\\nKathmandu is a cauldron mixing culture and commerce in the lap of Himalayas. Thousands of years of history and art of different eras define this city. Kathmandu is the primary spot to enter Nepal through the air as well. This city oozes culture and architecture which has been there for hundreds of years.\\r\\n\\r\\nLegends say that this valley once was a giant lake cut open for the residents by the Buddhist Deity Manjushree. The local people here are Newars. Newars are known for their traditional way of living and business. These people are also known for their artistic decoration on houses, wooden beams, sculptures and more in the valley.\\r\\n\\r\\nWith seven UNESCO world heritage sites in the valley, travelers can find a pristine repository of history, art, and culture in the valley. Pashupatinath, the monkey temple of Swayambhunath, Boudhanath with other main palaces of medieval Malla Kings defines the city. A small tour of these sites treats visitors with wonderful experiences.\\r\\n\\r\\nCompleting the brief introductory tour of the valley, we will drive you back to the hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at Dwarikas Hotel, Kathmandu <a href=\\"https://www.dwarikas.com/home/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.dwarikas.com/home/</a>", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "After a hearty breakfast in the hotel, you will prepare to embrace the Everest. Our guide will escort you to the TIA for your flight. Passing by the green hills and scenic landscape, eye-catching mountain views, rural villages and local communities, we will enter Lukla.\\r\\n<h4>About Lukla</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Heli flight approx Time from Kathmandu to Lukla: </strong>45 minutes helicopter ride from Kathmandu (140 km/87 miles)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Lukla Elevation: </strong>2,845 meters / 9,334 feet above sea level\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Weather/Temperature of Lukla: </strong>The month of July (Warmest Month), with an average temperature of 14.7 °C | 58.5 °F. The month of January (Coldest Month), with temperatures averaging 2.8 °C | 37.0 °F.\\r\\n\\r\\nLukla is an iconic town in Khumbu with the most significant airstrip for travelers to Everest. Also sated as the Gateway to Everest, Lukla is a link to the higher Khumbu region and the Himalayas. At an elevation of 9380 ft. most flights here are in the morning for clear weather. One can get the first glance of Sherpa culture at Lukla.\\r\\n\\r\\nA quick refill-stop here and we are up over the Everest Base Camp and landing at Kalapatther.\\r\\n<blockquote>Helicopter ride start from Lukla to Syangboche to Kalapatthar and land there. Landing time around 10 minutes as the high elevation reason (Helicopter engine will not stop during your landing experience because of high elevation and coldness) and back to Everest View Hotel via Gokyo lake overfly.</blockquote>\\r\\n<em>Note: A helicopter can lift only 3 person at a time in Everest base camp due to high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Pheriche or Shyangboche.</em>\\r\\n<h4>About Everest Base Camp (EBC)</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time to Everest Base Camp / Kalapatthar from Lukla: </strong>25 minutes\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Lukla to EBC: </strong>22.65 miles / 36.46 kilometers\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>EBC Elevation: 5,380 m (17,600 ft) above sea level</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Kalapatther Elevation: 5,643 m (18,514 ft) above sea level</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nEverest Base Camp is about 6 days trek or 25 minutes flight from Lukla. At an elevation of over 17,600 ft., the Southern Base Camp is the starting point of the climb for mountaineers climbing to the Summit from the Nepali side. Once here one can have an unobstructed view of the massive south face of the Everest alongside the other mountains. We can view the base camps with orange tents beside the massive Khumbu glacier flying over it.\\r\\n<h4>About Kalapatther/ Kala Patthar (Black Stone)</h4>\\r\\nKalapatther is one of the most popular and gifted spots to view the massive Everest Massif in its full glory in the Himalayas. It is one of the popular day hiking destinations from the Everest Base Camp as well. This ridge at an elevation of 18500 ft.<a name=\\"_GoBack\\"></a>, this wonderful peak lies before the Everest. Landing here one can have a fantastic view of Mt. Everest (8848 m), Mt.Lhotse (8516 m), Nuptse (7861 m ) and many more. This Panoramic spot is one of the most picturesque places to be in the Everest region.\\r\\n\\r\\nLanding at an elevation as high as Kalapatther, you will have some 15 minutes of ground time due to thin air. After some wonderful memories and pictures from the Kalapatther, we will take off from there.\\r\\n\\r\\nEnjoy the serenity of being close to Everest at Kalapatther and we will continue the Heli Flight to Everest view Hotel. Midway in the flight is the beautiful Gokyo lake complex.\\r\\n<h4>About Gokyo Lake</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time from Kalapatthar/EBC to Hotel Everest View via Gokyo Lake:</strong> 25 minutes\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance: </strong>15.47 miles / 24.90 kilometers\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Gokyo Lakes are the glacial lake complex in the Gokyo valley at an elevation of 4700-5000 m. There are five major lakes and hundreds of others fed by the Ngozumpa glacier. The view of Everest and Cho Oyu is pristine from the valley. These lakes are also considered holy by both Hindu and Buddhist pilgrims. Near the Tibetan border, you can see the ranges on both Nepalese and Tibetan sides touching the horizon.\\r\\n\\r\\nFor our overnight stay, we will land ad rest in the luxurious Hotel Everest View in Syangboche.\\r\\n<h4>About Everest View Hotel</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Syangboche / Hotel Everest View Elevation: </strong>3880 meters (12,730 ft.) above sea level\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Everest View Hotel in Syangboche is a hotel located in one of the highest altitudes in the world. This hotel was listed as the world's highest hotel by the Guinness book of world records in 2004 AD. It is located near the top of the ridge in Syangboche. As the name suggests from the premises of the hotel one can have a breathtaking view of Everest and beyond. Luxury is what best explains the hotel and you can get the best of the Everest here.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at Hotel Everest View, Syangboche. <a href=\\"https://hoteleverestview.com/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://hoteleverestview.com</a>", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "<strong>Approx Time:</strong> 1 hours from Shangboche to Kathmandu\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Hotel Everest View to Kathmandu:</strong> 86.12 miles / 138.60 kilometers\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom the Everest View Hotel, view the best of the Sunrise views and breakfast. Leaving the Hotel, we will take a flight back to Kathmandu. Following a brief check and refueling at TIA, we will leave for the Manaslu Base Camp.\\r\\n<h4>About Manaslu Base Camp and Samagaun</h4>\\r\\n<blockquote>Helicopter continue flight from Syangboche to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu (At Manaslu Base Camp, helicopter engine will not stop due to the high elevation), 10-15 minutes landing experiences to take photos, videos or eye catching view of mountains and flying to Pokhara.</blockquote>\\r\\n<em>A helicopter can lift only 3 person at a time in Manaslu base camp due to high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Sama Gaun.</em>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time:</strong> 50 minutes from Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp:</strong> 75.27 miles / 121.13 kilometers\\r\\n\\r\\nManaslu is the eighth highest mountain in the world located in the northern ends of the Gorkha District. Standing 8,163 meters tall this beautiful peak is translated as the 'Mountain of Spirit' in Sanskrit. The base of the mountain is about 5 hours trek or 15 minutes flight from Samagaon village. Manaslu Base Camp is one of the best places to view the Manaslu and Ganesh range.\\r\\n\\r\\nSamagaon is the last major settlement near the Manaslu Base Camp. This Tibetan village is one of the major attractions of the Manaslu Base Camp region. As Manaslu base camp is in a high elevation, you will have a similar brief stop as Kalapatther.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf you are in a group of more than three you will take a shuttle from Samagaun. After leaving the Manaslu Base Camp we will fly to Pokhara. After landing at the airport in Pokhara, we will escort you to the hotel. You will explore the major attractions of the city.\\r\\n<h4>About Pokhara</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Manaslu BC to Pokhara</strong>: 45.55 miles , 73.31 kilometers (km)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time</strong>: 40 minutes from Manaslu Base Camp to Pokhara\\r\\n\\r\\nPokhara is the adventure capital of Nepal. For visitors, this city has everything from viewpoints, to natural sites and religious monuments. Pokhara is also the city of lakes. The Phewa, Rupa, and Begnas lakes are three of the most beautiful ones here. The Tal Barahi (an island temple) in Phewa and Bindabashini temples are the most significant temples of the Pokhara valley. You can involve in paragliding, bungee, kayaking, rock climbing, and other outdoor activities as well in the Pokhara city. The nightlife of Pokhara is also one not to miss while you are here.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at Hotel Tiger Mountain Pokhara. <a href=\\"https://www.tigermountainpokhara.com/\\">https://www.tigermountainpokhara.com</a>", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "After breakfast today you will experience the best of the Annapurna region. Often considered as one of the best destinations of the Himalayas, the tour begins with a flight to the base camp.\\r\\n<h4>About Annapurna Base Camp</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Time:</strong> 25 minutes from Pokhara to Annapurna Base Camp\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Pokhara:</strong> 23.24 miles , 37.40 kilometers (km)\\r\\n<strong>ABC Elevation:</strong> 4130m/13549ft from sea level\\r\\n\\r\\nAnnapurna base Cap is one of the best-selected trekking destinations in Nepal. Located at an elevation of over 4000 meters, it faces the majestic Annapurna Massif. Once in the base camp, you can have a 360° view of the Annapurna, Machhapuchhre (fishtail), and Dhaulagiri mountains. Considered as one of the most difficult peaks to climb of the 8 thousanders, Annapurna is beautiful. The base camp is gifted with scenery and views like no other place in the Himalayas.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter the pristine view of snow-capped mountains and landscape, we will leave the base camp and head towards Muktinath via Pokhara.\\r\\n<h4>About Muktinath</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time</strong>: 55 minutes from Pokhara to Muktinath Temple\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance</strong>: Pokhara and Muktinath is 67 KM (kilometers) and 119.89 meters. The mile based measurement distance is 41.7 miles\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Muktinath Elevation: </strong>World's highest temples (altitude 3,800 m) above sea level\\r\\n<blockquote>Pokhara to Annapurna base camp, after refreshment there will return Pokhara for fueling and flight to Muktinath Temple. And 10 minutes flight to Jomsom and continue flight to Lo Manthang (Upper MUstang) and back to Jomsom for overnight.</blockquote>\\r\\nMuktinath is one of the most significant shrines in the Himalayas of Nepal. This temple is visited by hundreds of thousand Buddhist and Hindu pilgrims alike from different Asian countries. Located at the Mustang district, trekkers doing the Annapurna Circuit do the Thorung La Pass (5416 m) from Manang to reach here. Muktinath is also amongst the highest Hindu shrines around the world. Pilgrims believe that a visit here and a bath can wash away the sins of the past and present life. The Landscape surrounding the temple is also wonderful.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter a spiritual tour of Muktinath, we will head to Jomsom (10 minutes flight) for refueling.\\r\\n<h4>About Jomsom</h4>\\r\\n<strong>Jomsom Elevation: </strong>Altitude 2700 m above sea level\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time:</strong> 10 minutes from Muktinath to Jomsom.\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Muktinath:</strong> 8.61 miles , 13.86 kilometers (km)\\r\\n\\r\\nJomsom is an iconic town in the Mustang District also acting as its administrative headquarters. The Airstrip here is one of the busiest in the Annapurna region and easily accessible from the Pokhara airport. Jomsom is also one of the best places to start the trekking to different destinations of the region.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will fly from Jomsom to Lo Manthang next. As a restricted area, we will need permits and a legend officer will accompany you to Lo Manthang.\\r\\n<h4>About Lo Manthang</h4>\\r\\n<blockquote>As a Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang) is a restricted area, a legend officer flying with you to Lo Manthang from Jomsom.</blockquote>\\r\\n<strong>Approx Time</strong>: 20 minutes from Jomsom to Lomanthang\\r\\n<strong>Distance: </strong>30.75 miles / 49.49 kilometers (km) from Jomsom\\r\\n<strong>Lo-Manthang Elevation</strong>: 3,840 m (12,600 ft)<strong> </strong>above sea level\\r\\nLanding time: around 1 Hour in Lo-Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\r\\n\\r\\nLo Manthang in Upper Mustang was the ancient capital of the Kingdom of Lho. This walled city in the heart of Mustang is a repository of culture and traditional art of the local people here. The monasteries, Chhortens, houses and Mani walls of the city reflect the constituents of Tibetan Buddhism. in the center of the city is the ancient palace of the king of Lho. Visiting the region gives one an opportunity to embrace and discover the lifestyle, history, and culture of the locals here. Lo Manthang is one of the major destinations of the upper Mustang tour.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter the tour of Lo Manthang, we will fly back to a lodge in Thasang near Jomsom and rest for the day.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at Thasang Village Lodge, Jomsom. <a href=\\"http://lodgethasangvillage.com/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">http://lodgethasangvillage.com</a>", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description": "After breakfast at Jomsom, we will fly to Pokhara. Here we will have a brief stop and fly to Dhulikhel city near Kathmandu.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Time from Jomsom to Pokhara</strong>: 45 minutes; Distance: 42.72 miles , 68.76 kilometers\\r\\n<strong>Time from Pokhara to Dhulikhel</strong>: 1 hour via Kathmandu\\r\\n<strong>Distance from Pokhara to Dhulikhel</strong>: 103.70 miles / 166.89 kilometers\\r\\n<strong>Dhulikhel Elevation</strong>: 1550 m above sea level\\r\\n<h4>About Dhulikhel</h4>\\r\\nDhulikhel is a cultural city just outside the Kathmandu valley in the Kabhrepalanchowk district. Popular for the wood arts, monuments, and traditions, Dhulikhel also offers some fantastic views of hills and Himalayas. The temples, houses, and streets here reflect the well-preserved culture of the local Newari people here. You can visit some of the nearby viewpoints and dive into the scenic nature during the Dhulikhel tour.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will return to the Dwarika resort for the night known for authentic royal services and luxury throughout Nepal.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at Dwarika's Resort Dhulikhel. <a href=\\"https://dwarikas-dhulikhel.com/home\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://dwarikas-dhulikhel.com/home</a>", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description": "<div id=\\"collapse-6\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-6\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will drive you back to Kathmandu in a luxury vehicle after breakfast. You have an option to visit the Bhaktapur city midway of the drive from Dhulikhel.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Driving distance:</strong> 18.96 miles , 30.52 kilometers (km) from Dhulikhel to Kathmandu TIA airport\\r\\n<h4>About Bhaktapur</h4>\\r\\nBhaktapur is the most preserved of the main three cities in Kathmandu. Locals still follow their traditional lifestyle here. You can try some of the best Newari cuisines here. Bhaktapur is also home to two of the UNESCO world heritage sites the Bhaktapur Durbar Square and Changunarayan Temple. Apart from these, there are many temples, squares, monuments, and shrines worth visiting in the city.\\r\\n\\r\\nOur guides will escort you back to the airport before the flight. You can also do some souvenir shopping accompanied by our guides in Thamel. Return with some magnificent memories and moments from the luxury helicopter tour of Nepal.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630"}, "categoryId": null, "meta_title": "Luxury Helicopter tour in the Himalayas Nepal | Everest Vacation", "blogContent": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"EXPENSIVE TOUR: Luxury Helicopter Tours with Luxury Accommodation in Nepal Himalayas including Everest and Annapurna Region\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"Only Helicopter Tour - Luxury Trip with Luxury Accommodation, Luxury vehicle from Hotel to Helipad/Airport, Hotels with Helipad, Kathmandu to Everest Helicopter, Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp Heli, Manaslu Base Camp to Pokhara Heli Services, Pokhara to Annapurna Base Camp, Pokhara to Jomsom Muktinath Heli ride, Jomsom to Lo Manthang Helicopter, Jomsom to Pokhara and to Dhulikhel Helicopter Tour\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Heli Tour Kathmandu, Everest, Manaslu, Pokhara, Annapurna, Muktinath, Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang) \\\\u0026 Dhulikhel\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"Luxury Hotels/Resorts\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Helicopter\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"When it comes to a Luxury vacation in Asia few come close to what the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLuxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNepal\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e can offer. This tour is proven time and again to give the best scenic view of the Everest, Manaslu, Jomsom with Upper Mustang and Annapurna.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWith the major delights of Everest Base Camp \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kala_Patthar\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKalapatthar\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e, Manaslu Base Camp, Annapurna Base Camp, Jomsom, Lo Manthang, Pokhara, and Dhulikhel, the best of Nepal are off the charts of anyone’s expectation. All these and more are bound professionally with exquisite hotels, luxury transportation, and the best guides to make sure the trip is exemplary.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLuxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNepal\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022\\\\u003eEverest Region\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAnnapurna Region (Jomsom with Upper Mustang)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eManaslu Region\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eOutline Itinerary\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nDay 01: Arrival at Kathmandu, heritage Tour of the Valley\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cspan class=\\\\u0022redactor-invisible-space\\\\u0022\\\\u003eDay 02: Helicopter tour in the Everest region (Everest Base Camp, Kalapatthar, and Hotel Everest View overnight)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/span\\\\u003e\\\\u003cspan class=\\\\u0022redactor-invisible-space\\\\u0022\\\\u003eDay 03: Helicopter flight to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu, and to Pokhara\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/span\\\\u003e\\\\u003cspan class=\\\\u0022redactor-invisible-space\\\\u0022\\\\u003eDay 04: Heli flight tour of Annapurna Base Camp, Muktinath temple, Jomsom, and Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/span\\\\u003e\\\\u003cspan class=\\\\u0022redactor-invisible-space\\\\u0022\\\\u003eDay 05: Flight by Heli from Jomsom to Pokhara to Dhulikhel (Dwarikas Resort)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/span\\\\u003e\\\\u003cspan class=\\\\u0022redactor-invisible-space\\\\u0022\\\\u003eDay 06: Drive to Kathmandu via Bhaktapur tour, Departure\\\\u003c/span\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"543\\",\\"596\\",\\"599\\",\\"586\\",\\"688\\",\\"798\\",\\"799\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Arrival at Kathmandu, heritage Tour of the Valley\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"You will be escorted to the hotel in Thamel after landing at the airport in Kathmandu. After some rest and refreshment, you will take a brief tour of the valley in a luxury vehicle.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Kathmandu\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nKathmandu is a cauldron mixing culture and commerce in the lap of Himalayas. Thousands of years of history and art of different eras define this city. Kathmandu is the primary spot to enter Nepal through the air as well. This city oozes culture and architecture which has been there for hundreds of years.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLegends say that this valley once was a giant lake cut open for the residents by the Buddhist Deity Manjushree. The local people here are Newars. Newars are known for their traditional way of living and business. These people are also known for their artistic decoration on houses, wooden beams, sculptures and more in the valley.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWith seven UNESCO world heritage sites in the valley, travelers can find a pristine repository of history, art, and culture in the valley. Pashupatinath, the monkey temple of Swayambhunath, Boudhanath with other main palaces of medieval Malla Kings defines the city. A small tour of these sites treats visitors with wonderful experiences.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nCompleting the brief introductory tour of the valley, we will drive you back to the hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at Dwarikas Hotel, Kathmandu \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://www.dwarikas.com/home/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttps://www.dwarikas.com/home/\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Heli tour in the Everest region (Everest Base Camp, Kalapatthar, and Hotel Everest View)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After a hearty breakfast in the hotel, you will prepare to embrace the Everest. Our guide will escort you to the TIA for your flight. Passing by the green hills and scenic landscape, eye-catching mountain views, rural villages and local communities, we will enter Lukla.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Lukla\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHeli flight approx Time from Kathmandu to Lukla: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e45 minutes helicopter ride from Kathmandu (140 km/87 miles)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLukla Elevation: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e2,845 meters / 9,334 feet above sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eWeather/Temperature of Lukla: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eThe month of July (Warmest Month), with an average temperature of 14.7 °C | 58.5 °F. The month of January (Coldest Month), with temperatures averaging 2.8 °C | 37.0 °F.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLukla is an iconic town in Khumbu with the most significant airstrip for travelers to Everest. Also sated as the Gateway to Everest, Lukla is a link to the higher Khumbu region and the Himalayas. At an elevation of 9380 ft. most flights here are in the morning for clear weather. One can get the first glance of Sherpa culture at Lukla.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nA quick refill-stop here and we are up over the Everest Base Camp and landing at Kalapatther.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003eHelicopter ride start from Lukla to Syangboche to Kalapatthar and land there. Landing time around 10 minutes as the high elevation reason (Helicopter engine will not stop during your landing experience because of high elevation and coldness) and back to Everest View Hotel via Gokyo lake overfly.\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cem\\\\u003eNote: A helicopter can lift only 3 person at a time in Everest base camp due to high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Pheriche or Shyangboche.\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Everest Base Camp (EBC)\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time to Everest Base Camp / Kalapatthar from Lukla: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e25 minutes\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Lukla to EBC: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e22.65 miles / 36.46 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eEBC Elevation: 5,380 m (17,600 ft) above sea level\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKalapatther Elevation: 5,643 m (18,514 ft) above sea level\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nEverest Base Camp is about 6 days trek or 25 minutes flight from Lukla. At an elevation of over 17,600 ft., the Southern Base Camp is the starting point of the climb for mountaineers climbing to the Summit from the Nepali side. Once here one can have an unobstructed view of the massive south face of the Everest alongside the other mountains. We can view the base camps with orange tents beside the massive Khumbu glacier flying over it.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Kalapatther/ Kala Patthar (Black Stone)\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nKalapatther is one of the most popular and gifted spots to view the massive Everest Massif in its full glory in the Himalayas. It is one of the popular day hiking destinations from the Everest Base Camp as well. This ridge at an elevation of 18500 ft.\\\\u003ca name=\\\\u0022_GoBack\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e, this wonderful peak lies before the Everest. Landing here one can have a fantastic view of Mt. Everest (8848 m), Mt.Lhotse (8516 m), Nuptse (7861 m ) and many more. This Panoramic spot is one of the most picturesque places to be in the Everest region.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLanding at an elevation as high as Kalapatther, you will have some 15 minutes of ground time due to thin air. After some wonderful memories and pictures from the Kalapatther, we will take off from there.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nEnjoy the serenity of being close to Everest at Kalapatther and we will continue the Heli Flight to Everest view Hotel. Midway in the flight is the beautiful Gokyo lake complex.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Gokyo Lake\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time from Kalapatthar/EBC to Hotel Everest View via Gokyo Lake:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 25 minutes\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e15.47 miles / 24.90 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe Gokyo Lakes are the glacial lake complex in the Gokyo valley at an elevation of 4700-5000 m. There are five major lakes and hundreds of others fed by the Ngozumpa glacier. The view of Everest and Cho Oyu is pristine from the valley. These lakes are also considered holy by both Hindu and Buddhist pilgrims. Near the Tibetan border, you can see the ranges on both Nepalese and Tibetan sides touching the horizon.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFor our overnight stay, we will land ad rest in the luxurious Hotel Everest View in Syangboche.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Everest View Hotel\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSyangboche / Hotel Everest View Elevation: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e3880 meters (12,730 ft.) above sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe Everest View Hotel in Syangboche is a hotel located in one of the highest altitudes in the world. This hotel was listed as the world's highest hotel by the Guinness book of world records in 2004 AD. It is located near the top of the ridge in Syangboche. As the name suggests from the premises of the hotel one can have a breathtaking view of Everest and beyond. Luxury is what best explains the hotel and you can get the best of the Everest here.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at Hotel Everest View, Syangboche. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://hoteleverestview.com/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttps://hoteleverestview.com\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Helicopter flight to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu, and to Pokhara\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 1 hours from Shangboche to Kathmandu\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Hotel Everest View to Kathmandu:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 86.12 miles / 138.60 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom the Everest View Hotel, view the best of the Sunrise views and breakfast. Leaving the Hotel, we will take a flight back to Kathmandu. Following a brief check and refueling at TIA, we will leave for the Manaslu Base Camp.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Manaslu Base Camp and Samagaun\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003eHelicopter continue flight from Syangboche to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu (At Manaslu Base Camp, helicopter engine will not stop due to the high elevation), 10-15 minutes landing experiences to take photos, videos or eye catching view of mountains and flying to Pokhara.\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cem\\\\u003eA helicopter can lift only 3 person at a time in Manaslu base camp due to high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Sama Gaun.\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 50 minutes from Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 75.27 miles / 121.13 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nManaslu is the eighth highest mountain in the world located in the northern ends of the Gorkha District. Standing 8,163 meters tall this beautiful peak is translated as the 'Mountain of Spirit' in Sanskrit. The base of the mountain is about 5 hours trek or 15 minutes flight from Samagaon village. Manaslu Base Camp is one of the best places to view the Manaslu and Ganesh range.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nSamagaon is the last major settlement near the Manaslu Base Camp. This Tibetan village is one of the major attractions of the Manaslu Base Camp region. As Manaslu base camp is in a high elevation, you will have a similar brief stop as Kalapatther.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIf you are in a group of more than three you will take a shuttle from Samagaun. After leaving the Manaslu Base Camp we will fly to Pokhara. After landing at the airport in Pokhara, we will escort you to the hotel. You will explore the major attractions of the city.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Pokhara\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Manaslu BC to Pokhara\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 45.55 miles , 73.31 kilometers (km)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 40 minutes from Manaslu Base Camp to Pokhara\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nPokhara is the adventure capital of Nepal. For visitors, this city has everything from viewpoints, to natural sites and religious monuments. Pokhara is also the city of lakes. The Phewa, Rupa, and Begnas lakes are three of the most beautiful ones here. The Tal Barahi (an island temple) in Phewa and Bindabashini temples are the most significant temples of the Pokhara valley. You can involve in paragliding, bungee, kayaking, rock climbing, and other outdoor activities as well in the Pokhara city. The nightlife of Pokhara is also one not to miss while you are here.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at Hotel Tiger Mountain Pokhara. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://www.tigermountainpokhara.com/\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttps://www.tigermountainpokhara.com\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Heli flight tour of Annapurna Base Camp, Muktinath temple, Jomsom and Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After breakfast today you will experience the best of the Annapurna region. Often considered as one of the best destinations of the Himalayas, the tour begins with a flight to the base camp.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Annapurna Base Camp\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eTime:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 25 minutes from Pokhara to Annapurna Base Camp\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Pokhara:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 23.24 miles , 37.40 kilometers (km)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eABC Elevation:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 4130m/13549ft from sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAnnapurna base Cap is one of the best-selected trekking destinations in Nepal. Located at an elevation of over 4000 meters, it faces the majestic Annapurna Massif. Once in the base camp, you can have a 360° view of the Annapurna, Machhapuchhre (fishtail), and Dhaulagiri mountains. Considered as one of the most difficult peaks to climb of the 8 thousanders, Annapurna is beautiful. The base camp is gifted with scenery and views like no other place in the Himalayas.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter the pristine view of snow-capped mountains and landscape, we will leave the base camp and head towards Muktinath via Pokhara.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Muktinath\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 55 minutes from Pokhara to Muktinath Temple\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Pokhara and Muktinath is 67 KM (kilometers) and 119.89 meters. The mile based measurement distance is 41.7 miles\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMuktinath Elevation: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eWorld's highest temples (altitude 3,800 m) above sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003ePokhara to Annapurna base camp, after refreshment there will return Pokhara for fueling and flight to Muktinath Temple. And 10 minutes flight to Jomsom and continue flight to Lo Manthang (Upper MUstang) and back to Jomsom for overnight.\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nMuktinath is one of the most significant shrines in the Himalayas of Nepal. This temple is visited by hundreds of thousand Buddhist and Hindu pilgrims alike from different Asian countries. Located at the Mustang district, trekkers doing the Annapurna Circuit do the Thorung La Pass (5416 m) from Manang to reach here. Muktinath is also amongst the highest Hindu shrines around the world. Pilgrims believe that a visit here and a bath can wash away the sins of the past and present life. The Landscape surrounding the temple is also wonderful.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter a spiritual tour of Muktinath, we will head to Jomsom (10 minutes flight) for refueling.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Jomsom\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eJomsom Elevation: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eAltitude 2700 m above sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 10 minutes from Muktinath to Jomsom.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Muktinath:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 8.61 miles , 13.86 kilometers (km)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nJomsom is an iconic town in the Mustang District also acting as its administrative headquarters. The Airstrip here is one of the busiest in the Annapurna region and easily accessible from the Pokhara airport. Jomsom is also one of the best places to start the trekking to different destinations of the region.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe will fly from Jomsom to Lo Manthang next. As a restricted area, we will need permits and a legend officer will accompany you to Lo Manthang.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Lo Manthang\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003eAs a Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang) is a restricted area, a legend officer flying with you to Lo Manthang from Jomsom.\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 20 minutes from Jomsom to Lomanthang\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e30.75 miles / 49.49 kilometers (km) from Jomsom\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLo-Manthang Elevation\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 3,840 m (12,600 ft)\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eabove sea level\\\\r\\\\nLanding time: around 1 Hour in Lo-Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLo Manthang in Upper Mustang was the ancient capital of the Kingdom of Lho. This walled city in the heart of Mustang is a repository of culture and traditional art of the local people here. The monasteries, Chhortens, houses and Mani walls of the city reflect the constituents of Tibetan Buddhism. in the center of the city is the ancient palace of the king of Lho. Visiting the region gives one an opportunity to embrace and discover the lifestyle, history, and culture of the locals here. Lo Manthang is one of the major destinations of the upper Mustang tour.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter the tour of Lo Manthang, we will fly back to a lodge in Thasang near Jomsom and rest for the day.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at Thasang Village Lodge, Jomsom. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022http://lodgethasangvillage.com/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttp://lodgethasangvillage.com\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"05\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Flight by Heli from Jomsom to Pokhara to Dhulikhel (Dwarika Resort)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After breakfast at Jomsom, we will fly to Pokhara. Here we will have a brief stop and fly to Dhulikhel city near Kathmandu.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eTime from Jomsom to Pokhara\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 45 minutes; Distance: 42.72 miles , 68.76 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eTime from Pokhara to Dhulikhel\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 1 hour via Kathmandu\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Pokhara to Dhulikhel\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 103.70 miles / 166.89 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhulikhel Elevation\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 1550 m above sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Dhulikhel\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nDhulikhel is a cultural city just outside the Kathmandu valley in the Kabhrepalanchowk district. Popular for the wood arts, monuments, and traditions, Dhulikhel also offers some fantastic views of hills and Himalayas. The temples, houses, and streets here reflect the well-preserved culture of the local Newari people here. You can visit some of the nearby viewpoints and dive into the scenic nature during the Dhulikhel tour.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe will return to the Dwarika resort for the night known for authentic royal services and luxury throughout Nepal.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at Dwarika's Resort Dhulikhel. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://dwarikas-dhulikhel.com/home\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttps://dwarikas-dhulikhel.com/home\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"06\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Drive to Kathmandu via Bhaktapur tour, Departure\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-6\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-6\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe will drive you back to Kathmandu in a luxury vehicle after breakfast. You have an option to visit the Bhaktapur city midway of the drive from Dhulikhel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDriving distance:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 18.96 miles , 30.52 kilometers (km) from Dhulikhel to Kathmandu TIA airport\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Bhaktapur\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nBhaktapur is the most preserved of the main three cities in Kathmandu. Locals still follow their traditional lifestyle here. You can try some of the best Newari cuisines here. Bhaktapur is also home to two of the UNESCO world heritage sites the Bhaktapur Durbar Square and Changunarayan Temple. Apart from these, there are many temples, squares, monuments, and shrines worth visiting in the city.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOur guides will escort you back to the airport before the flight. You can also do some souvenir shopping accompanied by our guides in Thamel. Return with some magnificent memories and moments from the luxury helicopter tour of Nepal.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":6,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eThe price (cost) for this helicopter tour \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003emight vary with the number of travelers, accommodation type, meals, tour duration, travel season (travel date), routes and activities being the major factors. You can customize these find your ideal package which might not be same with cheaper deals elsewhere. Rest assured, make your visit worth every bit with us.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nPlease, send your tentative tour plan with interested region (Everest, Annapurna, Manaslu etc.) by submitting our right (below) side form.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour - 2 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"EXPENSIVE TOUR: Luxury Helicopter Tours with Luxury Accommodation in Nepal Himalayas including Everest and Annapurna Region\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"Only Helicopter Tour - Luxury Trip with Luxury Accommodation, Luxury vehicle from Hotel to Helipad/Airport, Hotels with Helipad, Kathmandu to Everest Helicopter, Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp Heli, Manaslu Base Camp to Pokhara Heli Services, Pokhara to Annapurna Base Camp, Pokhara to Jomsom Muktinath Heli ride, Jomsom to Lo Manthang Helicopter, Jomsom to Pokhara and to Dhulikhel Helicopter Tour\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Heli Tour Kathmandu, Everest, Manaslu, Pokhara, Annapurna, Muktinath, Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang) \\\\u0026 Dhulikhel\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"Luxury Hotels/Resorts\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Helicopter\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"When it comes to a Luxury vacation in Asia few come close to what the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLuxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNepal\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e can offer. This tour is proven time and again to give the best scenic view of the Everest, Manaslu, Jomsom with Upper Mustang and Annapurna.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWith the major delights of Everest Base Camp \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kala_Patthar\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKalapatthar\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e, Manaslu Base Camp, Annapurna Base Camp, Jomsom, Lo Manthang, Pokhara, and Dhulikhel, the best of Nepal are off the charts of anyone’s expectation. All these and more are bound professionally with exquisite hotels, luxury transportation, and the best guides to make sure the trip is exemplary.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLuxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNepal\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022\\\\u003eEverest Region\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAnnapurna Region (Jomsom with Upper Mustang)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eManaslu Region\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eOutline Itinerary\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nDay 01: Arrival at Kathmandu, heritage Tour of the Valley\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cspan class=\\\\u0022redactor-invisible-space\\\\u0022\\\\u003eDay 02: Helicopter tour in the Everest region (Everest Base Camp, Kalapatthar, and Hotel Everest View overnight)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/span\\\\u003e\\\\u003cspan class=\\\\u0022redactor-invisible-space\\\\u0022\\\\u003eDay 03: Helicopter flight to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu, and to Pokhara\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/span\\\\u003e\\\\u003cspan class=\\\\u0022redactor-invisible-space\\\\u0022\\\\u003eDay 04: Heli flight tour of Annapurna Base Camp, Muktinath temple, Jomsom, and Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/span\\\\u003e\\\\u003cspan class=\\\\u0022redactor-invisible-space\\\\u0022\\\\u003eDay 05: Flight by Heli from Jomsom to Pokhara to Dhulikhel (Dwarikas Resort)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/span\\\\u003e\\\\u003cspan class=\\\\u0022redactor-invisible-space\\\\u0022\\\\u003eDay 06: Drive to Kathmandu via Bhaktapur tour, Departure\\\\u003c/span\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"543\\",\\"596\\",\\"599\\",\\"586\\",\\"688\\",\\"798\\",\\"799\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Arrival at Kathmandu, heritage Tour of the Valley\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"You will be escorted to the hotel in Thamel after landing at the airport in Kathmandu. After some rest and refreshment, you will take a brief tour of the valley in a luxury vehicle.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Kathmandu\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nKathmandu is a cauldron mixing culture and commerce in the lap of Himalayas. Thousands of years of history and art of different eras define this city. Kathmandu is the primary spot to enter Nepal through the air as well. This city oozes culture and architecture which has been there for hundreds of years.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLegends say that this valley once was a giant lake cut open for the residents by the Buddhist Deity Manjushree. The local people here are Newars. Newars are known for their traditional way of living and business. These people are also known for their artistic decoration on houses, wooden beams, sculptures and more in the valley.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWith seven UNESCO world heritage sites in the valley, travelers can find a pristine repository of history, art, and culture in the valley. Pashupatinath, the monkey temple of Swayambhunath, Boudhanath with other main palaces of medieval Malla Kings defines the city. A small tour of these sites treats visitors with wonderful experiences.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nCompleting the brief introductory tour of the valley, we will drive you back to the hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at Dwarikas Hotel, Kathmandu \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://www.dwarikas.com/home/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttps://www.dwarikas.com/home/\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Heli tour in the Everest region (Everest Base Camp, Kalapatthar, and Hotel Everest View)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After a hearty breakfast in the hotel, you will prepare to embrace the Everest. Our guide will escort you to the TIA for your flight. Passing by the green hills and scenic landscape, eye-catching mountain views, rural villages and local communities, we will enter Lukla.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Lukla\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHeli flight approx Time from Kathmandu to Lukla: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e45 minutes helicopter ride from Kathmandu (140 km/87 miles)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLukla Elevation: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e2,845 meters / 9,334 feet above sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eWeather/Temperature of Lukla: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eThe month of July (Warmest Month), with an average temperature of 14.7 °C | 58.5 °F. The month of January (Coldest Month), with temperatures averaging 2.8 °C | 37.0 °F.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLukla is an iconic town in Khumbu with the most significant airstrip for travelers to Everest. Also sated as the Gateway to Everest, Lukla is a link to the higher Khumbu region and the Himalayas. At an elevation of 9380 ft. most flights here are in the morning for clear weather. One can get the first glance of Sherpa culture at Lukla.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nA quick refill-stop here and we are up over the Everest Base Camp and landing at Kalapatther.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003eHelicopter ride start from Lukla to Syangboche to Kalapatthar and land there. Landing time around 10 minutes as the high elevation reason (Helicopter engine will not stop during your landing experience because of high elevation and coldness) and back to Everest View Hotel via Gokyo lake overfly.\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cem\\\\u003eNote: A helicopter can lift only 3 person at a time in Everest base camp due to high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Pheriche or Shyangboche.\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Everest Base Camp (EBC)\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time to Everest Base Camp / Kalapatthar from Lukla: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e25 minutes\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Lukla to EBC: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e22.65 miles / 36.46 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eEBC Elevation: 5,380 m (17,600 ft) above sea level\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKalapatther Elevation: 5,643 m (18,514 ft) above sea level\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nEverest Base Camp is about 6 days trek or 25 minutes flight from Lukla. At an elevation of over 17,600 ft., the Southern Base Camp is the starting point of the climb for mountaineers climbing to the Summit from the Nepali side. Once here one can have an unobstructed view of the massive south face of the Everest alongside the other mountains. We can view the base camps with orange tents beside the massive Khumbu glacier flying over it.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Kalapatther/ Kala Patthar (Black Stone)\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nKalapatther is one of the most popular and gifted spots to view the massive Everest Massif in its full glory in the Himalayas. It is one of the popular day hiking destinations from the Everest Base Camp as well. This ridge at an elevation of 18500 ft.\\\\u003ca name=\\\\u0022_GoBack\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e, this wonderful peak lies before the Everest. Landing here one can have a fantastic view of Mt. Everest (8848 m), Mt.Lhotse (8516 m), Nuptse (7861 m ) and many more. This Panoramic spot is one of the most picturesque places to be in the Everest region.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLanding at an elevation as high as Kalapatther, you will have some 15 minutes of ground time due to thin air. After some wonderful memories and pictures from the Kalapatther, we will take off from there.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nEnjoy the serenity of being close to Everest at Kalapatther and we will continue the Heli Flight to Everest view Hotel. Midway in the flight is the beautiful Gokyo lake complex.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Gokyo Lake\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time from Kalapatthar/EBC to Hotel Everest View via Gokyo Lake:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 25 minutes\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e15.47 miles / 24.90 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe Gokyo Lakes are the glacial lake complex in the Gokyo valley at an elevation of 4700-5000 m. There are five major lakes and hundreds of others fed by the Ngozumpa glacier. The view of Everest and Cho Oyu is pristine from the valley. These lakes are also considered holy by both Hindu and Buddhist pilgrims. Near the Tibetan border, you can see the ranges on both Nepalese and Tibetan sides touching the horizon.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFor our overnight stay, we will land ad rest in the luxurious Hotel Everest View in Syangboche.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Everest View Hotel\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSyangboche / Hotel Everest View Elevation: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e3880 meters (12,730 ft.) above sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe Everest View Hotel in Syangboche is a hotel located in one of the highest altitudes in the world. This hotel was listed as the world's highest hotel by the Guinness book of world records in 2004 AD. It is located near the top of the ridge in Syangboche. As the name suggests from the premises of the hotel one can have a breathtaking view of Everest and beyond. Luxury is what best explains the hotel and you can get the best of the Everest here.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at Hotel Everest View, Syangboche. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://hoteleverestview.com/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttps://hoteleverestview.com\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Helicopter flight to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu, and to Pokhara\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 1 hours from Shangboche to Kathmandu\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Hotel Everest View to Kathmandu:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 86.12 miles / 138.60 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom the Everest View Hotel, view the best of the Sunrise views and breakfast. Leaving the Hotel, we will take a flight back to Kathmandu. Following a brief check and refueling at TIA, we will leave for the Manaslu Base Camp.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Manaslu Base Camp and Samagaun\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003eHelicopter continue flight from Syangboche to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu (At Manaslu Base Camp, helicopter engine will not stop due to the high elevation), 10-15 minutes landing experiences to take photos, videos or eye catching view of mountains and flying to Pokhara.\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cem\\\\u003eA helicopter can lift only 3 person at a time in Manaslu base camp due to high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Sama Gaun.\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 50 minutes from Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 75.27 miles / 121.13 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nManaslu is the eighth highest mountain in the world located in the northern ends of the Gorkha District. Standing 8,163 meters tall this beautiful peak is translated as the 'Mountain of Spirit' in Sanskrit. The base of the mountain is about 5 hours trek or 15 minutes flight from Samagaon village. Manaslu Base Camp is one of the best places to view the Manaslu and Ganesh range.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nSamagaon is the last major settlement near the Manaslu Base Camp. This Tibetan village is one of the major attractions of the Manaslu Base Camp region. As Manaslu base camp is in a high elevation, you will have a similar brief stop as Kalapatther.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIf you are in a group of more than three you will take a shuttle from Samagaun. After leaving the Manaslu Base Camp we will fly to Pokhara. After landing at the airport in Pokhara, we will escort you to the hotel. You will explore the major attractions of the city.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Pokhara\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Manaslu BC to Pokhara\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 45.55 miles , 73.31 kilometers (km)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 40 minutes from Manaslu Base Camp to Pokhara\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nPokhara is the adventure capital of Nepal. For visitors, this city has everything from viewpoints, to natural sites and religious monuments. Pokhara is also the city of lakes. The Phewa, Rupa, and Begnas lakes are three of the most beautiful ones here. The Tal Barahi (an island temple) in Phewa and Bindabashini temples are the most significant temples of the Pokhara valley. You can involve in paragliding, bungee, kayaking, rock climbing, and other outdoor activities as well in the Pokhara city. The nightlife of Pokhara is also one not to miss while you are here.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at Hotel Tiger Mountain Pokhara. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://www.tigermountainpokhara.com/\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttps://www.tigermountainpokhara.com\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Heli flight tour of Annapurna Base Camp, Muktinath temple, Jomsom and Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After breakfast today you will experience the best of the Annapurna region. Often considered as one of the best destinations of the Himalayas, the tour begins with a flight to the base camp.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Annapurna Base Camp\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eTime:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 25 minutes from Pokhara to Annapurna Base Camp\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Pokhara:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 23.24 miles , 37.40 kilometers (km)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eABC Elevation:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 4130m/13549ft from sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAnnapurna base Cap is one of the best-selected trekking destinations in Nepal. Located at an elevation of over 4000 meters, it faces the majestic Annapurna Massif. Once in the base camp, you can have a 360° view of the Annapurna, Machhapuchhre (fishtail), and Dhaulagiri mountains. Considered as one of the most difficult peaks to climb of the 8 thousanders, Annapurna is beautiful. The base camp is gifted with scenery and views like no other place in the Himalayas.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter the pristine view of snow-capped mountains and landscape, we will leave the base camp and head towards Muktinath via Pokhara.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Muktinath\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 55 minutes from Pokhara to Muktinath Temple\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Pokhara and Muktinath is 67 KM (kilometers) and 119.89 meters. The mile based measurement distance is 41.7 miles\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMuktinath Elevation: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eWorld's highest temples (altitude 3,800 m) above sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003ePokhara to Annapurna base camp, after refreshment there will return Pokhara for fueling and flight to Muktinath Temple. And 10 minutes flight to Jomsom and continue flight to Lo Manthang (Upper MUstang) and back to Jomsom for overnight.\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nMuktinath is one of the most significant shrines in the Himalayas of Nepal. This temple is visited by hundreds of thousand Buddhist and Hindu pilgrims alike from different Asian countries. Located at the Mustang district, trekkers doing the Annapurna Circuit do the Thorung La Pass (5416 m) from Manang to reach here. Muktinath is also amongst the highest Hindu shrines around the world. Pilgrims believe that a visit here and a bath can wash away the sins of the past and present life. The Landscape surrounding the temple is also wonderful.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter a spiritual tour of Muktinath, we will head to Jomsom (10 minutes flight) for refueling.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Jomsom\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eJomsom Elevation: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eAltitude 2700 m above sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 10 minutes from Muktinath to Jomsom.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Muktinath:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 8.61 miles , 13.86 kilometers (km)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nJomsom is an iconic town in the Mustang District also acting as its administrative headquarters. The Airstrip here is one of the busiest in the Annapurna region and easily accessible from the Pokhara airport. Jomsom is also one of the best places to start the trekking to different destinations of the region.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe will fly from Jomsom to Lo Manthang next. As a restricted area, we will need permits and a legend officer will accompany you to Lo Manthang.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Lo Manthang\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003eAs a Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang) is a restricted area, a legend officer flying with you to Lo Manthang from Jomsom.\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApprox Time\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 20 minutes from Jomsom to Lomanthang\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e30.75 miles / 49.49 kilometers (km) from Jomsom\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLo-Manthang Elevation\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 3,840 m (12,600 ft)\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eabove sea level\\\\r\\\\nLanding time: around 1 Hour in Lo-Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLo Manthang in Upper Mustang was the ancient capital of the Kingdom of Lho. This walled city in the heart of Mustang is a repository of culture and traditional art of the local people here. The monasteries, Chhortens, houses and Mani walls of the city reflect the constituents of Tibetan Buddhism. in the center of the city is the ancient palace of the king of Lho. Visiting the region gives one an opportunity to embrace and discover the lifestyle, history, and culture of the locals here. Lo Manthang is one of the major destinations of the upper Mustang tour.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter the tour of Lo Manthang, we will fly back to a lodge in Thasang near Jomsom and rest for the day.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at Thasang Village Lodge, Jomsom. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022http://lodgethasangvillage.com/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttp://lodgethasangvillage.com\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"05\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Flight by Heli from Jomsom to Pokhara to Dhulikhel (Dwarika Resort)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After breakfast at Jomsom, we will fly to Pokhara. Here we will have a brief stop and fly to Dhulikhel city near Kathmandu.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eTime from Jomsom to Pokhara\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 45 minutes; Distance: 42.72 miles , 68.76 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eTime from Pokhara to Dhulikhel\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 1 hour via Kathmandu\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDistance from Pokhara to Dhulikhel\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 103.70 miles / 166.89 kilometers\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhulikhel Elevation\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: 1550 m above sea level\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Dhulikhel\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nDhulikhel is a cultural city just outside the Kathmandu valley in the Kabhrepalanchowk district. Popular for the wood arts, monuments, and traditions, Dhulikhel also offers some fantastic views of hills and Himalayas. The temples, houses, and streets here reflect the well-preserved culture of the local Newari people here. You can visit some of the nearby viewpoints and dive into the scenic nature during the Dhulikhel tour.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe will return to the Dwarika resort for the night known for authentic royal services and luxury throughout Nepal.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at Dwarika's Resort Dhulikhel. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://dwarikas-dhulikhel.com/home\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttps://dwarikas-dhulikhel.com/home\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"06\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Drive to Kathmandu via Bhaktapur tour, Departure\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-6\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-6\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe will drive you back to Kathmandu in a luxury vehicle after breakfast. You have an option to visit the Bhaktapur city midway of the drive from Dhulikhel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDriving distance:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 18.96 miles , 30.52 kilometers (km) from Dhulikhel to Kathmandu TIA airport\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Bhaktapur\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nBhaktapur is the most preserved of the main three cities in Kathmandu. Locals still follow their traditional lifestyle here. You can try some of the best Newari cuisines here. Bhaktapur is also home to two of the UNESCO world heritage sites the Bhaktapur Durbar Square and Changunarayan Temple. Apart from these, there are many temples, squares, monuments, and shrines worth visiting in the city.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOur guides will escort you back to the airport before the flight. You can also do some souvenir shopping accompanied by our guides in Thamel. Return with some magnificent memories and moments from the luxury helicopter tour of Nepal.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":6,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eThe price (cost) for this helicopter tour \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003emight vary with the number of travelers, accommodation type, meals, tour duration, travel season (travel date), routes and activities being the major factors. You can customize these find your ideal package which might not be same with cheaper deals elsewhere. Rest assured, make your visit worth every bit with us.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nPlease, send your tentative tour plan with interested region (Everest, Annapurna, Manaslu etc.) by submitting our right (below) side form.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour - 2 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Helicopter-at-Everest-View-Hotel-Syangboche.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/everest-helicopter.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/everest-heclicopter-review-eric.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/amazing-view-of-mt-everest-with-white-cloud.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/helicopter-at-pheriche.jpeg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=792", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "792", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-04 06:08:13", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-04 06:08:13", "post_modified": "2024-02-02 09:23:04", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-02-02 09:23:04"}}, "customSections": [{"id": 1, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Extended Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": 2, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Alternate Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["When it comes to a Luxury vacation in Asia few come close to what the <strong>Luxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas</strong> <strong>Nepal</strong> can offer. This tour is proven time and again to give the best scenic view of the Everest, Manaslu, Jomsom with Upper Mustang and Annapurna.\\r\\n\\r\\nWith the major delights of Everest Base Camp <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kala_Patthar\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kalapatthar</a>, Manaslu Base Camp, Annapurna Base Camp, Jomsom, Lo Manthang, Pokhara, and Dhulikhel, the best of Nepal are off the charts of anyone’s expectation. All these and more are bound professionally with exquisite hotels, luxury transportation, and the best guides to make sure the trip is exemplary.\\r\\n<h4><strong>Luxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas</strong> <strong>Nepal</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\">Everest Region</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Annapurna Region (Jomsom with Upper Mustang)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Manaslu Region</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Outline Itinerary</h3>\\r\\nDay 01: Arrival at Kathmandu, heritage Tour of the Valley\\r\\n<span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 02: Helicopter tour in the Everest region (Everest Base Camp, Kalapatthar, and Hotel Everest View overnight)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 03: Helicopter flight to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu, and to Pokhara\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 04: Heli flight tour of Annapurna Base Camp, Muktinath temple, Jomsom, and Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 05: Flight by Heli from Jomsom to Pokhara to Dhulikhel (Dwarikas Resort)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 06: Drive to Kathmandu via Bhaktapur tour, Departure</span>"], "description": "When it comes to a Luxury vacation in Asia few come close to what the <strong>Luxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas</strong> <strong>Nepal</strong> can offer. This tour is proven time and again to give the best scenic view of the Everest, Manaslu, Jomsom with Upper Mustang and Annapurna.\\r\\n\\r\\nWith the major delights of Everest Base Camp <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kala_Patthar\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kalapatthar</a>, Manaslu Base Camp, Annapurna Base Camp, Jomsom, Lo Manthang, Pokhara, and Dhulikhel, the best of Nepal are off the charts of anyone’s expectation. All these and more are bound professionally with exquisite hotels, luxury transportation, and the best guides to make sure the trip is exemplary.\\r\\n<h4><strong>Luxury helicopter tour in the Himalayas</strong> <strong>Nepal</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\">Everest Region</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Annapurna Region (Jomsom with Upper Mustang)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Manaslu Region</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Outline Itinerary</h3>\\r\\nDay 01: Arrival at Kathmandu, heritage Tour of the Valley\\r\\n<span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 02: Helicopter tour in the Everest region (Everest Base Camp, Kalapatthar, and Hotel Everest View overnight)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 03: Helicopter flight to Manaslu Base Camp via Kathmandu, and to Pokhara\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 04: Heli flight tour of Annapurna Base Camp, Muktinath temple, Jomsom, and Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 05: Flight by Heli from Jomsom to Pokhara to Dhulikhel (Dwarikas Resort)\\r\\n</span><span class=\\"redactor-invisible-space\\">Day 06: Drive to Kathmandu via Bhaktapur tour, Departure</span>"}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["The price (cost) for this helicopter tour might vary with the number of travelers, accommodation type, meals, tour duration, travel season (travel date), routes and activities being the major factors. You can customize these find your ideal package which might not be same with cheaper deals elsewhere. Rest assured, make your visit worth every bit with us. Please, send your tentative tour plan with interested region (Everest, Annapurna, Manaslu etc.) by submitting our right (below) side form."], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["The price (cost) for this helicopter tour might vary with the number of travelers, accommodation type, meals, tour duration, travel season (travel date), routes and activities being the major factors. You can customize these find your ideal package which might not be same with cheaper deals elsewhere. Rest assured, make your visit worth every bit with us. Please, send your tentative tour plan with interested region (Everest, Annapurna, Manaslu etc.) by submitting our right (below) side form."], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "Explore Luxury Helicopter tour in the Himalayas Nepal with Everest Vacation.", "trip_highlights": "Only Helicopter Tour - Luxury Trip with Luxury Accommodation, Luxury vehicle from Hotel to Helipad/Airport, Hotels with Helipad, Kathmandu to Everest Helicopter, Kathmandu to Manaslu Base Camp Heli, Manaslu Base Camp to Pokhara Heli Services, Pokhara to Annapurna Base Camp, Pokhara to Jomsom Muktinath Heli ride, Jomsom to Lo Manthang Helicopter, Jomsom to Pokhara and to Dhulikhel Helicopter Tour", "trip_type_level": "Easy", "meta_description": "Luxury Helicopter tour in the Himalayas Nepal gives the best scenic view of Everest, Manaslu, and Jomsom with Upper Mustang and Annapurna.", "trip_attractions": "Heli Tour Kathmandu, Everest, Manaslu, Pokhara, Annapurna, Muktinath, Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang) & Dhulikhel", "faq_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "Heli Tour Kathmandu, Everest, Manaslu, Pokhara, Annapurna, Muktinath, Lo Manthang (Upper Mustang) & Dhulikhel", "best_season": "", "accommodation": "Luxury Hotels/Resorts", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": "Helicopter"}, "trip_accommodation": "Luxury Hotels/Resorts", "trip_transportations": "Helicopter", "trip_highlights_title": "EXPENSIVE TOUR: Luxury Helicopter Tours with Luxury Accommodation in Nepal Himalayas including E