170	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "1", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy"}, "faq": [{"answer": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "question": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "question": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "question": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "question": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "question": "5. What to expect on tours?"}], "meta": {"_edit_last": "1", "_edit_lock": "1727333022:1", "_dp_original": "538", "_thumbnail_id": "802", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "1", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "44", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp treats the up-close view of many 7000 to 8000-meter peaks including the world’s highest Mt. Everest.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp", "tags": [], "title": "Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp", "duration": "1 Day", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "<strong>Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp: Phenomenal and Thrilling</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Heli Trip Duration/Time:</strong> 3:00 to 5:00 hours\\r\\n<strong>Landing Spot of Helicopter:</strong> Kalapatthar (5,555m), Everest View Hotel for Breakfast &amp; Lukla (<a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenzing%E2%80%93Hillary_Airport\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Edmund Hillary Airport</a>) for fueling.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Route of Everest Base Camp helicopter tour:</strong> Kathmandu Airport to Lukla then Namche Bazaar, Pheriche, Gorakshep, and <strong>Mt. Everest Base Camp, Kalapathar</strong>, and return to Everest View Hotel then to Lukla and continues to Kathmandu.\\r\\n<blockquote>WE OFFER ONLY PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOURS, A MAXIMUM OF 5 TRAVELERS CAN DO AT A TIME. IT DEPENDS ON THE WEIGHT OF TRAVELERS TOO. THERE ARE MANY FACTORS TO CHOOSING A PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOUR OVER A GROUP JOINING TOUR</blockquote>\\r\\n<h2>About Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</h2>\\r\\n<h3>Highlights Points</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fly over the highest peak in the world, including Mount Everest and other ranges.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Set foot on Kalapatthar (5555m), from where you can see the awesome views of Mount Everest(8848m), Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse (7861m), Ama Dablam and more</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Enjoy the view of many 7000 to 8000-meter peaks including the world’s highest Mt. Everest. It sure will be the experience of a lifetime.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Aerial view of Everest Base Camp, Khumbu Glacier, Khumbu Icefall, and Gokyo Lakes.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Breakfast at Everest View Hotel surrounded by snowy walls of Himalayan giants.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nEarly morning depart from your respective hotels to Kathmandu domestic airport for the amazing trip of <strong>Everest base camp helicopter</strong>. This mind-blowing and wonderful helicopter flight towards Mt. Everest Base Camp starts from there. Soon after taking off from the airport, we see the high panoramic view of the <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Kathmandu valley</a>, followed by small villages, and green hills. We have a view of an awesome parallel range of snow-capped mountains. The major peaks are towards the west <a href=\\"https://www.summitpost.org/manaslu/150687\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Mt. Manaslu</a>, Ganesh Himal, Langtang, and Jugal Himal. As the flight continues more views of the mid-east and far-eastern Himalayan peaks of Mt. Gaurishankar, Melung Tse, Numbur, Cho-Oyu &amp; more come into the frame.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Everest Base Camp helicopter tour</strong> reaches Lukla 2,820 meters high and can stop a helicopter for fueling. From here, we get the best views of Kwangde Peak and the lower valley. The flight continues heading to the famous <a href=\\"https://wikitravel.org/en/Namche_Bazaar\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Namche Bazaar 3,440 meters high “Sherpa Capital</a>“. After Namche, we will be heading towards a scenic and renowned spot at Tyangboche Monastery located at 3,867 meters of altitude. From this hill, we can enjoy the panorama view of Mt. Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Lhotse Shar, Kangtega, Thamserku, and Kwangde. The close views of the stunning peak of Ama Dablam are a treat to your senses. From here head towards Pheriche where the tree lines fade in the barren landscape.\\r\\n\\r\\nFind the video tour of <a href=\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_7G41764ipc\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">the Everest base camp helicopter tour</a> here.\\r\\n<h3>Why Should You Choose Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp?</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Everest Heli Tour gives you a chance to experience the tallest mountain in the world from the comfort of a helicopter instead of a long and difficult trek.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit the Everest Region without paying a huge and unnecessary amount of money that one would spend during the trek.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fly near or above Mount Everest (8848m) and also enjoy the Bird’s eye view of 7000m to 8000m peaks– Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse(7861m), Makalu (8,481m), Cho Oyu(8201).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Exciting landing at one of the highest airports in the world, Tenzing-Hillary Airport (2,845m) in Lukla, and experience the view of Everest region, Kala Patthar, and savor 360-degree views of Himalayan Peaks.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>View of radically weather changes, up in the mountains.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Cost of Private Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</h3>\\r\\nDaily flights for <strong>private Everest base camp helicopter tour with landing at Kalapatther (5,555m.) and experience high altitude breakfast at Everest View Hotel.</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>5 Pax or more – <strong>US$1,380.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>4 Pax – <strong>US$1,650.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>3 Pax – <strong>US$2,100.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>2 Pax – <strong>US$2,980.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>1 Pax – <strong>US$5,800.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<em><strong>Note:</strong> We need to calculate the weight of the passengers so please mention your weight for the helicopter flight to Everest during your inquiry.\\r\\n</em><em>A helicopter can lift only 3 people at a time in Everest base camp due to the high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Pheriche or Shyangboche.</em>\\r\\n\\r\\nWith a view of this area, we continue to our main destination at <strong>Mount Everest Base Camp</strong> at 5,367 meters altitude. We fly over Khumbu Icefall and glaciers. During the climbing season, this place is flooded with camping tents and climbers. Here you will have <strong>an exciting moment by stopping on the way to Kalapatthar where views of Mt. Everest</strong> can be seen at a close distance with Mt. Pumori towards the North.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter having a short, fascinating time here on a helicopter tour to Everest base camp, we continued the flight back to Everest View Hotel for a short break and had breakfast with the views of Mt. Everest. Then fly to Kathmandu and transfer back to the hotel. This wonderful and overwhelming time of about 3-4 hours in the lap of the world’s highest peak Mt. Everest will be your lifetime experience and the stories about these majestic destinations for your friends and family."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Everest Basecamp heli tour", "richText": "- 6:00 am pickup from hotel.\\r\\n- 6:30 am at airport.\\r\\n- 7:00 am helicopter take up.\\r\\n- 1 stop at Lukla for fueling\\r\\n- 1 stop at Pheriche for shuttle, if more than 3pax (helicopter leave 2 pax there, Pheriche stop approx 20 minutes use to take photos of surrounding mountain and high elevation lifetime experiences. After back 2 pax from everest base camp, turn for next two pax for everest base camp landing.)\\r\\n- 1 stop at Syangboche Everest View Hotel for half an hour for breakfast and amazing mountain views.\\r\\n- Back to Kathmandu airport.\\r\\n- Drop you at hotel by our vehicle.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/EVEREST.jpg", "title": "EVEREST", "altText": "EVEREST", "caption": "EVEREST", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["802", "801", "799", "798", "744", "757", "797"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "ws_trip_faqs_lists": 5, "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists": "field_63ede38e351c7", "ws_block_attractions": "Helicopter flight over to the Mt. Everest, landing experience at Everest Base camp & Breakfast in Everest View hotel.", "ws_block_best_season": "Any Season", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-light", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "5555 meters", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": " Overview", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc6695edb31", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_block_transportation": "AC Luxury Car/Hiace", "ws_trip_galleries_title": "Photo/Visual Gallery", "_ws_block_transportation": "field_63eeee74072de", "_ws_trip_galleries_title": "field_63ec89128acaa", "starter_kit_padding_type": "p-medium", "ws_trip_block_highlights": "<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nOur fascinating Everest base camp helicopter tour commences with landing in the highest viewpoint of EBC Kalapatther (5,555 meters) for the best view of Mount Everest. This trip is on a chopper to the world’s highest valley of Khumbu and Mount Everest Region. Everest Helicopter Tour gives you a chance to experience the tallest mountain in the world from the comfort of a helicopter instead of the long and difficult trek of Everest base camp.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>", "ws_trip_information_list": 3, "_starter_kit_padding_type": "field_5f8584c998bc2", "_ws_trip_block_highlights": "field_63ec73a6a0d8f", "_ws_trip_information_list": "field_63ec90a574f02", "starter_kit_section_title": "Day by Day Activities", "_starter_kit_section_title": "field_63ec948c94a16", "starter_kit_enable_section": "1", "ws_trip_faqs_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "_starter_kit_enable_section": "field_63edeb1c7635c", "_ws_trip_faqs_section_title": "field_63ede33e5b304", "starter_kit_section_padding": "", "ws_trip_include_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Car/van transportation to and from the domestic airport and hotel in Kathmandu.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Escorting guide for this Everest flight.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Private helicopter for 4 hours.</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_starter_kit_section_padding": "field_5f3e0f86a2634", "_ws_trip_include_description": "field_63edd6a337cd0", "ws_trip_overview_description": "<strong>Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp: Phenomenal and Thrilling</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Heli Trip Duration/Time:</strong> 3:00 to 5:00 hours\\r\\n<strong>Landing Spot of Helicopter:</strong> Kalapatthar (5,555m), Everest View Hotel for Breakfast &amp; Lukla (<a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenzing%E2%80%93Hillary_Airport\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Edmund Hillary Airport</a>) for fueling.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Route of Everest Base Camp helicopter tour:</strong> Kathmandu Airport to Lukla then Namche Bazaar, Pheriche, Gorakshep, and <strong>Mt. Everest Base Camp, Kalapathar</strong>, and return to Everest View Hotel then to Lukla and continues to Kathmandu.\\r\\n<blockquote>WE OFFER ONLY PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOURS, A MAXIMUM OF 5 TRAVELERS CAN DO AT A TIME. IT DEPENDS ON THE WEIGHT OF TRAVELERS TOO. THERE ARE MANY FACTORS TO CHOOSING A PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOUR OVER A GROUP JOINING TOUR</blockquote>\\r\\n<h2>About Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</h2>\\r\\n<h3>Highlights Points</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fly over the highest peak in the world, including Mount Everest and other ranges.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Set foot on Kalapatthar (5555m), from where you can see the awesome views of Mount Everest(8848m), Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse (7861m), Ama Dablam and more</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Enjoy the view of many 7000 to 8000-meter peaks including the world’s highest Mt. Everest. It sure will be the experience of a lifetime.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Aerial view of Everest Base Camp, Khumbu Glacier, Khumbu Icefall, and Gokyo Lakes.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Breakfast at Everest View Hotel surrounded by snowy walls of Himalayan giants.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nEarly morning depart from your respective hotels to Kathmandu domestic airport for the amazing trip of <strong>Everest base camp helicopter</strong>. This mind-blowing and wonderful helicopter flight towards Mt. Everest Base Camp starts from there. Soon after taking off from the airport, we see the high panoramic view of the <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Kathmandu valley</a>, followed by small villages, and green hills. We have a view of an awesome parallel range of snow-capped mountains. The major peaks are towards the west <a href=\\"https://www.summitpost.org/manaslu/150687\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Mt. Manaslu</a>, Ganesh Himal, Langtang, and Jugal Himal. As the flight continues more views of the mid-east and far-eastern Himalayan peaks of Mt. Gaurishankar, Melung Tse, Numbur, Cho-Oyu &amp; more come into the frame.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Everest Base Camp helicopter tour</strong> reaches Lukla 2,820 meters high and can stop a helicopter for fueling. From here, we get the best views of Kwangde Peak and the lower valley. The flight continues heading to the famous <a href=\\"https://wikitravel.org/en/Namche_Bazaar\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Namche Bazaar 3,440 meters high “Sherpa Capital</a>“. After Namche, we will be heading towards a scenic and renowned spot at Tyangboche Monastery located at 3,867 meters of altitude. From this hill, we can enjoy the panorama view of Mt. Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Lhotse Shar, Kangtega, Thamserku, and Kwangde. The close views of the stunning peak of Ama Dablam are a treat to your senses. From here head towards Pheriche where the tree lines fade in the barren landscape.\\r\\n\\r\\nFind the video tour of <a href=\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_7G41764ipc\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">the Everest base camp helicopter tour</a> here.\\r\\n<h3>Why Should You Choose Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp?</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Everest Heli Tour gives you a chance to experience the tallest mountain in the world from the comfort of a helicopter instead of a long and difficult trek.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit the Everest Region without paying a huge and unnecessary amount of money that one would spend during the trek.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fly near or above Mount Everest (8848m) and also enjoy the Bird’s eye view of 7000m to 8000m peaks– Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse(7861m), Makalu (8,481m), Cho Oyu(8201).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Exciting landing at one of the highest airports in the world, Tenzing-Hillary Airport (2,845m) in Lukla, and experience the view of Everest region, Kala Patthar, and savor 360-degree views of Himalayan Peaks.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>View of radically weather changes, up in the mountains.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Cost of Private Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</h3>\\r\\nDaily flights for <strong>private Everest base camp helicopter tour with landing at Kalapatther (5,555m.) and experience high altitude breakfast at Everest View Hotel.</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>5 Pax or more – <strong>US$1,380.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>4 Pax – <strong>US$1,650.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>3 Pax – <strong>US$2,100.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>2 Pax – <strong>US$2,980.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>1 Pax – <strong>US$5,800.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<em><strong>Note:</strong> We need to calculate the weight of the passengers so please mention your weight for the helicopter flight to Everest during your inquiry.\\r\\n</em><em>A helicopter can lift only 3 people at a time in Everest base camp due to the high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Pheriche or Shyangboche.</em>\\r\\n\\r\\nWith a view of this area, we continue to our main destination at <strong>Mount Everest Base Camp</strong> at 5,367 meters altitude. We fly over Khumbu Icefall and glaciers. During the climbing season, this place is flooded with camping tents and climbers. Here you will have <strong>an exciting moment by stopping on the way to Kalapatthar where views of Mt. Everest</strong> can be seen at a close distance with Mt. Pumori towards the North.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter having a short, fascinating time here on a helicopter tour to Everest base camp, we continued the flight back to Everest View Hotel for a short break and had breakfast with the views of Mt. Everest. Then fly to Kathmandu and transfer back to the hotel. This wonderful and overwhelming time of about 3-4 hours in the lap of the world’s highest peak Mt. Everest will be your lifetime experience and the stories about these majestic destinations for your friends and family.", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "Charter Helicopter Tour to Mount Everest | Chopper ride to Mount Everest Base Camp", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "5. What to expect on tours?", "_ws_trip_fact_short_description": "field_63ec73a69d305", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "01", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "Everest Basecamp heli tour", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "Recent Experience by Emily Carpio:", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title": "Extended Tours", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_title": "Alternate Tours", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "- 6:00 am pickup from hotel.\\r\\n- 6:30 am at airport.\\r\\n- 7:00 am helicopter take up.\\r\\n- 1 stop at Lukla for fueling\\r\\n- 1 stop at Pheriche for shuttle, if more than 3pax (helicopter leave 2 pax there, Pheriche stop approx 20 minutes use to take photos of surrounding mountain and high elevation lifetime experiences. After back 2 pax from everest base camp, turn for next two pax for everest base camp landing.)\\r\\n- 1 stop at Syangboche Everest View Hotel for half an hour for breakfast and amazing mountain views.\\r\\n- Back to Kathmandu airport.\\r\\n- Drop you at hotel by our vehicle.", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "<strong>MOUNT EVEREST HELICOPTER DAY TOUR- NEPAL 2020 LIFETIME EXPERIENCE 2020 NEPAL LIFETIME EXPERIENCES #VNY2020</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Mount Everest Helicopter Day Tour with three (3) Landing on the last base camp from the Summit is probably one of the most exciting tour in the World. This tour in Nepal takes you from your hotel that rolls to Tribhuvan International Airport at Kathmandu with a Helicopter, flying across the Himalayan range which presents you with the snow-capped mountain vistas around 5-7 hrs depending on the weather condition in which during our time Temperature is neg -27C with a very-very-very thin air at Mount Everest.\\r\\n\\r\\nThere upon you will be landing at Lukha for fueling, then you will fly and across Namche Bazar, Syngoche, Tengboche and Everest Base Camp .Its once in a lifetime opportunity that you admire the beauty of Mount Everest and our Helicopter landed again at Kalapattar, (after we had some coffee on the second base camp). Kalapattar (5545 / 18192ft) provides the best view fronting Mount Everest (8,848m or 29012 ft), Pumori(7,161m), Ama Dablam (6,812m), Lhotse (8,516m), Choyu (8,201m), Nuptse (7,861m)and thousands of snow capped peaks.\\r\\n\\r\\nDuring our Highest Landing Only the Pilot and three of us Family my husband Danny, my Son CJ and me were allowed due to limited weight (max 220kg) due to the high altitude. We are only given less than 20 minutes to stay in the highest point coz its very very very hard to breath. Our Pilots use Oxygen during the entire flight. When we reach on the Base Camp again for landing and waiting for another Helicopter, breakfast were serve at Everest View Hotel while Warming ourselves with the Chimmey.\\r\\n\\r\\nMy heartfelt thanks to Everest Vacation Agency in Nepal the owner - Netra as an instrument in fulfilling our Dreams.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo our Tour Guide Dipak who is always with us from the very start until the end of our tour to the airport and for being very kind and hospitable assisting all our needs, tours, accommodation and everything. Words can't describe how grateful we are during the entire tour including Pokhara and Chitwan and to our co- tour guide as well. and to our Driver tyvm. <a href=\\"https://www.facebook.com/emilyemil.carpio/media_set?set=a.1742822405848741&amp;type=3\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.facebook.com/emilyemil.carpio/media_se...</a>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Note:</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nPrimarily used for helicopters in Nepal are rescue purposes at higher altitude. So first priority for rescue. If the need arises and there is a call for rescue during Everest Base Camp Helicopter Tour, the helicopters would need to make a rescue trip. Depending upon the rescue sometimes the guest might have to wait for more than 1 hour. The guests can meanwhile soak in the glory of the majestic Himalayas from Lukla or Everest View Hotel.", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630"}, "categoryId": null, "meta_title": "Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp | Everest Vacation", "blogContent": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Charter Helicopter Tour to Mount Everest | Chopper ride to Mount Everest Base Camp\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOur fascinating Everest base camp helicopter tour commences with landing in the highest viewpoint of EBC Kalapatther (5,555 meters) for the best view of Mount Everest. This trip is on a chopper to the world’s highest valley of Khumbu and Mount Everest Region. Everest Helicopter Tour gives you a chance to experience the tallest mountain in the world from the comfort of a helicopter instead of the long and difficult trek of Everest base camp.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"5555 meters\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Helicopter flight over to the Mt. Everest, landing experience at Everest Base camp \\\\u0026 Breakfast in Everest View hotel.\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"AC Luxury Car/Hiace\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\" Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp: Phenomenal and Thrilling\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHeli Trip Duration/Time:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 3:00 to 5:00 hours\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLanding Spot of Helicopter:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Kalapatthar (5,555m), Everest View Hotel for Breakfast \\\\u0026amp; Lukla (\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenzing%E2%80%93Hillary_Airport\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003eEdmund Hillary Airport\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e) for fueling.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eRoute of Everest Base Camp helicopter tour:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Kathmandu Airport to Lukla then Namche Bazaar, Pheriche, Gorakshep, and \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMt. Everest Base Camp, Kalapathar\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, and return to Everest View Hotel then to Lukla and continues to Kathmandu.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003eWE OFFER ONLY PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOURS, A MAXIMUM OF 5 TRAVELERS CAN DO AT A TIME. IT DEPENDS ON THE WEIGHT OF TRAVELERS TOO. THERE ARE MANY FACTORS TO CHOOSING A PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOUR OVER A GROUP JOINING TOUR\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch2\\\\u003eAbout Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp\\\\u003c/h2\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eHighlights Points\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFly over the highest peak in the world, including Mount Everest and other ranges.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSet foot on Kalapatthar (5555m), from where you can see the awesome views of Mount Everest(8848m), Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse (7861m), Ama Dablam and more\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnjoy the view of many 7000 to 8000-meter peaks including the world’s highest Mt. Everest. It sure will be the experience of a lifetime.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAerial view of Everest Base Camp, Khumbu Glacier, Khumbu Icefall, and Gokyo Lakes.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast at Everest View Hotel surrounded by snowy walls of Himalayan giants.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nEarly morning depart from your respective hotels to Kathmandu domestic airport for the amazing trip of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eEverest base camp helicopter\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. This mind-blowing and wonderful helicopter flight towards Mt. Everest Base Camp starts from there. Soon after taking off from the airport, we see the high panoramic view of the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu valley\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e, followed by small villages, and green hills. We have a view of an awesome parallel range of snow-capped mountains. The major peaks are towards the west \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://www.summitpost.org/manaslu/150687\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMt. Manaslu\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e, Ganesh Himal, Langtang, and Jugal Himal. As the flight continues more views of the mid-east and far-eastern Himalayan peaks of Mt. Gaurishankar, Melung Tse, Numbur, Cho-Oyu \\\\u0026amp; more come into the frame.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eEverest Base Camp helicopter tour\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e reaches Lukla 2,820 meters high and can stop a helicopter for fueling. From here, we get the best views of Kwangde Peak and the lower valley. The flight continues heading to the famous \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://wikitravel.org/en/Namche_Bazaar\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003eNamche Bazaar 3,440 meters high “Sherpa Capital\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e“. After Namche, we will be heading towards a scenic and renowned spot at Tyangboche Monastery located at 3,867 meters of altitude. From this hill, we can enjoy the panorama view of Mt. Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Lhotse Shar, Kangtega, Thamserku, and Kwangde. The close views of the stunning peak of Ama Dablam are a treat to your senses. From here head towards Pheriche where the tree lines fade in the barren landscape.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFind the video tour of \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_7G41764ipc\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003ethe Everest base camp helicopter tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e here.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eWhy Should You Choose Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp?\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEverest Heli Tour gives you a chance to experience the tallest mountain in the world from the comfort of a helicopter instead of a long and difficult trek.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVisit the Everest Region without paying a huge and unnecessary amount of money that one would spend during the trek.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFly near or above Mount Everest (8848m) and also enjoy the Bird’s eye view of 7000m to 8000m peaks– Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse(7861m), Makalu (8,481m), Cho Oyu(8201).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eExciting landing at one of the highest airports in the world, Tenzing-Hillary Airport (2,845m) in Lukla, and experience the view of Everest region, Kala Patthar, and savor 360-degree views of Himalayan Peaks.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eView of radically weather changes, up in the mountains.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eCost of Private Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nDaily flights for \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eprivate Everest base camp helicopter tour with landing at Kalapatther (5,555m.) and experience high altitude breakfast at Everest View Hotel.\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e5 Pax or more – \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUS$1,380.00\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Per Traveler\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e4 Pax – \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUS$1,650.00\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Per Traveler\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e3 Pax – \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUS$2,100.00\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Per Traveler\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e2 Pax – \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUS$2,980.00\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Per Traveler\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e1 Pax – \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUS$5,800.00\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Per Traveler\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cem\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNote:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e We need to calculate the weight of the passengers so please mention your weight for the helicopter flight to Everest during your inquiry.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\u003cem\\\\u003eA helicopter can lift only 3 people at a time in Everest base camp due to the high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Pheriche or Shyangboche.\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWith a view of this area, we continue to our main destination at \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMount Everest Base Camp\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e at 5,367 meters altitude. We fly over Khumbu Icefall and glaciers. During the climbing season, this place is flooded with camping tents and climbers. Here you will have \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ean exciting moment by stopping on the way to Kalapatthar where views of Mt. Everest\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e can be seen at a close distance with Mt. Pumori towards the North.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter having a short, fascinating time here on a helicopter tour to Everest base camp, we continued the flight back to Everest View Hotel for a short break and had breakfast with the views of Mt. Everest. Then fly to Kathmandu and transfer back to the hotel. This wonderful and overwhelming time of about 3-4 hours in the lap of the world’s highest peak Mt. Everest will be your lifetime experience and the stories about these majestic destinations for your friends and family.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"802\\",\\"801\\",\\"799\\",\\"798\\",\\"744\\",\\"757\\",\\"797\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Everest Basecamp heli tour\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"- 6:00 am pickup from hotel.\\\\r\\\\n- 6:30 am at airport.\\\\r\\\\n- 7:00 am helicopter take up.\\\\r\\\\n- 1 stop at Lukla for fueling\\\\r\\\\n- 1 stop at Pheriche for shuttle, if more than 3pax (helicopter leave 2 pax there, Pheriche stop approx 20 minutes use to take photos of surrounding mountain and high elevation lifetime experiences. After back 2 pax from everest base camp, turn for next two pax for everest base camp landing.)\\\\r\\\\n- 1 stop at Syangboche Everest View Hotel for half an hour for breakfast and amazing mountain views.\\\\r\\\\n- Back to Kathmandu airport.\\\\r\\\\n- Drop you at hotel by our vehicle.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":1,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eCar/van transportation to and from the domestic airport and hotel in Kathmandu.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEscorting guide for this Everest flight.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate helicopter for 4 hours.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Recent Experience by Emily Carpio:\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMOUNT EVEREST HELICOPTER DAY TOUR- NEPAL 2020 LIFETIME EXPERIENCE 2020 NEPAL LIFETIME EXPERIENCES #VNY2020\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe Mount Everest Helicopter Day Tour with three (3) Landing on the last base camp from the Summit is probably one of the most exciting tour in the World. This tour in Nepal takes you from your hotel that rolls to Tribhuvan International Airport at Kathmandu with a Helicopter, flying across the Himalayan range which presents you with the snow-capped mountain vistas around 5-7 hrs depending on the weather condition in which during our time Temperature is neg -27C with a very-very-very thin air at Mount Everest.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThere upon you will be landing at Lukha for fueling, then you will fly and across Namche Bazar, Syngoche, Tengboche and Everest Base Camp .Its once in a lifetime opportunity that you admire the beauty of Mount Everest and our Helicopter landed again at Kalapattar, (after we had some coffee on the second base camp). Kalapattar (5545 / 18192ft) provides the best view fronting Mount Everest (8,848m or 29012 ft), Pumori(7,161m), Ama Dablam (6,812m), Lhotse (8,516m), Choyu (8,201m), Nuptse (7,861m)and thousands of snow capped peaks.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nDuring our Highest Landing Only the Pilot and three of us Family my husband Danny, my Son CJ and me were allowed due to limited weight (max 220kg) due to the high altitude. We are only given less than 20 minutes to stay in the highest point coz its very very very hard to breath. Our Pilots use Oxygen during the entire flight. When we reach on the Base Camp again for landing and waiting for another Helicopter, breakfast were serve at Everest View Hotel while Warming ourselves with the Chimmey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMy heartfelt thanks to Everest Vacation Agency in Nepal the owner - Netra as an instrument in fulfilling our Dreams.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTo our Tour Guide Dipak who is always with us from the very start until the end of our tour to the airport and for being very kind and hospitable assisting all our needs, tours, accommodation and everything. Words can't describe how grateful we are during the entire tour including Pokhara and Chitwan and to our co- tour guide as well. and to our Driver tyvm. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://www.facebook.com/emilyemil.carpio/media_set?set=a.1742822405848741\\\\u0026amp;type=3\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttps://www.facebook.com/emilyemil.carpio/media_se...\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNote:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nPrimarily used for helicopters in Nepal are rescue purposes at higher altitude. So first priority for rescue. If the need arises and there is a call for rescue during Everest Base Camp Helicopter Tour, the helicopters would need to make a rescue trip. Depending upon the rescue sometimes the guest might have to wait for more than 1 hour. The guests can meanwhile soak in the glory of the majestic Himalayas from Lukla or Everest View Hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour - 2 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":3,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Charter Helicopter Tour to Mount Everest | Chopper ride to Mount Everest Base Camp\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOur fascinating Everest base camp helicopter tour commences with landing in the highest viewpoint of EBC Kalapatther (5,555 meters) for the best view of Mount Everest. This trip is on a chopper to the world’s highest valley of Khumbu and Mount Everest Region. Everest Helicopter Tour gives you a chance to experience the tallest mountain in the world from the comfort of a helicopter instead of the long and difficult trek of Everest base camp.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"5555 meters\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Helicopter flight over to the Mt. Everest, landing experience at Everest Base camp \\\\u0026 Breakfast in Everest View hotel.\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"AC Luxury Car/Hiace\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\" Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp: Phenomenal and Thrilling\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHeli Trip Duration/Time:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e 3:00 to 5:00 hours\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLanding Spot of Helicopter:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Kalapatthar (5,555m), Everest View Hotel for Breakfast \\\\u0026amp; Lukla (\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenzing%E2%80%93Hillary_Airport\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003eEdmund Hillary Airport\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e) for fueling.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eRoute of Everest Base Camp helicopter tour:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Kathmandu Airport to Lukla then Namche Bazaar, Pheriche, Gorakshep, and \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMt. Everest Base Camp, Kalapathar\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, and return to Everest View Hotel then to Lukla and continues to Kathmandu.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003eWE OFFER ONLY PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOURS, A MAXIMUM OF 5 TRAVELERS CAN DO AT A TIME. IT DEPENDS ON THE WEIGHT OF TRAVELERS TOO. THERE ARE MANY FACTORS TO CHOOSING A PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOUR OVER A GROUP JOINING TOUR\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch2\\\\u003eAbout Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp\\\\u003c/h2\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eHighlights Points\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFly over the highest peak in the world, including Mount Everest and other ranges.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSet foot on Kalapatthar (5555m), from where you can see the awesome views of Mount Everest(8848m), Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse (7861m), Ama Dablam and more\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnjoy the view of many 7000 to 8000-meter peaks including the world’s highest Mt. Everest. It sure will be the experience of a lifetime.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAerial view of Everest Base Camp, Khumbu Glacier, Khumbu Icefall, and Gokyo Lakes.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast at Everest View Hotel surrounded by snowy walls of Himalayan giants.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nEarly morning depart from your respective hotels to Kathmandu domestic airport for the amazing trip of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eEverest base camp helicopter\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. This mind-blowing and wonderful helicopter flight towards Mt. Everest Base Camp starts from there. Soon after taking off from the airport, we see the high panoramic view of the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu valley\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e, followed by small villages, and green hills. We have a view of an awesome parallel range of snow-capped mountains. The major peaks are towards the west \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://www.summitpost.org/manaslu/150687\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMt. Manaslu\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e, Ganesh Himal, Langtang, and Jugal Himal. As the flight continues more views of the mid-east and far-eastern Himalayan peaks of Mt. Gaurishankar, Melung Tse, Numbur, Cho-Oyu \\\\u0026amp; more come into the frame.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eEverest Base Camp helicopter tour\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e reaches Lukla 2,820 meters high and can stop a helicopter for fueling. From here, we get the best views of Kwangde Peak and the lower valley. The flight continues heading to the famous \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://wikitravel.org/en/Namche_Bazaar\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003eNamche Bazaar 3,440 meters high “Sherpa Capital\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e“. After Namche, we will be heading towards a scenic and renowned spot at Tyangboche Monastery located at 3,867 meters of altitude. From this hill, we can enjoy the panorama view of Mt. Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Lhotse Shar, Kangtega, Thamserku, and Kwangde. The close views of the stunning peak of Ama Dablam are a treat to your senses. From here head towards Pheriche where the tree lines fade in the barren landscape.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFind the video tour of \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_7G41764ipc\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003ethe Everest base camp helicopter tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e here.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eWhy Should You Choose Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp?\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEverest Heli Tour gives you a chance to experience the tallest mountain in the world from the comfort of a helicopter instead of a long and difficult trek.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVisit the Everest Region without paying a huge and unnecessary amount of money that one would spend during the trek.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFly near or above Mount Everest (8848m) and also enjoy the Bird’s eye view of 7000m to 8000m peaks– Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse(7861m), Makalu (8,481m), Cho Oyu(8201).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eExciting landing at one of the highest airports in the world, Tenzing-Hillary Airport (2,845m) in Lukla, and experience the view of Everest region, Kala Patthar, and savor 360-degree views of Himalayan Peaks.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eView of radically weather changes, up in the mountains.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eCost of Private Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nDaily flights for \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eprivate Everest base camp helicopter tour with landing at Kalapatther (5,555m.) and experience high altitude breakfast at Everest View Hotel.\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e5 Pax or more – \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUS$1,380.00\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Per Traveler\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e4 Pax – \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUS$1,650.00\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Per Traveler\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e3 Pax – \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUS$2,100.00\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Per Traveler\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e2 Pax – \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUS$2,980.00\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Per Traveler\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e1 Pax – \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eUS$5,800.00\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Per Traveler\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cem\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNote:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e We need to calculate the weight of the passengers so please mention your weight for the helicopter flight to Everest during your inquiry.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\u003cem\\\\u003eA helicopter can lift only 3 people at a time in Everest base camp due to the high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Pheriche or Shyangboche.\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWith a view of this area, we continue to our main destination at \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMount Everest Base Camp\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e at 5,367 meters altitude. We fly over Khumbu Icefall and glaciers. During the climbing season, this place is flooded with camping tents and climbers. Here you will have \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ean exciting moment by stopping on the way to Kalapatthar where views of Mt. Everest\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e can be seen at a close distance with Mt. Pumori towards the North.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter having a short, fascinating time here on a helicopter tour to Everest base camp, we continued the flight back to Everest View Hotel for a short break and had breakfast with the views of Mt. Everest. Then fly to Kathmandu and transfer back to the hotel. This wonderful and overwhelming time of about 3-4 hours in the lap of the world’s highest peak Mt. Everest will be your lifetime experience and the stories about these majestic destinations for your friends and family.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"802\\",\\"801\\",\\"799\\",\\"798\\",\\"744\\",\\"757\\",\\"797\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Everest Basecamp heli tour\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"- 6:00 am pickup from hotel.\\\\r\\\\n- 6:30 am at airport.\\\\r\\\\n- 7:00 am helicopter take up.\\\\r\\\\n- 1 stop at Lukla for fueling\\\\r\\\\n- 1 stop at Pheriche for shuttle, if more than 3pax (helicopter leave 2 pax there, Pheriche stop approx 20 minutes use to take photos of surrounding mountain and high elevation lifetime experiences. After back 2 pax from everest base camp, turn for next two pax for everest base camp landing.)\\\\r\\\\n- 1 stop at Syangboche Everest View Hotel for half an hour for breakfast and amazing mountain views.\\\\r\\\\n- Back to Kathmandu airport.\\\\r\\\\n- Drop you at hotel by our vehicle.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":1,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eCar/van transportation to and from the domestic airport and hotel in Kathmandu.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEscorting guide for this Everest flight.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate helicopter for 4 hours.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Recent Experience by Emily Carpio:\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMOUNT EVEREST HELICOPTER DAY TOUR- NEPAL 2020 LIFETIME EXPERIENCE 2020 NEPAL LIFETIME EXPERIENCES #VNY2020\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe Mount Everest Helicopter Day Tour with three (3) Landing on the last base camp from the Summit is probably one of the most exciting tour in the World. This tour in Nepal takes you from your hotel that rolls to Tribhuvan International Airport at Kathmandu with a Helicopter, flying across the Himalayan range which presents you with the snow-capped mountain vistas around 5-7 hrs depending on the weather condition in which during our time Temperature is neg -27C with a very-very-very thin air at Mount Everest.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThere upon you will be landing at Lukha for fueling, then you will fly and across Namche Bazar, Syngoche, Tengboche and Everest Base Camp .Its once in a lifetime opportunity that you admire the beauty of Mount Everest and our Helicopter landed again at Kalapattar, (after we had some coffee on the second base camp). Kalapattar (5545 / 18192ft) provides the best view fronting Mount Everest (8,848m or 29012 ft), Pumori(7,161m), Ama Dablam (6,812m), Lhotse (8,516m), Choyu (8,201m), Nuptse (7,861m)and thousands of snow capped peaks.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nDuring our Highest Landing Only the Pilot and three of us Family my husband Danny, my Son CJ and me were allowed due to limited weight (max 220kg) due to the high altitude. We are only given less than 20 minutes to stay in the highest point coz its very very very hard to breath. Our Pilots use Oxygen during the entire flight. When we reach on the Base Camp again for landing and waiting for another Helicopter, breakfast were serve at Everest View Hotel while Warming ourselves with the Chimmey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMy heartfelt thanks to Everest Vacation Agency in Nepal the owner - Netra as an instrument in fulfilling our Dreams.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTo our Tour Guide Dipak who is always with us from the very start until the end of our tour to the airport and for being very kind and hospitable assisting all our needs, tours, accommodation and everything. Words can't describe how grateful we are during the entire tour including Pokhara and Chitwan and to our co- tour guide as well. and to our Driver tyvm. \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://www.facebook.com/emilyemil.carpio/media_set?set=a.1742822405848741\\\\u0026amp;type=3\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003ehttps://www.facebook.com/emilyemil.carpio/media_se...\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNote:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nPrimarily used for helicopters in Nepal are rescue purposes at higher altitude. So first priority for rescue. If the need arises and there is a call for rescue during Everest Base Camp Helicopter Tour, the helicopters would need to make a rescue trip. Depending upon the rescue sometimes the guest might have to wait for more than 1 hour. The guests can meanwhile soak in the glory of the majestic Himalayas from Lukla or Everest View Hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour - 2 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":3,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/EVEREST.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/everest-heclicopter-review.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/helicopter-at-pheriche.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Helicopter-at-Everest-View-Hotel-Syangboche.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Everest-Base-Camp-Kalapatthar-Landing-Heli-Tour.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/KALAPATTHAR.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=806", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "806", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-04 06:37:30", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-04 06:37:30", "post_modified": "2024-09-26 06:43:41", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-09-26 06:43:41"}}, "customSections": [{"id": 1, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Recent Experience by Emily Carpio:", "content": ["<strong>MOUNT EVEREST HELICOPTER DAY TOUR- NEPAL 2020 LIFETIME EXPERIENCE 2020 NEPAL LIFETIME EXPERIENCES #VNY2020</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Mount Everest Helicopter Day Tour with three (3) Landing on the last base camp from the Summit is probably one of the most exciting tour in the World. This tour in Nepal takes you from your hotel that rolls to Tribhuvan International Airport at Kathmandu with a Helicopter, flying across the Himalayan range which presents you with the snow-capped mountain vistas around 5-7 hrs depending on the weather condition in which during our time Temperature is neg -27C with a very-very-very thin air at Mount Everest.\\r\\n\\r\\nThere upon you will be landing at Lukha for fueling, then you will fly and across Namche Bazar, Syngoche, Tengboche and Everest Base Camp .Its once in a lifetime opportunity that you admire the beauty of Mount Everest and our Helicopter landed again at Kalapattar, (after we had some coffee on the second base camp). Kalapattar (5545 / 18192ft) provides the best view fronting Mount Everest (8,848m or 29012 ft), Pumori(7,161m), Ama Dablam (6,812m), Lhotse (8,516m), Choyu (8,201m), Nuptse (7,861m)and thousands of snow capped peaks.\\r\\n\\r\\nDuring our Highest Landing Only the Pilot and three of us Family my husband Danny, my Son CJ and me were allowed due to limited weight (max 220kg) due to the high altitude. We are only given less than 20 minutes to stay in the highest point coz its very very very hard to breath. Our Pilots use Oxygen during the entire flight. When we reach on the Base Camp again for landing and waiting for another Helicopter, breakfast were serve at Everest View Hotel while Warming ourselves with the Chimmey.\\r\\n\\r\\nMy heartfelt thanks to Everest Vacation Agency in Nepal the owner - Netra as an instrument in fulfilling our Dreams.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo our Tour Guide Dipak who is always with us from the very start until the end of our tour to the airport and for being very kind and hospitable assisting all our needs, tours, accommodation and everything. Words can't describe how grateful we are during the entire tour including Pokhara and Chitwan and to our co- tour guide as well. and to our Driver tyvm. <a href=\\"https://www.facebook.com/emilyemil.carpio/media_set?set=a.1742822405848741&amp;type=3\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.facebook.com/emilyemil.carpio/media_se...</a>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Note:</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nPrimarily used for helicopters in Nepal are rescue purposes at higher altitude. So first priority for rescue. If the need arises and there is a call for rescue during Everest Base Camp Helicopter Tour, the helicopters would need to make a rescue trip. Depending upon the rescue sometimes the guest might have to wait for more than 1 hour. The guests can meanwhile soak in the glory of the majestic Himalayas from Lukla or Everest View Hotel."], "description": "<strong>MOUNT EVEREST HELICOPTER DAY TOUR- NEPAL 2020 LIFETIME EXPERIENCE 2020 NEPAL LIFETIME EXPERIENCES #VNY2020</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nThe Mount Everest Helicopter Day Tour with three (3) Landing on the last base camp from the Summit is probably one of the most exciting tour in the World. This tour in Nepal takes you from your hotel that rolls to Tribhuvan International Airport at Kathmandu with a Helicopter, flying across the Himalayan range which presents you with the snow-capped mountain vistas around 5-7 hrs depending on the weather condition in which during our time Temperature is neg -27C with a very-very-very thin air at Mount Everest.\\r\\n\\r\\nThere upon you will be landing at Lukha for fueling, then you will fly and across Namche Bazar, Syngoche, Tengboche and Everest Base Camp .Its once in a lifetime opportunity that you admire the beauty of Mount Everest and our Helicopter landed again at Kalapattar, (after we had some coffee on the second base camp). Kalapattar (5545 / 18192ft) provides the best view fronting Mount Everest (8,848m or 29012 ft), Pumori(7,161m), Ama Dablam (6,812m), Lhotse (8,516m), Choyu (8,201m), Nuptse (7,861m)and thousands of snow capped peaks.\\r\\n\\r\\nDuring our Highest Landing Only the Pilot and three of us Family my husband Danny, my Son CJ and me were allowed due to limited weight (max 220kg) due to the high altitude. We are only given less than 20 minutes to stay in the highest point coz its very very very hard to breath. Our Pilots use Oxygen during the entire flight. When we reach on the Base Camp again for landing and waiting for another Helicopter, breakfast were serve at Everest View Hotel while Warming ourselves with the Chimmey.\\r\\n\\r\\nMy heartfelt thanks to Everest Vacation Agency in Nepal the owner - Netra as an instrument in fulfilling our Dreams.\\r\\n\\r\\nTo our Tour Guide Dipak who is always with us from the very start until the end of our tour to the airport and for being very kind and hospitable assisting all our needs, tours, accommodation and everything. Words can't describe how grateful we are during the entire tour including Pokhara and Chitwan and to our co- tour guide as well. and to our Driver tyvm. <a href=\\"https://www.facebook.com/emilyemil.carpio/media_set?set=a.1742822405848741&amp;type=3\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.facebook.com/emilyemil.carpio/media_se...</a>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Note:</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nPrimarily used for helicopters in Nepal are rescue purposes at higher altitude. So first priority for rescue. If the need arises and there is a call for rescue during Everest Base Camp Helicopter Tour, the helicopters would need to make a rescue trip. Depending upon the rescue sometimes the guest might have to wait for more than 1 hour. The guests can meanwhile soak in the glory of the majestic Himalayas from Lukla or Everest View Hotel."}, {"id": 2, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Extended Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": 3, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Alternate Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["<strong>Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp: Phenomenal and Thrilling</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Heli Trip Duration/Time:</strong> 3:00 to 5:00 hours\\r\\n<strong>Landing Spot of Helicopter:</strong> Kalapatthar (5,555m), Everest View Hotel for Breakfast &amp; Lukla (<a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenzing%E2%80%93Hillary_Airport\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Edmund Hillary Airport</a>) for fueling.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Route of Everest Base Camp helicopter tour:</strong> Kathmandu Airport to Lukla then Namche Bazaar, Pheriche, Gorakshep, and <strong>Mt. Everest Base Camp, Kalapathar</strong>, and return to Everest View Hotel then to Lukla and continues to Kathmandu.\\r\\n<blockquote>WE OFFER ONLY PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOURS, A MAXIMUM OF 5 TRAVELERS CAN DO AT A TIME. IT DEPENDS ON THE WEIGHT OF TRAVELERS TOO. THERE ARE MANY FACTORS TO CHOOSING A PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOUR OVER A GROUP JOINING TOUR</blockquote>\\r\\n<h2>About Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</h2>\\r\\n<h3>Highlights Points</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fly over the highest peak in the world, including Mount Everest and other ranges.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Set foot on Kalapatthar (5555m), from where you can see the awesome views of Mount Everest(8848m), Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse (7861m), Ama Dablam and more</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Enjoy the view of many 7000 to 8000-meter peaks including the world’s highest Mt. Everest. It sure will be the experience of a lifetime.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Aerial view of Everest Base Camp, Khumbu Glacier, Khumbu Icefall, and Gokyo Lakes.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Breakfast at Everest View Hotel surrounded by snowy walls of Himalayan giants.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nEarly morning depart from your respective hotels to Kathmandu domestic airport for the amazing trip of <strong>Everest base camp helicopter</strong>. This mind-blowing and wonderful helicopter flight towards Mt. Everest Base Camp starts from there. Soon after taking off from the airport, we see the high panoramic view of the <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Kathmandu valley</a>, followed by small villages, and green hills. We have a view of an awesome parallel range of snow-capped mountains. The major peaks are towards the west <a href=\\"https://www.summitpost.org/manaslu/150687\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Mt. Manaslu</a>, Ganesh Himal, Langtang, and Jugal Himal. As the flight continues more views of the mid-east and far-eastern Himalayan peaks of Mt. Gaurishankar, Melung Tse, Numbur, Cho-Oyu &amp; more come into the frame.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Everest Base Camp helicopter tour</strong> reaches Lukla 2,820 meters high and can stop a helicopter for fueling. From here, we get the best views of Kwangde Peak and the lower valley. The flight continues heading to the famous <a href=\\"https://wikitravel.org/en/Namche_Bazaar\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Namche Bazaar 3,440 meters high “Sherpa Capital</a>“. After Namche, we will be heading towards a scenic and renowned spot at Tyangboche Monastery located at 3,867 meters of altitude. From this hill, we can enjoy the panorama view of Mt. Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Lhotse Shar, Kangtega, Thamserku, and Kwangde. The close views of the stunning peak of Ama Dablam are a treat to your senses. From here head towards Pheriche where the tree lines fade in the barren landscape.\\r\\n\\r\\nFind the video tour of <a href=\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_7G41764ipc\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">the Everest base camp helicopter tour</a> here.\\r\\n<h3>Why Should You Choose Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp?</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Everest Heli Tour gives you a chance to experience the tallest mountain in the world from the comfort of a helicopter instead of a long and difficult trek.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit the Everest Region without paying a huge and unnecessary amount of money that one would spend during the trek.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fly near or above Mount Everest (8848m) and also enjoy the Bird’s eye view of 7000m to 8000m peaks– Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse(7861m), Makalu (8,481m), Cho Oyu(8201).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Exciting landing at one of the highest airports in the world, Tenzing-Hillary Airport (2,845m) in Lukla, and experience the view of Everest region, Kala Patthar, and savor 360-degree views of Himalayan Peaks.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>View of radically weather changes, up in the mountains.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Cost of Private Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</h3>\\r\\nDaily flights for <strong>private Everest base camp helicopter tour with landing at Kalapatther (5,555m.) and experience high altitude breakfast at Everest View Hotel.</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>5 Pax or more – <strong>US$1,380.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>4 Pax – <strong>US$1,650.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>3 Pax – <strong>US$2,100.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>2 Pax – <strong>US$2,980.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>1 Pax – <strong>US$5,800.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<em><strong>Note:</strong> We need to calculate the weight of the passengers so please mention your weight for the helicopter flight to Everest during your inquiry.\\r\\n</em><em>A helicopter can lift only 3 people at a time in Everest base camp due to the high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Pheriche or Shyangboche.</em>\\r\\n\\r\\nWith a view of this area, we continue to our main destination at <strong>Mount Everest Base Camp</strong> at 5,367 meters altitude. We fly over Khumbu Icefall and glaciers. During the climbing season, this place is flooded with camping tents and climbers. Here you will have <strong>an exciting moment by stopping on the way to Kalapatthar where views of Mt. Everest</strong> can be seen at a close distance with Mt. Pumori towards the North.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter having a short, fascinating time here on a helicopter tour to Everest base camp, we continued the flight back to Everest View Hotel for a short break and had breakfast with the views of Mt. Everest. Then fly to Kathmandu and transfer back to the hotel. This wonderful and overwhelming time of about 3-4 hours in the lap of the world’s highest peak Mt. Everest will be your lifetime experience and the stories about these majestic destinations for your friends and family."], "description": "<strong>Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp: Phenomenal and Thrilling</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Heli Trip Duration/Time:</strong> 3:00 to 5:00 hours\\r\\n<strong>Landing Spot of Helicopter:</strong> Kalapatthar (5,555m), Everest View Hotel for Breakfast &amp; Lukla (<a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenzing%E2%80%93Hillary_Airport\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Edmund Hillary Airport</a>) for fueling.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Route of Everest Base Camp helicopter tour:</strong> Kathmandu Airport to Lukla then Namche Bazaar, Pheriche, Gorakshep, and <strong>Mt. Everest Base Camp, Kalapathar</strong>, and return to Everest View Hotel then to Lukla and continues to Kathmandu.\\r\\n<blockquote>WE OFFER ONLY PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOURS, A MAXIMUM OF 5 TRAVELERS CAN DO AT A TIME. IT DEPENDS ON THE WEIGHT OF TRAVELERS TOO. THERE ARE MANY FACTORS TO CHOOSING A PRIVATE HELICOPTER TOUR OVER A GROUP JOINING TOUR</blockquote>\\r\\n<h2>About Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</h2>\\r\\n<h3>Highlights Points</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fly over the highest peak in the world, including Mount Everest and other ranges.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Set foot on Kalapatthar (5555m), from where you can see the awesome views of Mount Everest(8848m), Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse (7861m), Ama Dablam and more</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Enjoy the view of many 7000 to 8000-meter peaks including the world’s highest Mt. Everest. It sure will be the experience of a lifetime.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Aerial view of Everest Base Camp, Khumbu Glacier, Khumbu Icefall, and Gokyo Lakes.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Breakfast at Everest View Hotel surrounded by snowy walls of Himalayan giants.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nEarly morning depart from your respective hotels to Kathmandu domestic airport for the amazing trip of <strong>Everest base camp helicopter</strong>. This mind-blowing and wonderful helicopter flight towards Mt. Everest Base Camp starts from there. Soon after taking off from the airport, we see the high panoramic view of the <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Kathmandu valley</a>, followed by small villages, and green hills. We have a view of an awesome parallel range of snow-capped mountains. The major peaks are towards the west <a href=\\"https://www.summitpost.org/manaslu/150687\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Mt. Manaslu</a>, Ganesh Himal, Langtang, and Jugal Himal. As the flight continues more views of the mid-east and far-eastern Himalayan peaks of Mt. Gaurishankar, Melung Tse, Numbur, Cho-Oyu &amp; more come into the frame.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Everest Base Camp helicopter tour</strong> reaches Lukla 2,820 meters high and can stop a helicopter for fueling. From here, we get the best views of Kwangde Peak and the lower valley. The flight continues heading to the famous <a href=\\"https://wikitravel.org/en/Namche_Bazaar\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Namche Bazaar 3,440 meters high “Sherpa Capital</a>“. After Namche, we will be heading towards a scenic and renowned spot at Tyangboche Monastery located at 3,867 meters of altitude. From this hill, we can enjoy the panorama view of Mt. Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Lhotse Shar, Kangtega, Thamserku, and Kwangde. The close views of the stunning peak of Ama Dablam are a treat to your senses. From here head towards Pheriche where the tree lines fade in the barren landscape.\\r\\n\\r\\nFind the video tour of <a href=\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_7G41764ipc\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">the Everest base camp helicopter tour</a> here.\\r\\n<h3>Why Should You Choose Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp?</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Everest Heli Tour gives you a chance to experience the tallest mountain in the world from the comfort of a helicopter instead of a long and difficult trek.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit the Everest Region without paying a huge and unnecessary amount of money that one would spend during the trek.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fly near or above Mount Everest (8848m) and also enjoy the Bird’s eye view of 7000m to 8000m peaks– Lhotse(8516m), Nuptse(7861m), Makalu (8,481m), Cho Oyu(8201).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Exciting landing at one of the highest airports in the world, Tenzing-Hillary Airport (2,845m) in Lukla, and experience the view of Everest region, Kala Patthar, and savor 360-degree views of Himalayan Peaks.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>View of radically weather changes, up in the mountains.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Cost of Private Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</h3>\\r\\nDaily flights for <strong>private Everest base camp helicopter tour with landing at Kalapatther (5,555m.) and experience high altitude breakfast at Everest View Hotel.</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>5 Pax or more – <strong>US$1,380.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>4 Pax – <strong>US$1,650.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>3 Pax – <strong>US$2,100.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>2 Pax – <strong>US$2,980.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>1 Pax – <strong>US$5,800.00</strong> Per Traveler</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<em><strong>Note:</strong> We need to calculate the weight of the passengers so please mention your weight for the helicopter flight to Everest during your inquiry.\\r\\n</em><em>A helicopter can lift only 3 people at a time in Everest base camp due to the high altitude. So, if more than 3 pax, it may have to do a shuttle from Pheriche or Shyangboche.</em>\\r\\n\\r\\nWith a view of this area, we continue to our main destination at <strong>Mount Everest Base Camp</strong> at 5,367 meters altitude. We fly over Khumbu Icefall and glaciers. During the climbing season, this place is flooded with camping tents and climbers. Here you will have <strong>an exciting moment by stopping on the way to Kalapatthar where views of Mt. Everest</strong> can be seen at a close distance with Mt. Pumori towards the North.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter having a short, fascinating time here on a helicopter tour to Everest base camp, we continued the flight back to Everest View Hotel for a short break and had breakfast with the views of Mt. Everest. Then fly to Kathmandu and transfer back to the hotel. This wonderful and overwhelming time of about 3-4 hours in the lap of the world’s highest peak Mt. Everest will be your lifetime experience and the stories about these majestic destinations for your friends and family."}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Car/van transportation to and from the domestic airport and hotel in Kathmandu.", "Escorting guide for this Everest flight.", "Private helicopter for 4 hours."], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Car/van transportation to and from the domestic airport and hotel in Kathmandu.", "Escorting guide for this Everest flight.", "Private helicopter for 4 hours."], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "Explore Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp with Everest Vacation.", "trip_highlights": "<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nOur fascinating Everest base camp helicopter tour commences with landing in the highest viewpoint of EBC Kalapatther (5,555 meters) for the best view of Mount Everest. This trip is on a chopper to the world’s highest valley of Khumbu and Mount Everest Region. Everest Helicopter Tour gives you a chance to experience the tallest mountain in the world from the comfort of a helicopter instead of the long and difficult trek of Everest base camp.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>", "trip_type_level": "Easy", "meta_description": "Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp treats the up-close view of many 7000 to 8000-meter peaks including the world’s highest Mt. Everest.", "trip_attractions": "Helicopter flight over to the Mt. Everest, landing experience at Everest Base camp & Breakfast in Everest View hotel.", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "faq_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "Helicopter flight over to the Mt. Everest, landing experience at Everest Base camp & Breakfast in Everest View hotel.", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "5555 meters", "transportation": "AC Luxury Car/Hiace"}, "trip_max_elevation": "5555 meters", "trip_transportations": "AC Luxury Car/Hiace", "trip_highlights_title": "Charter Helicopter Tour to Mount Everest | Chopper ride to Mount Everest Base Camp"}	2023-12-04 06:37:30+00	2024-09-26 07:43:41+01
171	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "4 nights Kathmandu, Pokhara and 5 nights Bhutan", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "10", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour"}, "meta": {"_edit_last": "5", "_edit_lock": "1723977282:5", "_dp_original": "790", "_thumbnail_id": "4414", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "4 nights Kathmandu, Pokhara and 5 nights Bhutan", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "10", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Bhutan Nepal Tour 9 nights 10 days", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "44", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Bhutan Nepal Tour 9 nights 10 days is a phenomenal tour where visitors can explore the true beauty of Nepal and Bhutan.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "nepal-bhutan-tour-9-nights-10-days", "tags": [], "title": "Bhutan Nepal Tour 9 nights 10 days", "duration": "10 Days", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Nepal Bhutan Tour 9 nights 10 days (4 nights in Nepal and 5 nights in Bhutan)</strong></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Travel Route (Bhutan and then Nepal also possible), Flexible monuments to visit, Flexible number of nights in both countries.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We take care of your Visa of Bhutan and internal flights. A Nepal visa is easily available upon your arrival at Kathmandu (TIA) airport.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n&nbsp;\\r\\n\\r\\nThe <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-bhutan-tour-7-nights-8-days/\\">Nepal Bhutan Tour</a> 9 nights 10 days by Everest Vacation is the complete package for all travelers seeking natural and cultural exploration. Visitors have the flexibility to customize the itinerary to their preferences. Travel around the UNESCO-listed sites in Nepal including the marvelous Bhaktapur Durbar Square. Pokhara sightseeing includes a hike to beautiful Sarangkot popular for sunrise and boating on the serene Phewa Lake. Free time walking around the Thamel area and shopping is a great way to conclude the Nepal tour.\\r\\n\\r\\nExplore the lovely cities of Paro, Thimphu, <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phobjikha_Valley\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Phobjikha</a>, and Punakha during the Bhutan tour. The mountain range views from Dochu La Pass are stunning. Visit fabulous landmarks such as Tashichho Dzong, Memorial Chorten, Great Buddha Dordenma, Chhimi Lhakhang Temple, Punakha Dzong, Paro Dzong, Kyichu Lhakhang, etc. The Phobjikha Nature trail hike offers a beautiful view of the valley. The iconic Tiger’s Nest Monastery hike in Paro is amusing."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Arrival in Kathmandu and Kathmandu Sightseeing", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pickup from Kathmandu (TIA) airport</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Boudhanath ( A large Buddhist Stupa)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pashupatinath (Largest Hindu Temple having an open cremation area)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Swoyambhu Stupa (Monkey Temple)</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you arrive lately in Kathmandu, we will manage the tour in next day (before flight to Bhutan)</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Kathmandu", "driveTime": "Approx, 30 minutes drive from airport to hotel.", "elevation": "1400m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 2, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Drive/Flight to Pokhara and Relax around lakeside", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive/flight to Pokhara</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Walking Tour around lakeside.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Pokhara", "driveTime": "Approx, 30 minutes flight or 6 hours drive from Kathmandu to Pokhara.", "elevation": "822m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 3, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Sarangkot Sunrise and Pokhara Sightseeing", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit/tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Early morning drive to Sarangkot</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Sunrise view from Himalayas</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive back to Pokhara valley</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Phewa Lake boating</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Devi’s Falls</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Gupteshwor Mahadev Cave</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>International Mountain Museum</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bindhyabasini Temple</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Pokhara", "driveTime": "Approx, 30 minutes drive to Sarangkot hill from Pokhara valley.", "elevation": "1600m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 4, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Drive/flight to Kathmandu and Bhaktapur Tour", "richText": "<div id=\\"collapse-4\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-4\\">\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive/flight back to Kathmandu and then Bhaktapur</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Tour of Bhaktapur Durbar Square</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive back to Kathmandu.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Kathmandu\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "driveTime": "Approx, 30 minutes flight or 6 hours drive to Kathmandu from Pokhara.", "elevation": "1400m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 5, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Fly Kathmandu to Paro(Bhutan), drive to Thimphu and Thimphu sightseeing", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drop to Kathmandu airport</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pickup from Paro airport</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive to Thimphu</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Memorial Chorten (temple)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Changangkha Lhakhang</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Statue of Buddha</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit the fortress of Thimphu, Tashichho Dzong</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Weekend market (Friday, Saturday, Sunday)</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you arrive lately in Paro, we will manage the tour in next day morning.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Thimphu", "driveTime": "Approx, 1 hour 30 minutes drive from Paro to Thimphu.", "elevation": "2200m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 6, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Drive to Punakha and Punakha Sightseeing", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive to Punakha crossing over Dochu La Pass (3100 mts)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Dochu La Pass (views of the highest mountain peaks &amp; walk around the 108 stupas)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike through the paddy field and old village to visit Chhimi Lhakhang, the temple of fertility</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Punakha Dzong</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Khamsum Yuley Lhakhang</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Punakha", "driveTime": "Approx, 2 hours 30 minutes drive from Thimphu to Punakha", "elevation": "1200m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 7, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Drive to Phobjikha and Phobjikha remote village tour", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive to Phobjikha after breakfast.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit/tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Phobjikha Nature trail hike (2.5 Hrs), which offers beautiful view of the valley. It starts from the valley and end with Gangtey Goempa</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit Gangtey Goempa Temple</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Crane Canter</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>An option to visit a village and a farmhouse for lunch/dinner</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Phobjikha", "driveTime": "Approx, 2 hours 30 minutes drive from Punakha to Pobhjikha", "elevation": "3000m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 8, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Drive to Paro and Paro Sightseeing", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive to Paro after breakfast</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Paro Dzong (Fortress)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Old Paro Town</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Could get some opportunity to see the traditional game, Archery.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Paro", "driveTime": "Approx, 5 hours drive from Phobjikha to Paro", "elevation": "2200m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 9, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Hike to Taktsang Monastery and visit Kyichu Lakhang", "richText": "<div id=\\"collapse-9\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-9\\">\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive to base for the hike</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike to Taktsang Monastery (Tiger’s Nest) – 3 hours uphill</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kichu Lakhang, one of the oldest temples in Bhutan</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Paro\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "driveTime": "Approx, 20 minutes drive from Paro town to base camp of hike", "elevation": "3120m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 10, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Final Departure / Tour end", "richText": "<div id=\\"collapse-10\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-10\\">\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drop you to Paro airport from your hotel</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Return with some magnificent memories and moments from Nepal and Bhutan trip.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flight available from Paro to Kathmandu, Bangkok, New Delhi, Kolkata, Bagdogra, Singapore, Dhaka etc.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</div>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/horse-in-bhutan.jpg", "title": "horse-in-bhutan", "altText": "Horse/Pony ride during Tiger's Nest Hike", "caption": "Horse/Pony ride during Tiger's Nest Hike", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["4348", "4620", "4309", "4305", "4306", "4280", "4072", "4038", "4035", "4033", "4022", "4015", "3992", "3869"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "ws_block_attractions": "", "ws_block_best_season": "", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "Cost Inclusion ", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-light", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": "Why Travel With Us?", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc4e9c19160", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_blo