m/luxury-helicopter-tour-himalayas-nepal/\\">Helicopter Tour</a></h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fly over the Himalayas viewing the landscape diversity of Nepal live as you can have a view of Terai Plains, Green Hills, and Snow-capped Himalayas in a single flight.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Major mountain sightings like Annapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma ( 8013 m), Langtang Lirung (7246 m), Ganesh (7604 m), Gaurishankar (7145 m), and many other ranges.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Witnessing the Himalayan art of living with the short flight over the stone-patched Tamang villages.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Picturesque view throughout the flight of the vegetation and landscapes of Langtang National Park.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Amazing view of the Langtang Valley and an organic tea treat your soul in your brief stay.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kyanjin Gompa tour watching the murals and sculptures in this old Monastery</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Rare but lucky spotting of the red panda and Himalayan birds.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Outline Itinerary</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Early morning pick up from the hotel</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transfer to the Domestic section of the TIA, Kathmandu</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Take off after 20-30 minutes of the arrival</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>30-35 minutes of scene packed flight to Langtang region.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Landing at Kyanjin Gompa, 20 minutes of ground time</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Breakfast at the lap of Langtang Lirung, Picture taking and strolling</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Return flight to TIA</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive back to your hotel</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>About Aircrafts</h4>\\r\\nModel: AS350b3e, AS350 FX II, AS350 FX II, AS350 BA , AS350 H125 ( Formally known as AS350 B3e)\\r\\nManufacturer: Air Bus, France\\r\\nEngine Type: Arriel 2D, LTS – 101 – 700D2, Arriel 1B, Arriel 2D\\r\\nMaximum operating altitude: 23,000 FT, 16,000 FT\\r\\nKey Features: Roomy cabin with wide windows offering best views, Dual control, Comfortable seats.\\r\\nOur helicopter outclasses all other helicopters for performance, versatility, safety and competitive acquisition and maintenance costs. It excels in hot conditions and very high altitudes. The features are easy take-off and land in small space and marginal weather conditions, these helicopters are simply the best in the industry and the safest way to enjoy Everest Base Camp mountain flights and all sorts of helicopter services.\\r\\n<h4>About Langtang</h4>\\r\\nThe Langtang region is a beautiful, ecologically diverse place in the central Himalayas. This region touches Tibet in the north and high hills to its south. This area consists of lush tropical forest, plain grasslands, small and high Passes, waterfalls, alpine forest and over it the beautiful Langtang and the peripheral Himalayas. Wildlife wise looking, Langtang is home to some of the rarest animals and birds of Asia. Red Panda, Snow Leopard, Black Bear, Himalayan Thar, Naur sheep, etc. are some of the protected species here. In the summer seasons, one can sight various species of migratory birds from Siberia and Mongolia regions heading here. Langtang NP is the area of Langtang protected by the government of Nepal, and one must take permits to enter here. Home to about 5,000 locals, mostly of Tamang ethnic group, one can have a twist of cultural experience here too. The area of Langtang is home to some of the holiest pilgrimage sites in Nepal. Gosainkunda Lake (also visible from the Langtang flight) is one of the prime pilgrim place and popular hiking option in this region. The area of Langtang, being near to epicenter of the 2015 earthquake in Nepal, suffered heavy loss. A massive avalanche took the life of more than 310 residents of the valley. One can still see the ruins around the valley of that great disaster.\\r\\n<h4>About Kyanjin Gompa</h4>\\r\\nThe Langtang valley is most famous for its natural location, culture and Buddhist monuments. As the Tamangs following Buddhism are abundant in these areas, Langtang is home to some of the majestic monasteries of Nepal. The KyanjinGompa (Monastery) lying in the heart of the valley is one of the oldest gompas in the region. It is a building of simple Tibetan inspired architecture and is home to beautiful murals and Thanga paintings. As the gompa suffered some heavy damage by the Earthquake in 2015, one has to enter the area with precaution. The devotion of the locals to the Gompa, however, makes it one of the most significant sites in the Langtang National Park region.\\r\\n<h4>Majestic Mountain views from the flight</h4>\\r\\nThe major attraction of the Langtang Helicopter flight is undoubtedly the sightings of some of the major ranges of the Himalayas. Mountain views of Nepal doesn't get better than what Langtang flight offers. In a brief time, you will experience the Himalayas like never before. This popular helicopter tour will take you close to beautiful mountains ofAnnapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma ( 8013 m), LangtangLirung (7246 m), Ganesh (7604 m), Gaurishanker (7145 m) with many other ranges. Once in the Langtang areas, you can also view the trails to Yala peak (5,500 m) and Naya Kanga. These are both perfect short hike options with a majestic view of the Himalayas.", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "Langtang Kyangjing Gompa Helicopter Tour", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "5. What to expect on tours?", "_ws_trip_fact_short_description": "field_63ec73a69d305", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "01", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "Single-Day Langtang heli tour", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "Extended Tours", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title": "Alternate Tours", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "The best viewing experience of the Himalayas is early after sunrise in clear weather. So, we will start the tour early in the morning. Our private vehicle or cab will pick you up from your hotel around 6:00 am. From the hotel, you will have about 30 minutes of drive to the domestic flight section of Tribhuwan International Airport (TIA). After 20-30 minutes of your arrival, your chopper will be ready, and you will board it timely. Taking off from the airport in about 7:00 am, you will fly over the valley and start to gain greater altitude. The pilot or your guide will narrate some of the significant mountains that fall alongside you. After a majestic flight over the hills and mountains, you will land in KyanjinGompa. As you will have around 20 minutes of ground time, you will take a quick breakfast/tea. Take some pictures as you soak in the beautiful scenes surrounding you. You can visit the KyanjinGompa, which was partially destroyed by the earthquake of 2015. Your return flight from this brief but worthy tour will take place after the pilots signal. You wil<a name=\\"_GoBack\\"></a>l head towards TIA and view some of the remaining mountains. After your arrival in TIA in about 9:30 am, we will drive you back to your hotel.", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630"}, "categoryId": null, "meta_title": "Langtang Helicopter Tour | Everest Vacation", "blogContent": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Langtang Kyangjing Gompa Helicopter Tour\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLangtang Helicopter tour is one of the pristine trips running in the Himalayas with magnificent views of the major ranges here, topped by a close view of the Mt.LangtangLirung (7,227m) and holy Kyanjin Gompa.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"3730 meters\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Views of Mt. Manaslu, Ganesh Himal, Langtang Himal range towards Jugal Himal including Dorji Lakpa from the air and on land at beautiful picturesque Langtang valley.\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\" Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"The \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLangtang Helicopter Tour\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e is a substitute for a 13-day trek to the Langtang region for those people who lack time to complete it. You will experience a whole lot of the important components of the Langtang from this brief Heli tour. Alongside the wonderful views, once you reach the Kyanjin Gompa, you will have a majestic sightseeing flight over the Himalayas. A brief time here will remain as the memories for eternity in Langtang.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nStarting from Kathmandu, the valley view is the starter for this amazing flight. Once in the air, you can witness the varied landscape of Nepal perfectly. From the plains of Terai and riverbeds to the green hills, the scene is pristine. Gradually rising from the hills to rocky and then snow-capped ones, you will experience them all. From the crowded cities to the villages in the hills to the Tamang settlements nearing Langtang, one will witness them all. The compact houses with stone-patched roofs will distinguish the Tamang settlements from others.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLanding on the Gompa, you will be welcomed with a cool breeze followed by a breathtaking peripheral view. You can meet some of the trekkers doing the surrounding hiking routes of Yala Peak and Naya Kanga. Both these are about two days long and require permits to do. The whole journey passes through some of the great, beautiful mountains. Langtang Lirung (7246 m), Annapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma/Gosainthan (8013 m), Makalu, Manaslu, \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaurishankar\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eGaurishankar\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e and many others. Leaving behind the plains these treasured Himalayas will give you some of the best memories of your life.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nHence, soar over the beautiful Himalayas, and with the daring Langtang on the doorsteps, explore the next step of adventure travel in Nepal. Experience Langtang in the luxury of a flight allowing you to glance Shangri-la on Earth. Discover and dwell the moment in the moments with the Langtang Helicopter Tour.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eMajor Highlights of Langtang \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/luxury-helicopter-tour-himalayas-nepal/\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFly over the Himalayas viewing the landscape diversity of Nepal live as you can have a view of Terai Plains, Green Hills, and Snow-capped Himalayas in a single flight.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eMajor mountain sightings like Annapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma ( 8013 m), Langtang Lirung (7246 m), Ganesh (7604 m), Gaurishankar (7145 m), and many other ranges.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eWitnessing the Himalayan art of living with the short flight over the stone-patched Tamang villages.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePicturesque view throughout the flight of the vegetation and landscapes of Langtang National Park.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAmazing view of the Langtang Valley and an organic tea treat your soul in your brief stay.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eKyanjin Gompa tour watching the murals and sculptures in this old Monastery\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRare but lucky spotting of the red panda and Himalayan birds.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eOutline Itinerary\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEarly morning pick up from the hotel\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransfer to the Domestic section of the TIA, Kathmandu\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTake off after 20-30 minutes of the arrival\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e30-35 minutes of scene packed flight to Langtang region.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLanding at Kyanjin Gompa, 20 minutes of ground time\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast at the lap of Langtang Lirung, Picture taking and strolling\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eReturn flight to TIA\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrive back to your hotel\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Aircrafts\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nModel: AS350b3e, AS350 FX II, AS350 FX II, AS350 BA , AS350 H125 ( Formally known as AS350 B3e)\\\\r\\\\nManufacturer: Air Bus, France\\\\r\\\\nEngine Type: Arriel 2D, LTS – 101 – 700D2, Arriel 1B, Arriel 2D\\\\r\\\\nMaximum operating altitude: 23,000 FT, 16,000 FT\\\\r\\\\nKey Features: Roomy cabin with wide windows offering best views, Dual control, Comfortable seats.\\\\r\\\\nOur helicopter outclasses all other helicopters for performance, versatility, safety and competitive acquisition and maintenance costs. It excels in hot conditions and very high altitudes. The features are easy take-off and land in small space and marginal weather conditions, these helicopters are simply the best in the industry and the safest way to enjoy Everest Base Camp mountain flights and all sorts of helicopter services.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Langtang\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nThe Langtang region is a beautiful, ecologically diverse place in the central Himalayas. This region touches Tibet in the north and high hills to its south. This area consists of lush tropical forest, plain grasslands, small and high Passes, waterfalls, alpine forest and over it the beautiful Langtang and the peripheral Himalayas. Wildlife wise looking, Langtang is home to some of the rarest animals and birds of Asia. Red Panda, Snow Leopard, Black Bear, Himalayan Thar, Naur sheep, etc. are some of the protected species here. In the summer seasons, one can sight various species of migratory birds from Siberia and Mongolia regions heading here. Langtang NP is the area of Langtang protected by the government of Nepal, and one must take permits to enter here. Home to about 5,000 locals, mostly of Tamang ethnic group, one can have a twist of cultural experience here too. The area of Langtang is home to some of the holiest pilgrimage sites in Nepal. Gosainkunda Lake (also visible from the Langtang flight) is one of the prime pilgrim place and popular hiking option in this region. The area of Langtang, being near to epicenter of the 2015 earthquake in Nepal, suffered heavy loss. A massive avalanche took the life of more than 310 residents of the valley. One can still see the ruins around the valley of that great disaster.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Kyanjin Gompa\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nThe Langtang valley is most famous for its natural location, culture and Buddhist monuments. As the Tamangs following Buddhism are abundant in these areas, Langtang is home to some of the majestic monasteries of Nepal. The KyanjinGompa (Monastery) lying in the heart of the valley is one of the oldest gompas in the region. It is a building of simple Tibetan inspired architecture and is home to beautiful murals and Thanga paintings. As the gompa suffered some heavy damage by the Earthquake in 2015, one has to enter the area with precaution. The devotion of the locals to the Gompa, however, makes it one of the most significant sites in the Langtang National Park region.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eMajestic Mountain views from the flight\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nThe major attraction of the Langtang Helicopter flight is undoubtedly the sightings of some of the major ranges of the Himalayas. Mountain views of Nepal doesn't get better than what Langtang flight offers. In a brief time, you will experience the Himalayas like never before. This popular helicopter tour will take you close to beautiful mountains ofAnnapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma ( 8013 m), LangtangLirung (7246 m), Ganesh (7604 m), Gaurishanker (7145 m) with many other ranges. Once in the Langtang areas, you can also view the trails to Yala peak (5,500 m) and Naya Kanga. These are both perfect short hike options with a majestic view of the Himalayas.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"819\\",\\"821\\",\\"822\\",\\"824\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Single-Day Langtang heli tour\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"The best viewing experience of the Himalayas is early after sunrise in clear weather. So, we will start the tour early in the morning. Our private vehicle or cab will pick you up from your hotel around 6:00 am. From the hotel, you will have about 30 minutes of drive to the domestic flight section of Tribhuwan International Airport (TIA). After 20-30 minutes of your arrival, your chopper will be ready, and you will board it timely. Taking off from the airport in about 7:00 am, you will fly over the valley and start to gain greater altitude. The pilot or your guide will narrate some of the significant mountains that fall alongside you. After a majestic flight over the hills and mountains, you will land in KyanjinGompa. As you will have around 20 minutes of ground time, you will take a quick breakfast/tea. Take some pictures as you soak in the beautiful scenes surrounding you. You can visit the KyanjinGompa, which was partially destroyed by the earthquake of 2015. Your return flight from this brief but worthy tour will take place after the pilots signal. You wil\\\\u003ca name=\\\\u0022_GoBack\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003el head towards TIA and view some of the remaining mountains. After your arrival in TIA in about 9:30 am, we will drive you back to your hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":1,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eCar/van transportation to and from the domestic airport and hotel in Kathmandu.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEscorting guide for this Langtang heli flight.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate helicopter for 1.5 hours.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour - 2 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Langtang Kyangjing Gompa Helicopter Tour\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLangtang Helicopter tour is one of the pristine trips running in the Himalayas with magnificent views of the major ranges here, topped by a close view of the Mt.LangtangLirung (7,227m) and holy Kyanjin Gompa.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"3730 meters\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Views of Mt. Manaslu, Ganesh Himal, Langtang Himal range towards Jugal Himal including Dorji Lakpa from the air and on land at beautiful picturesque Langtang valley.\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\" Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"The \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLangtang Helicopter Tour\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e is a substitute for a 13-day trek to the Langtang region for those people who lack time to complete it. You will experience a whole lot of the important components of the Langtang from this brief Heli tour. Alongside the wonderful views, once you reach the Kyanjin Gompa, you will have a majestic sightseeing flight over the Himalayas. A brief time here will remain as the memories for eternity in Langtang.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nStarting from Kathmandu, the valley view is the starter for this amazing flight. Once in the air, you can witness the varied landscape of Nepal perfectly. From the plains of Terai and riverbeds to the green hills, the scene is pristine. Gradually rising from the hills to rocky and then snow-capped ones, you will experience them all. From the crowded cities to the villages in the hills to the Tamang settlements nearing Langtang, one will witness them all. The compact houses with stone-patched roofs will distinguish the Tamang settlements from others.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nLanding on the Gompa, you will be welcomed with a cool breeze followed by a breathtaking peripheral view. You can meet some of the trekkers doing the surrounding hiking routes of Yala Peak and Naya Kanga. Both these are about two days long and require permits to do. The whole journey passes through some of the great, beautiful mountains. Langtang Lirung (7246 m), Annapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma/Gosainthan (8013 m), Makalu, Manaslu, \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaurishankar\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eGaurishankar\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e and many others. Leaving behind the plains these treasured Himalayas will give you some of the best memories of your life.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nHence, soar over the beautiful Himalayas, and with the daring Langtang on the doorsteps, explore the next step of adventure travel in Nepal. Experience Langtang in the luxury of a flight allowing you to glance Shangri-la on Earth. Discover and dwell the moment in the moments with the Langtang Helicopter Tour.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eMajor Highlights of Langtang \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/luxury-helicopter-tour-himalayas-nepal/\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFly over the Himalayas viewing the landscape diversity of Nepal live as you can have a view of Terai Plains, Green Hills, and Snow-capped Himalayas in a single flight.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eMajor mountain sightings like Annapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma ( 8013 m), Langtang Lirung (7246 m), Ganesh (7604 m), Gaurishankar (7145 m), and many other ranges.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eWitnessing the Himalayan art of living with the short flight over the stone-patched Tamang villages.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePicturesque view throughout the flight of the vegetation and landscapes of Langtang National Park.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAmazing view of the Langtang Valley and an organic tea treat your soul in your brief stay.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eKyanjin Gompa tour watching the murals and sculptures in this old Monastery\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRare but lucky spotting of the red panda and Himalayan birds.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eOutline Itinerary\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEarly morning pick up from the hotel\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransfer to the Domestic section of the TIA, Kathmandu\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTake off after 20-30 minutes of the arrival\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e30-35 minutes of scene packed flight to Langtang region.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLanding at Kyanjin Gompa, 20 minutes of ground time\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast at the lap of Langtang Lirung, Picture taking and strolling\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eReturn flight to TIA\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrive back to your hotel\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Aircrafts\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nModel: AS350b3e, AS350 FX II, AS350 FX II, AS350 BA , AS350 H125 ( Formally known as AS350 B3e)\\\\r\\\\nManufacturer: Air Bus, France\\\\r\\\\nEngine Type: Arriel 2D, LTS – 101 – 700D2, Arriel 1B, Arriel 2D\\\\r\\\\nMaximum operating altitude: 23,000 FT, 16,000 FT\\\\r\\\\nKey Features: Roomy cabin with wide windows offering best views, Dual control, Comfortable seats.\\\\r\\\\nOur helicopter outclasses all other helicopters for performance, versatility, safety and competitive acquisition and maintenance costs. It excels in hot conditions and very high altitudes. The features are easy take-off and land in small space and marginal weather conditions, these helicopters are simply the best in the industry and the safest way to enjoy Everest Base Camp mountain flights and all sorts of helicopter services.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Langtang\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nThe Langtang region is a beautiful, ecologically diverse place in the central Himalayas. This region touches Tibet in the north and high hills to its south. This area consists of lush tropical forest, plain grasslands, small and high Passes, waterfalls, alpine forest and over it the beautiful Langtang and the peripheral Himalayas. Wildlife wise looking, Langtang is home to some of the rarest animals and birds of Asia. Red Panda, Snow Leopard, Black Bear, Himalayan Thar, Naur sheep, etc. are some of the protected species here. In the summer seasons, one can sight various species of migratory birds from Siberia and Mongolia regions heading here. Langtang NP is the area of Langtang protected by the government of Nepal, and one must take permits to enter here. Home to about 5,000 locals, mostly of Tamang ethnic group, one can have a twist of cultural experience here too. The area of Langtang is home to some of the holiest pilgrimage sites in Nepal. Gosainkunda Lake (also visible from the Langtang flight) is one of the prime pilgrim place and popular hiking option in this region. The area of Langtang, being near to epicenter of the 2015 earthquake in Nepal, suffered heavy loss. A massive avalanche took the life of more than 310 residents of the valley. One can still see the ruins around the valley of that great disaster.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eAbout Kyanjin Gompa\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nThe Langtang valley is most famous for its natural location, culture and Buddhist monuments. As the Tamangs following Buddhism are abundant in these areas, Langtang is home to some of the majestic monasteries of Nepal. The KyanjinGompa (Monastery) lying in the heart of the valley is one of the oldest gompas in the region. It is a building of simple Tibetan inspired architecture and is home to beautiful murals and Thanga paintings. As the gompa suffered some heavy damage by the Earthquake in 2015, one has to enter the area with precaution. The devotion of the locals to the Gompa, however, makes it one of the most significant sites in the Langtang National Park region.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003eMajestic Mountain views from the flight\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nThe major attraction of the Langtang Helicopter flight is undoubtedly the sightings of some of the major ranges of the Himalayas. Mountain views of Nepal doesn't get better than what Langtang flight offers. In a brief time, you will experience the Himalayas like never before. This popular helicopter tour will take you close to beautiful mountains ofAnnapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma ( 8013 m), LangtangLirung (7246 m), Ganesh (7604 m), Gaurishanker (7145 m) with many other ranges. Once in the Langtang areas, you can also view the trails to Yala peak (5,500 m) and Naya Kanga. These are both perfect short hike options with a majestic view of the Himalayas.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"819\\",\\"821\\",\\"822\\",\\"824\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Single-Day Langtang heli tour\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"The best viewing experience of the Himalayas is early after sunrise in clear weather. So, we will start the tour early in the morning. Our private vehicle or cab will pick you up from your hotel around 6:00 am. From the hotel, you will have about 30 minutes of drive to the domestic flight section of Tribhuwan International Airport (TIA). After 20-30 minutes of your arrival, your chopper will be ready, and you will board it timely. Taking off from the airport in about 7:00 am, you will fly over the valley and start to gain greater altitude. The pilot or your guide will narrate some of the significant mountains that fall alongside you. After a majestic flight over the hills and mountains, you will land in KyanjinGompa. As you will have around 20 minutes of ground time, you will take a quick breakfast/tea. Take some pictures as you soak in the beautiful scenes surrounding you. You can visit the KyanjinGompa, which was partially destroyed by the earthquake of 2015. Your return flight from this brief but worthy tour will take place after the pilots signal. You wil\\\\u003ca name=\\\\u0022_GoBack\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003el head towards TIA and view some of the remaining mountains. After your arrival in TIA in about 9:30 am, we will drive you back to your hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":1,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eCar/van transportation to and from the domestic airport and hotel in Kathmandu.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEscorting guide for this Langtang heli flight.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate helicopter for 1.5 hours.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour - 2 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/langtang-helicopter-tour-1.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/langtang-kyanjing-gompa-heli-tour.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/helicopter-tour-from-kathmandu.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/langtang-helicopter.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=818", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "818", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-04 08:20:29", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-04 08:20:29", "post_modified": "2024-02-02 09:19:12", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-02-02 09:19:12"}}, "customSections": [{"id": 1, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Extended Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour - 2 days</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": 2, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Alternate Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["The <strong>Langtang Helicopter Tour</strong> is a substitute for a 13-day trek to the Langtang region for those people who lack time to complete it. You will experience a whole lot of the important components of the Langtang from this brief Heli tour. Alongside the wonderful views, once you reach the Kyanjin Gompa, you will have a majestic sightseeing flight over the Himalayas. A brief time here will remain as the memories for eternity in Langtang.\\r\\n\\r\\nStarting from Kathmandu, the valley view is the starter for this amazing flight. Once in the air, you can witness the varied landscape of Nepal perfectly. From the plains of Terai and riverbeds to the green hills, the scene is pristine. Gradually rising from the hills to rocky and then snow-capped ones, you will experience them all. From the crowded cities to the villages in the hills to the Tamang settlements nearing Langtang, one will witness them all. The compact houses with stone-patched roofs will distinguish the Tamang settlements from others.\\r\\n\\r\\nLanding on the Gompa, you will be welcomed with a cool breeze followed by a breathtaking peripheral view. You can meet some of the trekkers doing the surrounding hiking routes of Yala Peak and Naya Kanga. Both these are about two days long and require permits to do. The whole journey passes through some of the great, beautiful mountains. Langtang Lirung (7246 m), Annapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma/Gosainthan (8013 m), Makalu, Manaslu, <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaurishankar\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Gaurishankar</a> and many others. Leaving behind the plains these treasured Himalayas will give you some of the best memories of your life.\\r\\n\\r\\nHence, soar over the beautiful Himalayas, and with the daring Langtang on the doorsteps, explore the next step of adventure travel in Nepal. Experience Langtang in the luxury of a flight allowing you to glance Shangri-la on Earth. Discover and dwell the moment in the moments with the Langtang Helicopter Tour.\\r\\n<h3>Major Highlights of Langtang <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/luxury-helicopter-tour-himalayas-nepal/\\">Helicopter Tour</a></h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fly over the Himalayas viewing the landscape diversity of Nepal live as you can have a view of Terai Plains, Green Hills, and Snow-capped Himalayas in a single flight.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Major mountain sightings like Annapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma ( 8013 m), Langtang Lirung (7246 m), Ganesh (7604 m), Gaurishankar (7145 m), and many other ranges.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Witnessing the Himalayan art of living with the short flight over the stone-patched Tamang villages.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Picturesque view throughout the flight of the vegetation and landscapes of Langtang National Park.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Amazing view of the Langtang Valley and an organic tea treat your soul in your brief stay.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kyanjin Gompa tour watching the murals and sculptures in this old Monastery</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Rare but lucky spotting of the red panda and Himalayan birds.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Outline Itinerary</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Early morning pick up from the hotel</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transfer to the Domestic section of the TIA, Kathmandu</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Take off after 20-30 minutes of the arrival</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>30-35 minutes of scene packed flight to Langtang region.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Landing at Kyanjin Gompa, 20 minutes of ground time</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Breakfast at the lap of Langtang Lirung, Picture taking and strolling</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Return flight to TIA</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive back to your hotel</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>About Aircrafts</h4>\\r\\nModel: AS350b3e, AS350 FX II, AS350 FX II, AS350 BA , AS350 H125 ( Formally known as AS350 B3e)\\r\\nManufacturer: Air Bus, France\\r\\nEngine Type: Arriel 2D, LTS – 101 – 700D2, Arriel 1B, Arriel 2D\\r\\nMaximum operating altitude: 23,000 FT, 16,000 FT\\r\\nKey Features: Roomy cabin with wide windows offering best views, Dual control, Comfortable seats.\\r\\nOur helicopter outclasses all other helicopters for performance, versatility, safety and competitive acquisition and maintenance costs. It excels in hot conditions and very high altitudes. The features are easy take-off and land in small space and marginal weather conditions, these helicopters are simply the best in the industry and the safest way to enjoy Everest Base Camp mountain flights and all sorts of helicopter services.\\r\\n<h4>About Langtang</h4>\\r\\nThe Langtang region is a beautiful, ecologically diverse place in the central Himalayas. This region touches Tibet in the north and high hills to its south. This area consists of lush tropical forest, plain grasslands, small and high Passes, waterfalls, alpine forest and over it the beautiful Langtang and the peripheral Himalayas. Wildlife wise looking, Langtang is home to some of the rarest animals and birds of Asia. Red Panda, Snow Leopard, Black Bear, Himalayan Thar, Naur sheep, etc. are some of the protected species here. In the summer seasons, one can sight various species of migratory birds from Siberia and Mongolia regions heading here. Langtang NP is the area of Langtang protected by the government of Nepal, and one must take permits to enter here. Home to about 5,000 locals, mostly of Tamang ethnic group, one can have a twist of cultural experience here too. The area of Langtang is home to some of the holiest pilgrimage sites in Nepal. Gosainkunda Lake (also visible from the Langtang flight) is one of the prime pilgrim place and popular hiking option in this region. The area of Langtang, being near to epicenter of the 2015 earthquake in Nepal, suffered heavy loss. A massive avalanche took the life of more than 310 residents of the valley. One can still see the ruins around the valley of that great disaster.\\r\\n<h4>About Kyanjin Gompa</h4>\\r\\nThe Langtang valley is most famous for its natural location, culture and Buddhist monuments. As the Tamangs following Buddhism are abundant in these areas, Langtang is home to some of the majestic monasteries of Nepal. The KyanjinGompa (Monastery) lying in the heart of the valley is one of the oldest gompas in the region. It is a building of simple Tibetan inspired architecture and is home to beautiful murals and Thanga paintings. As the gompa suffered some heavy damage by the Earthquake in 2015, one has to enter the area with precaution. The devotion of the locals to the Gompa, however, makes it one of the most significant sites in the Langtang National Park region.\\r\\n<h4>Majestic Mountain views from the flight</h4>\\r\\nThe major attraction of the Langtang Helicopter flight is undoubtedly the sightings of some of the major ranges of the Himalayas. Mountain views of Nepal doesn't get better than what Langtang flight offers. In a brief time, you will experience the Himalayas like never before. This popular helicopter tour will take you close to beautiful mountains ofAnnapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma ( 8013 m), LangtangLirung (7246 m), Ganesh (7604 m), Gaurishanker (7145 m) with many other ranges. Once in the Langtang areas, you can also view the trails to Yala peak (5,500 m) and Naya Kanga. These are both perfect short hike options with a majestic view of the Himalayas."], "description": "The <strong>Langtang Helicopter Tour</strong> is a substitute for a 13-day trek to the Langtang region for those people who lack time to complete it. You will experience a whole lot of the important components of the Langtang from this brief Heli tour. Alongside the wonderful views, once you reach the Kyanjin Gompa, you will have a majestic sightseeing flight over the Himalayas. A brief time here will remain as the memories for eternity in Langtang.\\r\\n\\r\\nStarting from Kathmandu, the valley view is the starter for this amazing flight. Once in the air, you can witness the varied landscape of Nepal perfectly. From the plains of Terai and riverbeds to the green hills, the scene is pristine. Gradually rising from the hills to rocky and then snow-capped ones, you will experience them all. From the crowded cities to the villages in the hills to the Tamang settlements nearing Langtang, one will witness them all. The compact houses with stone-patched roofs will distinguish the Tamang settlements from others.\\r\\n\\r\\nLanding on the Gompa, you will be welcomed with a cool breeze followed by a breathtaking peripheral view. You can meet some of the trekkers doing the surrounding hiking routes of Yala Peak and Naya Kanga. Both these are about two days long and require permits to do. The whole journey passes through some of the great, beautiful mountains. Langtang Lirung (7246 m), Annapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma/Gosainthan (8013 m), Makalu, Manaslu, <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaurishankar\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Gaurishankar</a> and many others. Leaving behind the plains these treasured Himalayas will give you some of the best memories of your life.\\r\\n\\r\\nHence, soar over the beautiful Himalayas, and with the daring Langtang on the doorsteps, explore the next step of adventure travel in Nepal. Experience Langtang in the luxury of a flight allowing you to glance Shangri-la on Earth. Discover and dwell the moment in the moments with the Langtang Helicopter Tour.\\r\\n<h3>Major Highlights of Langtang <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/luxury-helicopter-tour-himalayas-nepal/\\">Helicopter Tour</a></h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fly over the Himalayas viewing the landscape diversity of Nepal live as you can have a view of Terai Plains, Green Hills, and Snow-capped Himalayas in a single flight.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Major mountain sightings like Annapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma ( 8013 m), Langtang Lirung (7246 m), Ganesh (7604 m), Gaurishankar (7145 m), and many other ranges.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Witnessing the Himalayan art of living with the short flight over the stone-patched Tamang villages.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Picturesque view throughout the flight of the vegetation and landscapes of Langtang National Park.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Amazing view of the Langtang Valley and an organic tea treat your soul in your brief stay.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kyanjin Gompa tour watching the murals and sculptures in this old Monastery</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Rare but lucky spotting of the red panda and Himalayan birds.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Outline Itinerary</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Early morning pick up from the hotel</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transfer to the Domestic section of the TIA, Kathmandu</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Take off after 20-30 minutes of the arrival</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>30-35 minutes of scene packed flight to Langtang region.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Landing at Kyanjin Gompa, 20 minutes of ground time</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Breakfast at the lap of Langtang Lirung, Picture taking and strolling</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Return flight to TIA</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive back to your hotel</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>About Aircrafts</h4>\\r\\nModel: AS350b3e, AS350 FX II, AS350 FX II, AS350 BA , AS350 H125 ( Formally known as AS350 B3e)\\r\\nManufacturer: Air Bus, France\\r\\nEngine Type: Arriel 2D, LTS – 101 – 700D2, Arriel 1B, Arriel 2D\\r\\nMaximum operating altitude: 23,000 FT, 16,000 FT\\r\\nKey Features: Roomy cabin with wide windows offering best views, Dual control, Comfortable seats.\\r\\nOur helicopter outclasses all other helicopters for performance, versatility, safety and competitive acquisition and maintenance costs. It excels in hot conditions and very high altitudes. The features are easy take-off and land in small space and marginal weather conditions, these helicopters are simply the best in the industry and the safest way to enjoy Everest Base Camp mountain flights and all sorts of helicopter services.\\r\\n<h4>About Langtang</h4>\\r\\nThe Langtang region is a beautiful, ecologically diverse place in the central Himalayas. This region touches Tibet in the north and high hills to its south. This area consists of lush tropical forest, plain grasslands, small and high Passes, waterfalls, alpine forest and over it the beautiful Langtang and the peripheral Himalayas. Wildlife wise looking, Langtang is home to some of the rarest animals and birds of Asia. Red Panda, Snow Leopard, Black Bear, Himalayan Thar, Naur sheep, etc. are some of the protected species here. In the summer seasons, one can sight various species of migratory birds from Siberia and Mongolia regions heading here. Langtang NP is the area of Langtang protected by the government of Nepal, and one must take permits to enter here. Home to about 5,000 locals, mostly of Tamang ethnic group, one can have a twist of cultural experience here too. The area of Langtang is home to some of the holiest pilgrimage sites in Nepal. Gosainkunda Lake (also visible from the Langtang flight) is one of the prime pilgrim place and popular hiking option in this region. The area of Langtang, being near to epicenter of the 2015 earthquake in Nepal, suffered heavy loss. A massive avalanche took the life of more than 310 residents of the valley. One can still see the ruins around the valley of that great disaster.\\r\\n<h4>About Kyanjin Gompa</h4>\\r\\nThe Langtang valley is most famous for its natural location, culture and Buddhist monuments. As the Tamangs following Buddhism are abundant in these areas, Langtang is home to some of the majestic monasteries of Nepal. The KyanjinGompa (Monastery) lying in the heart of the valley is one of the oldest gompas in the region. It is a building of simple Tibetan inspired architecture and is home to beautiful murals and Thanga paintings. As the gompa suffered some heavy damage by the Earthquake in 2015, one has to enter the area with precaution. The devotion of the locals to the Gompa, however, makes it one of the most significant sites in the Langtang National Park region.\\r\\n<h4>Majestic Mountain views from the flight</h4>\\r\\nThe major attraction of the Langtang Helicopter flight is undoubtedly the sightings of some of the major ranges of the Himalayas. Mountain views of Nepal doesn't get better than what Langtang flight offers. In a brief time, you will experience the Himalayas like never before. This popular helicopter tour will take you close to beautiful mountains ofAnnapurna I (8091 m), Shishapangma ( 8013 m), LangtangLirung (7246 m), Ganesh (7604 m), Gaurishanker (7145 m) with many other ranges. Once in the Langtang areas, you can also view the trails to Yala peak (5,500 m) and Naya Kanga. These are both perfect short hike options with a majestic view of the Himalayas."}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Car/van transportation to and from the domestic airport and hotel in Kathmandu.", "Escorting guide for this Langtang heli flight.", "Private helicopter for 1.5 hours."], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Car/van transportation to and from the domestic airport and hotel in Kathmandu.", "Escorting guide for this Langtang heli flight.", "Private helicopter for 1.5 hours."], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "Explore Langtang Helicopter Tour with Everest Vacation.", "trip_highlights": "<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nLangtang Helicopter tour is one of the pristine trips running in the Himalayas with magnificent views of the major ranges here, topped by a close view of the Mt.LangtangLirung (7,227m) and holy Kyanjin Gompa.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>", "trip_type_level": "Easy", "meta_description": "Langtang Helicopter Tour mesmerizes travelers with phenomenal views of Langtang Valley, scenic landscapes, and Langtang Mountain ranges.", "trip_attractions": "Views of Mt. Manaslu, Ganesh Himal, Langtang Himal range towards Jugal Himal including Dorji Lakpa from the air and on land at beautiful picturesque Langtang valley.", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "faq_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "Views of Mt. Manaslu, Ganesh Himal, Langtang Himal range towards Jugal Himal including Dorji Lakpa from the air and on land at beautiful picturesque Langtang valley.", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "3730 meters", "transportation": ""}, "trip_max_elevation": "3730 meters", "trip_highlights_title": "Langtang Kyangjing Gompa Helicopter Tour"}	2023-12-04 08:20:29+00	2024-02-02 09:19:12+00
177	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "Kathmandu Durbar Square, Pashupatinath Temple, Boudhanath Stupa, Swoyambhu / Monkey Temple", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "1", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour"}, "faq": [{"answer": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "question": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "question": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "question": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "question": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "question": "5. What to expect on tours?"}], "meta": {"_edit_last": "1", "_edit_lock": "1769224723:6", "_dp_original": "538", "_thumbnail_id": "4821", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "Kathmandu Durbar Square, Pashupatinath Temple, Boudhanath Stupa, Swoyambhu / Monkey Temple", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "1", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "1 Day Kathmandu Sightseeing Tour", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "1 Day Kathmandu Sightseeing Tour", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "47", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Explore the fascinating historical and cultural landmarks listed as UNESCO World Heritage Sites in 1 Day Kathmandu Sightseeing Tour.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour", "tags": [], "title": "1 Day Kathmandu Sightseeing Tour", "duration": "1 Day", "overview": {"title": "Kathmandu Nepal tour with 4 World Heritage Sites by UNESCO", "description": "<h2>Single-Day Kathmandu Nepal City Tour</h2>\\r\\n<strong>Here are the details of any option from above. If you need details for other options, we will send you.</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nEverest Vacation City and cultural guide will pick you up from your respective hotel in the valley for an exciting tour of <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathmandu\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu</a> Valley. Starting at the heart of the valley, the <strong>Kathmandu Durbar Square</strong> is the foremost destination for you today. This place is steeped in old history and rich Nepali culture from the 16th century till now. The former royal palace from where the Malla kings ruled over Kathmandu, is also renowned as the Hanuman Dhoka (palace). Once here there are many dazzling monuments you won’t like to miss.\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit the majestic Kastamandap Temple (the name of this city is derived from the word ‘Kasthamandap’), a temple built from woods coming from a single tree. Then you will have an opportunity to visit the temple of the<strong> Kumari Goddess (the only living goddess in Nepal)</strong>. Kumaris selected here are of tender child age and are considered and worshipped in the form of Divine power. After her puberty phase, the next kumari is selected. Visit the famous freak street, a popular place of budget tourist shopping, and the hippie’s meetup point before Thamel overshadowed it.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter a lively and exciting tour a short drive towards the west of the city to reach your next destination in the form of <strong>Swoyambhunath Stupa</strong>. It is located on a hilltop, with fabulous Panoramic views of Kathmandu city and green hills surrounding it. Further north from the hill in clear weather, you can view high snow-capped mountains.\\r\\n\\r\\nOne of the oldest historical sites in the UNESCO World Heritage sites from Nepal, Swoyambhunath ages back more than 2, 5000 years. The stupa complex consists of old Buddhist religious monuments topped with a colossal dome-shaped stupa. With four mystical eyes of Buddha overlooking four directions in the dome, you will have a sacred feeling of fulfillment in this place. This place is surrounded by green forest with many monkeys dwelling around this place. Hence the temple is also known as “Monkey Temple.”\\r\\n\\r\\nOur next destination lies a short distance towards the east of Kathmandu city. <strong>Pashupatinath Temple</strong> area is one of the most sacred places for Hindu Pilgrims around the world. Non-Hindu tourists are not allowed inside the main temple. However one can visit the surrounding shrines and also view the temple from a nearby spot. The Pashupatinath Temple lies on the banks of the Holy Bagmati River. The main temple has a golden pagoda-tier roof and four silver doors.\\r\\n\\r\\nSurrounded by lovely forests and lush vegetation, Pashupatinath is an important Pilgrimage for Hindu devotees. This place packs with domestic and international pilgrims in mid-February on Shiva Ratri (birth anniversary of Lord Shiva). On the opposite side of the Pashupatinath and bank of the Bagmati river, funeral and cremation take place according to the Hindu religion. A heart-touching site but a vital experience about the way of life.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen drive towards the northeast reaching <strong>Bouddhanath Stupa</strong>. Also famous as the “Little <a href=\\"https://asiaexperiences.com/tibet/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Tibet</a>” of Nepal due to the strong Tibetan influence here in culture, traditions, and religion. Bouddhanath is a vast white dome with a low tier from where one can walk up near the top. With lovely views of the culture and Buddhist Tradition, you will have a peaceful time. Surrounding the Bouddhanath area are Souvenir shops, stores, restaurants, and monasteries. You can experience nightlife in Boudhanath with Tibetan tea in the evening.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter this fascinating tour of lovely historical and cultural influence from your destination, return to your respective hotels.\\r\\n<h3>Distances of each other monuments- Kathmandu best place to see:</h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kathmandu Durbar square (Hanuman Dhaka) to Swoyambhu Stupa (Swoyambhunath Maha Chaitya / Monkey Temple) distance: 3.3 KM with 15 15-minute drive approximately.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Swoyambhu to Pashupati Temple distance: 8 km with a 30-minute drive.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pashupatinath Temple to  Boudhanath Stupa distance: 2 km with 10 10-minute drive approximately.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n&nbsp;\\r\\n<div class=\\"rll-youtube-player\\" data-src=\\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/GG5pCr9ghCI\\" data-id=\\"GG5pCr9ghCI\\" data-query=\\"feature=oembed\\"></div>"}, "taxonomy": {}, "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/boudhanath-stupa-1.jpg", "title": "boudhanath-stupa-1", "altText": "boudhanath-stupa", "caption": "boudhanath-stupa", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["4314", "4332", "4315", "4330", "4249", "4041", "3997", "3971", "3944", "3943", "3936", "3933", "3921", "4297"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "ws_trip_faqs_lists": 5, "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists": "field_63ede38e351c7", "ws_block_attractions": "Boudha Stupa, Pashpati Temple, Swoyambhu (Monkey Temple) & Basantapur Durbar Square (Hanuman Dhoka)", "ws_block_best_season": "Any Season", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-white", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "", "ws_block_vi