ith us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "Extended Tours", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</a> - 4-5 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area</a> - 1 hour</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu</a> - 4-6 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour</a> - 2 days</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour</a> - 4 days</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630"}, "categoryId": null, "meta_title": "1 Day Kathmandu Sightseeing Tour", "blogContent": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Embark on a delightful single-day tour of Kathmandu and explore the fascinating historical and cultural landmarks listed as UNESCO World Heritage Sites. Immerse yourself in the rich history, vibrant culture, diverse religion, delectable Nepalese cuisine, and local lifestyle, all with the guidance of our expert travel guides from Nepal.\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eKathmandu Durbar Square, Swoyambhu/Monkey Temple, Pashupatinath Temple, and Boudhanath Stupa in 1-day sightseeing.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePatan durbar Square, Pashupatinath and Swoyambhu/Monkey Temple in 1 day tour.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBhaktapur Durbar Square, Changunarayan and Pashupatinath Temple in a single day.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e Chandragiri Hills with a cable car ride, Swoyambhu/Monkey Temple, Hanuman Dhoka in one day. (\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/one-day-kathmandu-tour-with-chandragiri-hills/\\\\u0022\\\\u003eChandragiri Hills with cable car\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eOr, choose your preferred places to see and let us know, and we will operate your choices. You may add an Everest mountain flight or helicopter flight to Everest on the same day.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Boudha Stupa, Pashpati Temple, Swoyambhu (Monkey Temple) \\\\u0026 Basantapur Durbar Square (Hanuman Dhoka)\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Kathmandu Nepal tour with 4 World Heritage Sites by UNESCO\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003ch2\\\\u003eSingle-Day Kathmandu Nepal City Tour\\\\u003c/h2\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHere are the details of any option from above. If you need details for other options, we will send you.\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nEverest Vacation City and cultural guide will pick you up from your respective hotel in the valley for an exciting tour of \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathmandu\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e Valley. Starting at the heart of the valley, the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKathmandu Durbar Square\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e is the foremost destination for you today. This place is steeped in old history and rich Nepali culture from the 16th century till now. The former royal palace from where the Malla kings ruled over Kathmandu, is also renowned as the Hanuman Dhoka (palace). Once here there are many dazzling monuments you won’t like to miss.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nVisit the majestic Kastamandap Temple (the name of this city is derived from the word ‘Kasthamandap’), a temple built from woods coming from a single tree. Then you will have an opportunity to visit the temple of the\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Kumari Goddess (the only living goddess in Nepal)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. Kumaris selected here are of tender child age and are considered and worshipped in the form of Divine power. After her puberty phase, the next kumari is selected. Visit the famous freak street, a popular place of budget tourist shopping, and the hippie’s meetup point before Thamel overshadowed it.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter a lively and exciting tour a short drive towards the west of the city to reach your next destination in the form of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSwoyambhunath Stupa\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. It is located on a hilltop, with fabulous Panoramic views of Kathmandu city and green hills surrounding it. Further north from the hill in clear weather, you can view high snow-capped mountains.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOne of the oldest historical sites in the UNESCO World Heritage sites from Nepal, Swoyambhunath ages back more than 2, 5000 years. The stupa complex consists of old Buddhist religious monuments topped with a colossal dome-shaped stupa. With four mystical eyes of Buddha overlooking four directions in the dome, you will have a sacred feeling of fulfillment in this place. This place is surrounded by green forest with many monkeys dwelling around this place. Hence the temple is also known as “Monkey Temple.”\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOur next destination lies a short distance towards the east of Kathmandu city. \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePashupatinath Temple\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e area is one of the most sacred places for Hindu Pilgrims around the world. Non-Hindu tourists are not allowed inside the main temple. However one can visit the surrounding shrines and also view the temple from a nearby spot. The Pashupatinath Temple lies on the banks of the Holy Bagmati River. The main temple has a golden pagoda-tier roof and four silver doors.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nSurrounded by lovely forests and lush vegetation, Pashupatinath is an important Pilgrimage for Hindu devotees. This place packs with domestic and international pilgrims in mid-February on Shiva Ratri (birth anniversary of Lord Shiva). On the opposite side of the Pashupatinath and bank of the Bagmati river, funeral and cremation take place according to the Hindu religion. A heart-touching site but a vital experience about the way of life.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThen drive towards the northeast reaching \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBouddhanath Stupa\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. Also famous as the “Little \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://asiaexperiences.com/tibet/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eTibet\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e” of Nepal due to the strong Tibetan influence here in culture, traditions, and religion. Bouddhanath is a vast white dome with a low tier from where one can walk up near the top. With lovely views of the culture and Buddhist Tradition, you will have a peaceful time. Surrounding the Bouddhanath area are Souvenir shops, stores, restaurants, and monasteries. You can experience nightlife in Boudhanath with Tibetan tea in the evening.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter this fascinating tour of lovely historical and cultural influence from your destination, return to your respective hotels.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eDistances of each other monuments- Kathmandu best place to see:\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eKathmandu Durbar square (Hanuman Dhaka) to Swoyambhu Stupa (Swoyambhunath Maha Chaitya / Monkey Temple) distance: 3.3 KM with 15 15-minute drive approximately.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSwoyambhu to Pashupati Temple distance: 8 km with a 30-minute drive.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePashupatinath Temple to  Boudhanath Stupa distance: 2 km with 10 10-minute drive approximately.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u0026nbsp;\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022rll-youtube-player\\\\u0022 data-src=\\\\u0022https://www.youtube.com/embed/GG5pCr9ghCI\\\\u0022 data-id=\\\\u0022GG5pCr9ghCI\\\\u0022 data-query=\\\\u0022feature=oembed\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFully private trip \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVehicle fuel, vehicle tax.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking cultural city tour guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrinking Water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4314\\",\\"4332\\",\\"4315\\",\\"4330\\",\\"4249\\",\\"4041\\",\\"3997\\",\\"3971\\",\\"3944\\",\\"3943\\",\\"3936\\",\\"3933\\",\\"3921\\",\\"4297\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 1 hour\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 2 days\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4 days\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":1,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Embark on a delightful single-day tour of Kathmandu and explore the fascinating historical and cultural landmarks listed as UNESCO World Heritage Sites. Immerse yourself in the rich history, vibrant culture, diverse religion, delectable Nepalese cuisine, and local lifestyle, all with the guidance of our expert travel guides from Nepal.\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eKathmandu Durbar Square, Swoyambhu/Monkey Temple, Pashupatinath Temple, and Boudhanath Stupa in 1-day sightseeing.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePatan durbar Square, Pashupatinath and Swoyambhu/Monkey Temple in 1 day tour.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBhaktapur Durbar Square, Changunarayan and Pashupatinath Temple in a single day.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e Chandragiri Hills with a cable car ride, Swoyambhu/Monkey Temple, Hanuman Dhoka in one day. (\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/one-day-kathmandu-tour-with-chandragiri-hills/\\\\u0022\\\\u003eChandragiri Hills with cable car\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eOr, choose your preferred places to see and let us know, and we will operate your choices. You may add an Everest mountain flight or helicopter flight to Everest on the same day.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Boudha Stupa, Pashpati Temple, Swoyambhu (Monkey Temple) \\\\u0026 Basantapur Durbar Square (Hanuman Dhoka)\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Kathmandu Nepal tour with 4 World Heritage Sites by UNESCO\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003ch2\\\\u003eSingle-Day Kathmandu Nepal City Tour\\\\u003c/h2\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHere are the details of any option from above. If you need details for other options, we will send you.\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nEverest Vacation City and cultural guide will pick you up from your respective hotel in the valley for an exciting tour of \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathmandu\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e Valley. Starting at the heart of the valley, the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKathmandu Durbar Square\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e is the foremost destination for you today. This place is steeped in old history and rich Nepali culture from the 16th century till now. The former royal palace from where the Malla kings ruled over Kathmandu, is also renowned as the Hanuman Dhoka (palace). Once here there are many dazzling monuments you won’t like to miss.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nVisit the majestic Kastamandap Temple (the name of this city is derived from the word ‘Kasthamandap’), a temple built from woods coming from a single tree. Then you will have an opportunity to visit the temple of the\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Kumari Goddess (the only living goddess in Nepal)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. Kumaris selected here are of tender child age and are considered and worshipped in the form of Divine power. After her puberty phase, the next kumari is selected. Visit the famous freak street, a popular place of budget tourist shopping, and the hippie’s meetup point before Thamel overshadowed it.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter a lively and exciting tour a short drive towards the west of the city to reach your next destination in the form of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSwoyambhunath Stupa\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. It is located on a hilltop, with fabulous Panoramic views of Kathmandu city and green hills surrounding it. Further north from the hill in clear weather, you can view high snow-capped mountains.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOne of the oldest historical sites in the UNESCO World Heritage sites from Nepal, Swoyambhunath ages back more than 2, 5000 years. The stupa complex consists of old Buddhist religious monuments topped with a colossal dome-shaped stupa. With four mystical eyes of Buddha overlooking four directions in the dome, you will have a sacred feeling of fulfillment in this place. This place is surrounded by green forest with many monkeys dwelling around this place. Hence the temple is also known as “Monkey Temple.”\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOur next destination lies a short distance towards the east of Kathmandu city. \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePashupatinath Temple\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e area is one of the most sacred places for Hindu Pilgrims around the world. Non-Hindu tourists are not allowed inside the main temple. However one can visit the surrounding shrines and also view the temple from a nearby spot. The Pashupatinath Temple lies on the banks of the Holy Bagmati River. The main temple has a golden pagoda-tier roof and four silver doors.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nSurrounded by lovely forests and lush vegetation, Pashupatinath is an important Pilgrimage for Hindu devotees. This place packs with domestic and international pilgrims in mid-February on Shiva Ratri (birth anniversary of Lord Shiva). On the opposite side of the Pashupatinath and bank of the Bagmati river, funeral and cremation take place according to the Hindu religion. A heart-touching site but a vital experience about the way of life.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThen drive towards the northeast reaching \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBouddhanath Stupa\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. Also famous as the “Little \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://asiaexperiences.com/tibet/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eTibet\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e” of Nepal due to the strong Tibetan influence here in culture, traditions, and religion. Bouddhanath is a vast white dome with a low tier from where one can walk up near the top. With lovely views of the culture and Buddhist Tradition, you will have a peaceful time. Surrounding the Bouddhanath area are Souvenir shops, stores, restaurants, and monasteries. You can experience nightlife in Boudhanath with Tibetan tea in the evening.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter this fascinating tour of lovely historical and cultural influence from your destination, return to your respective hotels.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eDistances of each other monuments- Kathmandu best place to see:\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eKathmandu Durbar square (Hanuman Dhaka) to Swoyambhu Stupa (Swoyambhunath Maha Chaitya / Monkey Temple) distance: 3.3 KM with 15 15-minute drive approximately.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSwoyambhu to Pashupati Temple distance: 8 km with a 30-minute drive.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePashupatinath Temple to  Boudhanath Stupa distance: 2 km with 10 10-minute drive approximately.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u0026nbsp;\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022rll-youtube-player\\\\u0022 data-src=\\\\u0022https://www.youtube.com/embed/GG5pCr9ghCI\\\\u0022 data-id=\\\\u0022GG5pCr9ghCI\\\\u0022 data-query=\\\\u0022feature=oembed\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFully private trip \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVehicle fuel, vehicle tax.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking cultural city tour guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrinking Water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4314\\",\\"4332\\",\\"4315\\",\\"4330\\",\\"4249\\",\\"4041\\",\\"3997\\",\\"3971\\",\\"3944\\",\\"3943\\",\\"3936\\",\\"3933\\",\\"3921\\",\\"4297\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 1 hour\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 2 days\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4 days\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":1,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/boudhanath-stupa-1.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bouddha-nath-kathmandu.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmandu-travel.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bouddha-market.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmandu-durbar-square.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmandu-nepal-tripadvisor-number-1-1.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Thanka-of-Buddha.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/pashupatinath-kathmandu.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/narayan.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kritipur-temple.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Khokana-Taudaha-hike.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmanduvalley-view.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmandu-local-people.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Holi-Festival-Festival-of-Colors-at-Kathmandu-Durbar-Square.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/swyambhunath.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=825", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "825", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-04 08:56:25", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-04 08:56:25", "post_modified": "2024-05-20 08:53:17", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-05-20 08:53:17"}}, "customSections": [{"id": 1, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Extended Tours", "content": ["<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</a> - 4-5 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area</a> - 1 hour</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu</a> - 4-6 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour</a> - 2 days</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour</a> - 4 days</li>\\r\\n</ul>"], "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</a> - 4-5 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area</a> - 1 hour</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu</a> - 4-6 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour</a> - 2 days</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour</a> - 4 days</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, {"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Kathmandu Nepal tour with 4 World Heritage Sites by UNESCO", "content": ["<h2>Single-Day Kathmandu Nepal City Tour</h2>\\r\\n<strong>Here are the details of any option from above. If you need details for other options, we will send you.</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nEverest Vacation City and cultural guide will pick you up from your respective hotel in the valley for an exciting tour of <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathmandu\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu</a> Valley. Starting at the heart of the valley, the <strong>Kathmandu Durbar Square</strong> is the foremost destination for you today. This place is steeped in old history and rich Nepali culture from the 16th century till now. The former royal palace from where the Malla kings ruled over Kathmandu, is also renowned as the Hanuman Dhoka (palace). Once here there are many dazzling monuments you won’t like to miss.\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit the majestic Kastamandap Temple (the name of this city is derived from the word ‘Kasthamandap’), a temple built from woods coming from a single tree. Then you will have an opportunity to visit the temple of the<strong> Kumari Goddess (the only living goddess in Nepal)</strong>. Kumaris selected here are of tender child age and are considered and worshipped in the form of Divine power. After her puberty phase, the next kumari is selected. Visit the famous freak street, a popular place of budget tourist shopping, and the hippie’s meetup point before Thamel overshadowed it.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter a lively and exciting tour a short drive towards the west of the city to reach your next destination in the form of <strong>Swoyambhunath Stupa</strong>. It is located on a hilltop, with fabulous Panoramic views of Kathmandu city and green hills surrounding it. Further north from the hill in clear weather, you can view high snow-capped mountains.\\r\\n\\r\\nOne of the oldest historical sites in the UNESCO World Heritage sites from Nepal, Swoyambhunath ages back more than 2, 5000 years. The stupa complex consists of old Buddhist religious monuments topped with a colossal dome-shaped stupa. With four mystical eyes of Buddha overlooking four directions in the dome, you will have a sacred feeling of fulfillment in this place. This place is surrounded by green forest with many monkeys dwelling around this place. Hence the temple is also known as “Monkey Temple.”\\r\\n\\r\\nOur next destination lies a short distance towards the east of Kathmandu city. <strong>Pashupatinath Temple</strong> area is one of the most sacred places for Hindu Pilgrims around the world. Non-Hindu tourists are not allowed inside the main temple. However one can visit the surrounding shrines and also view the temple from a nearby spot. The Pashupatinath Temple lies on the banks of the Holy Bagmati River. The main temple has a golden pagoda-tier roof and four silver doors.\\r\\n\\r\\nSurrounded by lovely forests and lush vegetation, Pashupatinath is an important Pilgrimage for Hindu devotees. This place packs with domestic and international pilgrims in mid-February on Shiva Ratri (birth anniversary of Lord Shiva). On the opposite side of the Pashupatinath and bank of the Bagmati river, funeral and cremation take place according to the Hindu religion. A heart-touching site but a vital experience about the way of life.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen drive towards the northeast reaching <strong>Bouddhanath Stupa</strong>. Also famous as the “Little <a href=\\"https://asiaexperiences.com/tibet/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Tibet</a>” of Nepal due to the strong Tibetan influence here in culture, traditions, and religion. Bouddhanath is a vast white dome with a low tier from where one can walk up near the top. With lovely views of the culture and Buddhist Tradition, you will have a peaceful time. Surrounding the Bouddhanath area are Souvenir shops, stores, restaurants, and monasteries. You can experience nightlife in Boudhanath with Tibetan tea in the evening.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter this fascinating tour of lovely historical and cultural influence from your destination, return to your respective hotels.\\r\\n<h3>Distances of each other monuments- Kathmandu best place to see:</h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kathmandu Durbar square (Hanuman Dhaka) to Swoyambhu Stupa (Swoyambhunath Maha Chaitya / Monkey Temple) distance: 3.3 KM with 15 15-minute drive approximately.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Swoyambhu to Pashupati Temple distance: 8 km with a 30-minute drive.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pashupatinath Temple to  Boudhanath Stupa distance: 2 km with 10 10-minute drive approximately.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n&nbsp;\\r\\n<div class=\\"rll-youtube-player\\" data-src=\\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/GG5pCr9ghCI\\" data-id=\\"GG5pCr9ghCI\\" data-query=\\"feature=oembed\\"></div>"], "description": "<h2>Single-Day Kathmandu Nepal City Tour</h2>\\r\\n<strong>Here are the details of any option from above. If you need details for other options, we will send you.</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nEverest Vacation City and cultural guide will pick you up from your respective hotel in the valley for an exciting tour of <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathmandu\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu</a> Valley. Starting at the heart of the valley, the <strong>Kathmandu Durbar Square</strong> is the foremost destination for you today. This place is steeped in old history and rich Nepali culture from the 16th century till now. The former royal palace from where the Malla kings ruled over Kathmandu, is also renowned as the Hanuman Dhoka (palace). Once here there are many dazzling monuments you won’t like to miss.\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit the majestic Kastamandap Temple (the name of this city is derived from the word ‘Kasthamandap’), a temple built from woods coming from a single tree. Then you will have an opportunity to visit the temple of the<strong> Kumari Goddess (the only living goddess in Nepal)</strong>. Kumaris selected here are of tender child age and are considered and worshipped in the form of Divine power. After her puberty phase, the next kumari is selected. Visit the famous freak street, a popular place of budget tourist shopping, and the hippie’s meetup point before Thamel overshadowed it.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter a lively and exciting tour a short drive towards the west of the city to reach your next destination in the form of <strong>Swoyambhunath Stupa</strong>. It is located on a hilltop, with fabulous Panoramic views of Kathmandu city and green hills surrounding it. Further north from the hill in clear weather, you can view high snow-capped mountains.\\r\\n\\r\\nOne of the oldest historical sites in the UNESCO World Heritage sites from Nepal, Swoyambhunath ages back more than 2, 5000 years. The stupa complex consists of old Buddhist religious monuments topped with a colossal dome-shaped stupa. With four mystical eyes of Buddha overlooking four directions in the dome, you will have a sacred feeling of fulfillment in this place. This place is surrounded by green forest with many monkeys dwelling around this place. Hence the temple is also known as “Monkey Temple.”\\r\\n\\r\\nOur next destination lies a short distance towards the east of Kathmandu city. <strong>Pashupatinath Temple</strong> area is one of the most sacred places for Hindu Pilgrims around the world. Non-Hindu tourists are not allowed inside the main temple. However one can visit the surrounding shrines and also view the temple from a nearby spot. The Pashupatinath Temple lies on the banks of the Holy Bagmati River. The main temple has a golden pagoda-tier roof and four silver doors.\\r\\n\\r\\nSurrounded by lovely forests and lush vegetation, Pashupatinath is an important Pilgrimage for Hindu devotees. This place packs with domestic and international pilgrims in mid-February on Shiva Ratri (birth anniversary of Lord Shiva). On the opposite side of the Pashupatinath and bank of the Bagmati river, funeral and cremation take place according to the Hindu religion. A heart-touching site but a vital experience about the way of life.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen drive towards the northeast reaching <strong>Bouddhanath Stupa</strong>. Also famous as the “Little <a href=\\"https://asiaexperiences.com/tibet/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Tibet</a>” of Nepal due to the strong Tibetan influence here in culture, traditions, and religion. Bouddhanath is a vast white dome with a low tier from where one can walk up near the top. With lovely views of the culture and Buddhist Tradition, you will have a peaceful time. Surrounding the Bouddhanath area are Souvenir shops, stores, restaurants, and monasteries. You can experience nightlife in Boudhanath with Tibetan tea in the evening.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter this fascinating tour of lovely historical and cultural influence from your destination, return to your respective hotels.\\r\\n<h3>Distances of each other monuments- Kathmandu best place to see:</h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kathmandu Durbar square (Hanuman Dhaka) to Swoyambhu Stupa (Swoyambhunath Maha Chaitya / Monkey Temple) distance: 3.3 KM with 15 15-minute drive approximately.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Swoyambhu to Pashupati Temple distance: 8 km with a 30-minute drive.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pashupatinath Temple to  Boudhanath Stupa distance: 2 km with 10 10-minute drive approximately.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n&nbsp;\\r\\n<div class=\\"rll-youtube-player\\" data-src=\\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/GG5pCr9ghCI\\" data-id=\\"GG5pCr9ghCI\\" data-query=\\"feature=oembed\\"></div>"}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Fully private trip (even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.", "Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).", "Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.", "English speaking cultural city tour guide.", "Drinking Water."], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Fully private trip (even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.", "Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).", "Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.", "English speaking cultural city tour guide.", "Drinking Water."], "services": []}, "sub_description": "Kathmandu Durbar Square, Pashupatinath Temple, Boudhanath Stupa, Swoyambhu / Monkey Temple", "trip_highlights": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kathmandu Durbar Square, Swoyambhu/Monkey Temple, Pashupatinath Temple, and Boudhanath Stupa in 1-day sightseeing.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Patan durbar Square, Pashupatinath and Swoyambhu/Monkey Temple in 1 day tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bhaktapur Durbar Square, Changunarayan and Pashupatinath Temple in a single day.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li> Chandragiri Hills with a cable car ride, Swoyambhu/Monkey Temple, Hanuman Dhoka in one day. (<a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/one-day-kathmandu-tour-with-chandragiri-hills/\\">Chandragiri Hills with cable car</a>)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Or, choose your preferred places to see and let us know, and we will operate your choices. You may add an Everest mountain flight or helicopter flight to Everest on the same day.</li>\\r\\n</ol>", "trip_type_level": "Private Tour", "meta_description": "Explore the fascinating historical and cultural landmarks listed as UNESCO World Heritage Sites in 1 Day Kathmandu Sightseeing Tour.", "trip_attractions": "Boudha Stupa, Pashpati Temple, Swoyambhu (Monkey Temple) & Basantapur Durbar Square (Hanuman Dhoka)", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "faq_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "Boudha Stupa, Pashpati Temple, Swoyambhu (Monkey Temple) & Basantapur Durbar Square (Hanuman Dhoka)", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": "Private AC Vehicle"}, "trip_transportations": "Private AC Vehicle", "trip_highlights_title": "Embark on a delightful single-day tour of Kathmandu and explore the fascinating historical and cultural landmarks listed as UNESCO World Heritage Sites. Immerse yourself in the rich history, vibrant culture, diverse religion, delectable Nepalese cuisine, and local lifestyle, all with the guidance of our expert travel guides from Nepal."}	2023-12-04 08:56:25+00	2024-05-20 09:53:17+01
178	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "80", "ws_short_desc": "", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "100", "ws_number_of_days": "1", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy"}, "faq": [{"answer": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "question": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "question": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "question": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "question": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "question": "5. What to expect on tours?"}], "meta": {"_edit_last": "2", "_edit_lock": "1707804499:2", "_dp_original": "825", "_thumbnail_id": "835", "ws_sale_price": "80", "ws_short_desc": "", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "100", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "1", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "Day flat hike Taudaha Lake Khokana Bungmati", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Day flat hike Taudaha Lake Khokana Bungmati", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "44", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Day flat hike Taudaha Lake Khokana Bungmati with the bliss of nature, this hike gives a time-lapse of places with 6th-century culture and art.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "day-flat-hike-taudaha-lake-khokana-bungmati", "tags": [], "title": "Day flat hike Taudaha Lake Khokana Bungmati", "duration": "1 Day", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "The southern end of the Kathmandu Valley is certainly gifted with destinations of cultural and natural bounties although it mightn’t be the most hyped place here. The journey focuses on some amazing and culturally preserved destinations this region has to offer within a day’s hike. <strong>Day flat hike</strong> <strong>Taudaha Lake Khokana Bungmati</strong> with the bliss of nature, this hike gives a time-lapse of places with 6th-century culture and art. The local art of living, trading systems and units, stone and wooden art, flatlands with rice fields, and the family-like people here make your day stuffed with magnificent treats in Kathmandu. With <strong>Everest Vacation</strong> discover the best-preserved art and traditional lifestyle of Kathmandu Valley.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe hike starts at <strong>Taudaha Lake</strong> after we pick you up from your hotel and drive you there. Leaving the hustle and bustle behind, take a scenic road to <strong>Chovar</strong>. Make a brief stop in the 15th-century temple of <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adinath_Lokeshwar\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\"><strong>Adinath Lokeshwar</strong></a> here and enjoy the view of Kathmandu and beyond from here. With both Hindu and Buddhist devotees visiting this temple dedicated to the <strong>Rato Macchindranath deity</strong>, explore some related local legends here. A short drive from the temple takes us to the starting point of our trek, the Taudaha Lake.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Taudaha</strong> Lake locally known as <strong>‘Nagdaha’</strong> translates as ‘the lake of snakes’ and is a small lake with historical and religious significance about 12 km south of Kathmandu. It is locally believed that the original lake was the one which constituted the valley of today and a mythical Buddhist character Manjushree drained the water with his sword to make the land liveable. During this process to prevent the nagas from, leaving the areas as they were the divine creatures protecting it, this lake was created. To respect the nagas and avoid the disruption of water here, you aren’t allowed to swim or fish in the lake.\\r\\n\\r\\nApart from religious legends, <strong>Taudaha</strong> is also an ecological paradise for nature lovers. More than 40 different species of birds are found in the lake and the premises here. The lake is one of the significant places to view over 23 different varieties of Migratory birds some traveling from as far as Mongolia and Siberia in winter.\\r\\n\\r\\nThere is also frequent spotting of Golden Jackal, Grey mongoose, and many different species of rodents here. Checkered keelback snakes and garden lizards are also frequently spotted alongside numerous different species of fish in the lake. The view of the surrounding hills and green fields from the lake is also pristine. You can also feed the fish here in the lake. After a calm time here, we will start the first part of our trek to Khokana.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Khokana village</strong> is about one and a half hours of pleasant trek from Taudaha passing by small settlements on the way. <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khokana\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Khokana</a> is a lovely settlement of <strong>local Newari people with a significant population involved in farming</strong>. Also, on the tentative list for the <strong>UNESCO World Heritage Site</strong>, this village is a living reflection of medieval art and the history of the valley. Witness a unique experience of local mustard oil cultivation here. The fresh air and lovely people are the major reasons to visit the village. The local cuisine and family-like atmosphere make you feel at home.\\r\\n\\r\\nOn the tour of Khokana, <strong>discover medieval art, beautiful monuments, traditional lifestyle, and ways of housing</strong>. The <strong>Rudrayani temple</strong> (a place where Rudrayani traditional RudrayaniJatra takes place), De Pukhu (pond), Jitapur Mandap or ‘Gaa-cha,’ Shikali Temple of Sikhil Buddha, and the other small 6 ponds in Khokana are the major attractions here. Head towards Bungamati village after the Khokana visit.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Bungamati</strong> is a historical town about an hour’s walk from <strong>Khokana</strong> and is believed to be the birthplace of the <strong>Rato Macchindranath</strong> deity. Also called before as Bunga or Amarpur and also Bungapattan in the Malla period of the valley, this village is one of the most sacred communities of the Newari people. Overlooking the holy Bagmati river, each year a chariot carrying the sculpture of Rato Macchindranath is pulled by the locals to Patan named ‘Rato Macchindranath Jatra’ which is one of the most significant occasions in Newari communities.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe only living goddess of the world ‘<strong>Kumari’</strong> is also chosen from a community here, and you can visit the home of the present Kumari goddess with the guide here. Alongside numerous shrines and monuments constituting this village, make our way to the Temple of Macchindranath which is a Shikhara-style temple in the center of the village. You can also witness the reconstruction works from the 2015 earthquake here. Exploring the village, we can also try some local cuisine here.\\r\\n\\r\\nMaking yourself here in times of local festivals give you bonus experiences of the culture, traditional dance and music, Jatras, and overall unity of the people living in these areas. After a majestic bliss of tradition and culture here, we drive you back to your hotel in Kathmandu. Prepare to explore the lesser-seen side of Kathmandu Valley with Everest Vacation."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Single-Day Taudaha Lake Khokana Bungmati", "richText": "", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Khokana-Taudaha-flat-hike3.jpeg", "title": "Khokana-Taudaha-flat-hike3", "altText": "Khokana-Taudaha-flat-hike3", "caption": "Khokana-Taudaha-flat-hike3", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["838", "837", "836", "835", "834", "833", "832"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", 