": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ANNAPURNA.jpeg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=891", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "891", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-07 06:30:57", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-07 06:30:57", "post_modified": "2024-02-09 09:30:23", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-02-09 09:30:23"}}, "customSections": [{"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["The <strong>6 Days Classic Annapurna Trek</strong> is a comfortable trek package designed by Everest Vacation that caters to the trekker’s preference. The popular treks in the Annapurna regions take you through beautiful scenic landscapes, and views of snow-capped Annapurna and Dhaulagiri ranges.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe <strong>Classic Annapurna trek</strong> provides cultural and natural insights. Trekkers can immerse themselves in the local lifestyle and culture of the ethnicities living there. Also, capture nature wonders and scenic mountain vistas for an unforgettable memory during the tour.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis trek's elevation is comparatively low and easy for trekkers of all age groups with good physical fitness. You pass through beautiful Ghorepani village and climb Poon Hill for stunning sunrise views. Trek to attractive Gurung village Ghandruk and adore the natural scenery at its best. Traverse beautiful settlements of Tolkha, Australian Camp, and Kande and return to Pokhara."], "description": "The <strong>6 Days Classic Annapurna Trek</strong> is a comfortable trek package designed by Everest Vacation that caters to the trekker’s preference. The popular treks in the Annapurna regions take you through beautiful scenic landscapes, and views of snow-capped Annapurna and Dhaulagiri ranges.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe <strong>Classic Annapurna trek</strong> provides cultural and natural insights. Trekkers can immerse themselves in the local lifestyle and culture of the ethnicities living there. Also, capture nature wonders and scenic mountain vistas for an unforgettable memory during the tour.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis trek's elevation is comparatively low and easy for trekkers of all age groups with good physical fitness. You pass through beautiful Ghorepani village and climb Poon Hill for stunning sunrise views. Trek to attractive Gurung village Ghandruk and adore the natural scenery at its best. Traverse beautiful settlements of Tolkha, Australian Camp, and Kande and return to Pokhara."}], "itinerary_title": "Annapurna Trek", "sub_description": "Explore 6 Days Classic Annapurna Trek with Everest Vacation.", "trip_type_level": "Short and Easy", "meta_description": "The 6 Days Classic Annapurna Trek is a comfortable trek package designed by Everest Vacation that caters to the trekker’s preference.", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "", "best_season": "", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": ""}, "trip_highlights_title": "The 6 Days Classic Annapurna Trek is a comfortable trek package designed by Everest Vacation that caters to the trekker’s preference."}	2023-12-07 06:30:57+00	2024-02-09 09:30:23+00
197	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "85", "ws_short_desc": "", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "100", "ws_number_of_days": "2", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy"}, "faq": [{"answer": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "question": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "question": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "question": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "question": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "question": "5. What to expect on tours?"}], "meta": {"_edit_last": "2", "_edit_lock": "1707811981:2", "_dp_original": "510", "_thumbnail_id": "769", "ws_sale_price": "85", "ws_short_desc": "", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "100", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "2", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "Dhampus to Australian Camp Trekking from Pokhara", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Dhampus to Australian Camp Trekking from Pokhara", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "44", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Dhampus to Australian Camp Trekking from Pokhara treats you with beautiful Himalayan views and takes you to beautiful Dhampus village.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "dhampus-to-australian-camp-trekking-from-pokhara", "tags": [], "title": "Dhampus to Australian Camp Trekking from Pokhara", "duration": "2 Days", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "Australian Camp is the best hiking tour around <a href=\\"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/nepal/pokhara\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Pokhara</a>. This adventurous trek offers you some spectacular Mountain valleys, ethnic Nepalese villages, and beautiful landscapes. Have a relaxing time far from the hustle and bustle of the crowded city. Experience the colorful culture and the harmony and peace among the locals during this short trek.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Dhampus to Australian Camp</strong> trek starts with a scenic hour's drive from Pokhara to Kande. Then trek from Kande to reach Australian Camp. Witness the mesmerizing scenery of mountain ranges through the Camp to join the trek toward Dhampus. A Gurung village Dhampus is also famous for its cultural experience, amazing hospitality, and stunning mountain views. After exploring the Dhampus, descend to Phedi and the trek ends.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe informative itinerary we provide below is for short hiking every day. This hiking route goes through a more scenic route with typical local villages. If people want tough hiking within a short day’s plan, we can provide you with an optional itinerary. The hiking route has standard local guest houses for accommodation and food."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Drive to Kande and Trek to Australian Camp", "richText": "An early drive to Kande village will take about an hour. Then we start our hike up along the rocky trail for a couple of hours to reach Australian Camp. The camp offers some spectacular views of the Annapurna range, Machhapuchhre, Lamjung Himal, and many others. Overnight at Lodge.", "driveTime": "2-3 hours", "elevation": "2165m", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 2, "meal": "", "title": "Trek to Phedi via Dhampus and drive back to Pokhara", "richText": "Trek starts from Australian Camp with a gentle downhill through the rhododendron and oak forest and makes your way to Dhampus. After a brief rest in Dhampus continue the downhill through the stone staircase. This stone staircase was laid by the village development committee for the inflow and outflow of goods. After arriving at the Phedi, we drive back to Pokhara from Phedi for about 45 min. Overnight at lodge.", "driveTime": "5 hours", "elevation": "820m", "accommodation": 