 descend to Phedi and the trek ends.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe informative itinerary we provide below is for short hiking every day. This hiking route goes through a more scenic route with typical local villages. If people want tough hiking within a short day’s plan, we can provide you with an optional itinerary. The hiking route has standard local guest houses for accommodation and food.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4830\\",\\"4831\\",\\"4829\\",\\"4576\\",\\"4341\\",\\"4281\\",\\"733\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Drive to Kande and Trek to Australian Camp\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\" 2165m \\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"2-3 hours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"An early drive to Kande village will take about an hour. Then we start our hike up along the rocky trail for a couple of hours to reach Australian Camp. The camp offers some spectacular views of the Annapurna range, Machhapuchhre, Lamjung Himal, and many others. Overnight at Lodge.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Phedi via Dhampus and drive back to Pokhara\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"820m\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"5 hours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Trek starts from Australian Camp with a gentle downhill through the rhododendron and oak forest and makes your way to Dhampus. After a brief rest in Dhampus continue the downhill through the stone staircase. This stone staircase was laid by the village development committee for the inflow and outflow of goods. After arriving at the Phedi, we drive back to Pokhara from Phedi for about 45 min. Overnight at lodge.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFully private trip \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVehicle fuel, vehicle tax.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking cultural city tour guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrinking Water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e1 day Kathmandu sightseeing Tour - 4-8 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Short and easy day trek around Pokhara.\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhampus Australian Camp Trekking\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e is a short and easy day trek around Pokhara. The major attraction is the closed mountains view and local villages, local people and way of lifestyle, Sunset and sunrise.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview \\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"Australian Camp is the best hiking tour around \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://www.lonelyplanet.com/nepal/pokhara\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003ePokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e. This adventurous trek offers you some spectacular Mountain valleys, ethnic Nepalese villages, and beautiful landscapes. Have a relaxing time far from the hustle and bustle of the crowded city. Experience the colorful culture and the harmony and peace among the locals during this short trek.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhampus to Australian Camp\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e trek starts with a scenic hour's drive from Pokhara to Kande. Then trek from Kande to reach Australian Camp. Witness the mesmerizing scenery of mountain ranges through the Camp to join the trek toward Dhampus. A Gurung village Dhampus is also famous for its cultural experience, amazing hospitality, and stunning mountain views. After exploring the Dhampus, descend to Phedi and the trek ends.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe informative itinerary we provide below is for short hiking every day. This hiking route goes through a more scenic route with typical local villages. If people want tough hiking within a short day’s plan, we can provide you with an optional itinerary. The hiking route has standard local guest houses for accommodation and food.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4830\\",\\"4831\\",\\"4829\\",\\"4576\\",\\"4341\\",\\"4281\\",\\"733\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Drive to Kande and Trek to Australian Camp\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\" 2165m \\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"2-3 hours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"An early drive to Kande village will take about an hour. Then we start our hike up along the rocky trail for a couple of hours to reach Australian Camp. The camp offers some spectacular views of the Annapurna range, Machhapuchhre, Lamjung Himal, and many others. Overnight at Lodge.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Phedi via Dhampus and drive back to Pokhara\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"820m\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"5 hours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Trek starts from Australian Camp with a gentle downhill through the rhododendron and oak forest and makes your way to Dhampus. After a brief rest in Dhampus continue the downhill through the stone staircase. This stone staircase was laid by the village development committee for the inflow and outflow of goods. After arriving at the Phedi, we drive back to Pokhara from Phedi for about 45 min. Overnight at lodge.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFully private trip \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVehicle fuel, vehicle tax.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking cultural city tour guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrinking Water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e1 day Kathmandu sightseeing Tour - 4-8 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/pokhara-machhapuchre-sunrise.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/dhampus.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/sunrise-from-dhampus.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/way-to-dhampus.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/australian-camp-dhampud.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Peace-Pagoda-Pokhara1.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/phewa-lake-pokhara-1.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/pokhara-david-falls.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=904", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "904", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-08 05:28:16", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-08 05:28:16", "post_modified": "2024-02-13 08:13:00", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-02-13 08:13:00"}}, "customSections": [{"id": 1, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Extended Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">1 day Kathmandu sightseeing Tour - 4-8 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">1 day Kathmandu sightseeing Tour - 4-8 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": 2, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Alternate Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["Australian Camp is the best hiking tour around <a href=\\"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/nepal/pokhara\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Pokhara</a>. This adventurous trek offers you some spectacular Mountain valleys, ethnic Nepalese villages, and beautiful landscapes. Have a relaxing time far from the hustle and bustle of the crowded city. Experience the colorful culture and the harmony and peace among the locals during this short trek.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Dhampus to Australian Camp</strong> trek starts with a scenic hour's drive from Pokhara to Kande. Then trek from Kande to reach Australian Camp. Witness the mesmerizing scenery of mountain ranges through the Camp to join the trek toward Dhampus. A Gurung village Dhampus is also famous for its cultural experience, amazing hospitality, and stunning mountain views. After exploring the Dhampus, descend to Phedi and the trek ends.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe informative itinerary we provide below is for short hiking every day. This hiking route goes through a more scenic route with typical local villages. If people want tough hiking within a short day’s plan, we can provide you with an optional itinerary. The hiking route has standard local guest houses for accommodation and food."], "description": "Australian Camp is the best hiking tour around <a href=\\"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/nepal/pokhara\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Pokhara</a>. This adventurous trek offers you some spectacular Mountain valleys, ethnic Nepalese villages, and beautiful landscapes. Have a relaxing time far from the hustle and bustle of the crowded city. Experience the colorful culture and the harmony and peace among the locals during this short trek.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Dhampus to Australian Camp</strong> trek starts with a scenic hour's drive from Pokhara to Kande. Then trek from Kande to reach Australian Camp. Witness the mesmerizing scenery of mountain ranges through the Camp to join the trek toward Dhampus. A Gurung village Dhampus is also famous for its cultural experience, amazing hospitality, and stunning mountain views. After exploring the Dhampus, descend to Phedi and the trek ends.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe informative itinerary we provide below is for short hiking every day. This hiking route goes through a more scenic route with typical local villages. If people want tough hiking within a short day’s plan, we can provide you with an optional itinerary. The hiking route has standard local guest houses for accommodation and food."}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Fully private trip (even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.", "Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).", "Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.", "English speaking cultural city tour guide.", "Drinking Water."], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Fully private trip (even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.", "Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).", "Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.", "English speaking cultural city tour guide.", "Drinking Water."], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "Explore Dhampus to Australian Camp Trekking from Pokhara with Everest Vacation.", "trip_highlights": "<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Dhampus Australian Camp Trekking</strong> is a short and easy day trek around Pokhara. The major attraction is the closed mountains view and local villages, local people and way of lifestyle, Sunset and sunrise.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "trip_type_level": "Easy", "meta_description": "Dhampus to Australian Camp Trekking from Pokhara treats you with beautiful Himalayan views and takes you to beautiful Dhampus village.", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "faq_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": "Private AC Vehicle"}, "trip_transportations": "Private AC Vehicle", "trip_highlights_title": "Short and easy day trek around Pokhara."}	2023-12-08 05:28:16+00	2024-02-13 08:13:00+00
198	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "5", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy"}, "meta": {"_edit_last": "5", "_edit_lock": "1707471661:5", "_dp_original": "737", "_thumbnail_id": "4262", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "5", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "5 day Short Everest View Trekking", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "5 day Short Everest View Trekking", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "47", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "A 5 day short Everest View Trekking under Nepal trekking package designed by Everest Vacation is a perfect gateway to the Everest region.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "short-everest-view-trekking", "tags": [], "title": "5 day Short Everest View Trekking ", "duration": "5 Days", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "A <strong>5 day short Everest View Trekking</strong> under Nepal trekking package designed by Everest Vacation is a perfect gateway to the Everest region. The trek duration is short and trekkers can get a glimpse of Everest as well. A short scenic flight to Lukla is adventurous and from Phakding this trek begins.\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit the beautiful Namche Bazaar also popular as the Sherpa capital. Namche is the best place to get continental foods, coffee, an Irish Pub, and bakery goods at such an elevation of 3,440m. Treat yourself to such yummy food items. The weekend market is the highlight of Namche along with Sherpa people and their culture.\\r\\n\\r\\nTour around Everest View Hotel and adore the awesome views of Everest and other neighboring peaks. Visit the National Park Museum to get a deeper understanding of the Sherpa culture and lifestyle of Sherpa mountaineers. Then, visit the attractive <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khumjung\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Khumjung village</a> where you can visit a monastery that has a purported Yeti scalp. Don’t miss to tour around the school built by Sir Edmund Hillary’s Trust."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Flight to Lukla then Trek to Phakding.", "richText": "Early morning, we will drive you to the Tribhuwan International Airport (TIA) to board a domestic flight to the <a href=\\"https://wikitravel.org/en/Lukla_airport\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"><strong>Tenzing-Hillary airport in Lukla</strong></a>. This flight to Lukla is one of the most scenic flights in the whole world. On the flight, you can view all three major geographic partitions of Nepal. The high hills lead us near the snow-capped Himalayas before landing at the <strong>Lukla airport</strong>.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe entry point to the Everest region, <strong>Lukla</strong> is a small village with the main airport to further advance to any region of Khumbu. After a brief rest here, we will commence the trek of today heading towards <strong>Phakding</strong>. The trek is easy and smooth. We will reach Phakding after 3-4 hours of gradual trek from Lukla.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Phakding.\\r\\n<em>(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)</em>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 2, "meal": "", "title": "Trek to Namche Bazar", "richText": "We will start the trek early today through the beautiful pine forest. Small patches of the rhododendron forests make the trail even better. Besides the raging water of the Dudhkoshi River, we will have a perfect view of <strong>Thamserku Mountain</strong> as we advance towards <strong>Namche</strong>. After crossing a few hill settlements on the way, we will reach the entry point of the <strong>Sagarmatha(Everest) National Park</strong>.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will have our permits checked at the checkpoint here and continue the trek to Namche. Nearing <strong>Namche Bazaar</strong>, we will get the first glimpse of <strong>Mount Everest</strong>. Towards the Evening we will reach the Sherpa capital, Namche Bazaar, and rest for the day at a hotel here.\\r\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Namche Bazaar.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 3, "meal": "", "title": "Early morning climb Everest View Hotel, Khumjung village, and back to the Hotel", "richText": "We will start our day with a breathtaking view of the <strong>sunrise over Mt Everest, Nuptse, and Lhotse. </strong>From Namche, we will hike for a couple of hours to <strong>Hotel Everest View</strong>. We will take a short tour on the way and visit the <strong>National Park Museum</strong>. Here, you can learn a lot about the <strong>Sherpa culture, the lifestyle of the Mountaineers</strong>, and the gear and stories of the locals and visitors from the very first years. After the museum, hike to <strong>Syangboche</strong>; it has one of the highest airstrips in Nepal at an altitude of 3790 meters.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen we will continue to the Everest View hotel. The hotel lies on the other side of a ridge so; you can only get a sight of the hotel after getting near to it. After reaching the Everest View Hotel, we will be treated to some of the <strong>best views of Everest</strong> and surrounding any place in the world. The Panoramic view is pristine and picture-perfect\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom Everest View Hotel, we will take a <strong>hike to the <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khumjung\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Khumjung</a> and Kunde villages</strong>. Walking beside numerous small and big Chortens and Mani walls, we will catch a trail to Khumjung Village. Here we will take a short village tour and the <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yeti\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"><strong>Khumjung Monastery (You can see the Yeti Scalp/Skull at the Monastery)</strong></a> and the<strong> Hillary School</strong>. After lunch here, we will begin the walk to <strong>Kunde</strong>.  The steep ascend is then followed by a bit of relaxed uphill to the village of Khunde. Returning from here to Namche, we can choose different trails and visit the small villages and Yak grazing lands.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter reaching Namche, you can head for the local market tour. We will rest for the day in a hotel in Namche Bazaar.\\r\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Namche Bazaar.\\r\\n\\r\\n&nbsp;", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 4, "meal": "", "title": "Trek Back to Lukla", "richText": "Most of today’s trek will be on a gradual downhill trail leading to <strong>Lukla</strong>. We will get all the beautiful landscape views from different angles while descending to Phakding and Lukla. During the peak seasons in spring and autumn when the helicopter shuttle is available (generally mid-March to mid-May and early October to early December), there is an option to take the <strong>helicopter shuttle directly from Everest View Hotel to Lukla</strong>, saving you two days of trekking. After reaching Lukla, we can view the beautiful sunset and rest for the day. Overnight at a Lodge in Lukla.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 5, "meal": "", "title": "Flight to Kathmandu from Lukla", "richText": "After breakfast, we will leave the <strong>Khumbu region</strong> and fly back to the capital <strong>Kathmandu</strong>. You can view the Himalayas for one last time and relive the moment from the flight. After landing in Kathmandu, we will drive you back to your hotel. You can spend some more time in the street markets of Thamel and explore the local cuisines and souvenirs. Our team at Everest Vacation will stay connected for your valuable feedback and suggestions. With great memories and equally wonderful stories to share, we complete the <strong>short Everest tour of 5 days</strong>.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Mt-Everest-View-from-Hotel-Everest-View.jpg", "title": "Mt-Everest-View-from-Hotel-Everest-View", "altText": "5 day Short Everest View Trekking", "caption": "5 day Short Everest View Trekking", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["739", "738", "527", "740", "687", "612", "613", "610", "603", "602"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "ws_block_attractions": "", "ws_block_best_season": "", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-light", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": "Overview", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc6695edb31", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_block_transportation": "", "ws_trip_galleries_title": "Photo/Visual Gallery", "_ws_block_transportation": "field_63eeee74072de", "_ws_trip_galleries_title": "field_63ec89128acaa", "starter_kit_padding_type": "p-medium", "ws_trip_block_highlights": "", "ws_trip_information_list": 1, "_starter_kit_padding_type": "field_5f8584c998bc2", "_ws_trip_block_highlights": "field_63ec73a6a0d8f", "_ws_trip_information_list": "field_63ec90a574f02", "starter_kit_section_title": " Everest View Trekking ", "_starter_kit_section_title": "field_63ec948c94a16", "starter_kit_enable_section": "1", "_starter_kit_enable_section": "field_63edeb1c7635c", "starter_kit_section_padding": "", "ws_trip_include_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Fully private trip </strong>(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>English speaking cultural city tour guide.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drinking Water.</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_starter_kit_section_padding": "field_5f3e0f86a2634", "_ws_trip_include_description": "field_63edd6a337cd0", "ws_trip_overview_description": "A <strong>5 day short Everest View Trekking</strong> under Nepal trekking package designed by Everest Vacation is a perfect gateway to the Everest region. The trek duration is short and trekkers can get a glimpse of Everest as well. A short scenic flight to Lukla is adventurous and from Phakding this trek begins.\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit the beautiful Namche Bazaar also popular as the Sherpa capital. Namche is the best place to get continental foods, coffee, an Irish Pub, and bakery goods at such an elevation of 3,440m. Treat yourself to such yummy food items. The weekend market is the highlight of Namche along with Sherpa people and their culture.\\r\\n\\r\\nTour around Everest View Hotel and adore the awesome views of Everest and other neighboring peaks. Visit the National Park Museum to get a deeper understanding of the Sherpa culture and lifestyle of Sherpa mountaineers. Then, visit the attractive <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khumjung\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Khumjung village</a> where you can visit a monastery that has a purported Yeti scalp. Don’t miss to tour around the school built by Sir Edmund Hillary’s Trust.", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "Short trekking in Nepal are professionally composed treks offering the best scenic, cultural, and natural delights in a reduced amount of time. This kind of trek solely focuses on the best destinations approachable within the limited days and the best route to be there.", "_ws_trip_fact_short_description": "field_63ec73a69d305", "ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "01", "ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "02", "ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "03", "ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "04", "ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "05", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "Flight to Lukla then Trek to Phakding.", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "Trek to Namche Bazar", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "Early morning climb Everest View Hotel, Khumjung village, and back to the Hotel", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "Trek Back to Lukla", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title": "Flight to Kathmandu from Lukla", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "Extended Tours", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "Early morning, we will drive you to the Tribhuwan International Airport (TIA) to board a domestic flight to the <a href=\\"https://wikitravel.org/en/Lukla_airport\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"><strong>Tenzing-Hillary airport in Lukla</strong></a>. This flight to Lukla is one of the most scenic flights in the whole world. On the flight, you can view all three major geographic partitions of Nepal. The high hills lead us near the snow-capped Himalayas before landing at the <strong>Lukla airport</strong>.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe entry point to the Everest region, <strong>Lukla</strong> is a small village with the main airport to further advance to any region of Khumbu. After a brief rest here, we will commence the trek of today heading towards <strong>Phakding</strong>. The trek is easy and smooth. We will reach Phakding after 3-4 hours of gradual trek from Lukla.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Phakding.\\r\\n<em>(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)</em>", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "We will start the trek early today through the beautiful pine forest. Small patches of the rhododendron forests make the trail even better. Besides the raging water of the Dudhkoshi River, we will have a perfect view of <strong>Thamserku Mountain</strong> as we advance towards <strong>Namche</strong>. After crossing a few hill settlements on the way, we will reach the entry point of the <strong>Sagarmatha(Everest) National Park</strong>.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe will have our permits checked at the checkpoint here and continue the trek to Namche. Nearing <strong>Namche Bazaar</strong>, we will get the first glimpse of <strong>Mount Everest</strong>. Towards the Evening we will reach the Sherpa capital, Namche Bazaar, and rest for the day at a hotel here.\\r\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Namche Bazaar.", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "We will start our day with a breathtaking view of the <strong>sunrise over Mt Everest, Nuptse, and Lhotse. </strong>From Namche, we will hike for a couple of hours to <strong>Hotel Everest View</strong>. We will take a short tour on the way and visit the <strong>National Park Museum</strong>. Here, you can learn a lot about the <strong>Sherpa culture, the lifestyle of the Mountaineers</strong>, and the gear and stories of the locals and visitors from the very first years. After the museum, hike to <strong>Syangboche</strong>; it has one of the highest airstrips in Nepal at an altitude of 3790 meters.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen we will continue to the Everest View hotel. The hotel lies on the other side of a ridge so; you can only get a sight of the hotel after getting near to it. After reaching the Everest View Hotel, we will be treated to some of the <strong>best views of Everest</strong> and surrounding any place in the world. The Panoramic view is pristine and picture-perfect\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom Everest View Hotel, we will take a <strong>hike to the <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khumjung\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Khumjung</a> and Kunde villages</strong>. Walking beside numerous small and big Chortens and Mani walls, we will catch a trail to Khumjung Village. Here we will take a short village tour and the <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yeti\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"><strong>Khumjung Monastery (You can see the Yeti Scalp/Skull at the Monastery)</strong></a> and the<strong> Hillary School</strong>. After lunch here, we will begin the walk to <strong>Kunde</strong>.  The steep ascend is then followed by a bit of relaxed uphill to the village of Khunde. Returning from here to Namche, we can choose different trails and visit the small villages and Yak grazing lands.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter reaching Namche, you can head for the local market tour. We will rest for the day in a hotel in Namche Bazaar.\\r\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Namche Bazaar.\\r\\n\\r\\n&nbsp;", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "Most of today’s trek will be on a gradual downhill trail leading to <strong>Lukla</strong>. We will get all the beautiful landscape views from different angles while descending to Phakding and Lukla. During the peak seasons in spring and autumn when the helicopter shuttle is available (generally mid-March to mid-May and early October to early December), there is an option to take the <strong>helicopter shuttle directly from Everest View Hotel to Lukla</strong>, saving you two days of trekking. After reaching Lukla, we can view the beautiful sunset and rest for the day. Overnight at a Lodge in Lukla.", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description": "After breakfast, we will leave the <strong>Khumbu region</strong> and fly back to the capital <strong>Kathmandu</strong>. You can view the Himalayas for one last time and relive the moment from the flight. After landing in Kathmandu, we will drive you back to your hotel. You can spend some more time in the street markets of Thamel and explore the local cuisines and souvenirs. Our team at Everest Vacation will stay connected for your valuable feedback and suggestions. With great memories and equally wonderful stories to share, we complete the <strong>short Everest tour of 5 days</strong>.", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</a> - 4-5 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area</a> - 1 hour</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu</a> - 4-6 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour</a> - 2 days</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour</a> - 4 days</li>\\r\\n</ol>", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630"}, "categoryId": null, "meta_title": "5 day Short Everest View Trekking", "blogContent": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Short trekking in Nepal are professionally composed treks offering the best scenic, cultural, and natural delights in a reduced amount of time. This kind of trek solely focuses on the best destinations approachable within the limited days and the best route to be there.\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"A \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e5 day short Everest View Trekking\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e under Nepal trekking package designed by Everest Vacation is a perfect gateway to the Everest region. The trek duration is short and trekkers can get a glimpse of Everest as well. A short scenic flight to Lukla is adventurous and from Phakding this trek begins.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nVisit the beautiful Namche Bazaar also popular as the Sherpa capital. Namche is the best place to get continental foods, coffee, an Irish Pub, and bakery goods at such an elevation of 3,440m. Treat yourself to such yummy food items. The weekend market is the highlight of Namche along with Sherpa people and their culture.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTour around Everest View Hotel and adore the awesome views of Everest and other neighboring peaks. Visit the National Park Museum to get a deeper understanding of the Sherpa culture and lifestyle of Sherpa mountaineers. Then, visit the attractive \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khumjung\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKhumjung village\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e where you can visit a monastery that has a purported Yeti scalp. Don’t miss to tour around the school built by Sir Edmund Hillary’s Trust.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"739\\",\\"738\\",\\"527\\",\\"740\\",\\"687\\",\\"612\\",\\"613\\",\\"610\\",\\"603\\",\\"602\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\" Everest View Trekking \\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Flight to Lukla then Trek to Phakding.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Early morning, we will drive you to the Tribhuwan International Airport (TIA) to board a domestic flight to the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://wikitravel.org/en/Lukla_airport\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eTenzing-Hillary airport in Lukla\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e. This flight to Lukla is one of the most scenic flights in the whole world. On the flight, you can view all three major geographic partitions of Nepal. The high hills lead us near the snow-capped Himalayas before landing at the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLukla airport\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe entry point to the Everest region, \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLukla\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e is a small village with the main airport to further advance to any region of Khumbu. After a brief rest here, we will commence the trek of today heading towards \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePhakding\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. The trek is easy and smooth. We will reach Phakding after 3-4 hours of gradual trek from Lukla.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Phakding.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cem\\\\u003e(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Namche Bazar\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"We will start the trek early today through the beautiful pine forest. Small patches of the rhododendron forests make the trail even better. Besides the raging water of the Dudhkoshi River, we will have a perfect view of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eThamserku Mountain\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e as we advance towards \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNamche\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. After crossing a few hill settlements on the way, we will reach the entry point of the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSagarmatha(Everest) National Park\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe will have our permits checked at the checkpoint here and continue the trek to Namche. Nearing \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNamche Bazaar\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, we will get the first glimpse of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMount Everest\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. Towards the Evening we will reach the Sherpa capital, Namche Bazaar, and rest for the day at a hotel here.\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Namche Bazaar.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Early morning climb Everest View Hotel, Khumjung village, and back to the Hotel\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"We will start our day with a breathtaking view of the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003esunrise over Mt Everest, Nuptse, and Lhotse. \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eFrom Namche, we will hike for a couple of hours to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHotel Everest View\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. We will take a short tour on the way and visit the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNational Park Museum\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. Here, you can learn a lot about the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSherpa culture, the lifestyle of the Mountaineers\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, and the gear and stories of the locals and visitors from the very first years. After the museum, hike to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSyangboche\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e; it has one of the highest airstrips in Nepal at an altitude of 3790 meters.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThen we will continue to the Everest View hotel. The hotel lies on the other side of a ridge so; you can only get a sight of the hotel after getting near to it. After reaching the Everest View Hotel, we will be treated to some of the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ebest views of Everest\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e and surrounding any place in the world. The Panoramic view is pristine and picture-perfect\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom Everest View Hotel, we will take a \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ehike to the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khumjung\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKhumjung\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e and Kunde villages\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. Walking beside numerous small and big Chortens and Mani walls, we will catch a trail to Khumjung Village. Here we will take a short village tour and the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yeti\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKhumjung Monastery (You can see the Yeti Scalp/Skull at the Monastery)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e and the\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Hillary School\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. After lunch here, we will begin the walk to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKunde\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.  The steep ascend is then followed by a bit of relaxed uphill to the village of Khunde. Returning from here to Namche, we can choose different trails and visit the small villages and Yak grazing lands.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter reaching Namche, you can head for the local market tour. We will rest for the day in a hotel in Namche Bazaar.\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Namche Bazaar.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u0026nbsp;\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek Back to Lukla\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Most of today’s trek will be on a gradual downhill trail leading to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLukla\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. We will get all the beautiful landscape views from different angles while descending to Phakding and Lukla. During the peak seasons in spring and autumn when the helicopter shuttle is available (generally mid-March to mid-May and early October to early December), there is an option to take the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ehelicopter shuttle directly from Everest View Hotel to Lukla\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, saving you two days of trekking. After reaching Lukla, we can view the beautiful sunset and rest for the day. Overnight at a Lodge in Lukla.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"05\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Flight to Kathmandu from Lukla\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After breakfast, we will leave the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKhumbu region\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e and fly back to the capital \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKathmandu\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. You can view the Himalayas for one last time and relive the moment from the flight. After landing in Kathmandu, we will drive you back to your hotel. You can spend some more time in the street markets of Thamel and explore the local cuisines and souvenirs. Our team at Everest Vacation will stay connected for your valuable feedback and suggestions. With great memories and equally wonderful stories to share, we complete the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eshort Everest tour of 5 days\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFully private trip \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVehicle fuel, vehicle tax.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking cultural city tour guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrinking Water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 1 hour\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 2 days\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4 days\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":1,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Short trekking in Nepal are professionally composed treks offering the best scenic, cultural, and natural delights in a reduced amount of time. This kind of trek solely focuses on the best destinations approachable within the limited days and the best route to be there.\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"A \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e5 day short Everest View Trekking\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e under Nepal trekking package designed by Everest Vacation is a perfect gateway to the Everest region. The trek duration is short and trekkers can get a glimpse of Everest as well. A short scenic flight to Lukla is adventurous and from Phakding this trek begins.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nVisit the beautiful Namche Bazaar also popular as the Sherpa capital. Namche is the best place to get continental foods, coffee, an Irish Pub, and bakery goods at such an elevation of 3,440m. Treat yourself to such yummy food items. The weekend market is the highlight of Namche along with Sherpa people and their culture.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTour around Everest View Hotel and adore the awesome views of Everest and other neighboring peaks. Visit the National Park Museum to get a deeper understanding of the Sherpa culture and lifestyle of Sherpa mountaineers. Then, visit the attractive \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khumjung\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKhumjung village\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e where you can visit a monastery that has a purported Yeti scalp. Don’t miss to tour around the school built by Sir Edmund Hillary’s Trust.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"739\\",\\"738\\",\\"527\\",\\"740\\",\\"687\\",\\"612\\",\\"613\\",\\"610\\",\\"603\\",\\"602\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\" Everest View Trekking \\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Flight to Lukla then Trek to Phakding.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Early morning, we will drive you to the Tribhuwan International Airport (TIA) to board a domestic flight to the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://wikitravel.org/en/Lukla_airport\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eTenzing-Hillary airport in Lukla\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e. This flight to Lukla is one of the most scenic flights in the whole world. On the flight, you can view all three major geographic partitions of Nepal. The high hills lead us near the snow-capped Himalayas before landing at the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLukla airport\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe entry point to the Everest region, \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLukla\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e is a small village with the main airport to further advance to any region of Khumbu. After a brief rest here, we will commence the trek of today heading towards \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePhakding\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. The trek is easy and smooth. We will reach Phakding after 3-4 hours of gradual trek from Lukla.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Phakding.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cem\\\\u003e(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Namche Bazar\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"We will start the trek early today through the beautiful pine forest. Small patches of the rhododendron forests make the trail even better. Besides the raging water of the Dudhkoshi River, we will have a perfect view of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eThamserku Mountain\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e as we advance towards \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNamche\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. After crossing a few hill settlements on the way, we will reach the entry point of the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSagarmatha(Everest) National Park\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe will have our permits checked at the checkpoint here and continue the trek to Namche. Nearing \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNamche Bazaar\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, we will get the first glimpse of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMount Everest\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. Towards the Evening we will reach the Sherpa capital, Namche Bazaar, and rest for the day at a hotel here.\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Namche Bazaar.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Early morning climb Everest View Hotel, Khumjung village, and back to the Hotel\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"We will start our day with a breathtaking view of the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003esunrise over Mt Everest, Nuptse, and Lhotse. \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eFrom Namche, we will hike for a couple of hours to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHotel Everest View\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. We will take a short tour on the way and visit the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNational Park Museum\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. Here, you can learn a lot about the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSherpa culture, the lifestyle of the Mountaineers\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, and the gear and stories of the locals and visitors from the very first years. After the museum, hike to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSyangboche\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e; it has one of the highest airstrips in Nepal at an altitude of 3790 meters.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThen we will continue to the Everest View hotel. The hotel lies on the other side of a ridge so; you can only get a sight of the hotel after getting near to it. After reaching the Everest View Hotel, we will be treated to some of the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ebest views of Everest\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e and surrounding any place in the world. The Panoramic view is pristine and picture-perfect\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom Everest View Hotel, we will take a \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ehike to the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khumjung\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKhumjung\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e and Kunde villages\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. Walking beside numerous small and big Chortens and Mani walls, we will catch a trail to Khumjung Village. Here we will take a short village tour and the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yeti\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener noreferrer\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKhumjung Monastery (You can see the Yeti Scalp/Skull at the Monastery)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e and the\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Hillary School\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. After lunch here, we will begin the walk to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKunde\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.  The steep ascend is then followed by a bit of relaxed uphill to the village of Khunde. Returning from here to Namche, we can choose different trails and visit the small villages and Yak grazing lands.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter reaching Namche, you can head for the local market tour. We will rest for the day in a hotel in Namche Bazaar.\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Namche Bazaar.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u0026nbsp;\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek Back to Lukla\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Most of today’s trek will be on a gradual downhill trail leading to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLukla\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. We will get all the beautiful landscape views from different angles while descending to Phakding and Lukla. During the peak seasons in spring and autumn when the helicopter shuttle is available (generally mid-March to mid-May and early October to early December), there is an option to take the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ehelicopter shuttle directly from Everest View Hotel to Lukla\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, saving you two days of trekking. After reaching Lukla, we can view the beautiful sunset and rest for the day. Overnight at a Lodge in Lukla.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"05\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Flight to Kathmandu from Lukla\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After breakfast, we will leave the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKhumbu region\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e and fly back to the capital \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKathmandu\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. You can view the Himalayas for one last time and relive the moment from the flight. After landing in Kathmandu, we will drive you back to your hotel. You can spend some more time in the street markets of Thamel and explore the local cuisines and souvenirs. Our team at Everest Vacation will stay connected for your valuable feedback and suggestions. With great memories and equally wonderful stories to share, we complete the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eshort Everest tour of 5 days\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFully private trip \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVehicle fuel, vehicle tax.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking cultural city tour guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrinking Water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 1 hour\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu, Bhaktapur \\\\u0026amp; Patan Tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 2 days\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e - 4 days\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":1,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Mt-Everest-View-from-Hotel-Everest-View.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/dhulikhel-village.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/nagarkot-hill-hiking.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/bhaktapur-city-of-arts-e1706022904337.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/dhulikhel-banepa.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/local-people-of-newari-village-in-Kathmandu.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/dakshinkali-temple.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/swoyambhu-monkey-temple.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/farming-bungmati.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/sunrise-tour-nagarkot.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/nagakot.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=905", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "905", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-08 05:36:08", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-08 05:36:08", "post_modified": "2024-02-09 09:40:22", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-02-09 09:40:22"}}, "customSections": [{"id": 1, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Extended Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</a> - 4-5 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area</a> - 1 hour</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu</a> - 4-6 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour</a> - 2 days</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour</a> - 4 days</li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</a> - 4-5 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area</a> - 1 hour</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu</a> - 4-6 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour</a> - 2 days</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour</a> - 4 days</li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["A <strong>5 day short Everest View Trekking</strong> under Nepal trekking package designed by Everest Vacation is a perfect gateway to the Everest region. The trek duration is short and trekkers can get a glimpse of Everest as well. A short scenic flight to Lukla is adventurous and from Phakding this trek begins.\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit the beautiful Namche Bazaar also popular as the Sherpa capital. Namche is the best place to get continental foods, coffee, an Irish Pub, and bakery goods at such an elevation of 3,440m. Treat yourself to such yummy food items. The weekend market is the highlight of Namche along with Sherpa people and their culture.\\r\\n\\r\\nTour around Everest View Hotel and adore the awesome views of Everest and other neighboring peaks. Visit the National Park Museum to get a deeper understanding of the Sherpa culture and lifestyle of Sherpa mountaineers. Then, visit the attractive <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khumjung\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Khumjung village</a> where you can visit a monastery that has a purported Yeti scalp. Don’t miss to tour around the school built by Sir Edmund Hillary’s Trust."], "description": "A <strong>5 day short Everest View Trekking</strong> under Nepal trekking package designed by Everest Vacation is a perfect gateway to the Everest region. The trek duration is short and trekkers can get a glimpse of Everest as well. A short scenic flight to Lukla is adventurous and from Phakding this trek begins.\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit the beautiful Namche Bazaar also popular as the Sherpa capital. Namche is the best place to get continental foods, coffee, an Irish Pub, and bakery goods at such an elevation of 3,440m. Treat yourself to such yummy food items. The weekend market is the highlight of Namche along with Sherpa people and their culture.\\r\\n\\r\\nTour around Everest View Hotel and adore the awesome views of Everest and other neighboring peaks. Visit the National Park Museum to get a deeper understanding of the Sherpa culture and lifestyle of Sherpa mountaineers. Then, visit the attractive <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khumjung\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Khumjung village</a> where you can visit a monastery that has a purported Yeti scalp. Don’t miss to tour around the school built by Sir Edmund Hillary’s Trust."}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Fully private trip (even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.", "Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).", "Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.", "English speaking cultural city tour guide.", "Drinking Water."], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Fully private trip (even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.", "Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).", "Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.", "English speaking cultural city tour guide.", "Drinking Water."], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Everest View Trekking", "sub_description": "Explore 5 day Short Everest View Trekking  with Everest Vacation.", "trip_type_level": "Easy", "meta_description": "A 5 day short Everest View Trekking under Nepal trekking package designed by Everest Vacation is a perfect gateway to the Everest region.", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "", "best_season": "", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": ""}, "trip_highlights_title": "Short trekking in Nepal are professionally composed treks offering the best scenic, cultural, and natural delights in a reduced amount of time. This kind of trek solely focuses on the best destinations approachable within the limited days and the best route to be there."}	2023-12-08 05:36:08+00	2024-02-09 09:40:22+00
199	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "2", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy"}, "faq": [{"answer": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "question": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "question": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "question": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "question": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "question": "5. What to expect on tours?"}], "meta": {"_edit_last": "2", "_edit_lock": "1707804461:2", "_dp_original": "510", "_thumbnail_id": "738", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "2", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "Chisapani Sundarijal Trekking from Kathmandu", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Chisapani Sundarijal Trekking from Kathmandu", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "47", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Chisapani Sundarijal trekking from Kathmandu is one of the best destination places to spend some quality time far away from the busy city.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "chisapani-sundarijal-trekking-from-kathmandu", "tags": [], "title": "Chisapani Sundarijal Trekking from Kathmandu", "duration": "2 Days", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "<strong>Chisapani Sundarijal</strong> trekking is a short and exciting trip around the Kathmandu valley. This trek combines the best of nature with typical local life. It also includes a gorgeous Himalayan view, a captivating sunset, and ethereal sunrise from Chisapani and Nagarkot. This hike is an ideal vacation in a matter of two days and is suitable for all age groups.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe trip starts with a short drive to <strong>Sundarijal</strong>, a popular hangout and demanding picnic spot in the north of Kathmandu. It lies in the vicinity of Shivapuri Nagarjuna National Park which is a place of cool shades, beautiful streams, and a serene atmosphere.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe start our first-day trek to reach Chisapani <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagarkot\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Nagarkot</a> from Sundarijal which takes about 4 to 5 hours of walk. Chisapani is a beautiful place to host some majestic views of the Himalayan range. These Himalayas emit an ethereal glow in the setting sunlight.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe resume a second-day trip heading toward Nagarkot, along the ridge to the temple known as Changu Narayan temple. This temple hosts a nice view of Sankhu village and the Bhaktapur area. After some hours of exploration, we drive back to Kathmandu.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Chisapani Sundarijal trekking</strong> from Kathmandu is one of the best destination places to spend some quality time far away from the busy city. Witness the amazing hills, mountains, streams, and many more. The itinerary has been designed in detail keeping in mind the safety and enjoyment of the journey."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Early morning breakfast and one hour drive to Sundarijal then trek to Chisapani", "richText": "The drive from Kathmandu to Sundarijal takes about one hour. From Sundarijal, we start our trek toward Chisapani. Pass through a few settlements and dense forests to reach Chisapani. The total duration of the hike is nearly five hours. Chisapani is a Sherpa village, offering grand views of the mountains. Relive yourself in the evening by watching a picturesque sunset from the village. Overnight at teahouse.", "driveTime": "5 hours", "elevation": "2050m", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 2, "meal": "", "title": "Hike Chisapani to Sankhu. Drive back to Kathmandu.", "richText": "We resume our trek toward Nagarkot from Chisapani. It will take about 7 hours to walk. The trail passes mostly through the dense forest of the national park to reach Chauki Bhanjyang or Jhule. Then we continue our trek along the idyllic countryside to Nagarkot, a hilltop to the east of Kathmandu. Along the ridge of Nagarkot, you can witness the Changu Narayan temple. This place offers an amazing view of the Sankhu and Bhaktapur areas. After some hours of exploration, we drive back to Kathmandu. Overnight in Kathmandu.", "driveTime": "4-5 hours", "elevation": "1350m", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/nagarkot-hill-hiking.jpg", "title": "nagarkot-hill-hiking", "altText": "nagarkot-hill-hiking", "caption": "nagarkot-hill-hiking", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["4334", "4304", "3966", "738", "863", "3965", "603"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "ws_trip_faqs_lists": 5, "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists": "field_63ede38e351c7", "ws_block_attractions": " Chisapani and Nagarkot", "ws_block_best_season": "Any Season", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-light", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": "Overview", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc6695edb31", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_block_transportation": "Private AC Vehicle", "ws_trip_galleries_title": "Photo/Visual Gallery", "_ws_block_transportation": "field_63eeee74072de", "_ws_trip_galleries_title": "field_63ec89128acaa", "starter_kit_padding_type": "p-medium", "ws_trip_block_highlights": "<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Chisapani Sundarijal Trekking</strong> from Kathmandu is designed to provide you with a unique opportunity in a short time. You will explore the wonders of nature, the local lifestyle, the rural activities of Nepal, and the awe-inspiring majesty and beauty of dramatic mountain views.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "ws_trip_information_list": 2, "_starter_kit_padding_type": "field_5f8584c998bc2", "_ws_trip_block_highlights": "field_63ec73a6a0d8f", "_ws_trip_information_list": "field_63ec90a574f02", "starter_kit_section_title": "Day by Day Activities", "_starter_kit_section_title": "field_63ec948c94a16", "starter_kit_enable_section": "1", "ws_trip_faqs_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "_starter_kit_enable_section": "field_63edeb1c7635c", "_ws_trip_faqs_section_title": "field_63ede33e5b304", "starter_kit_section_padding": "", "ws_trip_include_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Fully private trip </strong>(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>English speaking cultural city tour guide.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drinking Water.</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_starter_kit_section_padding": "field_5f3e0f86a2634", "_ws_trip_include_description": "field_63edd6a337cd0", "ws_trip_overview_description": "<strong>Chisapani Sundarijal</strong> trekking is a short and exciting trip around the Kathmandu valley. This trek combines the best of nature with typical local life. It also includes a gorgeous Himalayan view, a captivating sunset, and ethereal sunrise from Chisapani and Nagarkot. This hike is an ideal vacation in a matter of two days and is suitable for all age groups.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe trip starts with a short drive to <strong>Sundarijal</strong>, a popular hangout and demanding picnic spot in the north of Kathmandu. It lies in the vicinity of Shivapuri Nagarjuna National Park which is a place of cool shades, beautiful streams, and a serene atmosphere.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe start our first-day trek to reach Chisapani <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagarkot\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Nagarkot</a> from Sundarijal which takes about 4 to 5 hours of walk. Chisapani is a beautiful place to host some majestic views of the Himalayan range. These Himalayas emit an ethereal glow in the setting sunlight.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe resume a second-day trip heading toward Nagarkot, along the ridge to the temple known as Changu Narayan temple. This temple hosts a nice view of Sankhu village and the Bhaktapur area. After some hours of exploration, we drive back to Kathmandu.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Chisapani Sundarijal trekking</strong> from Kathmandu is one of the best destination places to spend some quality time far away from the busy city. Witness the amazing hills, mountains, streams, and many more. The itinerary has been designed in detail keeping in mind the safety and enjoyment of the journey.", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "Explore the wonders of nature, the local lifestyle", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "5. What to expect on tours?", "_ws_trip_fact_short_description": "field_63ec73a69d305", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "01", "ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "02", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "Early morning breakfast and one hour drive to Sundarijal then trek to Chisapani ", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": " Hike Chisapani to Sankhu. Drive back to Kathmandu.", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "Extended Tours", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title": "Alternate Tours", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "5 hours", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "4-5 hours", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "2050m", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "1350m", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "The drive from Kathmandu to Sundarijal takes about one hour. From Sundarijal, we start our trek toward Chisapani. Pass through a few settlements and dense forests to reach Chisapani. The total duration of the hike is nearly five hours. Chisapani is a Sherpa village, offering grand views of the mountains. Relive yourself in the evening by watching a picturesque sunset from the village. Overnight at teahouse.", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "We resume our trek toward Nagarkot from Chisapani. It will take about 7 hours to walk. The trail passes mostly through the dense forest of the national park to reach Chauki Bhanjyang or Jhule. Then we continue our trek along the idyllic countryside to Nagarkot, a hilltop to the east of Kathmandu. Along the ridge of Nagarkot, you can witness the Changu Narayan temple. This place offers an amazing view of the Sankhu and Bhaktapur areas. After some hours of exploration, we drive back to Kathmandu. Overnight in Kathmandu.", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">1 day Kathmandu sightseeing Tour - 4-8 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630"}, "categoryId": null, "meta_title": "Chisapani Sundarijal Trekking from Kathmandu", "blogContent": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Explore the wonders of nature, the local lifestyle\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eChisapani Sundarijal Trekking\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e from Kathmandu is designed to provide you with a unique opportunity in a short time. You will explore the wonders of nature, the local lifestyle, the rural activities of Nepal, and the awe-inspiring majesty and beauty of dramatic mountain views.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\" Chisapani and Nagarkot\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eChisapani Sundarijal\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e trekking is a short and exciting trip around the Kathmandu valley. This trek combines the best of nature with typical local life. It also includes a gorgeous Himalayan view, a captivating sunset, and ethereal sunrise from Chisapani and Nagarkot. This hike is an ideal vacation in a matter of two days and is suitable for all age groups.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe trip starts with a short drive to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSundarijal\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, a popular hangout and demanding picnic spot in the north of Kathmandu. It lies in the vicinity of Shivapuri Nagarjuna National Park which is a place of cool shades, beautiful streams, and a serene atmosphere.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe start our first-day trek to reach Chisapani \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagarkot\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eNagarkot\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e from Sundarijal which takes about 4 to 5 hours of walk. Chisapani is a beautiful place to host some majestic views of the Himalayan range. These Himalayas emit an ethereal glow in the setting sunlight.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe resume a second-day trip heading toward Nagarkot, along the ridge to the temple known as Changu Narayan temple. This temple hosts a nice view of Sankhu village and the Bhaktapur area. After some hours of exploration, we drive back to Kathmandu.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eChisapani Sundarijal trekking\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e from Kathmandu is one of the best destination places to spend some quality time far away from the busy city. Witness the amazing hills, mountains, streams, and many more. The itinerary has been designed in detail keeping in mind the safety and enjoyment of the journey.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4334\\",\\"4304\\",\\"3966\\",\\"738\\",\\"863\\",\\"3965\\",\\"603\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Early morning breakfast and one hour drive to Sundarijal then trek to Chisapani \\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"2050m\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"5 hours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"The drive from Kathmandu to Sundarijal takes about one hour. From Sundarijal, we start our trek toward Chisapani. Pass through a few settlements and dense forests to reach Chisapani. The total duration of the hike is nearly five hours. Chisapani is a Sherpa village, offering grand views of the mountains. Relive yourself in the evening by watching a picturesque sunset from the village. Overnight at teahouse.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\" Hike Chisapani to Sankhu. Drive back to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"1350m\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"4-5 hours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"We resume our trek toward Nagarkot from Chisapani. It will take about 7 hours to walk. The trail passes mostly through the dense forest of the national park to reach Chauki Bhanjyang or Jhule. Then we continue our trek along the idyllic countryside to Nagarkot, a hilltop to the east of Kathmandu. Along the ridge of Nagarkot, you can witness the Changu Narayan temple. This place offers an amazing view of the Sankhu and Bhaktapur areas. After some hours of exploration, we drive back to Kathmandu. Overnight in Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFully private trip \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVehicle fuel, vehicle tax.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking cultural city tour guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrinking Water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e1 day Kathmandu sightseeing Tour - 4-8 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"Explore the wonders of nature, the local lifestyle\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eChisapani Sundarijal Trekking\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e from Kathmandu is designed to provide you with a unique opportunity in a short time. You will explore the wonders of nature, the local lifestyle, the rural activities of Nepal, and the awe-inspiring majesty and beauty of dramatic mountain views.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\" Chisapani and Nagarkot\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eChisapani Sundarijal\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e trekking is a short and exciting trip around the Kathmandu valley. This trek combines the best of nature with typical local life. It also includes a gorgeous Himalayan view, a captivating sunset, and ethereal sunrise from Chisapani and Nagarkot. This hike is an ideal vacation in a matter of two days and is suitable for all age groups.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe trip starts with a short drive to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSundarijal\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, a popular hangout and demanding picnic spot in the north of Kathmandu. It lies in the vicinity of Shivapuri Nagarjuna National Park which is a place of cool shades, beautiful streams, and a serene atmosphere.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe start our first-day trek to reach Chisapani \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagarkot\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eNagarkot\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e from Sundarijal which takes about 4 to 5 hours of walk. Chisapani is a beautiful place to host some majestic views of the Himalayan range. These Himalayas emit an ethereal glow in the setting sunlight.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe resume a second-day trip heading toward Nagarkot, along the ridge to the temple known as Changu Narayan temple. This temple hosts a nice view of Sankhu village and the Bhaktapur area. After some hours of exploration, we drive back to Kathmandu.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eChisapani Sundarijal trekking\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e from Kathmandu is one of the best destination places to spend some quality time far away from the busy city. Witness the amazing hills, mountains, streams, and many more. The itinerary has been designed in detail keeping in mind the safety and enjoyment of the journey.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4334\\",\\"4304\\",\\"3966\\",\\"738\\",\\"863\\",\\"3965\\",\\"603\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Early morning breakfast and one hour drive to Sundarijal then trek to Chisapani \\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"2050m\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"5 hours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"The drive from Kathmandu to Sundarijal takes about one hour. From Sundarijal, we start our trek toward Chisapani. Pass through a few settlements and dense forests to reach Chisapani. The total duration of the hike is nearly five hours. Chisapani is a Sherpa village, offering grand views of the mountains. Relive yourself in the evening by watching a picturesque sunset from the village. Overnight at teahouse.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\" Hike Chisapani to Sankhu. Drive back to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"1350m\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"4-5 hours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"We resume our trek toward Nagarkot from Chisapani. It will take about 7 hours to walk. The trail passes mostly through the dense forest of the national park to reach Chauki Bhanjyang or Jhule. Then we continue our trek along the idyllic countryside to Nagarkot, a hilltop to the east of Kathmandu. Along the ridge of Nagarkot, you can witness the Changu Narayan temple. This place offers an amazing view of the Sankhu and Bhaktapur areas. After some hours of exploration, we drive back to Kathmandu. Overnight in Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFully private trip \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVehicle fuel, vehicle tax.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking cultural city tour guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrinking Water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_section_title\\":\\"field_63ede33e5b304\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"Extended Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eHelicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShort 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e1 day Kathmandu sightseeing Tour - 4-8 hours\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eKathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"Alternate Tours\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_title\\":\\"field_63ec91180462f\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu \\\\u0026amp; Pokhara\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003e2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_information_description\\":\\"field_63ec913e04630\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":2,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec90a574f02\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/nagarkot-hill-hiking.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmandu-valley.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/village-local-life.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/nagarkot-evening.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/nagarkot-hike.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/nagakot.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/sunrise-tour-nagarkot.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=906", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "906", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-08 05:33:56", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-08 05:33:56", "post_modified": "2024-02-13 05:59:44", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-02-13 05:59:44"}}, "customSections": [{"id": 1, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Extended Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">1 day Kathmandu sightseeing Tour - 4-8 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp - 4-5 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area - 1 hour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu - 4-6 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/1-day-kathmandu-sightseeing-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">1 day Kathmandu sightseeing Tour - 4-8 hours</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour - 4 days</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": 2, "type": "paragraph", "title": "Alternate Tours", "content": ["<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"], "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 days easy hiking / trekking around Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/3-days-kathmandu-cultural-tour-with-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">2 Days Kathmandu Cultural Tour + 1 day hike</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>"}, {"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["<strong>Chisapani Sundarijal</strong> trekking is a short and exciting trip around the Kathmandu valley. This trek combines the best of nature with typical local life. It also includes a gorgeous Himalayan view, a captivating sunset, and ethereal sunrise from Chisapani and Nagarkot. This hike is an ideal vacation in a matter of two days and is suitable for all age groups.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe trip starts with a short drive to <strong>Sundarijal</strong>, a popular hangout and demanding picnic spot in the north of Kathmandu. It lies in the vicinity of Shivapuri Nagarjuna National Park which is a place of cool shades, beautiful streams, and a serene atmosphere.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe start our first-day trek to reach Chisapani <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagarkot\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Nagarkot</a> from Sundarijal which takes about 4 to 5 hours of walk. Chisapani is a beautiful place to host some majestic views of the Himalayan range. These Himalayas emit an ethereal glow in the setting sunlight.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe resume a second-day trip heading toward Nagarkot, along the ridge to the temple known as Changu Narayan temple. This temple hosts a nice view of Sankhu village and the Bhaktapur area. After some hours of exploration, we drive back to Kathmandu.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Chisapani Sundarijal trekking</strong> from Kathmandu is one of the best destination places to spend some quality time far away from the busy city. Witness the amazing hills, mountains, streams, and many more. The itinerary has been designed in detail keeping in mind the safety and enjoyment of the journey."], "description": "<strong>Chisapani Sundarijal</strong> trekking is a short and exciting trip around the Kathmandu valley. This trek combines the best of nature with typical local life. It also includes a gorgeous Himalayan view, a captivating sunset, and ethereal sunrise from Chisapani and Nagarkot. This hike is an ideal vacation in a matter of two days and is suitable for all age groups.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe trip starts with a short drive to <strong>Sundarijal</strong>, a popular hangout and demanding picnic spot in the north of Kathmandu. It lies in the vicinity of Shivapuri Nagarjuna National Park which is a place of cool shades, beautiful streams, and a serene atmosphere.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe start our first-day trek to reach Chisapani <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagarkot\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Nagarkot</a> from Sundarijal which takes about 4 to 5 hours of walk. Chisapani is a beautiful place to host some majestic views of the Himalayan range. These Himalayas emit an ethereal glow in the setting sunlight.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe resume a second-day trip heading toward Nagarkot, along the ridge to the temple known as Changu Narayan temple. This temple hosts a nice view of Sankhu village and the Bhaktapur area. After some hours of exploration, we drive back to Kathmandu.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Chisapani Sundarijal trekking</strong> from Kathmandu is one of the best destination places to spend some quality time far away from the busy city. Witness the amazing hills, mountains, streams, and many more. The itinerary has been designed in detail keeping in mind the safety and enjoyment of the journey."}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Fully private trip (even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.", "Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).", "Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.", "English speaking cultural city tour guide.", "Drinking Water."], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Fully private trip (even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.", "Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).", "Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.", "English speaking cultural city tour guide.", "Drinking Water."], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "Explore Chisapani Sundarijal Trekking from Kathmandu with Everest Vacation.", "trip_highlights": "<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Chisapani Sundarijal Trekking</strong> from Kathmandu is designed to provide you with a unique opportunity in a short time. You will explore the wonders of nature, the local lifestyle, the rural activities of Nepal, and the awe-inspiring majesty and beauty of dramatic mountain views.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "trip_type_level": "Easy", "meta_description": "Chisapani Sundarijal trekking from Kathmandu is one of the best destination places to spend some quality time far away from the busy city.", "trip_attractions": "Chisapani and Nagarkot", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "faq_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "Chisapani and Nagarkot", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": "Private AC Vehicle"}, "trip_transportations": "Private AC Vehicle", "trip_highlights_title": "Explore the wonders of nature, the local lifestyle"}	2023-12-08 05:33:56+00	2024-02-13 05:59:44+00
200	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "4", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Short and Easy"}, "faq": [{"answer": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "question": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "question": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "question": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "question": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "question": "5. What to expect on tours?"}], "meta": {"_edit_last": "1", "_edit_lock": "1760692571:1", "_dp_original": "904", "_thumbnail_id": "769", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "4", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "Dhampus to Ghandruk Village Trekking", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Dhampus to Ghandruk Village Trekking", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "58", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Dhampus to Ghandruk Village trekking is one of the best of the Annapurna treks which starts from Nayapul and ends at Phedi.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Short and Easy", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_content_score": "90", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "dhampus-to-ghandruk-village-trekking", "tags": [], "title": "Dhampus to Ghandruk Village Trekking", "duration": "4 Days", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "<strong>Dhampus to Ghandruk Village trekking </strong>is one of the best of the Annapurna treks which starts from Nayapul and ends at Phedi. It is one of the shortest treks in the Annapurna region. The main aim of this trek is to visit one of the most beautiful Gurung villages <strong>Ghandruk</strong>. It is located at an elevation of (2012m) and you can witness the Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Gangapurna, and <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machapuchare\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Machhapuchhre</a> (Fish Tail).\\r\\n\\r\\nIt is a huge Gurung village where you can visit the old and new Gurung museum which shows the real culture of the Gurung Community. Gurung is one of the ethnic groups of Nepal and they have their distinct language and customs. They are known as Gorkhali because most of the British armies are from their community.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis trek goes along the tiny villages of Syauli Bazar, Landruk, Tolkha, Pothana, and Dhampus. You can behold the excellent view of Mt. Dhaulagiri, Annapurna South, Fishtail, Annapurna III, Lamjung Himal, and the entire Pokhara Valley. The unique culture of Gurung and Magar, different sorts of flora and fauna, and the green view of the rural areas of Nepal and Pokhara Valley are the main attractions of this trek. The best season is from August to May."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Drive to Nayapul from Pokhara then Trek to Ghandruk", "richText": "Drive to Nayapul (1070m) which takes one and a half hours and trek to Ghandruk through the beautiful countryside with a panoramic view of Mt. Fishtail, Annapurna South, and Gangapurna. The way gently climbs up from Syauli Bazar and finally arrives at Ghandruk which takes around 6/7 hours.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 2, "meal": "", "title": "Trek to Tolka via Landruk", "richText": "Ghandruk is a huge Gurung village from where the trail descends to Kyumi Bridge and a short climb to Landruk. It is one of the most beautiful villages. From here, we continue to Tolka with the beautiful scenery of the green countryside. We spent a night there.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 3, "meal": "", "title": "Trek to Australian Camp", "richText": "On the next day, we started the trek after breakfast.  The way goes through dense forest and finally arrives at Deurali. From the trail continue through the green jungle to Pothana and arrive at the Australian camp at last. Australian Camp is a beautiful village best known for its sunrise, sunset, and view of the Annapurna range, Machhapuchhre, and beautiful green hills. We stayed there for a night.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 4, "meal": "", "title": "Trek to Dharmasala Phedi and Drive to Pokhara", "richText": "Then catch the transportation drive to Pokhara and transfer to a hotel (Breakfast will be served at Tea House Lodge restaurant). All the way follows a gradual descent to the final point Phedi. You will pass many cultural hamlets and their hill-terraced traditional Farmland. At the ending place, you will be picked up by transport and driven to Pokhara for lunch and rest overnight at a hotel.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/pokhara-machhapuchre-sunrise.jpg", "title": "pokhara-machhapuchre-sunrise", "altText": "pokhara-machhapuchre-sunrise", "caption": "pokhara-machhapuchre-sunrise", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["4831", "4830", "4829", "4828", "5895", "5896", "5897", "5898", "5899", "5900", "5901", "5902", "5903", "5904"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "ws_trip_faqs_lists": 5, "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists": "field_63ede38e351c7", "ws_block_attractions": "", "ws_block_best_season": "Any Season", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-light", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": "Dhampus to Ghandruk Village Trek Overview", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc6695edb31", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_block_transportation": "Private AC Vehicle", "ws_trip_galleries_title": "Photo/Visual Gallery", "_ws_block_transportation": "field_63eeee74072de", "_ws_trip_galleries_title": "field_63ec89128acaa", "starter_kit_padding_type": "p-medium", "ws_trip_block_highlights": "<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nThe main aim of this trek is to visit one of the most beautiful Gurung villages Ghandruk. It is located on an elevation of (1090m) and you can witness the Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Gangapurna, and Fish Tail.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "ws_trip_information_list": 4, "_starter_kit_padding_type": "field_5f8584c998bc2", "_ws_trip_block_highlights": "field_63ec73a6a0d8f", "_ws_trip_information_list": "field_63ec94565c587", "starter_kit_section_title": "Sample Itinerary: Day by Day Activities", "_starter_kit_section_title": "field_63ec948c94a16", "starter_kit_enable_section": "1", "_starter_kit_enable_section": "field_63edeb1c7635c", "starter_kit_section_padding": "", "ws_trip_include_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Fully private trip </strong>(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>English speaking cultural city tour guide.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drinking Water.</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_starter_kit_section_padding": "field_5f3e0f86a2634", "_ws_trip_include_description": "field_63edd6a337cd0", "ws_trip_overview_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Region: Annapurna, Nepal</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Difficulty: Easy to Moderate</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Duration: 2–5 days (depending on pace)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Max. Altitude: ~2,010m (Ghandruk)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Best Season: Spring (March–May) &amp; Autumn (Sept–Nov)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Permits: TIMS card + Annapurna Conservation Area Permit (ACAP)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Total Trekking Distance: ~25–30 km (varies by route).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Daily Walking: 2–6 hours (varies by number of days).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Trail Type: Stone steps, forest paths, terraced fields, and villages.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Here are 10 highlights of the Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek that make it a must-do adventure in Nepal’s Annapurna region:</strong></h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Stunning Mountain Views\\r\\n</strong>Panoramic vistas of <strong>Annapurna South, Machapuchare (Fishtail), Hiunchuli</strong>, and Dhaulagiri from Australian Camp, Dhampus, and Ghandruk.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"2\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Australian Camp Sunrise/Sunset\\r\\n</strong>One of the <strong>best viewpoints</strong> in the Annapurna foothills, offering golden sunrises over the Himalayas.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"3\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Authentic Gurung Culture\\r\\n</strong>Experience the <strong>traditional Gurung villages</strong> of Dhampus, Landruk, and Ghandruk, known for their stone houses, warm hospitality, and rich cultural heritage.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"4\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Ghandruk Village (Largest Gurung Settlement)\\r\\n</strong>A beautifully preserved Gurung village with <strong>mountain views, a cultural museum, and homestays</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"5\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Short &amp; Beginner-Friendly Trek\\r\\n</strong>Only <strong>2–4 days</strong> with easy-to-moderate trails, perfect for first-time trekkers or those with limited time.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"6\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Terraced Farmlands &amp; Rhododendron Forests\\r\\n</strong>Walk through lush <strong>rice fields, terraced farms</strong>, and (in spring) vibrant <strong>rhododendron blooms</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"7\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> No Risk of Altitude Sickness\\r\\n</strong>Max altitude is only <strong>2,010m (Ghandruk)</strong>, making it safe for all ages and fitness levels.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"8\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Great Teahouse Experience\\r\\n</strong>Cozy lodges with <strong>mountain views, local food (dal bhat, momos), and friendly hosts</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"9\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Flexible Route Options\\r\\n</strong>Start/end at <strong>Phedi, Kande, Nayapul, or Australian Camp</strong>, with options to extend to <strong>Poon Hill or Tadapani</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"10\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Close to Pokhara (Easy Access)\\r\\n</strong>Just <strong>1–2 hours’ drive</strong> from Pokhara, making it a perfect add-on to a Nepal trip.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<strong>Bonus Highlight: Wildlife Spotting\\r\\n</strong>Chance to see <strong>langur monkeys, Himalayan birds, and butterflies</strong> along the trail.\\r\\n<h3><strong>Here are </strong><strong>10 more compelling reasons</strong><strong> to choose the </strong><strong>Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek</strong><strong>, making it an unbeatable Himalayan experience:</strong></h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Perfect for Solo Trekkers &amp; Families\\r\\n</strong>Safe, well-marked trails with frequent teahouses—ideal for solo adventurers, couples, and families with kids.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"2\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> No Crowds (Compared to Everest or ABC)\\r\\n</strong>Enjoy peaceful trails without the mass tourism of longer treks, especially if you avoid peak season (Oct–Nov).</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"3\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Affordable (Low-Budget Friendly)\\r\\n</strong>Minimal costs for food/lodging—no need for expensive guides or flights like in remote regions.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"4\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Year-Round Trekking Possible\\r\\n</strong>Doable even in <strong>winter (Dec–Feb)</strong> and <strong>monsoon (June–Aug)</strong>—just expect rain or chilly nights.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"5\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Minimal Packing Needed\\r\\n</strong>No extreme cold gear required—just layers, good shoes, and a rain jacket (depending on season).</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"6\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Cultural Stops Along the Way\\r\\n</strong>Visit the <strong>Gurung Museum in Ghandruk</strong>, Buddhist stupas, and local craft workshops.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"7\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Delicious Local &amp; Western Food\\r\\n</strong>Teahouses serve everything from <strong>dal bhat</strong> to pasta, apple pie, and even espresso!</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"8\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Optional Adventure Add-Ons\\r\\n</strong>Extend to <strong>Poon Hill (3,210m)</strong> or <strong>Tadapani</strong> for more challenging trails and epic views.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"9\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Photography Paradise\\r\\n</strong>Capture <strong>sunrises over Fishtail, terraced farms, traditional villages, and starry night skies</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"10\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Easy Escape to Pokhara’s Comfort\\r\\n</strong>After the trek, unwind by <strong>Phewa Lake</strong> with cafes, spas, and paragliding!</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Common Route:</strong></h3>\\r\\nStarting Point: Phedi or Dhampus (1–2 hrs drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nEnding Point: Ghandruk (return via Nayapul or loop back to Pokhara).\\r\\n\\r\\nDay 1: Pokhara → Phedi (drive) → Trek to Dhampus (1.5–2 hrs).\\r\\nDay 2: Dhampus → Pothana → Landruk (5–6 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nDay 4: Ghandruk → Nayapul (4–5 hrs) → Drive to Pokhara.\\r\\n<h3><strong>Multiple Starting Points for Dhampus-Ghandruk Trek</strong></h3>\\r\\n<h3><strong style=\\"font-size: 16px;\\">Phedi/Dhampus (Standard Route)</strong></h3>\\r\\nStart: Phedi (1-hour drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Phedi → Dhampus (1.5–2 hrs trek).\\r\\nDay 2: Dhampus → Australian Camp → Pothana → Landruk (5–6 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nEnd: Ghandruk → Nayapul (4–5 hrs) → Drive to Pokhara.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Kande (Via Australian Camp – Popular Route)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nStart: Kande (1.5-hour drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Kande → Australian Camp (1–1.5 hrs steep climb).\\r\\nDay 2: Australian Camp → Pothana → Landruk (4–5 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nEnd: Ghandruk → Nayapul → Pokhara.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Australian Camp Direct (Short &amp; Scenic)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nStart: Drive to Australian Camp (private jeep from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Explore Australian Camp (sunset/sunrise views).\\r\\nDay 2: Australian Camp → Landruk (4–5 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nEnd: Return via Nayapul or extend to Tadapani.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Nayapul (Classic Annapurna Route)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nStart: Nayapul (2-hour drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Nayapul → Birethanti → Ghandruk (5–6 hrs).\\r\\nDay 2: Ghandruk → Landruk → Tolka (optional).\\r\\nDay 3: Tolka → Australian Camp → Kande (loop back).\\r\\n<h3><strong>Multiple Ending Points</strong></h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Nayapul (Most Common)\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>From Ghandruk, descend to Birethanti → Nayapul (4–5 hrs).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Take a bus/taxi to Pokhara (1.5 hrs).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kimche (Jeep Option)\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>From Ghandruk, trek 1.5 hrs to Kimche → Take a jeep to Pokhara.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Loop Back to Australian Camp/Kande\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ghandruk → Landruk → Pothana → Australian Camp → Kande (longer loop).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Extend to Tadapani/Poon Hill\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>From Ghandruk, trek to Tadapani (3–4 hrs) → Continue to Ghorepani/Poon Hill.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<strong>Key Variations &amp; Highlights</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp → Best for sunrise/sunset over Annapurna range.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kande Start → Saves time; steep but rewarding.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Landruk Detour → Quieter than Ghandruk, great homestays.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Nayapul Start/End → Classic Annapurna Sanctuary approach.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<strong>Which Route to Choose?</strong>\\r\\n<table class=\\"table table-bordered table-responsive\\">\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Phedi → Dhampus → Ghandruk</td>\\r\\n<td>3–4 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Easy-Moderate</td>\\r\\n<td>First-timers</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Kande → Australian Camp → Ghandruk</td>\\r\\n<td>3 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Moderate</td>\\r\\n<td>Scenic views</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Australian Camp Direct → Ghandruk</td>\\r\\n<td>2–3 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Easy</td>\\r\\n<td>Short &amp; sweet</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Nayapul → Ghandruk Loop</td>\\r\\n<td>4–5 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Moderate</td>\\r\\n<td>Extended trek</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n</tbody>\\r\\n</table>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Altitude Sickness (AMS)</strong></h4>\\r\\nRisk: Low (Ghandruk is only 2,010m).\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Precautions:</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Stay hydrated.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ascend gradually (no rapid climbs).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Watch for headaches/nausea (descend if severe).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Packing List</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Clothing: Layers, rain jacket, trekking pants, hat, gloves.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Footwear: Sturdy trekking shoes + sandals.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Gear: Backpack, water bottle, trekking poles, sunscreen.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Misc: First-aid kit, cash (no ATMs), camera.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Permits and Costs</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>ACAP Permit: NPR 3,000 (foreigners), NPR 1,000 (SAARC).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>TIMS Card: NPR 2,000.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Accommodation &amp; Meals</strong></h3>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Basic Accommodation</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Teahouses/Lodges: Basic but comfortable; costs around NPR 1000 per night.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Rooms: Twin-sharing with common toilets (hot showers may cost extra).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Electricity/WiFi: Limited; charging devices may cost NPR 100–300/hour.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Mid-Range Hotels/Lodges with Attached Bathrooms</strong></h4>\\r\\n<h6><strong>Australian Camp Area</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Himalayan Front Hotel\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (hot water included).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Stunning Annapurna views, clean rooms, cozy dining area.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Australian Camp Guest House\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Some rooms (confirm when booking).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Friendly hosts, great sunrise views.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Dhampus Village</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Dhampus Peak Lodge\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (24-hour solar hot water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Spacious rooms, mountain-facing balconies.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Landruk Village</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Gurung Cottage\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (hot shower).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Authentic Gurung hospitality, rooftop terrace.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Sunset Lodge\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (electric-heated water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Quiet location, great food.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Ghandruk Village</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Himalaya Lodge\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (reliable hot water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Best views of Annapurna South, cozy fireplace lounge.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Ghandruk Guest House\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (solar-heated water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Central location, clean and modern.\\r\\n<h4><strong>Luxury Resorts &amp; Boutique Hotels on the Trek</strong></h4>\\r\\n<h6><strong>Mountain Lodges of Nepal - Dhampus)</strong></h6>\\r\\nType: Eco-luxury resort with private villas.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Private plunge pools with Annapurna views.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Organic farm-to-table dining.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Spa services (Ayurvedic massages).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Solar-powered, eco-friendly design.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Honeymooners or travelers seeking luxury before/after the trek.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Gurung Cottage (Ghandruk)</strong></h6>\\r\\nLocation: Ghandruk village.\\r\\n\\r\\nType: Boutique family-run lodge with upgraded facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Attached bathrooms with hot showers.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Rooftop terrace for sunrise/sunset views.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Authentic Gurung cuisine (dhal bhat, homemade wine).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Cozy fireplaces in rooms.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Trekkers wanting comfort in Ghandruk.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Himalayan Front Hotel (Australian Camp)</strong></h6>\\r\\nLocation: Australian Camp.\\r\\n\\r\\nType: Mid-range luxury with premium services.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Panoramic views of Annapurna and Machapuchare.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Glass-walled dining hall.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Warm blankets, clean rooms, and Western toilets.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Sunrise photographers and comfort seekers.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Ker &amp; Downey Lodges (Landruk)</strong></h6>\\r\\nLocation: Landruk village (between Dhampus &amp; Ghandruk).\\r\\n\\r\\nType: High-end lodge chain.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Luxury bedding and modern bathrooms.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Gourmet meals (international + Nepali dishes).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Quiet, less-touristed location.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Peaceful luxury in a traditional village.\\r\\n<h3>Budget vs. Mid-range vs. Luxury Comparison</h3>\\r\\n<table class=\\"table table-bordered table-responsive\\">\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td><strong>Feature</strong></td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\"><strong>Budget Teahouse</strong></td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\"><strong>Mid-Range Lodge</strong></td>\\r\\n<td><strong>Luxury Lodges</strong></td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Price/Night</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\">Below USD 10</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">USD 20-40</td>\\r\\n<td>USD 100–400+</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Bathroom</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\">Shared (cold water)</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">Private (hot water)</td>\\r\\n<td>Private (hot shower)</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Room Quality</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\">Basic wooden beds</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">Clean, comfy beds</td>\\r\\n<td>Heated, premium linens</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Food</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\"><strong>Breakfast</strong>: Porridge, toast, eggs, Tibetan bread, tea/coffee.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Lunch/Dinner</strong>: Dal Bhat (lentil soup + rice), noodles, pasta, momos, soups.</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">As per your choice,\\r\\nEg: Pasta, pizza, better coffee</td>\\r\\n<td>As per your choice, Eg: Gourmet / International</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n</tbody>\\r\\n</table>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Senior-friendly &amp; luxury-focused itinerary for the Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek</strong></h3>\\r\\n<strong>Designed for travelers who prefer shorter walking days (2–4 hours/day), comfortable stays, and scenic drives to minimize exertion while maximizing Himalayan views and cultural experiences.</strong>\\r\\n<h4><strong><u>5-Day Luxury Itinerary (With Minimal Trekking)</u></strong></h4>\\r\\nTheme: <em>\\"Slow-Paced Comfort in the Annapurna Foothills\\"</em>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 1: Pokhara → Drive to Australian Camp (Sunset Magic)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nMorning: Private jeep transfer from Pokhara to Kande (1.5 hrs).\\r\\nTrek: Gentle 1-hour uphill walk to Australian Camp (2,050m).\\r\\nStay: <em>Himalayan Front Hotel</em> (private bathroom, mountain-view balcony).\\r\\nHighlight: Sunset over Annapurna South with champagne!\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 2: Australian Camp → Landruk (Easy Descent)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nTrek: 2–3 hours downhill via Pothana and Deurali to Landruk (1,560m).\\r\\nStay: <em>Ker &amp; Downey Lodge Landruk</em> (luxury rooms, hot showers, garden seating).\\r\\nHighlight: Gurung cultural dinner with local dance (optional).\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (Short Riverside Walk)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nTrek: 2.5 hours along the Modi Khola River to Ghandruk (2,010m).\\r\\nStay: <em>Himalaya Lodge</em> (deluxe room with fireplace, attached bathroom).\\r\\nHighlight: Visit the Gurung Museum and relax with a hot stone massage.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 4: Ghandruk Exploration (Zero Trekking Day)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nMorning: Sunrise yoga session with Annapurna views.\\r\\nActivity: Guided village tour (traditional homes, weaving demo).\\r\\nStay: Second night at <em>Himalaya Lodge</em>.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 5: Ghandruk → Nayapul → Pokhara (Jeep Option)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nOption 1 (Trek + Drive): 2-hour gentle walk to Kimche → Private jeep to Pokhara (1.5 hrs).\\r\\nOption 2 (No Trek): Direct jeep from Ghandruk to Pokhara (3 hrs, bumpy but scenic).\\r\\n<h4><strong>Alternatives for Zero-Trekking Travelers</strong></h4>\\r\\n<strong>Heli-Trek Combo:</strong>\\r\\nDay 1: Pokhara → Heli to Ghandruk (15 mins). Stay 2 nights, explore village.\\r\\nDay 3: Heli return or jeep to Pokhara.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Pokhara-Based Day Trips:</strong>\\r\\nDrive to Australian Camp for lunch/sunset → Return same day.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Packing Tips for Seniors/Luxury Trekkers</strong></h6>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Footwear: Non-slip hiking sandals (e.g., Keen) + trekking poles.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Extras: Portable oxygen canister (for breathlessness), knee braces.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Clothing: Light down jacket (mornings are chilly even in spring).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h6><strong>Why This Itinerary Works?</strong></h6>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Max Elevation: Only 2,010m (Ghandruk)—no altitude risks.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Walking Hours: ≤3 hours/day with breaks.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Cultural Depth: More time to interact with locals vs. rushing trails.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3><strong>FAQs </strong></h3>\\r\\nQ: Is a guide necessary?\\r\\nA: Not mandatory, but helpful for navigation/culture.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can solo trekkers join groups?\\r\\nA: Yes, teahouses are social; or join organized tours.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Phone network?\\r\\nA: Ncell/NTC work sporadically; WiFi is paid.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Is it safe for beginners?\\r\\nA: Yes, but fitness helps for stone steps/long walks.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Wildlife sightings?\\r\\nA: Possible: monkeys, birds, occasional langurs.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I start from Pokhara directly?\\r\\nA: No, you need to drive to Phedi/Kande/Nayapul (1–2 hrs).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Is Australian Camp worth adding?\\r\\nA: Yes! Best mountain views and cozy lodges.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Which route has fewer stairs?\\r\\nA: Kande → Australian Camp has fewer steps than Phedi → Dhampus.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I end at Kimche instead of Nayapul?\\r\\nA: Yes, Kimche has jeeps to Pokhara (saves trekking time).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Is a guide needed for these routes?\\r\\nA: Not mandatory, but helpful for navigation in loop trails.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are there hotels with attached bathrooms and hot showers on this trek?\\r\\nA: Yes! Mid-range and luxury lodges like <em>Himalayan Front Hotel (Australian Camp)</em>, <em>Himalaya Lodge (Ghandruk)</em>, and <em>Ker &amp; Downey Lodges (Landruk)</em> offer private bathrooms, 24/7 hot water, and comfortable beds. Budget teahouses may charge extra for hot showers.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I book accommodations in advance?\\r\\nA: Yes, especially in peak season (Oct–Nov, Mar–Apr). Luxury lodges require advance reservations. Your guide/agency can arrange this.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are there electric blankets or heaters in rooms?\\r\\nA: Most luxury lodges provide heaters or extra blankets. Budget teahouses rely on thick quilts—ask for a \\"deluxe room\\" for better comfort.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: What’s the best way to reach the trek start point from Pokhara?\\r\\nA: Private jeep (most comfortable) to Phedi (1 hr) or Kande (1.5 hrs) or Nayapul (2 hrs)\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I skip trekking entirely and use vehicles?\\r\\nA: Partially! You can:\\r\\nDrive to Australian Camp (via Kande, then 1-hr walk).\\r\\nJeep from Ghandruk to Kimche/Nayapul (bumpy but saves walking).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are roads safe for seniors?\\r\\nA: Roads are rough but manageable in a 4WD jeep. Avoid monsoon (June–Aug) due to landslides.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: What cultural activities can I do in Ghandruk?\\r\\nA: Visit the Gurung Museum (traditional costumes, weapons).\\r\\nAttend a local dance performance (arranged by lodges).\\r\\nTry Gurung cuisine: <em>dal bhat</em>, <em>gundruk</em> (fermented greens), and <em>raksi</em> (local alcohol).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I participate in a homestay?\\r\\nA: Yes! Gurung Cottage (Ghandruk) and Landruk homestays offer authentic experiences. Book ahead.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are villages wheelchair-friendly?\\r\\nA: No—trails have stone steps and uneven paths. Seniors with mobility issues should opt for jeep/heli access.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are there yoga retreats or sessions along the trek?\\r\\nA: Yes!\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp: Sunrise yoga with mountain views (ask your lodge or guide).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ghandruk: <em>Himalaya Lodge</em>offers yoga mats and guided sessions.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pokhara Add-On: Post-trek relaxation with yoga.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Can I meditate in the mountains?\\r\\nA: Absolutely! Silent spots:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp (sunrise meditation).\\r\\nGhandruk’s sunrise viewpoint.\\r\\nLandruk’s terraced farms.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Is altitude sickness a risk?\\r\\nA: Minimal (max altitude: 2,010m). Seniors should still:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Stay hydrated.\\r\\nWalk slowly.\\r\\nAvoid alcohol.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: What if I get tired during the trek?\\r\\nA: Options:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hire a mule to ride between villages.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Shorten walks (e.g., drive to Landruk, then trek 1 hr to Ghandruk).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Are there pharmacies or doctors on the trail?\\r\\nA: Basic clinics in Ghandruk/Landruk. Carry medications, knee braces, and a first-aid kit.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I get vegetarian/vegan food?\\r\\nA: Yes! Teahouses serve:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Veg <em>dal bhat</em>, noodles, soups, and fresh <em>sel roti</em>(Nepali donuts).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Luxury lodges offer pasta, salads, and desserts.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Is bottled water available?\\r\\nA: Yes ($1–$3/bottle), but reduce plastic use by:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Carrying a SteriPen or purification tablets.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Asking lodges for boiled/filtered water.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Packing Tips for Seniors?\\r\\n\\r\\nA: Must-Haves: Trekking poles, knee sleeves, slip-proof shoes, and a small daypack.\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Luxury Add-Ons: Portable oxygen canister, inflatable neck pillow, and down booties for cold nights.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: When is the least crowded time?\\r\\nA: December–February (cold but clear) or September (post-monsoon greenery). Avoid monsoon (June–Aug).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: How cold does it get at night?\\r\\nA: 5–10°C (41–50°F) in autumn/spring. Luxury lodges provide heaters/extra blankets.\\r\\n<h3>Final Tips</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Start early to avoid afternoon clouds.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bargain lightly for souvenirs in Ghandruk.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Respect local customs (ask before photographing people).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp is crowded in peak season (Oct–Nov).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Landruk offers authentic Gurung culture with fewer tourists.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If short on time, do Kande → Australian Camp → Ghandruk → Nayapul (3 days).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>For a stress-free trek, book a private guide/porter (~$25–$50/day) to handle logistics, carry bags, and adjust pacing.</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "It is one of the shortest treks in the Annapurna region", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "5. What to expect on tours?", "_ws_trip_fact_short_description": "field_63ec73a69d305", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "field_63ede3af351c8", "ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "01", "ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "02", "ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "03", "ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "04", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description": "field_63ede3bf351c9", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": " Drive to Nayapul from Pokhara then Trek to Ghandruk", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "Trek to Tolka via Landruk", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "Trek to Australian Camp", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "Trek to Dharmasala Phedi and Drive to Pokhara", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "Drive to Nayapul (1070m) which takes one and a half hours and trek to Ghandruk through the beautiful countryside with a panoramic view of Mt. Fishtail, Annapurna South, and Gangapurna. The way gently climbs up from Syauli Bazar and finally arrives at Ghandruk which takes around 6/7 hours.", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "Ghandruk is a huge Gurung village from where the trail descends to Kyumi Bridge and a short climb to Landruk. It is one of the most beautiful villages. From here, we continue to Tolka with the beautiful scenery of the green countryside. We spent a night there.", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "On the next day, we started the trek after breakfast.  The way goes through dense forest and finally arrives at Deurali. From the trail continue through the green jungle to Pothana and arrive at the Australian camp at last. Australian Camp is a beautiful village best known for its sunrise, sunset, and view of the Annapurna range, Machhapuchhre, and beautiful green hills. We stayed there for a night.", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "Then catch the transportation drive to Pokhara and transfer to a hotel (Breakfast will be served at Tea House Lodge restaurant). All the way follows a gradual descent to the final point Phedi. You will pass many cultural hamlets and their hill-terraced traditional Farmland. At the ending place, you will be picked up by transport and driven to Pokhara for lunch and rest overnight at a hotel.", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6"}, "categoryId": null, "meta_title": "Dhampus to Ghandruk Village Trekking", "blogContent": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"It is one of the shortest treks in the Annapurna region\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe main aim of this trek is to visit one of the most beautiful Gurung villages Ghandruk. It is located on an elevation of (1090m) and you can witness the Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Gangapurna, and Fish Tail.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview \\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhampus to Ghandruk Village trekking \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eis one of the best of the Annapurna treks which starts from Nayapul and ends at Phedi. It is one of the shortest treks in the Annapurna region. The main aim of this trek is to visit one of the most beautiful Gurung villages \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGhandruk\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. It is located at an elevation of (2012m) and you can witness the Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Gangapurna, and \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machapuchare\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMachhapuchhre\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e (Fish Tail).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIt is a huge Gurung village where you can visit the old and new Gurung museum which shows the real culture of the Gurung Community. Gurung is one of the ethnic groups of Nepal and they have their distinct language and customs. They are known as Gorkhali because most of the British armies are from their community.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThis trek goes along the tiny villages of Syauli Bazar, Landruk, Tolkha, Pothana, and Dhampus. You can behold the excellent view of Mt. Dhaulagiri, Annapurna South, Fishtail, Annapurna III, Lamjung Himal, and the entire Pokhara Valley. The unique culture of Gurung and Magar, different sorts of flora and fauna, and the green view of the rural areas of Nepal and Pokhara Valley are the main attractions of this trek. The best season is from August to May.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4831\\",\\"4830\\",\\"4829\\",\\"4828\\",\\"5895\\",\\"5896\\",\\"5897\\",\\"5898\\",\\"5899\\",\\"5900\\",\\"5901\\",\\"5902\\",\\"5903\\",\\"5904\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Sample Itinerary: Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\" Drive to Nayapul from Pokhara then Trek to Ghandruk\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Drive to Nayapul (1070m) which takes one and a half hours and trek to Ghandruk through the beautiful countryside with a panoramic view of Mt. Fishtail, Annapurna South, and Gangapurna. The way gently climbs up from Syauli Bazar and finally arrives at Ghandruk which takes around 6/7 hours.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Tolka via Landruk\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Ghandruk is a huge Gurung village from where the trail descends to Kyumi Bridge and a short climb to Landruk. It is one of the most beautiful villages. From here, we continue to Tolka with the beautiful scenery of the green countryside. We spent a night there.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Australian Camp\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"On the next day, we started the trek after breakfast.  The way goes through dense forest and finally arrives at Deurali. From the trail continue through the green jungle to Pothana and arrive at the Australian camp at last. Australian Camp is a beautiful village best known for its sunrise, sunset, and view of the Annapurna range, Machhapuchhre, and beautiful green hills. We stayed there for a night.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Dharmasala Phedi and Drive to Pokhara\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Then catch the transportation drive to Pokhara and transfer to a hotel (Breakfast will be served at Tea House Lodge restaurant). All the way follows a gradual descent to the final point Phedi. You will pass many cultural hamlets and their hill-terraced traditional Farmland. At the ending place, you will be picked up by transport and driven to Pokhara for lunch and rest overnight at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":4,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":[\\"pt-0\\"],\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Dhampus to Ghandruk Village Trek Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRegion: Annapurna, Nepal\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDifficulty: Easy to Moderate\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDuration: 2–5 days (depending on pace)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eMax. Altitude: ~2,010m (Ghandruk)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBest Season: Spring (March–May) \\\\u0026amp; Autumn (Sept–Nov)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePermits: TIMS card + Annapurna Conservation Area Permit (ACAP)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTotal Trekking Distance: ~25–30 km (varies by route).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDaily Walking: 2–6 hours (varies by number of days).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTrail Type: Stone steps, forest paths, terraced fields, and villages.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHere are 10 highlights of the Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek that make it a must-do adventure in Nepal’s Annapurna region:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Stunning Mountain Views\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003ePanoramic vistas of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAnnapurna South, Machapuchare (Fishtail), Hiunchuli\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, and Dhaulagiri from Australian Camp, Dhampus, and Ghandruk.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00222\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Australian Camp Sunrise/Sunset\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eOne of the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ebest viewpoints\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e in the Annapurna foothills, offering golden sunrises over the Himalayas.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00223\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Authentic Gurung Culture\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eExperience the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003etraditional Gurung villages\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e of Dhampus, Landruk, and Ghandruk, known for their stone houses, warm hospitality, and rich cultural heritage.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00224\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Ghandruk Village (Largest Gurung Settlement)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eA beautifully preserved Gurung village with \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003emountain views, a cultural museum, and homestays\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00225\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Short \\\\u0026amp; Beginner-Friendly Trek\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eOnly \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e2–4 days\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e with easy-to-moderate trails, perfect for first-time trekkers or those with limited time.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00226\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Terraced Farmlands \\\\u0026amp; Rhododendron Forests\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eWalk through lush \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003erice fields, terraced farms\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, and (in spring) vibrant \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003erhododendron blooms\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00227\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e No Risk of Altitude Sickness\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eMax altitude is only \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e2,010m (Ghandruk)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, making it safe for all ages and fitness levels.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00228\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Great Teahouse Experience\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eCozy lodges with \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003emountain views, local food (dal bhat, momos), and friendly hosts\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00229\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Flexible Route Options\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eStart/end at \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePhedi, Kande, Nayapul, or Australian Camp\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, with options to extend to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePoon Hill or Tadapani\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u002210\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Close to Pokhara (Easy Access)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eJust \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e1–2 hours’ drive\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e from Pokhara, making it a perfect add-on to a Nepal trip.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBonus Highlight: Wildlife Spotting\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eChance to see \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003elangur monkeys, Himalayan birds, and butterflies\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e along the trail.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHere are \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e10 more compelling reasons\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e to choose the \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhampus to Ghandruk Trek\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e, making it an unbeatable Himalayan experience:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Perfect for Solo Trekkers \\\\u0026amp; Families\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eSafe, well-marked trails with frequent teahouses—ideal for solo adventurers, couples, and families with kids.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00222\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e No Crowds (Compared to Everest or ABC)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eEnjoy peaceful trails without the mass tourism of longer treks, especially if you avoid peak season (Oct–Nov).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00223\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Affordable (Low-Budget Friendly)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eMinimal costs for food/lodging—no need for expensive guides or flights like in remote regions.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00224\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Year-Round Trekking Possible\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eDoable even in \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ewinter (Dec–Feb)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e and \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003emonsoon (June–Aug)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e—just expect rain or chilly nights.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00225\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Minimal Packing Needed\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eNo extreme cold gear required—just layers, good shoes, and a rain jacket (depending on season).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00226\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Cultural Stops Along the Way\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eVisit the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGurung Museum in Ghandruk\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, Buddhist stupas, and local craft workshops.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00227\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Delicious Local \\\\u0026amp; Western Food\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eTeahouses serve everything from \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003edal bhat\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e to pasta, apple pie, and even espresso!\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00228\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Optional Adventure Add-Ons\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eExtend to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePoon Hill (3,210m)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e or \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eTadapani\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e for more challenging trails and epic views.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00229\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Photography Paradise\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eCapture \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003esunrises over Fishtail, terraced farms, traditional villages, and starry night skies\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u002210\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Easy Escape to Pokhara’s Comfort\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eAfter the trek, unwind by \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePhewa Lake\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e with cafes, spas, and paragliding!\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eCommon Route:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nStarting Point: Phedi or Dhampus (1–2 hrs drive from Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\nEnding Point: Ghandruk (return via Nayapul or loop back to Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Pokhara → Phedi (drive) → Trek to Dhampus (1.5–2 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 2: Dhampus → Pothana → Landruk (5–6 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 4: Ghandruk → Nayapul (4–5 hrs) → Drive to Pokhara.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMultiple Starting Points for Dhampus-Ghandruk Trek\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong style=\\\\u0022font-size: 16px;\\\\u0022\\\\u003ePhedi/Dhampus (Standard Route)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nStart: Phedi (1-hour drive from Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Phedi → Dhampus (1.5–2 hrs trek).\\\\r\\\\nDay 2: Dhampus → Australian Camp → Pothana → Landruk (5–6 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nEnd: Ghandruk → Nayapul (4–5 hrs) → Drive to Pokhara.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKande (Via Australian Camp – Popular Route)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nStart: Kande (1.5-hour drive from Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Kande → Australian Camp (1–1.5 hrs steep climb).\\\\r\\\\nDay 2: Australian Camp → Pothana → Landruk (4–5 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nEnd: Ghandruk → Nayapul → Pokhara.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAustralian Camp Direct (Short \\\\u0026amp; Scenic)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nStart: Drive to Australian Camp (private jeep from Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Explore Australian Camp (sunset/sunrise views).\\\\r\\\\nDay 2: Australian Camp → Landruk (4–5 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nEnd: Return via Nayapul or extend to Tadapani.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNayapul (Classic Annapurna Route)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nStart: Nayapul (2-hour drive from Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Nayapul → Birethanti → Ghandruk (5–6 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 2: Ghandruk → Landruk → Tolka (optional).\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Tolka → Australian Camp → Kande (loop back).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMultiple Ending Points\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eNayapul (Most Common)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFrom Ghandruk, descend to Birethanti → Nayapul (4–5 hrs).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTake a bus/taxi to Pokhara (1.5 hrs).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eKimche (Jeep Option)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFrom Ghandruk, trek 1.5 hrs to Kimche → Take a jeep to Pokhara.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLoop Back to Australian Camp/Kande\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGhandruk → Landruk → Pothana → Australian Camp → Kande (longer loop).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eExtend to Tadapani/Poon Hill\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFrom Ghandruk, trek to Tadapani (3–4 hrs) → Continue to Ghorepani/Poon Hill.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKey Variations \\\\u0026amp; Highlights\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAustralian Camp → Best for sunrise/sunset over Annapurna range.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eKande Start → Saves time; steep but rewarding.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLandruk Detour → Quieter than Ghandruk, great homestays.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eNayapul Start/End → Classic Annapurna Sanctuary approach.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eWhich Route to Choose?\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctable class=\\\\u0022table table-bordered table-responsive\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctbody\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003ePhedi → Dhampus → Ghandruk\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e3–4 days\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eEasy-Moderate\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eFirst-timers\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eKande → Australian Camp → Ghandruk\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e3 days\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eModerate\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eScenic views\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eAustralian Camp Direct → Ghandruk\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e2–3 days\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eEasy\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eShort \\\\u0026amp; sweet\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eNayapul → Ghandruk Loop\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e4–5 days\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eModerate\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eExtended trek\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tbody\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/table\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAltitude Sickness (AMS)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nRisk: Low (Ghandruk is only 2,010m).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePrecautions:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eStay hydrated.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAscend gradually (no rapid climbs).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eWatch for headaches/nausea (descend if severe).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePacking List\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eClothing: Layers, rain jacket, trekking pants, hat, gloves.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFootwear: Sturdy trekking shoes + sandals.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGear: Backpack, water bottle, trekking poles, sunscreen.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eMisc: First-aid kit, cash (no ATMs), camera.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePermits and Costs\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eACAP Permit: NPR 3,000 (foreigners), NPR 1,000 (SAARC).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTIMS Card: NPR 2,000.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAccommodation \\\\u0026amp; Meals\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBasic Accommodation\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTeahouses/Lodges: Basic but comfortable; costs around NPR 1000 per night.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRooms: Twin-sharing with common toilets (hot showers may cost extra).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eElectricity/WiFi: Limited; charging devices may cost NPR 100–300/hour.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMid-Range Hotels/Lodges with Attached Bathrooms\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAustralian Camp Area\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHimalayan Front Hotel\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (hot water included).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Stunning Annapurna views, clean rooms, cozy dining area.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAustralian Camp Guest House\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Some rooms (confirm when booking).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Friendly hosts, great sunrise views.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhampus Village\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhampus Peak Lodge\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (24-hour solar hot water).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Spacious rooms, mountain-facing balconies.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLandruk Village\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGurung Cottage\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (hot shower).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Authentic Gurung hospitality, rooftop terrace.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSunset Lodge\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (electric-heated water).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Quiet location, great food.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGhandruk Village\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHimalaya Lodge\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (reliable hot water).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Best views of Annapurna South, cozy fireplace lounge.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGhandruk Guest House\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (solar-heated water).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Central location, clean and modern.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLuxury Resorts \\\\u0026amp; Boutique Hotels on the Trek\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMountain Lodges of Nepal - Dhampus)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nType: Eco-luxury resort with private villas.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFeatures:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate plunge pools with Annapurna views.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eOrganic farm-to-table dining.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSpa services (Ayurvedic massages).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSolar-powered, eco-friendly design.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nBest For: Honeymooners or travelers seeking luxury before/after the trek.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGurung Cottage (Ghandruk)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nLocation: Ghandruk village.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nType: Boutique family-run lodge with upgraded facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFeatures:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAttached bathrooms with hot showers.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRooftop terrace for sunrise/sunset views.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAuthentic Gurung cuisine (dhal bhat, homemade wine).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eCozy fireplaces in rooms.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nBest For: Trekkers wanting comfort in Ghandruk.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHimalayan Front Hotel (Australian Camp)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nLocation: Australian Camp.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nType: Mid-range luxury with premium services.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFeatures:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePanoramic views of Annapurna and Machapuchare.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGlass-walled dining hall.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eWarm blankets, clean rooms, and Western toilets.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nBest For: Sunrise photographers and comfort seekers.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKer \\\\u0026amp; Downey Lodges (Landruk)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nLocation: Landruk village (between Dhampus \\\\u0026amp; Ghandruk).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nType: High-end lodge chain.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFeatures:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLuxury bedding and modern bathrooms.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGourmet meals (international + Nepali dishes).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eQuiet, less-touristed location.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nBest For: Peaceful luxury in a traditional village.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eBudget vs. Mid-range vs. Luxury Comparison\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctable class=\\\\u0022table table-bordered table-responsive\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctbody\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFeature\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022206\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBudget Teahouse\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022154\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMid-Range Lodge\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLuxury Lodges\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003ePrice/Night\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022206\\\\u0022\\\\u003eBelow USD 10\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022154\\\\u0022\\\\u003eUSD 20-40\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eUSD 100–400+\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eBathroom\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022206\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShared (cold water)\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022154\\\\u0022\\\\u003ePrivate (hot water)\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003ePrivate (hot shower)\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eRoom Quality\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022206\\\\u0022\\\\u003eBasic wooden beds\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022154\\\\u0022\\\\u003eClean, comfy beds\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eHeated, premium linens\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eFood\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022206\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBreakfast\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Porridge, toast, eggs, Tibetan bread, tea/coffee.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLunch/Dinner\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Dal Bhat (lentil soup + rice), noodles, pasta, momos, soups.\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022154\\\\u0022\\\\u003eAs per your choice,\\\\r\\\\nEg: Pasta, pizza, better coffee\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eAs per your choice, Eg: Gourmet / International\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tbody\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/table\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSenior-friendly \\\\u0026amp; luxury-focused itinerary for the Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDesigned for travelers who prefer shorter walking days (2–4 hours/day), comfortable stays, and scenic drives to minimize exertion while maximizing Himalayan views and cultural experiences.\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cu\\\\u003e5-Day Luxury Itinerary (With Minimal Trekking)\\\\u003c/u\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nTheme: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003e\\\\u0022Slow-Paced Comfort in the Annapurna Foothills\\\\u0022\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 1: Pokhara → Drive to Australian Camp (Sunset Magic)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMorning: Private jeep transfer from Pokhara to Kande (1.5 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nTrek: Gentle 1-hour uphill walk to Australian Camp (2,050m).\\\\r\\\\nStay: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalayan Front Hotel\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e (private bathroom, mountain-view balcony).\\\\r\\\\nHighlight: Sunset over Annapurna South with champagne!\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 2: Australian Camp → Landruk (Easy Descent)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTrek: 2–3 hours downhill via Pothana and Deurali to Landruk (1,560m).\\\\r\\\\nStay: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eKer \\\\u0026amp; Downey Lodge Landruk\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e (luxury rooms, hot showers, garden seating).\\\\r\\\\nHighlight: Gurung cultural dinner with local dance (optional).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (Short Riverside Walk)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTrek: 2.5 hours along the Modi Khola River to Ghandruk (2,010m).\\\\r\\\\nStay: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalaya Lodge\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e (deluxe room with fireplace, attached bathroom).\\\\r\\\\nHighlight: Visit the Gurung Museum and relax with a hot stone massage.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 4: Ghandruk Exploration (Zero Trekking Day)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMorning: Sunrise yoga session with Annapurna views.\\\\r\\\\nActivity: Guided village tour (traditional homes, weaving demo).\\\\r\\\\nStay: Second night at \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalaya Lodge\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 5: Ghandruk → Nayapul → Pokhara (Jeep Option)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOption 1 (Trek + Drive): 2-hour gentle walk to Kimche → Private jeep to Pokhara (1.5 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nOption 2 (No Trek): Direct jeep from Ghandruk to Pokhara (3 hrs, bumpy but scenic).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAlternatives for Zero-Trekking Travelers\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHeli-Trek Combo:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Pokhara → Heli to Ghandruk (15 mins). Stay 2 nights, explore village.\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Heli return or jeep to Pokhara.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePokhara-Based Day Trips:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nDrive to Australian Camp for lunch/sunset → Return same day.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePacking Tips for Seniors/Luxury Trekkers\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFootwear: Non-slip hiking sandals (e.g., Keen) + trekking poles.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eExtras: Portable oxygen canister (for breathlessness), knee braces.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eClothing: Light down jacket (mornings are chilly even in spring).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eWhy This Itinerary Works?\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eMax Elevation: Only 2,010m (Ghandruk)—no altitude risks.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eWalking Hours: ≤3 hours/day with breaks.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eCultural Depth: More time to interact with locals vs. rushing trails.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFAQs \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is a guide necessary?\\\\r\\\\nA: Not mandatory, but helpful for navigation/culture.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can solo trekkers join groups?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes, teahouses are social; or join organized tours.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Phone network?\\\\r\\\\nA: Ncell/NTC work sporadically; WiFi is paid.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is it safe for beginners?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes, but fitness helps for stone steps/long walks.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Wildlife sightings?\\\\r\\\\nA: Possible: monkeys, birds, occasional langurs.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I start from Pokhara directly?\\\\r\\\\nA: No, you need to drive to Phedi/Kande/Nayapul (1–2 hrs).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is Australian Camp worth adding?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes! Best mountain views and cozy lodges.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Which route has fewer stairs?\\\\r\\\\nA: Kande → Australian Camp has fewer steps than Phedi → Dhampus.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I end at Kimche instead of Nayapul?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes, Kimche has jeeps to Pokhara (saves trekking time).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is a guide needed for these routes?\\\\r\\\\nA: Not mandatory, but helpful for navigation in loop trails.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are there hotels with attached bathrooms and hot showers on this trek?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes! Mid-range and luxury lodges like \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalayan Front Hotel (Australian Camp)\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e, \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalaya Lodge (Ghandruk)\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e, and \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eKer \\\\u0026amp; Downey Lodges (Landruk)\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e offer private bathrooms, 24/7 hot water, and comfortable beds. Budget teahouses may charge extra for hot showers.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I book accommodations in advance?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes, especially in peak season (Oct–Nov, Mar–Apr). Luxury lodges require advance reservations. Your guide/agency can arrange this.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are there electric blankets or heaters in rooms?\\\\r\\\\nA: Most luxury lodges provide heaters or extra blankets. Budget teahouses rely on thick quilts—ask for a \\\\u0022deluxe room\\\\u0022 for better comfort.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: What’s the best way to reach the trek start point from Pokhara?\\\\r\\\\nA: Private jeep (most comfortable) to Phedi (1 hr) or Kande (1.5 hrs) or Nayapul (2 hrs)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I skip trekking entirely and use vehicles?\\\\r\\\\nA: Partially! You can:\\\\r\\\\nDrive to Australian Camp (via Kande, then 1-hr walk).\\\\r\\\\nJeep from Ghandruk to Kimche/Nayapul (bumpy but saves walking).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are roads safe for seniors?\\\\r\\\\nA: Roads are rough but manageable in a 4WD jeep. Avoid monsoon (June–Aug) due to landslides.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: What cultural activities can I do in Ghandruk?\\\\r\\\\nA: Visit the Gurung Museum (traditional costumes, weapons).\\\\r\\\\nAttend a local dance performance (arranged by lodges).\\\\r\\\\nTry Gurung cuisine: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003edal bhat\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e, \\\\u003cem\\\\u003egundruk\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e (fermented greens), and \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eraksi\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e (local alcohol).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I participate in a homestay?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes! Gurung Cottage (Ghandruk) and Landruk homestays offer authentic experiences. Book ahead.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are villages wheelchair-friendly?\\\\r\\\\nA: No—trails have stone steps and uneven paths. Seniors with mobility issues should opt for jeep/heli access.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are there yoga retreats or sessions along the trek?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes!\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAustralian Camp: Sunrise yoga with mountain views (ask your lodge or guide).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGhandruk: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalaya Lodge\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003eoffers yoga mats and guided sessions.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePokhara Add-On: Post-trek relaxation with yoga.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I meditate in the mountains?\\\\r\\\\nA: Absolutely! Silent spots:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAustralian Camp (sunrise meditation).\\\\r\\\\nGhandruk’s sunrise viewpoint.\\\\r\\\\nLandruk’s terraced farms.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is altitude sickness a risk?\\\\r\\\\nA: Minimal (max altitude: 2,010m). Seniors should still:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eStay hydrated.\\\\r\\\\nWalk slowly.\\\\r\\\\nAvoid alcohol.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: What if I get tired during the trek?\\\\r\\\\nA: Options:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHire a mule to ride between villages.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eShorten walks (e.g., drive to Landruk, then trek 1 hr to Ghandruk).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are there pharmacies or doctors on the trail?\\\\r\\\\nA: Basic clinics in Ghandruk/Landruk. Carry medications, knee braces, and a first-aid kit.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I get vegetarian/vegan food?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes! Teahouses serve:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVeg \\\\u003cem\\\\u003edal bhat\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e, noodles, soups, and fresh \\\\u003cem\\\\u003esel roti\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e(Nepali donuts).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLuxury lodges offer pasta, salads, and desserts.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is bottled water available?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes ($1–$3/bottle), but reduce plastic use by:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eCarrying a SteriPen or purification tablets.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAsking lodges for boiled/filtered water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Packing Tips for Seniors?\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nA: Must-Haves: Trekking poles, knee sleeves, slip-proof shoes, and a small daypack.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLuxury Add-Ons: Portable oxygen canister, inflatable neck pillow, and down booties for cold nights.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: When is the least crowded time?\\\\r\\\\nA: December–February (cold but clear) or September (post-monsoon greenery). Avoid monsoon (June–Aug).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: How cold does it get at night?\\\\r\\\\nA: 5–10°C (41–50°F) in autumn/spring. Luxury lodges provide heaters/extra blankets.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eFinal Tips\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eStart early to avoid afternoon clouds.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBargain lightly for souvenirs in Ghandruk.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRespect local customs (ask before photographing people).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAustralian Camp is crowded in peak season (Oct–Nov).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLandruk offers authentic Gurung culture with fewer tourists.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eIf short on time, do Kande → Australian Camp → Ghandruk → Nayapul (3 days).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFor a stress-free trek, book a private guide/porter (~$25–$50/day) to handle logistics, carry bags, and adjust pacing.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFully private trip \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVehicle fuel, vehicle tax.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking cultural city tour guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrinking Water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"0\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"0\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"It is one of the shortest treks in the Annapurna region\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv class=\\\\u0022col-lg-12 info first_para\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe main aim of this trek is to visit one of the most beautiful Gurung villages Ghandruk. It is located on an elevation of (1090m) and you can witness the Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Gangapurna, and Fish Tail.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview \\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhampus to Ghandruk Village trekking \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eis one of the best of the Annapurna treks which starts from Nayapul and ends at Phedi. It is one of the shortest treks in the Annapurna region. The main aim of this trek is to visit one of the most beautiful Gurung villages \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGhandruk\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e. It is located at an elevation of (2012m) and you can witness the Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Gangapurna, and \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machapuchare\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMachhapuchhre\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e (Fish Tail).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIt is a huge Gurung village where you can visit the old and new Gurung museum which shows the real culture of the Gurung Community. Gurung is one of the ethnic groups of Nepal and they have their distinct language and customs. They are known as Gorkhali because most of the British armies are from their community.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThis trek goes along the tiny villages of Syauli Bazar, Landruk, Tolkha, Pothana, and Dhampus. You can behold the excellent view of Mt. Dhaulagiri, Annapurna South, Fishtail, Annapurna III, Lamjung Himal, and the entire Pokhara Valley. The unique culture of Gurung and Magar, different sorts of flora and fauna, and the green view of the rural areas of Nepal and Pokhara Valley are the main attractions of this trek. The best season is from August to May.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4831\\",\\"4830\\",\\"4829\\",\\"4828\\",\\"5895\\",\\"5896\\",\\"5897\\",\\"5898\\",\\"5899\\",\\"5900\\",\\"5901\\",\\"5902\\",\\"5903\\",\\"5904\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Sample Itinerary: Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\" Drive to Nayapul from Pokhara then Trek to Ghandruk\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Drive to Nayapul (1070m) which takes one and a half hours and trek to Ghandruk through the beautiful countryside with a panoramic view of Mt. Fishtail, Annapurna South, and Gangapurna. The way gently climbs up from Syauli Bazar and finally arrives at Ghandruk which takes around 6/7 hours.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Tolka via Landruk\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Ghandruk is a huge Gurung village from where the trail descends to Kyumi Bridge and a short climb to Landruk. It is one of the most beautiful villages. From here, we continue to Tolka with the beautiful scenery of the green countryside. We spent a night there.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Australian Camp\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"On the next day, we started the trek after breakfast.  The way goes through dense forest and finally arrives at Deurali. From the trail continue through the green jungle to Pothana and arrive at the Australian camp at last. Australian Camp is a beautiful village best known for its sunrise, sunset, and view of the Annapurna range, Machhapuchhre, and beautiful green hills. We stayed there for a night.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Dharmasala Phedi and Drive to Pokhara\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Then catch the transportation drive to Pokhara and transfer to a hotel (Breakfast will be served at Tea House Lodge restaurant). All the way follows a gradual descent to the final point Phedi. You will pass many cultural hamlets and their hill-terraced traditional Farmland. At the ending place, you will be picked up by transport and driven to Pokhara for lunch and rest overnight at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":4,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":[\\"pt-0\\"],\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Dhampus to Ghandruk Village Trek Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRegion: Annapurna, Nepal\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDifficulty: Easy to Moderate\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDuration: 2–5 days (depending on pace)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eMax. Altitude: ~2,010m (Ghandruk)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBest Season: Spring (March–May) \\\\u0026amp; Autumn (Sept–Nov)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePermits: TIMS card + Annapurna Conservation Area Permit (ACAP)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTotal Trekking Distance: ~25–30 km (varies by route).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDaily Walking: 2–6 hours (varies by number of days).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTrail Type: Stone steps, forest paths, terraced fields, and villages.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHere are 10 highlights of the Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek that make it a must-do adventure in Nepal’s Annapurna region:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Stunning Mountain Views\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003ePanoramic vistas of \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAnnapurna South, Machapuchare (Fishtail), Hiunchuli\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, and Dhaulagiri from Australian Camp, Dhampus, and Ghandruk.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00222\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Australian Camp Sunrise/Sunset\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eOne of the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ebest viewpoints\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e in the Annapurna foothills, offering golden sunrises over the Himalayas.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00223\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Authentic Gurung Culture\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eExperience the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003etraditional Gurung villages\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e of Dhampus, Landruk, and Ghandruk, known for their stone houses, warm hospitality, and rich cultural heritage.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00224\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Ghandruk Village (Largest Gurung Settlement)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eA beautifully preserved Gurung village with \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003emountain views, a cultural museum, and homestays\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00225\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Short \\\\u0026amp; Beginner-Friendly Trek\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eOnly \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e2–4 days\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e with easy-to-moderate trails, perfect for first-time trekkers or those with limited time.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00226\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Terraced Farmlands \\\\u0026amp; Rhododendron Forests\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eWalk through lush \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003erice fields, terraced farms\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, and (in spring) vibrant \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003erhododendron blooms\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00227\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e No Risk of Altitude Sickness\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eMax altitude is only \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e2,010m (Ghandruk)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, making it safe for all ages and fitness levels.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00228\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Great Teahouse Experience\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eCozy lodges with \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003emountain views, local food (dal bhat, momos), and friendly hosts\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00229\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Flexible Route Options\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eStart/end at \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePhedi, Kande, Nayapul, or Australian Camp\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, with options to extend to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePoon Hill or Tadapani\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u002210\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Close to Pokhara (Easy Access)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eJust \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e1–2 hours’ drive\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e from Pokhara, making it a perfect add-on to a Nepal trip.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBonus Highlight: Wildlife Spotting\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eChance to see \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003elangur monkeys, Himalayan birds, and butterflies\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e along the trail.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHere are \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e10 more compelling reasons\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e to choose the \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhampus to Ghandruk Trek\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e, making it an unbeatable Himalayan experience:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Perfect for Solo Trekkers \\\\u0026amp; Families\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eSafe, well-marked trails with frequent teahouses—ideal for solo adventurers, couples, and families with kids.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00222\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e No Crowds (Compared to Everest or ABC)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eEnjoy peaceful trails without the mass tourism of longer treks, especially if you avoid peak season (Oct–Nov).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00223\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Affordable (Low-Budget Friendly)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eMinimal costs for food/lodging—no need for expensive guides or flights like in remote regions.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00224\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Year-Round Trekking Possible\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eDoable even in \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ewinter (Dec–Feb)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e and \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003emonsoon (June–Aug)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e—just expect rain or chilly nights.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00225\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Minimal Packing Needed\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eNo extreme cold gear required—just layers, good shoes, and a rain jacket (depending on season).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00226\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Cultural Stops Along the Way\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eVisit the \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGurung Museum in Ghandruk\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, Buddhist stupas, and local craft workshops.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00227\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Delicious Local \\\\u0026amp; Western Food\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eTeahouses serve everything from \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003edal bhat\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e to pasta, apple pie, and even espresso!\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00228\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Optional Adventure Add-Ons\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eExtend to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePoon Hill (3,210m)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e or \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eTadapani\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e for more challenging trails and epic views.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u00229\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Photography Paradise\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eCapture \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003esunrises over Fishtail, terraced farms, traditional villages, and starry night skies\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003col start=\\\\u002210\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e Easy Escape to Pokhara’s Comfort\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eAfter the trek, unwind by \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePhewa Lake\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e with cafes, spas, and paragliding!\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ol\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eCommon Route:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nStarting Point: Phedi or Dhampus (1–2 hrs drive from Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\nEnding Point: Ghandruk (return via Nayapul or loop back to Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Pokhara → Phedi (drive) → Trek to Dhampus (1.5–2 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 2: Dhampus → Pothana → Landruk (5–6 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 4: Ghandruk → Nayapul (4–5 hrs) → Drive to Pokhara.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMultiple Starting Points for Dhampus-Ghandruk Trek\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong style=\\\\u0022font-size: 16px;\\\\u0022\\\\u003ePhedi/Dhampus (Standard Route)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nStart: Phedi (1-hour drive from Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Phedi → Dhampus (1.5–2 hrs trek).\\\\r\\\\nDay 2: Dhampus → Australian Camp → Pothana → Landruk (5–6 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nEnd: Ghandruk → Nayapul (4–5 hrs) → Drive to Pokhara.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKande (Via Australian Camp – Popular Route)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nStart: Kande (1.5-hour drive from Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Kande → Australian Camp (1–1.5 hrs steep climb).\\\\r\\\\nDay 2: Australian Camp → Pothana → Landruk (4–5 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nEnd: Ghandruk → Nayapul → Pokhara.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAustralian Camp Direct (Short \\\\u0026amp; Scenic)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nStart: Drive to Australian Camp (private jeep from Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Explore Australian Camp (sunset/sunrise views).\\\\r\\\\nDay 2: Australian Camp → Landruk (4–5 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nEnd: Return via Nayapul or extend to Tadapani.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNayapul (Classic Annapurna Route)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nStart: Nayapul (2-hour drive from Pokhara).\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Nayapul → Birethanti → Ghandruk (5–6 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nDay 2: Ghandruk → Landruk → Tolka (optional).\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Tolka → Australian Camp → Kande (loop back).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMultiple Ending Points\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eNayapul (Most Common)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFrom Ghandruk, descend to Birethanti → Nayapul (4–5 hrs).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTake a bus/taxi to Pokhara (1.5 hrs).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eKimche (Jeep Option)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFrom Ghandruk, trek 1.5 hrs to Kimche → Take a jeep to Pokhara.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLoop Back to Australian Camp/Kande\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGhandruk → Landruk → Pothana → Australian Camp → Kande (longer loop).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eExtend to Tadapani/Poon Hill\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFrom Ghandruk, trek to Tadapani (3–4 hrs) → Continue to Ghorepani/Poon Hill.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKey Variations \\\\u0026amp; Highlights\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAustralian Camp → Best for sunrise/sunset over Annapurna range.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eKande Start → Saves time; steep but rewarding.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLandruk Detour → Quieter than Ghandruk, great homestays.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eNayapul Start/End → Classic Annapurna Sanctuary approach.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eWhich Route to Choose?\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctable class=\\\\u0022table table-bordered table-responsive\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctbody\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003ePhedi → Dhampus → Ghandruk\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e3–4 days\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eEasy-Moderate\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eFirst-timers\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eKande → Australian Camp → Ghandruk\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e3 days\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eModerate\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eScenic views\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eAustralian Camp Direct → Ghandruk\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e2–3 days\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eEasy\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eShort \\\\u0026amp; sweet\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eNayapul → Ghandruk Loop\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e4–5 days\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eModerate\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eExtended trek\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tbody\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/table\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAltitude Sickness (AMS)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nRisk: Low (Ghandruk is only 2,010m).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePrecautions:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eStay hydrated.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAscend gradually (no rapid climbs).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eWatch for headaches/nausea (descend if severe).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePacking List\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eClothing: Layers, rain jacket, trekking pants, hat, gloves.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFootwear: Sturdy trekking shoes + sandals.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGear: Backpack, water bottle, trekking poles, sunscreen.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eMisc: First-aid kit, cash (no ATMs), camera.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePermits and Costs\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eACAP Permit: NPR 3,000 (foreigners), NPR 1,000 (SAARC).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTIMS Card: NPR 2,000.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAccommodation \\\\u0026amp; Meals\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBasic Accommodation\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTeahouses/Lodges: Basic but comfortable; costs around NPR 1000 per night.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRooms: Twin-sharing with common toilets (hot showers may cost extra).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eElectricity/WiFi: Limited; charging devices may cost NPR 100–300/hour.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMid-Range Hotels/Lodges with Attached Bathrooms\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAustralian Camp Area\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHimalayan Front Hotel\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (hot water included).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Stunning Annapurna views, clean rooms, cozy dining area.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAustralian Camp Guest House\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Some rooms (confirm when booking).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Friendly hosts, great sunrise views.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhampus Village\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDhampus Peak Lodge\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (24-hour solar hot water).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Spacious rooms, mountain-facing balconies.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLandruk Village\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGurung Cottage\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (hot shower).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Authentic Gurung hospitality, rooftop terrace.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSunset Lodge\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (electric-heated water).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Quiet location, great food.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGhandruk Village\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHimalaya Lodge\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (reliable hot water).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Best views of Annapurna South, cozy fireplace lounge.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGhandruk Guest House\\\\r\\\\nAttached Bathroom\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Yes (solar-heated water).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePerks\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Central location, clean and modern.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLuxury Resorts \\\\u0026amp; Boutique Hotels on the Trek\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMountain Lodges of Nepal - Dhampus)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nType: Eco-luxury resort with private villas.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFeatures:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate plunge pools with Annapurna views.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eOrganic farm-to-table dining.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSpa services (Ayurvedic massages).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSolar-powered, eco-friendly design.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nBest For: Honeymooners or travelers seeking luxury before/after the trek.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eGurung Cottage (Ghandruk)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nLocation: Ghandruk village.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nType: Boutique family-run lodge with upgraded facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFeatures:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAttached bathrooms with hot showers.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRooftop terrace for sunrise/sunset views.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAuthentic Gurung cuisine (dhal bhat, homemade wine).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eCozy fireplaces in rooms.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nBest For: Trekkers wanting comfort in Ghandruk.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHimalayan Front Hotel (Australian Camp)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nLocation: Australian Camp.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nType: Mid-range luxury with premium services.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFeatures:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePanoramic views of Annapurna and Machapuchare.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGlass-walled dining hall.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eWarm blankets, clean rooms, and Western toilets.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nBest For: Sunrise photographers and comfort seekers.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eKer \\\\u0026amp; Downey Lodges (Landruk)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nLocation: Landruk village (between Dhampus \\\\u0026amp; Ghandruk).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nType: High-end lodge chain.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFeatures:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLuxury bedding and modern bathrooms.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGourmet meals (international + Nepali dishes).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eQuiet, less-touristed location.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nBest For: Peaceful luxury in a traditional village.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eBudget vs. Mid-range vs. Luxury Comparison\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctable class=\\\\u0022table table-bordered table-responsive\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctbody\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFeature\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022206\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBudget Teahouse\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022154\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMid-Range Lodge\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLuxury Lodges\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003ePrice/Night\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022206\\\\u0022\\\\u003eBelow USD 10\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022154\\\\u0022\\\\u003eUSD 20-40\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eUSD 100–400+\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eBathroom\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022206\\\\u0022\\\\u003eShared (cold water)\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022154\\\\u0022\\\\u003ePrivate (hot water)\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003ePrivate (hot shower)\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eRoom Quality\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022206\\\\u0022\\\\u003eBasic wooden beds\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022154\\\\u0022\\\\u003eClean, comfy beds\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eHeated, premium linens\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eFood\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022206\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBreakfast\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Porridge, toast, eggs, Tibetan bread, tea/coffee.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLunch/Dinner\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e: Dal Bhat (lentil soup + rice), noodles, pasta, momos, soups.\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd width=\\\\u0022154\\\\u0022\\\\u003eAs per your choice,\\\\r\\\\nEg: Pasta, pizza, better coffee\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ctd\\\\u003eAs per your choice, Eg: Gourmet / International\\\\u003c/td\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tr\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/tbody\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/table\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSenior-friendly \\\\u0026amp; luxury-focused itinerary for the Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDesigned for travelers who prefer shorter walking days (2–4 hours/day), comfortable stays, and scenic drives to minimize exertion while maximizing Himalayan views and cultural experiences.\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cu\\\\u003e5-Day Luxury Itinerary (With Minimal Trekking)\\\\u003c/u\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nTheme: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003e\\\\u0022Slow-Paced Comfort in the Annapurna Foothills\\\\u0022\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 1: Pokhara → Drive to Australian Camp (Sunset Magic)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMorning: Private jeep transfer from Pokhara to Kande (1.5 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nTrek: Gentle 1-hour uphill walk to Australian Camp (2,050m).\\\\r\\\\nStay: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalayan Front Hotel\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e (private bathroom, mountain-view balcony).\\\\r\\\\nHighlight: Sunset over Annapurna South with champagne!\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 2: Australian Camp → Landruk (Easy Descent)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTrek: 2–3 hours downhill via Pothana and Deurali to Landruk (1,560m).\\\\r\\\\nStay: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eKer \\\\u0026amp; Downey Lodge Landruk\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e (luxury rooms, hot showers, garden seating).\\\\r\\\\nHighlight: Gurung cultural dinner with local dance (optional).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (Short Riverside Walk)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTrek: 2.5 hours along the Modi Khola River to Ghandruk (2,010m).\\\\r\\\\nStay: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalaya Lodge\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e (deluxe room with fireplace, attached bathroom).\\\\r\\\\nHighlight: Visit the Gurung Museum and relax with a hot stone massage.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 4: Ghandruk Exploration (Zero Trekking Day)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMorning: Sunrise yoga session with Annapurna views.\\\\r\\\\nActivity: Guided village tour (traditional homes, weaving demo).\\\\r\\\\nStay: Second night at \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalaya Lodge\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 5: Ghandruk → Nayapul → Pokhara (Jeep Option)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nOption 1 (Trek + Drive): 2-hour gentle walk to Kimche → Private jeep to Pokhara (1.5 hrs).\\\\r\\\\nOption 2 (No Trek): Direct jeep from Ghandruk to Pokhara (3 hrs, bumpy but scenic).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch4\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eAlternatives for Zero-Trekking Travelers\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h4\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHeli-Trek Combo:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nDay 1: Pokhara → Heli to Ghandruk (15 mins). Stay 2 nights, explore village.\\\\r\\\\nDay 3: Heli return or jeep to Pokhara.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePokhara-Based Day Trips:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nDrive to Australian Camp for lunch/sunset → Return same day.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003ePacking Tips for Seniors/Luxury Trekkers\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFootwear: Non-slip hiking sandals (e.g., Keen) + trekking poles.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eExtras: Portable oxygen canister (for breathlessness), knee braces.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eClothing: Light down jacket (mornings are chilly even in spring).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch6\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eWhy This Itinerary Works?\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h6\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eMax Elevation: Only 2,010m (Ghandruk)—no altitude risks.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eWalking Hours: ≤3 hours/day with breaks.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eCultural Depth: More time to interact with locals vs. rushing trails.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFAQs \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is a guide necessary?\\\\r\\\\nA: Not mandatory, but helpful for navigation/culture.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can solo trekkers join groups?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes, teahouses are social; or join organized tours.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Phone network?\\\\r\\\\nA: Ncell/NTC work sporadically; WiFi is paid.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is it safe for beginners?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes, but fitness helps for stone steps/long walks.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Wildlife sightings?\\\\r\\\\nA: Possible: monkeys, birds, occasional langurs.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I start from Pokhara directly?\\\\r\\\\nA: No, you need to drive to Phedi/Kande/Nayapul (1–2 hrs).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is Australian Camp worth adding?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes! Best mountain views and cozy lodges.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Which route has fewer stairs?\\\\r\\\\nA: Kande → Australian Camp has fewer steps than Phedi → Dhampus.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I end at Kimche instead of Nayapul?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes, Kimche has jeeps to Pokhara (saves trekking time).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is a guide needed for these routes?\\\\r\\\\nA: Not mandatory, but helpful for navigation in loop trails.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are there hotels with attached bathrooms and hot showers on this trek?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes! Mid-range and luxury lodges like \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalayan Front Hotel (Australian Camp)\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e, \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalaya Lodge (Ghandruk)\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e, and \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eKer \\\\u0026amp; Downey Lodges (Landruk)\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e offer private bathrooms, 24/7 hot water, and comfortable beds. Budget teahouses may charge extra for hot showers.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I book accommodations in advance?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes, especially in peak season (Oct–Nov, Mar–Apr). Luxury lodges require advance reservations. Your guide/agency can arrange this.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are there electric blankets or heaters in rooms?\\\\r\\\\nA: Most luxury lodges provide heaters or extra blankets. Budget teahouses rely on thick quilts—ask for a \\\\u0022deluxe room\\\\u0022 for better comfort.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: What’s the best way to reach the trek start point from Pokhara?\\\\r\\\\nA: Private jeep (most comfortable) to Phedi (1 hr) or Kande (1.5 hrs) or Nayapul (2 hrs)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I skip trekking entirely and use vehicles?\\\\r\\\\nA: Partially! You can:\\\\r\\\\nDrive to Australian Camp (via Kande, then 1-hr walk).\\\\r\\\\nJeep from Ghandruk to Kimche/Nayapul (bumpy but saves walking).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are roads safe for seniors?\\\\r\\\\nA: Roads are rough but manageable in a 4WD jeep. Avoid monsoon (June–Aug) due to landslides.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: What cultural activities can I do in Ghandruk?\\\\r\\\\nA: Visit the Gurung Museum (traditional costumes, weapons).\\\\r\\\\nAttend a local dance performance (arranged by lodges).\\\\r\\\\nTry Gurung cuisine: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003edal bhat\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e, \\\\u003cem\\\\u003egundruk\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e (fermented greens), and \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eraksi\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e (local alcohol).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I participate in a homestay?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes! Gurung Cottage (Ghandruk) and Landruk homestays offer authentic experiences. Book ahead.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are villages wheelchair-friendly?\\\\r\\\\nA: No—trails have stone steps and uneven paths. Seniors with mobility issues should opt for jeep/heli access.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are there yoga retreats or sessions along the trek?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes!\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAustralian Camp: Sunrise yoga with mountain views (ask your lodge or guide).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGhandruk: \\\\u003cem\\\\u003eHimalaya Lodge\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003eoffers yoga mats and guided sessions.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePokhara Add-On: Post-trek relaxation with yoga.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I meditate in the mountains?\\\\r\\\\nA: Absolutely! Silent spots:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAustralian Camp (sunrise meditation).\\\\r\\\\nGhandruk’s sunrise viewpoint.\\\\r\\\\nLandruk’s terraced farms.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is altitude sickness a risk?\\\\r\\\\nA: Minimal (max altitude: 2,010m). Seniors should still:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eStay hydrated.\\\\r\\\\nWalk slowly.\\\\r\\\\nAvoid alcohol.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: What if I get tired during the trek?\\\\r\\\\nA: Options:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHire a mule to ride between villages.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eShorten walks (e.g., drive to Landruk, then trek 1 hr to Ghandruk).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Are there pharmacies or doctors on the trail?\\\\r\\\\nA: Basic clinics in Ghandruk/Landruk. Carry medications, knee braces, and a first-aid kit.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: Can I get vegetarian/vegan food?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes! Teahouses serve:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVeg \\\\u003cem\\\\u003edal bhat\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e, noodles, soups, and fresh \\\\u003cem\\\\u003esel roti\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e(Nepali donuts).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLuxury lodges offer pasta, salads, and desserts.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Is bottled water available?\\\\r\\\\nA: Yes ($1–$3/bottle), but reduce plastic use by:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eCarrying a SteriPen or purification tablets.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAsking lodges for boiled/filtered water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: Packing Tips for Seniors?\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nA: Must-Haves: Trekking poles, knee sleeves, slip-proof shoes, and a small daypack.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLuxury Add-Ons: Portable oxygen canister, inflatable neck pillow, and down booties for cold nights.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nQ: When is the least crowded time?\\\\r\\\\nA: December–February (cold but clear) or September (post-monsoon greenery). Avoid monsoon (June–Aug).\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nQ: How cold does it get at night?\\\\r\\\\nA: 5–10°C (41–50°F) in autumn/spring. Luxury lodges provide heaters/extra blankets.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eFinal Tips\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eStart early to avoid afternoon clouds.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBargain lightly for souvenirs in Ghandruk.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRespect local customs (ask before photographing people).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAustralian Camp is crowded in peak season (Oct–Nov).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLandruk offers authentic Gurung culture with fewer tourists.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eIf short on time, do Kande → Australian Camp → Ghandruk → Nayapul (3 days).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFor a stress-free trek, book a private guide/porter (~$25–$50/day) to handle logistics, carry bags, and adjust pacing.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eFully private trip \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVehicle fuel, vehicle tax.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking cultural city tour guide.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrinking Water.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-faqs\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"0\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ede33e5764a\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_641162e6b5849\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"3. How to find \\\\u0026 book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"4. How is the weather like in Nepal?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"5. What to expect on tours?\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title\\":\\"field_63ede3af351c8\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.\\",\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faqs_description\\":\\"field_63ede3bf351c9\\",\\"ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_faqs_lists\\":\\"field_63ede38e351c7\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-information {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-information\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"0\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec90a5664e4\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc6695edb31\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/pokhara-machhapuchre-sunrise.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/sunrise-from-dhampus.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/dhampus.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/way-to-dhampus.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/kande.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/hiking-route.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/travelers-at-landruk-village.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/landruk-village.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/annapurna-mountain-from-landruk.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/ghandruk-village.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/way-from-ghandruk-to-landruk.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/mountain-view-from-ghandruk.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/way-to-ghandruk.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/at-ghandruk-village.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Way-to-Ghandruk-village.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=909", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "909", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-08 05:55:29", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-08 05:55:29", "post_modified": "2025-10-17 09:15:42", "post_modified_gmt": "2025-10-17 09:15:42"}}, "customSections": [{"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["<strong>Dhampus to Ghandruk Village trekking </strong>is one of the best of the Annapurna treks which starts from Nayapul and ends at Phedi. It is one of the shortest treks in the Annapurna region. The main aim of this trek is to visit one of the most beautiful Gurung villages <strong>Ghandruk</strong>. It is located at an elevation of (2012m) and you can witness the Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Gangapurna, and <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machapuchare\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Machhapuchhre</a> (Fish Tail).\\r\\n\\r\\nIt is a huge Gurung village where you can visit the old and new Gurung museum which shows the real culture of the Gurung Community. Gurung is one of the ethnic groups of Nepal and they have their distinct language and customs. They are known as Gorkhali because most of the British armies are from their community.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis trek goes along the tiny villages of Syauli Bazar, Landruk, Tolkha, Pothana, and Dhampus. You can behold the excellent view of Mt. Dhaulagiri, Annapurna South, Fishtail, Annapurna III, Lamjung Himal, and the entire Pokhara Valley. The unique culture of Gurung and Magar, different sorts of flora and fauna, and the green view of the rural areas of Nepal and Pokhara Valley are the main attractions of this trek. The best season is from August to May."], "description": "<strong>Dhampus to Ghandruk Village trekking </strong>is one of the best of the Annapurna treks which starts from Nayapul and ends at Phedi. It is one of the shortest treks in the Annapurna region. The main aim of this trek is to visit one of the most beautiful Gurung villages <strong>Ghandruk</strong>. It is located at an elevation of (2012m) and you can witness the Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Gangapurna, and <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machapuchare\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Machhapuchhre</a> (Fish Tail).\\r\\n\\r\\nIt is a huge Gurung village where you can visit the old and new Gurung museum which shows the real culture of the Gurung Community. Gurung is one of the ethnic groups of Nepal and they have their distinct language and customs. They are known as Gorkhali because most of the British armies are from their community.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis trek goes along the tiny villages of Syauli Bazar, Landruk, Tolkha, Pothana, and Dhampus. You can behold the excellent view of Mt. Dhaulagiri, Annapurna South, Fishtail, Annapurna III, Lamjung Himal, and the entire Pokhara Valley. The unique culture of Gurung and Magar, different sorts of flora and fauna, and the green view of the rural areas of Nepal and Pokhara Valley are the main attractions of this trek. The best season is from August to May."}, {"id": "overview-2", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Dhampus to Ghandruk Village Trek Overview", "content": ["<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Region: Annapurna, Nepal</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Difficulty: Easy to Moderate</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Duration: 2–5 days (depending on pace)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Max. Altitude: ~2,010m (Ghandruk)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Best Season: Spring (March–May) &amp; Autumn (Sept–Nov)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Permits: TIMS card + Annapurna Conservation Area Permit (ACAP)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Total Trekking Distance: ~25–30 km (varies by route).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Daily Walking: 2–6 hours (varies by number of days).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Trail Type: Stone steps, forest paths, terraced fields, and villages.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Here are 10 highlights of the Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek that make it a must-do adventure in Nepal’s Annapurna region:</strong></h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Stunning Mountain Views\\r\\n</strong>Panoramic vistas of <strong>Annapurna South, Machapuchare (Fishtail), Hiunchuli</strong>, and Dhaulagiri from Australian Camp, Dhampus, and Ghandruk.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"2\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Australian Camp Sunrise/Sunset\\r\\n</strong>One of the <strong>best viewpoints</strong> in the Annapurna foothills, offering golden sunrises over the Himalayas.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"3\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Authentic Gurung Culture\\r\\n</strong>Experience the <strong>traditional Gurung villages</strong> of Dhampus, Landruk, and Ghandruk, known for their stone houses, warm hospitality, and rich cultural heritage.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"4\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Ghandruk Village (Largest Gurung Settlement)\\r\\n</strong>A beautifully preserved Gurung village with <strong>mountain views, a cultural museum, and homestays</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"5\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Short &amp; Beginner-Friendly Trek\\r\\n</strong>Only <strong>2–4 days</strong> with easy-to-moderate trails, perfect for first-time trekkers or those with limited time.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"6\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Terraced Farmlands &amp; Rhododendron Forests\\r\\n</strong>Walk through lush <strong>rice fields, terraced farms</strong>, and (in spring) vibrant <strong>rhododendron blooms</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"7\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> No Risk of Altitude Sickness\\r\\n</strong>Max altitude is only <strong>2,010m (Ghandruk)</strong>, making it safe for all ages and fitness levels.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"8\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Great Teahouse Experience\\r\\n</strong>Cozy lodges with <strong>mountain views, local food (dal bhat, momos), and friendly hosts</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"9\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Flexible Route Options\\r\\n</strong>Start/end at <strong>Phedi, Kande, Nayapul, or Australian Camp</strong>, with options to extend to <strong>Poon Hill or Tadapani</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"10\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Close to Pokhara (Easy Access)\\r\\n</strong>Just <strong>1–2 hours’ drive</strong> from Pokhara, making it a perfect add-on to a Nepal trip.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<strong>Bonus Highlight: Wildlife Spotting\\r\\n</strong>Chance to see <strong>langur monkeys, Himalayan birds, and butterflies</strong> along the trail.\\r\\n<h3><strong>Here are </strong><strong>10 more compelling reasons</strong><strong> to choose the </strong><strong>Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek</strong><strong>, making it an unbeatable Himalayan experience:</strong></h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Perfect for Solo Trekkers &amp; Families\\r\\n</strong>Safe, well-marked trails with frequent teahouses—ideal for solo adventurers, couples, and families with kids.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"2\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> No Crowds (Compared to Everest or ABC)\\r\\n</strong>Enjoy peaceful trails without the mass tourism of longer treks, especially if you avoid peak season (Oct–Nov).</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"3\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Affordable (Low-Budget Friendly)\\r\\n</strong>Minimal costs for food/lodging—no need for expensive guides or flights like in remote regions.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"4\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Year-Round Trekking Possible\\r\\n</strong>Doable even in <strong>winter (Dec–Feb)</strong> and <strong>monsoon (June–Aug)</strong>—just expect rain or chilly nights.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"5\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Minimal Packing Needed\\r\\n</strong>No extreme cold gear required—just layers, good shoes, and a rain jacket (depending on season).</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"6\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Cultural Stops Along the Way\\r\\n</strong>Visit the <strong>Gurung Museum in Ghandruk</strong>, Buddhist stupas, and local craft workshops.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"7\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Delicious Local &amp; Western Food\\r\\n</strong>Teahouses serve everything from <strong>dal bhat</strong> to pasta, apple pie, and even espresso!</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"8\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Optional Adventure Add-Ons\\r\\n</strong>Extend to <strong>Poon Hill (3,210m)</strong> or <strong>Tadapani</strong> for more challenging trails and epic views.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"9\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Photography Paradise\\r\\n</strong>Capture <strong>sunrises over Fishtail, terraced farms, traditional villages, and starry night skies</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"10\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Easy Escape to Pokhara’s Comfort\\r\\n</strong>After the trek, unwind by <strong>Phewa Lake</strong> with cafes, spas, and paragliding!</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Common Route:</strong></h3>\\r\\nStarting Point: Phedi or Dhampus (1–2 hrs drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nEnding Point: Ghandruk (return via Nayapul or loop back to Pokhara).\\r\\n\\r\\nDay 1: Pokhara → Phedi (drive) → Trek to Dhampus (1.5–2 hrs).\\r\\nDay 2: Dhampus → Pothana → Landruk (5–6 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nDay 4: Ghandruk → Nayapul (4–5 hrs) → Drive to Pokhara.\\r\\n<h3><strong>Multiple Starting Points for Dhampus-Ghandruk Trek</strong></h3>\\r\\n<h3><strong style=\\"font-size: 16px;\\">Phedi/Dhampus (Standard Route)</strong></h3>\\r\\nStart: Phedi (1-hour drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Phedi → Dhampus (1.5–2 hrs trek).\\r\\nDay 2: Dhampus → Australian Camp → Pothana → Landruk (5–6 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nEnd: Ghandruk → Nayapul (4–5 hrs) → Drive to Pokhara.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Kande (Via Australian Camp – Popular Route)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nStart: Kande (1.5-hour drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Kande → Australian Camp (1–1.5 hrs steep climb).\\r\\nDay 2: Australian Camp → Pothana → Landruk (4–5 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nEnd: Ghandruk → Nayapul → Pokhara.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Australian Camp Direct (Short &amp; Scenic)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nStart: Drive to Australian Camp (private jeep from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Explore Australian Camp (sunset/sunrise views).\\r\\nDay 2: Australian Camp → Landruk (4–5 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nEnd: Return via Nayapul or extend to Tadapani.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Nayapul (Classic Annapurna Route)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nStart: Nayapul (2-hour drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Nayapul → Birethanti → Ghandruk (5–6 hrs).\\r\\nDay 2: Ghandruk → Landruk → Tolka (optional).\\r\\nDay 3: Tolka → Australian Camp → Kande (loop back).\\r\\n<h3><strong>Multiple Ending Points</strong></h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Nayapul (Most Common)\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>From Ghandruk, descend to Birethanti → Nayapul (4–5 hrs).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Take a bus/taxi to Pokhara (1.5 hrs).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kimche (Jeep Option)\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>From Ghandruk, trek 1.5 hrs to Kimche → Take a jeep to Pokhara.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Loop Back to Australian Camp/Kande\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ghandruk → Landruk → Pothana → Australian Camp → Kande (longer loop).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Extend to Tadapani/Poon Hill\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>From Ghandruk, trek to Tadapani (3–4 hrs) → Continue to Ghorepani/Poon Hill.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<strong>Key Variations &amp; Highlights</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp → Best for sunrise/sunset over Annapurna range.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kande Start → Saves time; steep but rewarding.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Landruk Detour → Quieter than Ghandruk, great homestays.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Nayapul Start/End → Classic Annapurna Sanctuary approach.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<strong>Which Route to Choose?</strong>\\r\\n<table class=\\"table table-bordered table-responsive\\">\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Phedi → Dhampus → Ghandruk</td>\\r\\n<td>3–4 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Easy-Moderate</td>\\r\\n<td>First-timers</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Kande → Australian Camp → Ghandruk</td>\\r\\n<td>3 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Moderate</td>\\r\\n<td>Scenic views</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Australian Camp Direct → Ghandruk</td>\\r\\n<td>2–3 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Easy</td>\\r\\n<td>Short &amp; sweet</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Nayapul → Ghandruk Loop</td>\\r\\n<td>4–5 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Moderate</td>\\r\\n<td>Extended trek</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n</tbody>\\r\\n</table>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Altitude Sickness (AMS)</strong></h4>\\r\\nRisk: Low (Ghandruk is only 2,010m).\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Precautions:</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Stay hydrated.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ascend gradually (no rapid climbs).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Watch for headaches/nausea (descend if severe).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Packing List</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Clothing: Layers, rain jacket, trekking pants, hat, gloves.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Footwear: Sturdy trekking shoes + sandals.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Gear: Backpack, water bottle, trekking poles, sunscreen.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Misc: First-aid kit, cash (no ATMs), camera.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Permits and Costs</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>ACAP Permit: NPR 3,000 (foreigners), NPR 1,000 (SAARC).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>TIMS Card: NPR 2,000.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Accommodation &amp; Meals</strong></h3>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Basic Accommodation</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Teahouses/Lodges: Basic but comfortable; costs around NPR 1000 per night.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Rooms: Twin-sharing with common toilets (hot showers may cost extra).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Electricity/WiFi: Limited; charging devices may cost NPR 100–300/hour.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Mid-Range Hotels/Lodges with Attached Bathrooms</strong></h4>\\r\\n<h6><strong>Australian Camp Area</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Himalayan Front Hotel\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (hot water included).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Stunning Annapurna views, clean rooms, cozy dining area.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Australian Camp Guest House\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Some rooms (confirm when booking).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Friendly hosts, great sunrise views.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Dhampus Village</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Dhampus Peak Lodge\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (24-hour solar hot water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Spacious rooms, mountain-facing balconies.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Landruk Village</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Gurung Cottage\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (hot shower).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Authentic Gurung hospitality, rooftop terrace.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Sunset Lodge\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (electric-heated water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Quiet location, great food.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Ghandruk Village</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Himalaya Lodge\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (reliable hot water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Best views of Annapurna South, cozy fireplace lounge.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Ghandruk Guest House\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (solar-heated water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Central location, clean and modern.\\r\\n<h4><strong>Luxury Resorts &amp; Boutique Hotels on the Trek</strong></h4>\\r\\n<h6><strong>Mountain Lodges of Nepal - Dhampus)</strong></h6>\\r\\nType: Eco-luxury resort with private villas.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Private plunge pools with Annapurna views.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Organic farm-to-table dining.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Spa services (Ayurvedic massages).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Solar-powered, eco-friendly design.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Honeymooners or travelers seeking luxury before/after the trek.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Gurung Cottage (Ghandruk)</strong></h6>\\r\\nLocation: Ghandruk village.\\r\\n\\r\\nType: Boutique family-run lodge with upgraded facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Attached bathrooms with hot showers.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Rooftop terrace for sunrise/sunset views.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Authentic Gurung cuisine (dhal bhat, homemade wine).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Cozy fireplaces in rooms.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Trekkers wanting comfort in Ghandruk.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Himalayan Front Hotel (Australian Camp)</strong></h6>\\r\\nLocation: Australian Camp.\\r\\n\\r\\nType: Mid-range luxury with premium services.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Panoramic views of Annapurna and Machapuchare.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Glass-walled dining hall.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Warm blankets, clean rooms, and Western toilets.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Sunrise photographers and comfort seekers.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Ker &amp; Downey Lodges (Landruk)</strong></h6>\\r\\nLocation: Landruk village (between Dhampus &amp; Ghandruk).\\r\\n\\r\\nType: High-end lodge chain.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Luxury bedding and modern bathrooms.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Gourmet meals (international + Nepali dishes).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Quiet, less-touristed location.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Peaceful luxury in a traditional village.\\r\\n<h3>Budget vs. Mid-range vs. Luxury Comparison</h3>\\r\\n<table class=\\"table table-bordered table-responsive\\">\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td><strong>Feature</strong></td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\"><strong>Budget Teahouse</strong></td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\"><strong>Mid-Range Lodge</strong></td>\\r\\n<td><strong>Luxury Lodges</strong></td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Price/Night</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\">Below USD 10</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">USD 20-40</td>\\r\\n<td>USD 100–400+</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Bathroom</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\">Shared (cold water)</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">Private (hot water)</td>\\r\\n<td>Private (hot shower)</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Room Quality</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\">Basic wooden beds</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">Clean, comfy beds</td>\\r\\n<td>Heated, premium linens</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Food</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\"><strong>Breakfast</strong>: Porridge, toast, eggs, Tibetan bread, tea/coffee.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Lunch/Dinner</strong>: Dal Bhat (lentil soup + rice), noodles, pasta, momos, soups.</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">As per your choice,\\r\\nEg: Pasta, pizza, better coffee</td>\\r\\n<td>As per your choice, Eg: Gourmet / International</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n</tbody>\\r\\n</table>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Senior-friendly &amp; luxury-focused itinerary for the Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek</strong></h3>\\r\\n<strong>Designed for travelers who prefer shorter walking days (2–4 hours/day), comfortable stays, and scenic drives to minimize exertion while maximizing Himalayan views and cultural experiences.</strong>\\r\\n<h4><strong><u>5-Day Luxury Itinerary (With Minimal Trekking)</u></strong></h4>\\r\\nTheme: <em>\\"Slow-Paced Comfort in the Annapurna Foothills\\"</em>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 1: Pokhara → Drive to Australian Camp (Sunset Magic)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nMorning: Private jeep transfer from Pokhara to Kande (1.5 hrs).\\r\\nTrek: Gentle 1-hour uphill walk to Australian Camp (2,050m).\\r\\nStay: <em>Himalayan Front Hotel</em> (private bathroom, mountain-view balcony).\\r\\nHighlight: Sunset over Annapurna South with champagne!\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 2: Australian Camp → Landruk (Easy Descent)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nTrek: 2–3 hours downhill via Pothana and Deurali to Landruk (1,560m).\\r\\nStay: <em>Ker &amp; Downey Lodge Landruk</em> (luxury rooms, hot showers, garden seating).\\r\\nHighlight: Gurung cultural dinner with local dance (optional).\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (Short Riverside Walk)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nTrek: 2.5 hours along the Modi Khola River to Ghandruk (2,010m).\\r\\nStay: <em>Himalaya Lodge</em> (deluxe room with fireplace, attached bathroom).\\r\\nHighlight: Visit the Gurung Museum and relax with a hot stone massage.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 4: Ghandruk Exploration (Zero Trekking Day)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nMorning: Sunrise yoga session with Annapurna views.\\r\\nActivity: Guided village tour (traditional homes, weaving demo).\\r\\nStay: Second night at <em>Himalaya Lodge</em>.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 5: Ghandruk → Nayapul → Pokhara (Jeep Option)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nOption 1 (Trek + Drive): 2-hour gentle walk to Kimche → Private jeep to Pokhara (1.5 hrs).\\r\\nOption 2 (No Trek): Direct jeep from Ghandruk to Pokhara (3 hrs, bumpy but scenic).\\r\\n<h4><strong>Alternatives for Zero-Trekking Travelers</strong></h4>\\r\\n<strong>Heli-Trek Combo:</strong>\\r\\nDay 1: Pokhara → Heli to Ghandruk (15 mins). Stay 2 nights, explore village.\\r\\nDay 3: Heli return or jeep to Pokhara.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Pokhara-Based Day Trips:</strong>\\r\\nDrive to Australian Camp for lunch/sunset → Return same day.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Packing Tips for Seniors/Luxury Trekkers</strong></h6>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Footwear: Non-slip hiking sandals (e.g., Keen) + trekking poles.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Extras: Portable oxygen canister (for breathlessness), knee braces.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Clothing: Light down jacket (mornings are chilly even in spring).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h6><strong>Why This Itinerary Works?</strong></h6>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Max Elevation: Only 2,010m (Ghandruk)—no altitude risks.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Walking Hours: ≤3 hours/day with breaks.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Cultural Depth: More time to interact with locals vs. rushing trails.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3><strong>FAQs </strong></h3>\\r\\nQ: Is a guide necessary?\\r\\nA: Not mandatory, but helpful for navigation/culture.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can solo trekkers join groups?\\r\\nA: Yes, teahouses are social; or join organized tours.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Phone network?\\r\\nA: Ncell/NTC work sporadically; WiFi is paid.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Is it safe for beginners?\\r\\nA: Yes, but fitness helps for stone steps/long walks.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Wildlife sightings?\\r\\nA: Possible: monkeys, birds, occasional langurs.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I start from Pokhara directly?\\r\\nA: No, you need to drive to Phedi/Kande/Nayapul (1–2 hrs).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Is Australian Camp worth adding?\\r\\nA: Yes! Best mountain views and cozy lodges.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Which route has fewer stairs?\\r\\nA: Kande → Australian Camp has fewer steps than Phedi → Dhampus.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I end at Kimche instead of Nayapul?\\r\\nA: Yes, Kimche has jeeps to Pokhara (saves trekking time).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Is a guide needed for these routes?\\r\\nA: Not mandatory, but helpful for navigation in loop trails.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are there hotels with attached bathrooms and hot showers on this trek?\\r\\nA: Yes! Mid-range and luxury lodges like <em>Himalayan Front Hotel (Australian Camp)</em>, <em>Himalaya Lodge (Ghandruk)</em>, and <em>Ker &amp; Downey Lodges (Landruk)</em> offer private bathrooms, 24/7 hot water, and comfortable beds. Budget teahouses may charge extra for hot showers.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I book accommodations in advance?\\r\\nA: Yes, especially in peak season (Oct–Nov, Mar–Apr). Luxury lodges require advance reservations. Your guide/agency can arrange this.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are there electric blankets or heaters in rooms?\\r\\nA: Most luxury lodges provide heaters or extra blankets. Budget teahouses rely on thick quilts—ask for a \\"deluxe room\\" for better comfort.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: What’s the best way to reach the trek start point from Pokhara?\\r\\nA: Private jeep (most comfortable) to Phedi (1 hr) or Kande (1.5 hrs) or Nayapul (2 hrs)\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I skip trekking entirely and use vehicles?\\r\\nA: Partially! You can:\\r\\nDrive to Australian Camp (via Kande, then 1-hr walk).\\r\\nJeep from Ghandruk to Kimche/Nayapul (bumpy but saves walking).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are roads safe for seniors?\\r\\nA: Roads are rough but manageable in a 4WD jeep. Avoid monsoon (June–Aug) due to landslides.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: What cultural activities can I do in Ghandruk?\\r\\nA: Visit the Gurung Museum (traditional costumes, weapons).\\r\\nAttend a local dance performance (arranged by lodges).\\r\\nTry Gurung cuisine: <em>dal bhat</em>, <em>gundruk</em> (fermented greens), and <em>raksi</em> (local alcohol).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I participate in a homestay?\\r\\nA: Yes! Gurung Cottage (Ghandruk) and Landruk homestays offer authentic experiences. Book ahead.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are villages wheelchair-friendly?\\r\\nA: No—trails have stone steps and uneven paths. Seniors with mobility issues should opt for jeep/heli access.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are there yoga retreats or sessions along the trek?\\r\\nA: Yes!\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp: Sunrise yoga with mountain views (ask your lodge or guide).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ghandruk: <em>Himalaya Lodge</em>offers yoga mats and guided sessions.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pokhara Add-On: Post-trek relaxation with yoga.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Can I meditate in the mountains?\\r\\nA: Absolutely! Silent spots:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp (sunrise meditation).\\r\\nGhandruk’s sunrise viewpoint.\\r\\nLandruk’s terraced farms.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Is altitude sickness a risk?\\r\\nA: Minimal (max altitude: 2,010m). Seniors should still:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Stay hydrated.\\r\\nWalk slowly.\\r\\nAvoid alcohol.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: What if I get tired during the trek?\\r\\nA: Options:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hire a mule to ride between villages.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Shorten walks (e.g., drive to Landruk, then trek 1 hr to Ghandruk).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Are there pharmacies or doctors on the trail?\\r\\nA: Basic clinics in Ghandruk/Landruk. Carry medications, knee braces, and a first-aid kit.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I get vegetarian/vegan food?\\r\\nA: Yes! Teahouses serve:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Veg <em>dal bhat</em>, noodles, soups, and fresh <em>sel roti</em>(Nepali donuts).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Luxury lodges offer pasta, salads, and desserts.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Is bottled water available?\\r\\nA: Yes ($1–$3/bottle), but reduce plastic use by:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Carrying a SteriPen or purification tablets.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Asking lodges for boiled/filtered water.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Packing Tips for Seniors?\\r\\n\\r\\nA: Must-Haves: Trekking poles, knee sleeves, slip-proof shoes, and a small daypack.\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Luxury Add-Ons: Portable oxygen canister, inflatable neck pillow, and down booties for cold nights.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: When is the least crowded time?\\r\\nA: December–February (cold but clear) or September (post-monsoon greenery). Avoid monsoon (June–Aug).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: How cold does it get at night?\\r\\nA: 5–10°C (41–50°F) in autumn/spring. Luxury lodges provide heaters/extra blankets.\\r\\n<h3>Final Tips</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Start early to avoid afternoon clouds.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bargain lightly for souvenirs in Ghandruk.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Respect local customs (ask before photographing people).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp is crowded in peak season (Oct–Nov).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Landruk offers authentic Gurung culture with fewer tourists.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If short on time, do Kande → Australian Camp → Ghandruk → Nayapul (3 days).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>For a stress-free trek, book a private guide/porter (~$25–$50/day) to handle logistics, carry bags, and adjust pacing.</li>\\r\\n</ul>"], "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Region: Annapurna, Nepal</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Difficulty: Easy to Moderate</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Duration: 2–5 days (depending on pace)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Max. Altitude: ~2,010m (Ghandruk)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Best Season: Spring (March–May) &amp; Autumn (Sept–Nov)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Permits: TIMS card + Annapurna Conservation Area Permit (ACAP)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Total Trekking Distance: ~25–30 km (varies by route).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Daily Walking: 2–6 hours (varies by number of days).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Trail Type: Stone steps, forest paths, terraced fields, and villages.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Here are 10 highlights of the Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek that make it a must-do adventure in Nepal’s Annapurna region:</strong></h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Stunning Mountain Views\\r\\n</strong>Panoramic vistas of <strong>Annapurna South, Machapuchare (Fishtail), Hiunchuli</strong>, and Dhaulagiri from Australian Camp, Dhampus, and Ghandruk.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"2\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Australian Camp Sunrise/Sunset\\r\\n</strong>One of the <strong>best viewpoints</strong> in the Annapurna foothills, offering golden sunrises over the Himalayas.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"3\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Authentic Gurung Culture\\r\\n</strong>Experience the <strong>traditional Gurung villages</strong> of Dhampus, Landruk, and Ghandruk, known for their stone houses, warm hospitality, and rich cultural heritage.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"4\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Ghandruk Village (Largest Gurung Settlement)\\r\\n</strong>A beautifully preserved Gurung village with <strong>mountain views, a cultural museum, and homestays</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"5\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Short &amp; Beginner-Friendly Trek\\r\\n</strong>Only <strong>2–4 days</strong> with easy-to-moderate trails, perfect for first-time trekkers or those with limited time.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"6\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Terraced Farmlands &amp; Rhododendron Forests\\r\\n</strong>Walk through lush <strong>rice fields, terraced farms</strong>, and (in spring) vibrant <strong>rhododendron blooms</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"7\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> No Risk of Altitude Sickness\\r\\n</strong>Max altitude is only <strong>2,010m (Ghandruk)</strong>, making it safe for all ages and fitness levels.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"8\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Great Teahouse Experience\\r\\n</strong>Cozy lodges with <strong>mountain views, local food (dal bhat, momos), and friendly hosts</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"9\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Flexible Route Options\\r\\n</strong>Start/end at <strong>Phedi, Kande, Nayapul, or Australian Camp</strong>, with options to extend to <strong>Poon Hill or Tadapani</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"10\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Close to Pokhara (Easy Access)\\r\\n</strong>Just <strong>1–2 hours’ drive</strong> from Pokhara, making it a perfect add-on to a Nepal trip.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<strong>Bonus Highlight: Wildlife Spotting\\r\\n</strong>Chance to see <strong>langur monkeys, Himalayan birds, and butterflies</strong> along the trail.\\r\\n<h3><strong>Here are </strong><strong>10 more compelling reasons</strong><strong> to choose the </strong><strong>Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek</strong><strong>, making it an unbeatable Himalayan experience:</strong></h3>\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Perfect for Solo Trekkers &amp; Families\\r\\n</strong>Safe, well-marked trails with frequent teahouses—ideal for solo adventurers, couples, and families with kids.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"2\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> No Crowds (Compared to Everest or ABC)\\r\\n</strong>Enjoy peaceful trails without the mass tourism of longer treks, especially if you avoid peak season (Oct–Nov).</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"3\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Affordable (Low-Budget Friendly)\\r\\n</strong>Minimal costs for food/lodging—no need for expensive guides or flights like in remote regions.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"4\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Year-Round Trekking Possible\\r\\n</strong>Doable even in <strong>winter (Dec–Feb)</strong> and <strong>monsoon (June–Aug)</strong>—just expect rain or chilly nights.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"5\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Minimal Packing Needed\\r\\n</strong>No extreme cold gear required—just layers, good shoes, and a rain jacket (depending on season).</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"6\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Cultural Stops Along the Way\\r\\n</strong>Visit the <strong>Gurung Museum in Ghandruk</strong>, Buddhist stupas, and local craft workshops.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"7\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Delicious Local &amp; Western Food\\r\\n</strong>Teahouses serve everything from <strong>dal bhat</strong> to pasta, apple pie, and even espresso!</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"8\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Optional Adventure Add-Ons\\r\\n</strong>Extend to <strong>Poon Hill (3,210m)</strong> or <strong>Tadapani</strong> for more challenging trails and epic views.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"9\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Photography Paradise\\r\\n</strong>Capture <strong>sunrises over Fishtail, terraced farms, traditional villages, and starry night skies</strong>.</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<ol start=\\"10\\">\\r\\n \\t<li><strong> Easy Escape to Pokhara’s Comfort\\r\\n</strong>After the trek, unwind by <strong>Phewa Lake</strong> with cafes, spas, and paragliding!</li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Common Route:</strong></h3>\\r\\nStarting Point: Phedi or Dhampus (1–2 hrs drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nEnding Point: Ghandruk (return via Nayapul or loop back to Pokhara).\\r\\n\\r\\nDay 1: Pokhara → Phedi (drive) → Trek to Dhampus (1.5–2 hrs).\\r\\nDay 2: Dhampus → Pothana → Landruk (5–6 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nDay 4: Ghandruk → Nayapul (4–5 hrs) → Drive to Pokhara.\\r\\n<h3><strong>Multiple Starting Points for Dhampus-Ghandruk Trek</strong></h3>\\r\\n<h3><strong style=\\"font-size: 16px;\\">Phedi/Dhampus (Standard Route)</strong></h3>\\r\\nStart: Phedi (1-hour drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Phedi → Dhampus (1.5–2 hrs trek).\\r\\nDay 2: Dhampus → Australian Camp → Pothana → Landruk (5–6 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nEnd: Ghandruk → Nayapul (4–5 hrs) → Drive to Pokhara.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Kande (Via Australian Camp – Popular Route)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nStart: Kande (1.5-hour drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Kande → Australian Camp (1–1.5 hrs steep climb).\\r\\nDay 2: Australian Camp → Pothana → Landruk (4–5 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nEnd: Ghandruk → Nayapul → Pokhara.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Australian Camp Direct (Short &amp; Scenic)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nStart: Drive to Australian Camp (private jeep from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Explore Australian Camp (sunset/sunrise views).\\r\\nDay 2: Australian Camp → Landruk (4–5 hrs).\\r\\nDay 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (3–4 hrs).\\r\\nEnd: Return via Nayapul or extend to Tadapani.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Nayapul (Classic Annapurna Route)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nStart: Nayapul (2-hour drive from Pokhara).\\r\\nDay 1: Nayapul → Birethanti → Ghandruk (5–6 hrs).\\r\\nDay 2: Ghandruk → Landruk → Tolka (optional).\\r\\nDay 3: Tolka → Australian Camp → Kande (loop back).\\r\\n<h3><strong>Multiple Ending Points</strong></h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Nayapul (Most Common)\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>From Ghandruk, descend to Birethanti → Nayapul (4–5 hrs).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Take a bus/taxi to Pokhara (1.5 hrs).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kimche (Jeep Option)\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>From Ghandruk, trek 1.5 hrs to Kimche → Take a jeep to Pokhara.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Loop Back to Australian Camp/Kande\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ghandruk → Landruk → Pothana → Australian Camp → Kande (longer loop).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Extend to Tadapani/Poon Hill\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>From Ghandruk, trek to Tadapani (3–4 hrs) → Continue to Ghorepani/Poon Hill.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<strong>Key Variations &amp; Highlights</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp → Best for sunrise/sunset over Annapurna range.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kande Start → Saves time; steep but rewarding.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Landruk Detour → Quieter than Ghandruk, great homestays.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Nayapul Start/End → Classic Annapurna Sanctuary approach.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<strong>Which Route to Choose?</strong>\\r\\n<table class=\\"table table-bordered table-responsive\\">\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Phedi → Dhampus → Ghandruk</td>\\r\\n<td>3–4 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Easy-Moderate</td>\\r\\n<td>First-timers</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Kande → Australian Camp → Ghandruk</td>\\r\\n<td>3 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Moderate</td>\\r\\n<td>Scenic views</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Australian Camp Direct → Ghandruk</td>\\r\\n<td>2–3 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Easy</td>\\r\\n<td>Short &amp; sweet</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Nayapul → Ghandruk Loop</td>\\r\\n<td>4–5 days</td>\\r\\n<td>Moderate</td>\\r\\n<td>Extended trek</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n</tbody>\\r\\n</table>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Altitude Sickness (AMS)</strong></h4>\\r\\nRisk: Low (Ghandruk is only 2,010m).\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Precautions:</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Stay hydrated.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ascend gradually (no rapid climbs).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Watch for headaches/nausea (descend if severe).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Packing List</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Clothing: Layers, rain jacket, trekking pants, hat, gloves.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Footwear: Sturdy trekking shoes + sandals.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Gear: Backpack, water bottle, trekking poles, sunscreen.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Misc: First-aid kit, cash (no ATMs), camera.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Permits and Costs</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>ACAP Permit: NPR 3,000 (foreigners), NPR 1,000 (SAARC).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>TIMS Card: NPR 2,000.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Accommodation &amp; Meals</strong></h3>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Basic Accommodation</strong></h4>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Teahouses/Lodges: Basic but comfortable; costs around NPR 1000 per night.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Rooms: Twin-sharing with common toilets (hot showers may cost extra).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Electricity/WiFi: Limited; charging devices may cost NPR 100–300/hour.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4><strong>Mid-Range Hotels/Lodges with Attached Bathrooms</strong></h4>\\r\\n<h6><strong>Australian Camp Area</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Himalayan Front Hotel\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (hot water included).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Stunning Annapurna views, clean rooms, cozy dining area.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Australian Camp Guest House\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Some rooms (confirm when booking).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Friendly hosts, great sunrise views.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Dhampus Village</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Dhampus Peak Lodge\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (24-hour solar hot water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Spacious rooms, mountain-facing balconies.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Landruk Village</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Gurung Cottage\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (hot shower).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Authentic Gurung hospitality, rooftop terrace.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Sunset Lodge\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (electric-heated water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Quiet location, great food.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Ghandruk Village</strong></h6>\\r\\n<strong>Himalaya Lodge\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (reliable hot water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Best views of Annapurna South, cozy fireplace lounge.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Ghandruk Guest House\\r\\nAttached Bathroom</strong>: Yes (solar-heated water).\\r\\n<strong>Perks</strong>: Central location, clean and modern.\\r\\n<h4><strong>Luxury Resorts &amp; Boutique Hotels on the Trek</strong></h4>\\r\\n<h6><strong>Mountain Lodges of Nepal - Dhampus)</strong></h6>\\r\\nType: Eco-luxury resort with private villas.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Private plunge pools with Annapurna views.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Organic farm-to-table dining.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Spa services (Ayurvedic massages).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Solar-powered, eco-friendly design.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Honeymooners or travelers seeking luxury before/after the trek.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Gurung Cottage (Ghandruk)</strong></h6>\\r\\nLocation: Ghandruk village.\\r\\n\\r\\nType: Boutique family-run lodge with upgraded facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Attached bathrooms with hot showers.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Rooftop terrace for sunrise/sunset views.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Authentic Gurung cuisine (dhal bhat, homemade wine).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Cozy fireplaces in rooms.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Trekkers wanting comfort in Ghandruk.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Himalayan Front Hotel (Australian Camp)</strong></h6>\\r\\nLocation: Australian Camp.\\r\\n\\r\\nType: Mid-range luxury with premium services.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Panoramic views of Annapurna and Machapuchare.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Glass-walled dining hall.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Warm blankets, clean rooms, and Western toilets.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Sunrise photographers and comfort seekers.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Ker &amp; Downey Lodges (Landruk)</strong></h6>\\r\\nLocation: Landruk village (between Dhampus &amp; Ghandruk).\\r\\n\\r\\nType: High-end lodge chain.\\r\\n\\r\\nFeatures:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Luxury bedding and modern bathrooms.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Gourmet meals (international + Nepali dishes).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Quiet, less-touristed location.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nBest For: Peaceful luxury in a traditional village.\\r\\n<h3>Budget vs. Mid-range vs. Luxury Comparison</h3>\\r\\n<table class=\\"table table-bordered table-responsive\\">\\r\\n<tbody>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td><strong>Feature</strong></td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\"><strong>Budget Teahouse</strong></td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\"><strong>Mid-Range Lodge</strong></td>\\r\\n<td><strong>Luxury Lodges</strong></td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Price/Night</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\">Below USD 10</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">USD 20-40</td>\\r\\n<td>USD 100–400+</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Bathroom</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\">Shared (cold water)</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">Private (hot water)</td>\\r\\n<td>Private (hot shower)</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Room Quality</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\">Basic wooden beds</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">Clean, comfy beds</td>\\r\\n<td>Heated, premium linens</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>Food</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"206\\"><strong>Breakfast</strong>: Porridge, toast, eggs, Tibetan bread, tea/coffee.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Lunch/Dinner</strong>: Dal Bhat (lentil soup + rice), noodles, pasta, momos, soups.</td>\\r\\n<td width=\\"154\\">As per your choice,\\r\\nEg: Pasta, pizza, better coffee</td>\\r\\n<td>As per your choice, Eg: Gourmet / International</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n</tbody>\\r\\n</table>\\r\\n<h3><strong>Senior-friendly &amp; luxury-focused itinerary for the Dhampus to Ghandruk Trek</strong></h3>\\r\\n<strong>Designed for travelers who prefer shorter walking days (2–4 hours/day), comfortable stays, and scenic drives to minimize exertion while maximizing Himalayan views and cultural experiences.</strong>\\r\\n<h4><strong><u>5-Day Luxury Itinerary (With Minimal Trekking)</u></strong></h4>\\r\\nTheme: <em>\\"Slow-Paced Comfort in the Annapurna Foothills\\"</em>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 1: Pokhara → Drive to Australian Camp (Sunset Magic)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nMorning: Private jeep transfer from Pokhara to Kande (1.5 hrs).\\r\\nTrek: Gentle 1-hour uphill walk to Australian Camp (2,050m).\\r\\nStay: <em>Himalayan Front Hotel</em> (private bathroom, mountain-view balcony).\\r\\nHighlight: Sunset over Annapurna South with champagne!\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 2: Australian Camp → Landruk (Easy Descent)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nTrek: 2–3 hours downhill via Pothana and Deurali to Landruk (1,560m).\\r\\nStay: <em>Ker &amp; Downey Lodge Landruk</em> (luxury rooms, hot showers, garden seating).\\r\\nHighlight: Gurung cultural dinner with local dance (optional).\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 3: Landruk → Ghandruk (Short Riverside Walk)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nTrek: 2.5 hours along the Modi Khola River to Ghandruk (2,010m).\\r\\nStay: <em>Himalaya Lodge</em> (deluxe room with fireplace, attached bathroom).\\r\\nHighlight: Visit the Gurung Museum and relax with a hot stone massage.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 4: Ghandruk Exploration (Zero Trekking Day)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nMorning: Sunrise yoga session with Annapurna views.\\r\\nActivity: Guided village tour (traditional homes, weaving demo).\\r\\nStay: Second night at <em>Himalaya Lodge</em>.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 5: Ghandruk → Nayapul → Pokhara (Jeep Option)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\nOption 1 (Trek + Drive): 2-hour gentle walk to Kimche → Private jeep to Pokhara (1.5 hrs).\\r\\nOption 2 (No Trek): Direct jeep from Ghandruk to Pokhara (3 hrs, bumpy but scenic).\\r\\n<h4><strong>Alternatives for Zero-Trekking Travelers</strong></h4>\\r\\n<strong>Heli-Trek Combo:</strong>\\r\\nDay 1: Pokhara → Heli to Ghandruk (15 mins). Stay 2 nights, explore village.\\r\\nDay 3: Heli return or jeep to Pokhara.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Pokhara-Based Day Trips:</strong>\\r\\nDrive to Australian Camp for lunch/sunset → Return same day.\\r\\n<h6><strong>Packing Tips for Seniors/Luxury Trekkers</strong></h6>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Footwear: Non-slip hiking sandals (e.g., Keen) + trekking poles.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Extras: Portable oxygen canister (for breathlessness), knee braces.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Clothing: Light down jacket (mornings are chilly even in spring).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h6><strong>Why This Itinerary Works?</strong></h6>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Max Elevation: Only 2,010m (Ghandruk)—no altitude risks.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Walking Hours: ≤3 hours/day with breaks.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Cultural Depth: More time to interact with locals vs. rushing trails.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3><strong>FAQs </strong></h3>\\r\\nQ: Is a guide necessary?\\r\\nA: Not mandatory, but helpful for navigation/culture.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can solo trekkers join groups?\\r\\nA: Yes, teahouses are social; or join organized tours.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Phone network?\\r\\nA: Ncell/NTC work sporadically; WiFi is paid.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Is it safe for beginners?\\r\\nA: Yes, but fitness helps for stone steps/long walks.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Wildlife sightings?\\r\\nA: Possible: monkeys, birds, occasional langurs.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I start from Pokhara directly?\\r\\nA: No, you need to drive to Phedi/Kande/Nayapul (1–2 hrs).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Is Australian Camp worth adding?\\r\\nA: Yes! Best mountain views and cozy lodges.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Which route has fewer stairs?\\r\\nA: Kande → Australian Camp has fewer steps than Phedi → Dhampus.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I end at Kimche instead of Nayapul?\\r\\nA: Yes, Kimche has jeeps to Pokhara (saves trekking time).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Is a guide needed for these routes?\\r\\nA: Not mandatory, but helpful for navigation in loop trails.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are there hotels with attached bathrooms and hot showers on this trek?\\r\\nA: Yes! Mid-range and luxury lodges like <em>Himalayan Front Hotel (Australian Camp)</em>, <em>Himalaya Lodge (Ghandruk)</em>, and <em>Ker &amp; Downey Lodges (Landruk)</em> offer private bathrooms, 24/7 hot water, and comfortable beds. Budget teahouses may charge extra for hot showers.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I book accommodations in advance?\\r\\nA: Yes, especially in peak season (Oct–Nov, Mar–Apr). Luxury lodges require advance reservations. Your guide/agency can arrange this.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are there electric blankets or heaters in rooms?\\r\\nA: Most luxury lodges provide heaters or extra blankets. Budget teahouses rely on thick quilts—ask for a \\"deluxe room\\" for better comfort.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: What’s the best way to reach the trek start point from Pokhara?\\r\\nA: Private jeep (most comfortable) to Phedi (1 hr) or Kande (1.5 hrs) or Nayapul (2 hrs)\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I skip trekking entirely and use vehicles?\\r\\nA: Partially! You can:\\r\\nDrive to Australian Camp (via Kande, then 1-hr walk).\\r\\nJeep from Ghandruk to Kimche/Nayapul (bumpy but saves walking).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are roads safe for seniors?\\r\\nA: Roads are rough but manageable in a 4WD jeep. Avoid monsoon (June–Aug) due to landslides.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: What cultural activities can I do in Ghandruk?\\r\\nA: Visit the Gurung Museum (traditional costumes, weapons).\\r\\nAttend a local dance performance (arranged by lodges).\\r\\nTry Gurung cuisine: <em>dal bhat</em>, <em>gundruk</em> (fermented greens), and <em>raksi</em> (local alcohol).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I participate in a homestay?\\r\\nA: Yes! Gurung Cottage (Ghandruk) and Landruk homestays offer authentic experiences. Book ahead.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are villages wheelchair-friendly?\\r\\nA: No—trails have stone steps and uneven paths. Seniors with mobility issues should opt for jeep/heli access.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Are there yoga retreats or sessions along the trek?\\r\\nA: Yes!\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp: Sunrise yoga with mountain views (ask your lodge or guide).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ghandruk: <em>Himalaya Lodge</em>offers yoga mats and guided sessions.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pokhara Add-On: Post-trek relaxation with yoga.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Can I meditate in the mountains?\\r\\nA: Absolutely! Silent spots:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp (sunrise meditation).\\r\\nGhandruk’s sunrise viewpoint.\\r\\nLandruk’s terraced farms.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Is altitude sickness a risk?\\r\\nA: Minimal (max altitude: 2,010m). Seniors should still:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Stay hydrated.\\r\\nWalk slowly.\\r\\nAvoid alcohol.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: What if I get tired during the trek?\\r\\nA: Options:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hire a mule to ride between villages.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Shorten walks (e.g., drive to Landruk, then trek 1 hr to Ghandruk).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Are there pharmacies or doctors on the trail?\\r\\nA: Basic clinics in Ghandruk/Landruk. Carry medications, knee braces, and a first-aid kit.\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: Can I get vegetarian/vegan food?\\r\\nA: Yes! Teahouses serve:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Veg <em>dal bhat</em>, noodles, soups, and fresh <em>sel roti</em>(Nepali donuts).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Luxury lodges offer pasta, salads, and desserts.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Is bottled water available?\\r\\nA: Yes ($1–$3/bottle), but reduce plastic use by:\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Carrying a SteriPen or purification tablets.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Asking lodges for boiled/filtered water.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: Packing Tips for Seniors?\\r\\n\\r\\nA: Must-Haves: Trekking poles, knee sleeves, slip-proof shoes, and a small daypack.\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Luxury Add-Ons: Portable oxygen canister, inflatable neck pillow, and down booties for cold nights.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nQ: When is the least crowded time?\\r\\nA: December–February (cold but clear) or September (post-monsoon greenery). Avoid monsoon (June–Aug).\\r\\n\\r\\nQ: How cold does it get at night?\\r\\nA: 5–10°C (41–50°F) in autumn/spring. Luxury lodges provide heaters/extra blankets.\\r\\n<h3>Final Tips</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Start early to avoid afternoon clouds.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bargain lightly for souvenirs in Ghandruk.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Respect local customs (ask before photographing people).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Australian Camp is crowded in peak season (Oct–Nov).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Landruk offers authentic Gurung culture with fewer tourists.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If short on time, do Kande → Australian Camp → Ghandruk → Nayapul (3 days).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>For a stress-free trek, book a private guide/porter (~$25–$50/day) to handle logistics, carry bags, and adjust pacing.</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Fully private trip (even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.", "Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).", "Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.", "English speaking cultural city tour guide.", "Drinking Water."], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Fully private trip (even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.", "Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).", "Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.", "English speaking cultural city tour guide.", "Drinking Water."], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Sample Itinerary: Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "Explore Dhampus to Ghandruk Village Trekking with Everest Vacation.", "trip_highlights": "<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nThe main aim of this trek is to visit one of the most beautiful Gurung villages Ghandruk. It is located on an elevation of (1090m) and you can witness the Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Gangapurna, and Fish Tail.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "trip_type_level": "Short and Easy", "meta_description": "Dhampus to Ghandruk Village trekking is one of the best of the Annapurna treks which starts from Nayapul and ends at Phedi.", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": "Private AC Vehicle"}, "trip_transportations": "Private AC Vehicle", "trip_highlights_title": "It is one of the shortest treks in the Annapurna region"}	2023-12-08 05:55:29+00	2025-10-17 10:15:42+01
201	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "4", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Short and Easy"}, "faq": [{"answer": "- You can enter Kathmandu by international flight from Europe and other parts of Asia, Australia and USA with stopover and transit on route flight to reaching Kathmandu (Tribhuvan International airport),\\r\\n\\r\\n- Overland from Delhi, Sikkim, and Darjeeling from India\\r\\n\\r\\n- To enter from China catch a flight or train to Lhasa (Tibet) and then drive/fly to Kathmandu.", "question": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "All valid Passports are required with a proper visa for you to enter Nepal. Visa can be obtained from your countries through Nepal Embassy and Consulate, or one can get a permit on arrival at any port of entry at the border or Kathmandu international airport. Minimum visa of a week and a maximum of 1 month can be obtained from here. If you urge to elongate the stay, your visa extension can be done for an extra cost per day or week basis.", "question": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?"}, {"answer": "Most of the travel agents in Nepal, especially in Kathmandu and other touristic areas, are reliable and certified by the government. Some of these agencies have been running for more than a decade with the utmost experience in travel line. However, as per your taste and duration in Nepal, you can book with us as we provide topnotch services with a flexible period of your journey.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe have an expert knowledgeable local guide with complete training and experience in culture, history of the destination you will visit. With us, you will be able to experience the destinations to your fullest without missing a thing. We keep in touch with you throughout your journey till your departure and aid you in your tour. Similarly, we have a wide range of transport vehicles for your ease and a standby team for any complications during your trip.", "question": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Nepal has four seasons including the monsoon (wet months). The climate is not too cold in winter and mildly hot in summer. The country experiences a moderate climate in every other time of the year.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou can experience the destinations differently in each weather, and the memories will be equally delightful. As for sightseeing and cultural tour, You can visit this country at any time of the year. However, the best time will be from the month of March to May and October to November when the views are clear especially of the high snow-capped mountain range.", "question": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?"}, {"answer": "Depending upon the duration and area of your tours, you can expect something new in every destination. Nepal will surprise you with delights as this place is like no other when it comes to traveling. Famous for numerous historical, cultural monuments which are mostly listed in World Heritage Sites by UNESCO, Nepal is a travel lover's Zion.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal is a melting pot of Hindu and Buddhist with small minority of Islamic, Christians, Jain and Sikh religions.\\r\\n\\r\\nMost of the monuments temples and monasteries are of Hindu and Buddhist religions, other places of interest are old historical Durbar squares as the palaces of former kings.\\r\\n\\r\\nNepal embraces you with its unique Himalayan setting full of mountains, rivers, and thick jungles as well. One can take an elephant safari in one most famous national park of Chitwan to observe wildlife and nature from close. Rare Royal Bengal Tiger, one-horned rhinoceros many different types of deer and other wildlife and 700 species of exotic birds live in these jungles.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe other experience of Nepal is its panoramic scene of snow-capped mountains in the comfort of nice and cozy hotels and resorts and with the warm hospitality of native villagers in homestay facilities.\\r\\n\\r\\nWhatever your taste and interest are? Nepal is an amazing country with everything you would want in a travel destination.", "question": "5. What to expect on tours?"}], "meta": {"_edit_last": "5", "_edit_lock": "1707375416:5", "_dp_original": "909", "_thumbnail_id": "730", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "4", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "Ghorepani Poonhill Hot Spring Trek", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Ghorepani Poonhill Hot Spring Trek", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "44", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Ghorepani PoonHill Hot Spring Trek is a comparatively easy walk that passes through beautiful Gurung village offering outstanding landscapes.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Short and Easy", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "ghorepani-poonhill-hot-spring-trek", "tags": [], "title": "Ghorepani Poonhill Hot Spring Trek", "duration": "4 Days", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "<strong>Ghorepani PoonHill Hot Spring Treks</strong> is a comparatively easy walk that begins at Nayapul. It takes about a one-hour drive from Pokhara. Pokhara is also a doorstep for most of the treks in the Annapurna region.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis <strong>Ghorepani Poonhill hot spring trek</strong> passes through beautiful Gurung village which offers outstanding landscapes and a variety of flora and fauna. Get an overview of the grand south Annapurna from Ulleri village. Passing through Ghorepani village you bump into beautiful orchids, massive Himalayan bamboo, and dense Rhododendron forest.\\r\\n\\r\\nOn the other hand, a well-designed rice field over the entire slope gives you a breathtaking experience. A downhill walk to Jhinu Danda through Tadapani. Ghorepani PoonHill trek with hot springs concludes and gives you the time for Kathmandu Valley Culture and paradise city <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pokhara\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Pokhara</a> and Annapurna Himalayan region of Nepal."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Drive to Nayapul and trek to Ulleri.", "richText": "We resume our morning drive to Birethati. It is a large and prosperous town beside the Modi River. After reaching Birethati, you will head up the main trail to Ramgai and Sudame. Ascend gradually up the side of the valley reaching Hile (1495m) before pushing on to TikheDhunga (1575m). Continue trial to cross a stream (Bhrungdi Khola) then ascend a steep stone staircase to the large Magar village at Ulleri. Overnight at Lodge.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 2, "meal": "", "title": "Trek to Ghorepani and explore.", "richText": "It is a pleasant walk through rhododendron and oak forests and crosses a stream before making a short and final climb to Nangethanti. Then you can ascend to reach Ghorepani. This place offers you some amazing panoramic views of surrounding mountains, nature, and stunning landscapes. Overnight at Lodge.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 3, "meal": "", "title": "Early Hike up to Poon Hill and Trek to the Tadapani via Shikha.", "richText": "An early hike up to Poon Hill (3210m) leads you to a spectacular vantage point that offers an unobstructed view of sunrise over the high Himalayas. The place also hosts a panoramic view of the Himalayas including Mt. Dhaulagiri (8167m), Mt. Annapurna’s massif, and many others.  You will find various kinds of butterflies and a blend of the cultures and traditions of various ethnic groups. Then downhill through the forest with an excellent mountain view to reach Tadapani. Overnight at lodge.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 4, "meal": "", "title": "Drive to Pokhara to Beni and drive back to Pokhara.", "richText": "Our drive starts early to Pokhara and directly to Beni. Beni offers some stunning beauty of nature and holy hot spring water. After having a warm bath, you can redirect your journey back to Pokhara. Overnight at Lodge.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/mountain-view-from-pokhara-scaled.jpg", "title": "mountain-view-from-pokhara", "altText": "mountain view from sarangkot, pokhara", "caption": "mountain view from sarangkot, pokhara", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["525", "526", "527", "528", "529"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "ws_trip_faqs_lists": 5, "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists": "field_63ede38e351c7", "ws_block_attractions": "", "ws_block_best_season": "Any Season", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-light", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": "Overview ", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc6695edb31", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_block_transportation": "Private AC Vehicle", "ws_trip_galleries_title": "Photo/Visual Gallery", "_ws_block_transportation": "field_63eeee74072de", "_ws_trip_galleries_title": "field_63ec89128acaa", "starter_kit_padding_type": "p-medium", "ws_trip_block_highlights": "<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nThe main aim of this trek is to visit one of the most beautiful Gurung villages Ghandruk. It is located on an elevation of (1090m) and you can witness the Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Gangapurna, and Fish Tail.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "ws_trip_information_list": 2, "_starter_kit_padding_type": "field_5f8584c998bc2", "_ws_trip_block_highlights": "field_63ec73a6a0d8f", "_ws_trip_information_list": "field_63ec90a574f02", "starter_kit_section_title": "Day by Day Activities", "_starter_kit_section_title": "field_63ec948c94a16", "starter_kit_enable_section": "1", "ws_trip_faqs_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "_starter_kit_enable_section": "field_63edeb1c7635c", "_ws_trip_faqs_section_title": "field_63ede33e5b304", "starter_kit_section_padding": "", "ws_trip_include_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Fully private trip </strong>(even 1 traveler) with private guide and vehicle.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transportation in comfortable private vehicle(s).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Vehicle fuel, vehicle tax.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>English speaking cultural city tour guide.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drinking Water.</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_starter_kit_section_padding": "field_5f3e0f86a2634", "_ws_trip_include_description": "field_63edd6a337cd0", "ws_trip_overview_description": "<strong>Ghorepani PoonHill Hot Spring Treks</strong> is a comparatively easy walk that begins at Nayapul. It takes about a one-hour drive from Pokhara. Pokhara is also a doorstep for most of the treks in the Annapurna region.\\r\\n\\r\\nThis <strong>Ghorepani Poonhill hot spring trek</strong> passes through beautiful Gurung village which offers outstanding landscapes and a variety of flora and fauna. Get an overview of the grand south Annapurna from Ulleri village. Passing through Ghorepani village you bump into beautiful orchids, massive Himalayan bamboo, and dense Rhododendron forest.\\r\\n\\r\\nOn the other hand, a well-designed rice field over the entire slope gives you a breathtaking experience. A downhill walk to Jhinu Danda through Tadapani. Ghorepani PoonHill trek with hot springs concludes and gives you the time for Kathmandu Valley Culture and paradise city <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pokhara\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Pokhara</a> and Annapurna Himalayan region of Nepal.", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "It is one of the shortest treks in the Annapurna region", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_0_faq_title": "1. How can I Reach Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_1_faq_title": "2. How to get Visa for Kathmandu?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_2_faq_title": "3. How to find & book a good and reliable travel agents in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_3_faq_title": "4. How is the weather like in Nepal?", "ws_trip_faqs_lists_4_faq_title": "5. What to expect o