\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"09\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\" Final departure\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"Breakfast\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Flight to China mainland city or back to Kathmandu for your next destination or for your home.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":9,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"Cost Inclusion \\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003eWe are dedicated to providing quality service to our clients where safety is our topmost priority. We have not mentioned our costs as they depend on factors like trip customization, group sizes, travel season, trip duration, and types of accommodation, meals, transportation, and choice of various activities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cem\\\\u003e(\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNote:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e On your request, we can send you cost details. Feel free to contact us for further details.)\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTibet Travel Permit\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTibet visa if you want to apply from Kathmandu, Nepal\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate vehicle with air conditioning\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate English-speaking Tibetan guide (Other language guide also available upon your request with extra cost.)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast in Tibet and Nepal\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAll accommodation as per your choice (Luxury/5-star or 4-star hotel or 3-star hotel)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eMonuments entrance/admission fees\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGuide and driver’s meals and accommodation\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eService Charge (the planning, handling, operational and communication charges) \\\\u0026amp; government taxes.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHandle your flight or train tickets (Kathmandu/Beijing/Chengdu/Kunming to Lhasa(Tibet))\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"How to travel Tibet? and Visa Processing?\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eIf you plan to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003etravel to Tibet from Kathmandu, Nepal\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, keep in mind that you must obtain a Tibet Visa from the Chinese Embassy in Kathmandu, which usually requires at least three business days to process. As part of the application process, your original passport will be held by the Chinese Embassy, and you will need to visit the embassy for biometric verification. While your Tibet Visa application is being processed, you can take advantage of this time to explore the sights of Kathmandu. We will handle all the tasks related to the visa processing.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eIf you plan to \\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003etravel to Tibet from your country\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e, travelers need to obtain a China visa in their country and spend a night in mainland China (such as Beijing, Chengdu, Chongqing, or Kunming) to obtain the Tibet Travel Permit. This permit will be provided in hard copy at the hotel before your arrival. We would be happy to assist you in booking a hotel for one night in any city in China.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Outdoor Extra Activities\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"Not only historical, cultural, and natural tours embark on an adventurous journey through our outdoor extra activities. Some of our popular outdoor activities to carry out during this tour are as follows:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHiking:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Short scenic hikes take you closer to nature and offer picturesque views\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eRiver rafting: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eThrilling White Water River rafting in Nepal  on rapid rivers relishing scenic landscapes\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eParagliding: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eRelish amazing panoramic Himalayan views, scenic landscapes, and beautiful surroundings\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eZipline: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eExperience the longest and steepest zipline in Nepal and admire scenic surroundings\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBungee jump: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eAdrenaline rush experience through bungee jumping in Nepal amidst beautiful surrounding scenery\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eYoga and meditation: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003ePractice Yoga and Meditation in serene places such as a monastery, yoga centers, or in the vicinity of nature\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHelicopter tours: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eExciting helicopter tours to the iconic Everest Base Camp in Nepal and get close-up views of the Himalayas and admire\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNational Park Tour: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eWildlife Jungle Safari in a jeep or elephant to explore the region’s rich biodiversity, witness diverse flora and fauna, and get close to nature\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Best time to visit\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHigh season (Best Time)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMay to September\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e months are the high seasons in Tibet with an average temperature ranging between 6°C to 23°C. The weather is mild and warm during May, summer rains in June, occasional rains in August, and pleasant and cool weather in September.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eShoulder season (Good Time)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eApril, October, and November\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e months are shoulder seasons in Tibet with cool, dry, and pleasant weather. The average temperature ranges between -2°C to 17°C in April and October and -7°C to 12°C in November.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eLow or Off-season (Average Time)\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDecember to January\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e months are low or off-season in Tibet where the temperature ranges between -12°C to 14°C. The day's weather gets colder and at night, the weather gets very colder and experiences snowfalls. But the sky is cleareroffering awesome scenic beauty.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003e(Note:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e In the months of February and March, Tibet is closed to foreign tourists.)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Nepal-Tibet Tour: Is It Right for You?\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eA perfect combination tour of history, culture, and nature\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSuitable for all age groups of travelers (Senior citizens to Kids)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAccompanied by experienced local guides\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eComfortable flat trails while sightseeing Heritage Sites\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTechnical Climbing is not involved during the trip\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHike through forested trails which is medium.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransfer via clean private vehicles that are comfortable during sightseeing tours\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Why Travel With Us?\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e24/7 International Support\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFlexible Private and Customize Trips\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSafety: Our Topmost Priority\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSecure Online Payment\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBookings and Payments Flexibility\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLifetime Deposit Guaranteed\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGuaranteed Departures\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTravel with Locals to support locals\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eExperienced Team and Expert Guides\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRespect Nature through Responsible Tourism\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHappiness and Best Priced Assured\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/lhasa-visit.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/potala-palace-tibet-at.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Infront-of-Jokhang-temple.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/lhasa-travel-and-tour.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/potala-palace.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/potala-palace-tibet-1.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/jokhang-temple-with-barkhor-street.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/best-place-to-tibet-lhasa.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmandu-durbar-square.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bouddha-nath-kathmandu.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/2-days-kathmandu-tour-by-turkey-people.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/sunrise-tour-nagarkot.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/nagarkot-hill-hiking.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bhaktapur-tour.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/local-people-of-newari-village-in-Kathmandu.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=931", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "931", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-19 07:40:26", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-19 07:40:26", "post_modified": "2024-10-06 10:04:28", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-10-06 10:04:28"}}, "customSections": [{"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "How to travel Tibet? and Visa Processing?", "content": ["<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you plan to <strong>travel to Tibet from Kathmandu, Nepal</strong>, keep in mind that you must obtain a Tibet Visa from the Chinese Embassy in Kathmandu, which usually requires at least three business days to process. As part of the application process, your original passport will be held by the Chinese Embassy, and you will need to visit the embassy for biometric verification. While your Tibet Visa application is being processed, you can take advantage of this time to explore the sights of Kathmandu. We will handle all the tasks related to the visa processing.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you plan to <strong>travel to Tibet from your country</strong>, travelers need to obtain a China visa in their country and spend a night in mainland China (such as Beijing, Chengdu, Chongqing, or Kunming) to obtain the Tibet Travel Permit. This permit will be provided in hard copy at the hotel before your arrival. We would be happy to assist you in booking a hotel for one night in any city in China.</li>\\r\\n</ul>"], "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you plan to <strong>travel to Tibet from Kathmandu, Nepal</strong>, keep in mind that you must obtain a Tibet Visa from the Chinese Embassy in Kathmandu, which usually requires at least three business days to process. As part of the application process, your original passport will be held by the Chinese Embassy, and you will need to visit the embassy for biometric verification. While your Tibet Visa application is being processed, you can take advantage of this time to explore the sights of Kathmandu. We will handle all the tasks related to the visa processing.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you plan to <strong>travel to Tibet from your country</strong>, travelers need to obtain a China visa in their country and spend a night in mainland China (such as Beijing, Chengdu, Chongqing, or Kunming) to obtain the Tibet Travel Permit. This permit will be provided in hard copy at the hotel before your arrival. We would be happy to assist you in booking a hotel for one night in any city in China.</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, {"id": "overview-2", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Outdoor Extra Activities", "content": ["Not only historical, cultural, and natural tours embark on an adventurous journey through our outdoor extra activities. Some of our popular outdoor activities to carry out during this tour are as follows:\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Hiking:</strong> Short scenic hikes take you closer to nature and offer picturesque views\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>River rafting: </strong>Thrilling White Water River rafting in Nepal  on rapid rivers relishing scenic landscapes\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Paragliding: </strong>Relish amazing panoramic Himalayan views, scenic landscapes, and beautiful surroundings\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Zipline: </strong>Experience the longest and steepest zipline in Nepal and admire scenic surroundings\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Bungee jump: </strong>Adrenaline rush experience through bungee jumping in Nepal amidst beautiful surrounding scenery\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Yoga and meditation: </strong>Practice Yoga and Meditation in serene places such as a monastery, yoga centers, or in the vicinity of nature\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Helicopter tours: </strong>Exciting helicopter tours to the iconic Everest Base Camp in Nepal and get close-up views of the Himalayas and admire\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>National Park Tour: </strong>Wildlife Jungle Safari in a jeep or elephant to explore the region’s rich biodiversity, witness diverse flora and fauna, and get close to nature"], "description": "Not only historical, cultural, and natural tours embark on an adventurous journey through our outdoor extra activities. Some of our popular outdoor activities to carry out during this tour are as follows:\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Hiking:</strong> Short scenic hikes take you closer to nature and offer picturesque views\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>River rafting: </strong>Thrilling White Water River rafting in Nepal  on rapid rivers relishing scenic landscapes\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Paragliding: </strong>Relish amazing panoramic Himalayan views, scenic landscapes, and beautiful surroundings\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Zipline: </strong>Experience the longest and steepest zipline in Nepal and admire scenic surroundings\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Bungee jump: </strong>Adrenaline rush experience through bungee jumping in Nepal amidst beautiful surrounding scenery\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Yoga and meditation: </strong>Practice Yoga and Meditation in serene places such as a monastery, yoga centers, or in the vicinity of nature\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Helicopter tours: </strong>Exciting helicopter tours to the iconic Everest Base Camp in Nepal and get close-up views of the Himalayas and admire\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>National Park Tour: </strong>Wildlife Jungle Safari in a jeep or elephant to explore the region’s rich biodiversity, witness diverse flora and fauna, and get close to nature"}, {"id": "overview-3", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Best time to visit", "content": ["<strong>High season (Best Time)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>May to September</strong> months are the high seasons in Tibet with an average temperature ranging between 6°C to 23°C. The weather is mild and warm during May, summer rains in June, occasional rains in August, and pleasant and cool weather in September.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong> </strong><strong>Shoulder season (Good Time)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>April, October, and November</strong> months are shoulder seasons in Tibet with cool, dry, and pleasant weather. The average temperature ranges between -2°C to 17°C in April and October and -7°C to 12°C in November.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong> </strong><strong>Low or Off-season (Average Time)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>December to January</strong> months are low or off-season in Tibet where the temperature ranges between -12°C to 14°C. The day's weather gets colder and at night, the weather gets very colder and experiences snowfalls. But the sky is cleareroffering awesome scenic beauty.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>(Note:</strong> In the months of February and March, Tibet is closed to foreign tourists.)\\r\\n<h3></h3>"], "description": "<strong>High season (Best Time)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>May to September</strong> months are the high seasons in Tibet with an average temperature ranging between 6°C to 23°C. The weather is mild and warm during May, summer rains in June, occasional rains in August, and pleasant and cool weather in September.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong> </strong><strong>Shoulder season (Good Time)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>April, October, and November</strong> months are shoulder seasons in Tibet with cool, dry, and pleasant weather. The average temperature ranges between -2°C to 17°C in April and October and -7°C to 12°C in November.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong> </strong><strong>Low or Off-season (Average Time)</strong>\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>December to January</strong> months are low or off-season in Tibet where the temperature ranges between -12°C to 14°C. The day's weather gets colder and at night, the weather gets very colder and experiences snowfalls. But the sky is cleareroffering awesome scenic beauty.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>(Note:</strong> In the months of February and March, Tibet is closed to foreign tourists.)\\r\\n<h3></h3>"}, {"id": "overview-4", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Nepal-Tibet Tour: Is It Right for You?", "content": ["<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>A perfect combination tour of history, culture, and nature</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Suitable for all age groups of travelers (Senior citizens to Kids)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Accompanied by experienced local guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Comfortable flat trails while sightseeing Heritage Sites</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Technical Climbing is not involved during the trip</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike through forested trails which is medium.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transfer via clean private vehicles that are comfortable during sightseeing tours</li>\\r\\n</ul>"], "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>A perfect combination tour of history, culture, and nature</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Suitable for all age groups of travelers (Senior citizens to Kids)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Accompanied by experienced local guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Comfortable flat trails while sightseeing Heritage Sites</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Technical Climbing is not involved during the trip</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike through forested trails which is medium.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transfer via clean private vehicles that are comfortable during sightseeing tours</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, {"id": "overview-5", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Why Travel With Us?", "content": ["<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>24/7 International Support</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Private and Customize Trips</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Safety: Our Topmost Priority</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Secure Online Payment</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bookings and Payments Flexibility</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Lifetime Deposit Guaranteed</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Guaranteed Departures</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Travel with Locals to support locals</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Experienced Team and Expert Guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Respect Nature through Responsible Tourism</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Happiness and Best Priced Assured</li>\\r\\n</ul>"], "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>24/7 International Support</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Private and Customize Trips</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Safety: Our Topmost Priority</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Secure Online Payment</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bookings and Payments Flexibility</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Lifetime Deposit Guaranteed</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Guaranteed Departures</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Travel with Locals to support locals</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Experienced Team and Expert Guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Respect Nature through Responsible Tourism</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Happiness and Best Priced Assured</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "<blockquote>We are dedicated to providing quality service to our clients where safety is our topmost priority. We have not mentioned our costs as they depend on factors like trip customization, group sizes, travel season, trip duration, and types of accommodation, meals, transportation, and choice of various activities.\\r\\n<em>(<strong>Note:</strong> On your request, we can send you cost details. Feel free to contact us for further details.)</em></blockquote>", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Tibet Travel Permit", "Tibet visa if you want to apply from Kathmandu, Nepal", "Private vehicle with air conditioning", "Private English-speaking Tibetan guide (Other language guide also available upon your request with extra cost.)", "Breakfast in Tibet and Nepal", "All accommodation as per your choice (Luxury/5-star or 4-star hotel or 3-star hotel)", "Monuments entrance/admission fees", "Guide and driver’s meals and accommodation", "Service Charge (the planning, handling, operational and communication charges) & government taxes.", "Handle your flight or train tickets (Kathmandu/Beijing/Chengdu/Kunming to Lhasa(Tibet))"], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Tibet Travel Permit", "Tibet visa if you want to apply from Kathmandu, Nepal", "Private vehicle with air conditioning", "Private English-speaking Tibetan guide (Other language guide also available upon your request with extra cost.)", "Breakfast in Tibet and Nepal", "All accommodation as per your choice (Luxury/5-star or 4-star hotel or 3-star hotel)", "Monuments entrance/admission fees", "Guide and driver’s meals and accommodation", "Service Charge (the planning, handling, operational and communication charges) & government taxes.", "Handle your flight or train tickets (Kathmandu/Beijing/Chengdu/Kunming to Lhasa(Tibet))"], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Suggested Itinerary & Flexible", "sub_description": "3 nights in Kathmandu & Nagarkot, 5 nights in Lhasa, Gyantse, Shigatse(Tibet)", "trip_highlights": "<h3>3 nights in Kathmandu including Nagarkot + 5 nights at Lhasa, Yamdrok lake and Shigatse</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Process: </strong>Arrival in Kathmandu, Tibet visa processing, Nagarkot, Lhasa city tour, Lhasa to Shigatse via Yamdrok Lake and return to Lhasa, flight to Chengdu or Kathmandu for international flight or next destination.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Distance:</strong> 1.5 hours flight from Kathmandu to Lhasa and 1.5 hours drive from Lhasa Gonggar Airport to downtown/hotel, 7-8 hours drive from Lhasa to Shigatse.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<strong>Nepal Tibet Multi Countries tour</strong> is a flexible and customizable package designed by Everest Vacation for all travel lovers. A delightful experience in Kathmandu to sightsee architecturally impressive cultural UNESCO-listed sites and fabulous Himalayan view with sunrise in Nagarkot.\\r\\n\\r\\nA short flight to Lhasa (Tibet) teases you with the scenic Himalayas. Experience a different aura once you land at the Lhasa Airport. Explore popular UNESCO Heritage sites and immerse yourself in the spiritual ambiance of Lhasa &amp; Shigatse while visiting sacred Buddhist monasteries. The natural freshwater Yamdrok Lake add beauty to this multi-country tour.", "trip_type_level": "Private Tour", "meta_description": "Nepal Tibet Multi countries Tour Itinerary is designed for visitors to excursion the best destinations to create fond memories.", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "", "best_season": "", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": ""}, "trip_highlights_title": "Tour Highlights"}	2023-12-19 07:40:26+00	2024-10-06 11:04:28+01
211	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "8 nights in Kathmandu, Chitwan & Pokhara and 4 nights in Lhasa(Tibet)", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "13", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour"}, "meta": {"_edit_last": "1", "_edit_lock": "1768983487:1", "_dp_original": "810", "_thumbnail_id": "4319", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "8 nights in Kathmandu, Chitwan & Pokhara and 4 nights in Lhasa(Tibet)", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "13", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Nepal and Tibet Tour Itinerary", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "47", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Nepal and Tibet Tour Itinerary is a great package to explore Kathmandu & Lhasa where visitors spend 8 nights in Nepal and 4 nights in Tibet.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "nepal-tibet-tour-12-nights-13-days", "tags": [], "title": "Nepal and Tibet Tour Itinerary", "duration": "13 Days", "overview": {"title": "How to travel Tibet? and Visa Processing?", "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you plan to <strong>travel to Tibet from Kathmandu, Nepal</strong>, keep in mind that you must obtain a Tibet Visa from the Chinese Embassy in Kathmandu, which usually requires at least three business days to process. As part of the application process, your original passport will be held by the Chinese Embassy, and you will need to visit the embassy for biometric verification. While your Tibet Visa application is being processed, you can take advantage of this time to explore the sights of Kathmandu. We will handle all the tasks related to the visa processing.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you plan to <strong>travel to Tibet from your country</strong>, travelers need to obtain a China visa in their country and spend a night in mainland China (such as Beijing, Chengdu, Chongqing, or Kunming) to obtain the Tibet Travel Permit. This permit will be provided in hard copy at the hotel before your arrival. We would be happy to assist you in booking a hotel for one night in any city in China.</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Arrival in Kathmandu and transfer to your hotel.", "richText": "Airport transfer, collect your original passport and photographs and request to fill up Tibet group visa form.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "1400m", "accommodation": "3 star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 2, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Kathmandu Tour.", "richText": "Boudhanath Stupa, Pashupatinath Temple, Patan Durbar Square.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "1400m", "accommodation": "3 star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 3, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Kathmandu – Bhaktapur – Nagarkot.", "richText": "Swoyambhunath Temple (Monkey Temple), Bhaktapur Durbar Square and Nagarkot for sunset and sunrise view.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "1400m", "accommodation": "3 star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 4, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Nagarkot – Kathmandu – Pokhara.", "richText": "Sunrise tour, drive to Kathmandu and collect your Tibet group visa with your original passport and flight/drive to Pokhara and Phewa lake boating.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "2175m", "accommodation": "3 star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 5, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "