rs 30 minutes drive from Thimphu to Punakha\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"3star to Luxury hotels\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"Breakfast, Lunch \\\\u0026 Dinner\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-8\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-8\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrive to Punakha crossing over Dochu La Pass (3100 meters)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePlace to visit / Tour\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDochu La Pass (views of the highest mountain peaks \\\\u0026amp; walk around the 108 stupas)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHike through the paddy field and old village to visit Chhimi Lhakhang, the temple of fertility.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePunakha Dzong\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eKhamsum Yuley Lhakhang\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nDrive back to Thimphu\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"09\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Drive to Paro, Hike to Taktsang Monastery and Paro Tour\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"2950m\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"Approx, 1 hour 30 minutes drive from Thimphu to Paro.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"3star to Luxury hotels\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"Breakfast, Lunch \\\\u0026 Dinner\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrive to Paro (base for the hike)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePlace to visit / Tour\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHike to Taktsang Monastery (Tiger’s Nest) – 3 hours uphill\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eParo Dzong (Fortress)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eOld Paro Town\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eCould get some opportunity to see the traditional game, Archery.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eParo Airport Bird's Eye View Point, Paro\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\nOvernight at Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_di_days\\":\\"10\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Final Departure / Tour end\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"Breakfast\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eDrop you to Paro airport from your hotel\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eReturn with some magnificent memories and moments from Nepal and Bhutan trip.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFlight available from Paro to Kathmandu, Bangkok, New Delhi, Kolkata, Bagdogra, Singapore, Dhaka etc.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":10,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"Cost Inclusion \\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003eWe are dedicated to providing quality service to our clients where safety is our topmost priority. We have not mentioned our costs as they depend on factors like trip customization, group sizes, travel season, trip duration, and types of accommodation, meals, transportation, and choice of various activities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cem\\\\u003e(\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNote:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e On your request, we can send you cost details. Feel free to contact us for further details.)\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBhutan Travel Permit and Visa\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBhutan Government sustainable development fee (SDF) USD 100 per person per night.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate vehicle with air conditioning\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate cultural English-speaking tour guide (Other language guide also available upon your request with extra cost.)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAll meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) in Bhutan\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast in Nepal\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAll accommodation as per your choice (Luxury/5-star or 4-star hotel or 3-star hotel)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eMonuments entrance/admission fees\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGuide and driver’s meals and accommodation\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eService Charge (the planning, handling, operational and communication charges) \\\\u0026amp; government taxes.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHandle your flight ticket (Kathmandu/Bangkok/New Delhi/Kolkata/Singapore/Dhaka/Singapore to Paro(Bhutan))\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Outdoor Extra Activities\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"Not only historical, cultural, and natural tours embark on an adventurous journey through our outdoor extra activities. Some of our popular outdoor activities to carry out during this tour are as follows:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHiking:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Short scenic hikes take you closer to nature and offer picturesque views\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eRiver rafting: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eThrilling White Water River rafting in Nepal and Bhutan on rapid rivers relishing scenic landscapes\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eParagliding: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eRelish amazing panoramic Himalayan views, scenic landscapes, and beautiful surroundings\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eZipline: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eExperience the longest and steepest zipline in Nepal and admire scenic surroundings (Currently no zip line in Bhutan)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBungee jump: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eAdrenaline rush experience through bungee jumping in Nepal amidst beautiful surrounding scenery (Not permitted in Bhutan)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eYoga and meditation: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003ePractice Yoga and Meditation in serene places such as a monastery, yoga centers, or in the vicinity of nature\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHelicopter tours: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eExciting helicopter tours to the iconic Everest Base Camp \\\\u0026amp; Annapurna Base Camp in Nepal and get close-up views of the Himalayas and admire its beauty in Bhutan\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Best time to visit\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eHigh season (Best Time):\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMarch to May\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e with the blooming flowers covering the hillsides, warm temperatures, stable weather with low humidity and rainfall, clear skies with clear views, and lush greenery everywhere.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSeptember to November \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003ewith mild temperatures, stable weather, clear skies, and phenomenal views.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eShoulder season (Good Time):\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDecember to February \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003ewith sunny day weather and slightly cold nights \\\\u0026amp; mornings, mild day temperatures, clear surrounding views, and fewer crowds which is perfect for visitors seeking a peaceful visit.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eLow or Off-season (Average Time):\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eJune to August \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003ewith unstable weather and temperature, high humidity, light to heavy rainfall, mostly obstructed views, but lush greenery everywhere. High chances of flight cancelations and roadblocks due to floods \\\\u0026amp; landslides in some places.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Nepal-Bhutan Tour: Is It Right for You?\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eA perfect combination tour of history, culture, and nature\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSuitable for all age groups of travelers (Senior citizens to Kids)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAccompanied by experienced local guides\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eComfortable flat trails while sightseeing Heritage Sites\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTechnical Climbing is not involved during the trip\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHike through forested trails which is medium.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAn experienced guide accompanies you to ensure a comfortable Taktsang Monastery Hike. Pony rides to the halfway are also available.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransfer via clean private vehicles that are comfortable during sightseeing tours\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Why Travel With Us?\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e24/7 International Support\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFlexible Private and Customize Trips\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSafety: Our Topmost Priority\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSecure Online Payment\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBookings and Payments Flexibility\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLifetime Deposit Guaranteed\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGuaranteed Departures\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTravel with Locals to support locals\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eExperienced Team and Expert Guides\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRespect Nature through Responsible Tourism\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHappiness and Best Priced Assured\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/At-Chitwan-Taj-Meghauli-Sedai-e1706022855394.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/bhaktapur-city-of-arts-e1706022904337.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/local-people-bungmati.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/swoyambhu-monkey-temple.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-bell.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/phewa-lake-pokhara-1.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/saangkot-pokhara.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/bhaktapur-durbar-square.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/jungle-safari-chitwan.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/chitwan-elephant-ridge-rotated.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/tharu-dance-chitwan.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Thimphu-Tour-bhutan.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/thimphu-buddha-statue.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/punakha-tour.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/tiger-nest-in-bhutan.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=940", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "940", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2023-12-27 06:46:10", "post_date_gmt": "2023-12-27 06:46:10", "post_modified": "2024-08-18 08:36:53", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-08-18 08:36:53"}}, "customSections": [{"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Nepal Bhutan Tour 10 days (6 nights in Nepal and 3 nights in Bhutan)</strong></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Travel Route (Bhutan and then Nepal also possible), Flexible monuments to visit, Flexible number of nights in both countries.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We take care of your Visa of Bhutan and internal flights. A Nepal visa is easily available upon your arrival at Kathmandu (TIA) airport.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n&nbsp;\\r\\n\\r\\nThe <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-bhutan-tour-7-nights-8-days/\\">Nepal Bhutan Tour</a>  9 nights 10 days by Everest Vacation is the perfect package for all travelers wishing to explore these majestic countries. Visitors have the flexibility to customize the itinerary to their preferences. Explore the UNESCO-listed sites in Nepal including the architecturally aesthetic Durbar Squares in Kathmandu and Bhaktapur. Delve deeply into nature while visiting Chitwan and <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pokhara\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Pokhara</a>. The Jungle Safari in Chitwan and mountain views while boating in Pokhara are appealing.\\r\\n\\r\\nExplore the 3 beautiful cities of Paro, Thimphu, and Punakha during the Bhutan tour. Visit fabulous landmarks such as Tashichho Dzong, Memorial Chorten, Great Buddha Dordenma, etc. in Thimphu. The mountain range views from Dochu La Pass are breathtaking. Punakha excursion includes visiting the Chhimi Lhakhang Temple, the second-oldest Punakha Dzong. Visiting amazing places like Paro Dzong, old Paro Town, Kyichu Lhakhang, and the iconic Tiger’s Nest Monastery in Paro is delightful."], "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Nepal Bhutan Tour 10 days (6 nights in Nepal and 3 nights in Bhutan)</strong></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Travel Route (Bhutan and then Nepal also possible), Flexible monuments to visit, Flexible number of nights in both countries.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We take care of your Visa of Bhutan and internal flights. A Nepal visa is easily available upon your arrival at Kathmandu (TIA) airport.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n&nbsp;\\r\\n\\r\\nThe <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-bhutan-tour-7-nights-8-days/\\">Nepal Bhutan Tour</a>  9 nights 10 days by Everest Vacation is the perfect package for all travelers wishing to explore these majestic countries. Visitors have the flexibility to customize the itinerary to their preferences. Explore the UNESCO-listed sites in Nepal including the architecturally aesthetic Durbar Squares in Kathmandu and Bhaktapur. Delve deeply into nature while visiting Chitwan and <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pokhara\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Pokhara</a>. The Jungle Safari in Chitwan and mountain views while boating in Pokhara are appealing.\\r\\n\\r\\nExplore the 3 beautiful cities of Paro, Thimphu, and Punakha during the Bhutan tour. Visit fabulous landmarks such as Tashichho Dzong, Memorial Chorten, Great Buddha Dordenma, etc. in Thimphu. The mountain range views from Dochu La Pass are breathtaking. Punakha excursion includes visiting the Chhimi Lhakhang Temple, the second-oldest Punakha Dzong. Visiting amazing places like Paro Dzong, old Paro Town, Kyichu Lhakhang, and the iconic Tiger’s Nest Monastery in Paro is delightful."}, {"id": "overview-2", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Outdoor Extra Activities", "content": ["Not only historical, cultural, and natural tours embark on an adventurous journey through our outdoor extra activities. Some of our popular outdoor activities to carry out during this tour are as follows:\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Hiking:</strong> Short scenic hikes take you closer to nature and offer picturesque views\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>River rafting: </strong>Thrilling White Water River rafting in Nepal and Bhutan on rapid rivers relishing scenic landscapes\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Paragliding: </strong>Relish amazing panoramic Himalayan views, scenic landscapes, and beautiful surroundings\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Zipline: </strong>Experience the longest and steepest zipline in Nepal and admire scenic surroundings (Currently no zip line in Bhutan)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Bungee jump: </strong>Adrenaline rush experience through bungee jumping in Nepal amidst beautiful surrounding scenery (Not permitted in Bhutan)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Yoga and meditation: </strong>Practice Yoga and Meditation in serene places such as a monastery, yoga centers, or in the vicinity of nature\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Helicopter tours: </strong>Exciting helicopter tours to the iconic Everest Base Camp &amp; Annapurna Base Camp in Nepal and get close-up views of the Himalayas and admire its beauty in Bhutan"], "description": "Not only historical, cultural, and natural tours embark on an adventurous journey through our outdoor extra activities. Some of our popular outdoor activities to carry out during this tour are as follows:\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Hiking:</strong> Short scenic hikes take you closer to nature and offer picturesque views\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>River rafting: </strong>Thrilling White Water River rafting in Nepal and Bhutan on rapid rivers relishing scenic landscapes\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Paragliding: </strong>Relish amazing panoramic Himalayan views, scenic landscapes, and beautiful surroundings\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Zipline: </strong>Experience the longest and steepest zipline in Nepal and admire scenic surroundings (Currently no zip line in Bhutan)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Bungee jump: </strong>Adrenaline rush experience through bungee jumping in Nepal amidst beautiful surrounding scenery (Not permitted in Bhutan)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Yoga and meditation: </strong>Practice Yoga and Meditation in serene places such as a monastery, yoga centers, or in the vicinity of nature\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Helicopter tours: </strong>Exciting helicopter tours to the iconic Everest Base Camp &amp; Annapurna Base Camp in Nepal and get close-up views of the Himalayas and admire its beauty in Bhutan"}, {"id": "overview-3", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Best time to visit", "content": ["<h3>High season (Best Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>March to May</strong> with the blooming flowers covering the hillsides, warm temperatures, stable weather with low humidity and rainfall, clear skies with clear views, and lush greenery everywhere.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>September to November </strong>with mild temperatures, stable weather, clear skies, and phenomenal views.\\r\\n<h3>Shoulder season (Good Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>December to February </strong>with sunny day weather and slightly cold nights &amp; mornings, mild day temperatures, clear surrounding views, and fewer crowds which is perfect for visitors seeking a peaceful visit.\\r\\n<h3>Low or Off-season (Average Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>June to August </strong>with unstable weather and temperature, high humidity, light to heavy rainfall, mostly obstructed views, but lush greenery everywhere. High chances of flight cancelations and roadblocks due to floods &amp; landslides in some places."], "description": "<h3>High season (Best Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>March to May</strong> with the blooming flowers covering the hillsides, warm temperatures, stable weather with low humidity and rainfall, clear skies with clear views, and lush greenery everywhere.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>September to November </strong>with mild temperatures, stable weather, clear skies, and phenomenal views.\\r\\n<h3>Shoulder season (Good Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>December to February </strong>with sunny day weather and slightly cold nights &amp; mornings, mild day temperatures, clear surrounding views, and fewer crowds which is perfect for visitors seeking a peaceful visit.\\r\\n<h3>Low or Off-season (Average Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>June to August </strong>with unstable weather and temperature, high humidity, light to heavy rainfall, mostly obstructed views, but lush greenery everywhere. High chances of flight cancelations and roadblocks due to floods &amp; landslides in some places."}, {"id": "overview-4", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Nepal-Bhutan Tour: Is It Right for You?", "content": ["<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>A perfect combination tour of history, culture, and nature</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Suitable for all age groups of travelers (Senior citizens to Kids)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Accompanied by experienced local guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Comfortable flat trails while sightseeing Heritage Sites</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Technical Climbing is not involved during the trip</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike through forested trails which is medium.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>An experienced guide accompanies you to ensure a comfortable Taktsang Monastery Hike. Pony rides to the halfway are also available.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transfer via clean private vehicles that are comfortable during sightseeing tours</li>\\r\\n</ul>"], "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>A perfect combination tour of history, culture, and nature</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Suitable for all age groups of travelers (Senior citizens to Kids)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Accompanied by experienced local guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Comfortable flat trails while sightseeing Heritage Sites</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Technical Climbing is not involved during the trip</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike through forested trails which is medium.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>An experienced guide accompanies you to ensure a comfortable Taktsang Monastery Hike. Pony rides to the halfway are also available.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transfer via clean private vehicles that are comfortable during sightseeing tours</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, {"id": "overview-5", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Why Travel With Us?", "content": ["<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>24/7 International Support</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Private and Customize Trips</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Safety: Our Topmost Priority</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Secure Online Payment</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bookings and Payments Flexibility</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Lifetime Deposit Guaranteed</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Guaranteed Departures</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Travel with Locals to support locals</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Experienced Team and Expert Guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Respect Nature through Responsible Tourism</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Happiness and Best Priced Assured</li>\\r\\n</ul>"], "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>24/7 International Support</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Private and Customize Trips</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Safety: Our Topmost Priority</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Secure Online Payment</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bookings and Payments Flexibility</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Lifetime Deposit Guaranteed</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Guaranteed Departures</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Travel with Locals to support locals</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Experienced Team and Expert Guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Respect Nature through Responsible Tourism</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Happiness and Best Priced Assured</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "<blockquote>We are dedicated to providing quality service to our clients where safety is our topmost priority. We have not mentioned our costs as they depend on factors like trip customization, group sizes, travel season, trip duration, and types of accommodation, meals, transportation, and choice of various activities.\\r\\n<em>(<strong>Note:</strong> On your request, we can send you cost details. Feel free to contact us for further details.)</em></blockquote>", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Bhutan Travel Permit and Visa", "Bhutan Government sustainable development fee (SDF) USD 100 per person per night.", "Private vehicle with air conditioning", "Private cultural English-speaking tour guide (Other language guide also available upon your request with extra cost.)", "All meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) in Bhutan", "Breakfast in Nepal", "All accommodation as per your choice (Luxury/5-star or 4-star hotel or 3-star hotel)", "Monuments entrance/admission fees", "Guide and driver’s meals and accommodation", "Service Charge (the planning, handling, operational and communication charges) & government taxes.", "Handle your flight ticket (Kathmandu/Bangkok/New Delhi/Kolkata/Singapore/Dhaka/Singapore to Paro(Bhutan))"], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Bhutan Travel Permit and Visa", "Bhutan Government sustainable development fee (SDF) USD 100 per person per night.", "Private vehicle with air conditioning", "Private cultural English-speaking tour guide (Other language guide also available upon your request with extra cost.)", "All meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) in Bhutan", "Breakfast in Nepal", "All accommodation as per your choice (Luxury/5-star or 4-star hotel or 3-star hotel)", "Monuments entrance/admission fees", "Guide and driver’s meals and accommodation", "Service Charge (the planning, handling, operational and communication charges) & government taxes.", "Handle your flight ticket (Kathmandu/Bangkok/New Delhi/Kolkata/Singapore/Dhaka/Singapore to Paro(Bhutan))"], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day to Day Journey", "sub_description": "6 nights in Kathmandu, Pokhara & Chitwan and 3 nights in Bhutan", "trip_highlights": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kathmandu sightseeing including UNESCO World Heritage Sites (Durbar Squares, Boudhanath, Swayambhunath, Pashupatinath)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Chitwan Sightseeing (Jungle Safari, Tharu Village Tour, Canoeing, Sunset View)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Phenomenal Sunrise View from Sarangkot</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pokhara Sightseeing (Lakeside View, Davis Fall, Phewa Lake Boating, etc.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit stunning landmarks such as Tashichho Dzong, Memorial Chorten, Great Buddha Dordenma, etc. in Thimphu</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Cherish the fabulous views of mountain ranges from Dochu La Pass</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Punakha Sightseeing (Chhimi Lhakhang Temple, Punakha Dzong, Kham Sum Yuley Lhakhang)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit Paro Dzong (Fortress), Old Paro Town, and enjoy the traditional Archery game in Paro</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike to the popular Tiger’s Nest Monastery</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "trip_type_level": "Private Tour", "meta_description": "Explore attractive destinations like Pokhara, Phobjikha, Kathmandu, Thimphu, and Paro during the Nepal Bhutan Tour 10 days.", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "", "best_season": "", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": ""}, "trip_highlights_title": "Including Kathmandu, Bhaktapur, Chitwan & Pokhara | Thimphu, Punakha & Paro with Taktsang Monastery Hike."}	2023-12-27 06:46:10+00	2024-08-18 09:36:53+01
