list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Sightseeing in Thimphu\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Exciting sightseeing in Thimphu commences after breakfast. A visit to the National Memorial Chorten followed by a trip to Bhutan’s Changangkha Lakhang. The protective divinity of the temple is believed to give protection and blessings to a newly born child. Step into Simtokha Dzong and admire the cultural phenomena: the statue of Shakyamuni Buddha, the images of eight Bodhisattvas, and 300 slate carvings depicting Buddhist masters and saints inside the chapel. Stop at colorful craft shops for souvenirs.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTour to the “Fortress of the Glorious Religion-Tashichho Dzong” which is a notable work of genius of Bhutanese architecture. Explore the huge Great Buddha Dordenma statue and relish the awesome panoramic view of Thimphu valley in Kuensel Phodrang. Return to the hotel and stay overnight.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Thimphu to Punakha (Stop at Dochula Pass and Sightseeing in Punakha)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"A pleasant ride to Punakha from Thimphu admiring the beautiful sceneries. On the way, stop at Dochula Pass and visit the Druk Wangyal Lhakhang. Also, appreciate the 108 memorial Chortens in memory of the soldiers. The picturesque view of the Himalayas and terrace fields from Dochula Pass to reach Punakha. Upon reaching Chimi Lhakhang, a short walk through attractive villages and meadows to reach the sacred “The Fertility Temple of Bhutan” dedicated to the “Divine Madman”. A renowned temple worldwide to seek blessings by childless couples. Rest, relax and have your lunch.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter lunch, visit the second oldest and the second largest beautiful Punakha dzong in Bhutan. Punakha dzong means “The palace of bliss” which was built without using nails. The historical and culturally significant dzong can be reached by crossing Bazam Bridge over Chu Rivers. The main temple, a Bodhi tree, and a big white stupa inside the dzong are the main highlights. Participate in the Punakha festival glorifying Bhutanese culture, tradition, arts, and architecture if you are here around mid-Feb. Spend a night at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Punakha to Gangtey (Phobjikha)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Wangdue Phodrang is admired for its stone carvings and bamboo works. A short drive on this road and passing through the blossoming rhododendron and oak forest. Enjoy the lovely dwarf green bamboos on the way. Drive downhill to reach beautiful Phobjika valley which is the winter home to sacred black-necked cranes.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nVisit the Gangtey Goempa monastery which best depicts the Bhutanese traditional architecture. The artistic facades, well-decorated balconies, and multi-layered roofs are perfect examples for art and photo lovers. One can meditate at a meditation hall or interact with monks and locals concerning why this valley is considered the happiest place in Bhutan. Later, tour nearby places in the valley. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"05\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Gangtey/Phobjikha to Bumthang\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Drive to Trongsa which means “new village” admiring the beautiful sceneries and enjoying the ride on the zigzag route. Trongsa is the lineage home of the Royal family of Bhutan. Visit Trongsa Dzong decorated with vibrant Mandalas and Buddhist statues. A perfect masterpiece and specimen of Bhutanese architecture. After a 2.5-hour drive, reach Bumthang meaning “beautiful field” or “the valley of beautiful girls”. Bumthang is comprised of four beautiful naturally beautiful valleys: Ura, Chumey, Tang, and Choekhor. Buddhism was first introduced to this valley in Bhutan. Thus, this place has great historic, religious and cultural importance. Rest and relax at a hotel after a long drive. Explore the surroundings in the evening. Spend a night there.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"06\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Sightseeing in Bumthang\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"A whole day sightseeing in this mystical hub Bumthang. The interesting places in Bumthang are Jakar Dzong, Jambay Lhakhang, Kurjey Lhakhang, and Tamshing Lhakhang in mesmerizing Choekhor valley. Jakar Dzong is simple in design but a beautiful protective dzong that was built for Bhutan’s safeguard. It is also called the “Castle of the white bird”. Jambay Lhakhang has many old and sacred temples. Many festivals are organized here. Kurjey Lhakhang is named after the guru’s body print (Kurjey) and has three temples. Tamshing Lhakhang includes antique religious 1000 Buddhas and 21 Taras paintings. Explore these artistic beautiful and spiritual places inside Choekhor valley. From there, visit a holy site Mebar Tsho to witness the “Burning Lake in Tang Valley. You can also travel to Ura, and Chumey if time permits. Explore the local markets of Bumthang and purchase some souvenirs after completing the sightseeing. Rest, relax and spend a quality night at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days\\":\\"07\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Fly from Bumthang to Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Take a domestic flight from Bumthang to beautiful Paro valley. The natural beauty of Paro is mesmerizing and admire the traditionally designed houses. Upon arrival, visit the oldest temple in Bhutan-“Kyichu Lhakhang Temple”. This temple is religiously significant as it was built to control female giants’ power creating obstacles to spreading Buddhism across Tibet. The holy sculpture of Jowo Rinpoche is another highlight here. After this, visit the Archery ground to see Bhutan’s traditional and national sport Archery. Enjoy the locals skillfully playing archery matches. One can wish to play archery for fun and gain experience too. Stay overnight in a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAlternatively, one can wish to take a 6/7 hour drive from Bumthang to Thimphu. Rest, relax and spend a night at Thimphu. Early morning travel to Paro to hike to the famous Tiger’s Nest Monastery.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days\\":\\"08\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Hike to Taktsang (Tiger’s Nest Monastery)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Hike to Taktsang Monastery is a non-missed destination in all itineraries of Bhutan. This shows the importance and popularity of this place. It is renowned as “Tiger’s Nest Monastery”. The Tiger’s Nest Monastery architecture is one of the finest and masterpiece works of Bhutan. It has a great history and also decodes Taktsang as a “Tigress lair” from its strong foundation. It is believed that Guru Rinpoche traveled back on a tigress and meditate in this cave to subdue evil spirits for over 3 years. This is a holy cave where one can witness artistic paintings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTo reach here, hike uphill admiring the beautiful scenery, and rest at a cafe halfway there. Anyone with good physical fitness and sound health can comfortably reach there. One can also ride on a pony to reach there. The monastery is considered to be pious, thus one needs to wear full sleeve clothes while visiting. One can meditate or interact with the monks. End your trip with spiritual blessings. Return to a hotel and spend a night there.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"09\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Final Departure from Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-9\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-9\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nBid farewell to this Land of Dragon nation with the good memories you make here. The Bhutanese guide see off you to the Paro International Airport for your final departure.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":9,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAccommodation in approved hotels\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUS$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVisa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUSD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fee\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (Restaurant)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking Bhutan licensed guide\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEntrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBottled drinking water throughout the journeys\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-tour-with-bumthang-valley/\\\\u0022\\\\u003eBhutan\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e is a mystic land abundant with beautiful natural beauty and artistically mesmerizing cultural heritages. The Bhutan tour 9 days in the western and central Bhutan’s tourist hub is simply superb and expect to have an unexpectedly exciting and memorable journey. The historic landmarks, rich cultural heritage, and impressive natural beauty make this tour remarkable. The warm hospitality of locals depicting their culture, tradition, and lifestyle is a beautiful attraction here.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThimphu, Punakha, Paro, Phobjikha, and \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumthang_District\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eBumthang\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e are major sightseeing destinations in this 9-day tour. The dzongs, the lovely valleys, the monasteries, the Fertility Temple, Gangtey Goempa, the Great Buddha Dordenma, and Tiger’s Nest Monastery are major attractions. Come and let’s join to discover in-depth this dreamlike spiritual Bhutan in this 9-day tour to rejuvenate and make unforgettable memories.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4439\\",\\"3861\\",\\"400\\",\\"4073\\",\\"4057\\",\\"4446\\",\\"4017\\",\\"4033\\",\\"3994\\",\\"4010\\",\\"4447\\",\\"4013\\",\\"3868\\",\\"4462\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Arrive in Paro and Drive to Thimphu\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-1\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-1\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nBhutanese guide welcomes you at Paro International Airport. Then, you are transported to the restaurant/cafe for lunch/coffee. Drive to the largest and capital city of Bhutan after lunch. Rest for a while after checking in to the hotel. Tour nearby places and enjoy the nightlife. Spend a night at a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Sightseeing in Thimphu\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Exciting sightseeing in Thimphu commences after breakfast. A visit to the National Memorial Chorten followed by a trip to Bhutan’s Changangkha Lakhang. The protective divinity of the temple is believed to give protection and blessings to a newly born child. Step into Simtokha Dzong and admire the cultural phenomena: the statue of Shakyamuni Buddha, the images of eight Bodhisattvas, and 300 slate carvings depicting Buddhist masters and saints inside the chapel. Stop at colorful craft shops for souvenirs.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTour to the “Fortress of the Glorious Religion-Tashichho Dzong” which is a notable work of genius of Bhutanese architecture. Explore the huge Great Buddha Dordenma statue and relish the awesome panoramic view of Thimphu valley in Kuensel Phodrang. Return to the hotel and stay overnight.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Thimphu to Punakha (Stop at Dochula Pass and Sightseeing in Punakha)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"A pleasant ride to Punakha from Thimphu admiring the beautiful sceneries. On the way, stop at Dochula Pass and visit the Druk Wangyal Lhakhang. Also, appreciate the 108 memorial Chortens in memory of the soldiers. The picturesque view of the Himalayas and terrace fields from Dochula Pass to reach Punakha. Upon reaching Chimi Lhakhang, a short walk through attractive villages and meadows to reach the sacred “The Fertility Temple of Bhutan” dedicated to the “Divine Madman”. A renowned temple worldwide to seek blessings by childless couples. Rest, relax and have your lunch.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter lunch, visit the second oldest and the second largest beautiful Punakha dzong in Bhutan. Punakha dzong means “The palace of bliss” which was built without using nails. The historical and culturally significant dzong can be reached by crossing Bazam Bridge over Chu Rivers. The main temple, a Bodhi tree, and a big white stupa inside the dzong are the main highlights. Participate in the Punakha festival glorifying Bhutanese culture, tradition, arts, and architecture if you are here around mid-Feb. Spend a night at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Punakha to Gangtey (Phobjikha)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Wangdue Phodrang is admired for its stone carvings and bamboo works. A short drive on this road and passing through the blossoming rhododendron and oak forest. Enjoy the lovely dwarf green bamboos on the way. Drive downhill to reach beautiful Phobjika valley which is the winter home to sacred black-necked cranes.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nVisit the Gangtey Goempa monastery which best depicts the Bhutanese traditional architecture. The artistic facades, well-decorated balconies, and multi-layered roofs are perfect examples for art and photo lovers. One can meditate at a meditation hall or interact with monks and locals concerning why this valley is considered the happiest place in Bhutan. Later, tour nearby places in the valley. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"05\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Gangtey/Phobjikha to Bumthang\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Drive to Trongsa which means “new village” admiring the beautiful sceneries and enjoying the ride on the zigzag route. Trongsa is the lineage home of the Royal family of Bhutan. Visit Trongsa Dzong decorated with vibrant Mandalas and Buddhist statues. A perfect masterpiece and specimen of Bhutanese architecture. After a 2.5-hour drive, reach Bumthang meaning “beautiful field” or “the valley of beautiful girls”. Bumthang is comprised of four beautiful naturally beautiful valleys: Ura, Chumey, Tang, and Choekhor. Buddhism was first introduced to this valley in Bhutan. Thus, this place has great historic, religious and cultural importance. Rest and relax at a hotel after a long drive. Explore the surroundings in the evening. Spend a night there.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"06\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Sightseeing in Bumthang\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"A whole day sightseeing in this mystical hub Bumthang. The interesting places in Bumthang are Jakar Dzong, Jambay Lhakhang, Kurjey Lhakhang, and Tamshing Lhakhang in mesmerizing Choekhor valley. Jakar Dzong is simple in design but a beautiful protective dzong that was built for Bhutan’s safeguard. It is also called the “Castle of the white bird”. Jambay Lhakhang has many old and sacred temples. Many festivals are organized here. Kurjey Lhakhang is named after the guru’s body print (Kurjey) and has three temples. Tamshing Lhakhang includes antique religious 1000 Buddhas and 21 Taras paintings. Explore these artistic beautiful and spiritual places inside Choekhor valley. From there, visit a holy site Mebar Tsho to witness the “Burning Lake in Tang Valley. You can also travel to Ura, and Chumey if time permits. Explore the local markets of Bumthang and purchase some souvenirs after completing the sightseeing. Rest, relax and spend a quality night at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days\\":\\"07\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Fly from Bumthang to Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Take a domestic flight from Bumthang to beautiful Paro valley. The natural beauty of Paro is mesmerizing and admire the traditionally designed houses. Upon arrival, visit the oldest temple in Bhutan-“Kyichu Lhakhang Temple”. This temple is religiously significant as it was built to control female giants’ power creating obstacles to spreading Buddhism across Tibet. The holy sculpture of Jowo Rinpoche is another highlight here. After this, visit the Archery ground to see Bhutan’s traditional and national sport Archery. Enjoy the locals skillfully playing archery matches. One can wish to play archery for fun and gain experience too. Stay overnight in a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAlternatively, one can wish to take a 6/7 hour drive from Bumthang to Thimphu. Rest, relax and spend a night at Thimphu. Early morning travel to Paro to hike to the famous Tiger’s Nest Monastery.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days\\":\\"08\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Hike to Taktsang (Tiger’s Nest Monastery)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Hike to Taktsang Monastery is a non-missed destination in all itineraries of Bhutan. This shows the importance and popularity of this place. It is renowned as “Tiger’s Nest Monastery”. The Tiger’s Nest Monastery architecture is one of the finest and masterpiece works of Bhutan. It has a great history and also decodes Taktsang as a “Tigress lair” from its strong foundation. It is believed that Guru Rinpoche traveled back on a tigress and meditate in this cave to subdue evil spirits for over 3 years. This is a holy cave where one can witness artistic paintings.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nTo reach here, hike uphill admiring the beautiful scenery, and rest at a cafe halfway there. Anyone with good physical fitness and sound health can comfortably reach there. One can also ride on a pony to reach there. The monastery is considered to be pious, thus one needs to wear full sleeve clothes while visiting. One can meditate or interact with the monks. End your trip with spiritual blessings. Return to a hotel and spend a night there.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"09\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Final Departure from Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-9\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-9\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nBid farewell to this Land of Dragon nation with the good memories you make here. The Bhutanese guide see off you to the Paro International Airport for your final departure.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":9,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAccommodation in approved hotels\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUS$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVisa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUSD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fee\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (Restaurant)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking Bhutan licensed guide\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEntrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBottled drinking water throughout the journeys\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Thimphu-Tour-bhutan.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bhutan-tour.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/Bhutan-experience.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Authentic-Bhutanese-Crafts.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Villages-of-Punakha-Bhutan.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/tiger-s-nest-well-worth.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Rinpung-Dzong-Paro.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Tachogang-Lhakhang-Bridge-Paro.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Paro-Airport-Landing.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Punakha-Dzong.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/travel-to-punakha.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Punakha-Dzong-with-bridge.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Bridge-of-Punakha-Dzong.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bhutan-airport.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=3508", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "3508", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2024-01-03 08:29:28", "post_date_gmt": "2024-01-03 08:29:28", "post_modified": "2024-02-06 07:58:47", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-02-06 07:58:47"}}, "customSections": [{"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["<a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-tour-with-bumthang-valley/\\">Bhutan</a> is a mystic land abundant with beautiful natural beauty and artistically mesmerizing cultural heritages. The Bhutan tour 9 days in the western and central Bhutan’s tourist hub is simply superb and expect to have an unexpectedly exciting and memorable journey. The historic landmarks, rich cultural heritage, and impressive natural beauty make this tour remarkable. The warm hospitality of locals depicting their culture, tradition, and lifestyle is a beautiful attraction here.\\r\\n\\r\\nThimphu, Punakha, Paro, Phobjikha, and <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumthang_District\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Bumthang</a> are major sightseeing destinations in this 9-day tour. The dzongs, the lovely valleys, the monasteries, the Fertility Temple, Gangtey Goempa, the Great Buddha Dordenma, and Tiger’s Nest Monastery are major attractions. Come and let’s join to discover in-depth this dreamlike spiritual Bhutan in this 9-day tour to rejuvenate and make unforgettable memories."], "description": "<a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-tour-with-bumthang-valley/\\">Bhutan</a> is a mystic land abundant with beautiful natural beauty and artistically mesmerizing cultural heritages. The Bhutan tour 9 days in the western and central Bhutan’s tourist hub is simply superb and expect to have an unexpectedly exciting and memorable journey. The historic landmarks, rich cultural heritage, and impressive natural beauty make this tour remarkable. The warm hospitality of locals depicting their culture, tradition, and lifestyle is a beautiful attraction here.\\r\\n\\r\\nThimphu, Punakha, Paro, Phobjikha, and <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumthang_District\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Bumthang</a> are major sightseeing destinations in this 9-day tour. The dzongs, the lovely valleys, the monasteries, the Fertility Temple, Gangtey Goempa, the Great Buddha Dordenma, and Tiger’s Nest Monastery are major attractions. Come and let’s join to discover in-depth this dreamlike spiritual Bhutan in this 9-day tour to rejuvenate and make unforgettable memories."}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Accommodation in approved hotels", "US$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)", "Visa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary", "USD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fee", "Breakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (Restaurant)", "English speaking Bhutan licensed guide", "Transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary", "Entrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary", "Bottled drinking water throughout the journeys"], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Accommodation in approved hotels", "US$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)", "Visa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary", "USD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fee", "Breakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (Restaurant)", "English speaking Bhutan licensed guide", "Transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary", "Entrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary", "Bottled drinking water throughout the journeys"], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "Thimphu, Punakha, Pobhjikha, Bumthang Valley and Paro", "trip_type_level": "Private Tour", "meta_description": "Bhutan tour 9 days in the western and central Bhutan’s tourist hub is simply superb and expect to have an unexpectedly memorable journey.", "trip_attractions": "Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": "Private AC Vehicle"}, "trip_transportations": "Private AC Vehicle", "trip_highlights_title": "What's included?"}	2024-01-03 08:29:28+00	2024-02-06 07:58:47+00
223	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "Thimphu, Punakha, Pobhjikha, Bumthang Valley and Paro with Taktsang", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "11", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour"}, "meta": {"_edit_last": "1", "_edit_lock": "1707790344:1", "_dp_original": "3508", "_thumbnail_id": "4033", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "Thimphu, Punakha, Pobhjikha, Bumthang Valley and Paro with Taktsang", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "11", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Bhutan Tour with Bumthang Valley", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "47", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Bhutan Tour with Bumthang Valley treats with breathtaking scenery, beautiful landscapes, stunning mountain peaks, and rich cultural heritage.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "bhutan-tour-with-bumthang-valley", "tags": [], "title": "Bhutan Tour with Bumthang Valley ", "duration": "11 Days", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "<a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-tour-9-days/\\">Bhutan</a> is best known as the Kingdom of Happiness. Bhutan Tour with Bumthang Valley 11 days offers you breathtaking scenery, beautiful landscapes, natural resources, stunning mountain peaks, cultural heritage, and a rich belief in Buddhism. A perfect gateway to relaxation and a holiday destination and lose oneself in tranquility and spirituality from the hustle-bustle of daily life.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe most traveled destinations such as Thimphu, Wangdue, Punakha, <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumthang_District\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Bumthang</a>, and Paro are the complete package of artistically beautiful and iconic landmarks. Tourists are very satisfied and pleased after exploring these landmarks.\\r\\n\\r\\nBuddhism and Bhutanese culture are interrelated. Buddhism is a way of living life and their practices can be seen in their warm behavior. The nation is not only rich in its arts, tradition, and culture but also its free services of health and education to the natives. Come and let’s join to discover in-depth this dreamlike spiritual Bhutan in this 11-day tour to rejuvenate and make unforgettable memories."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Arrival at Paro Airport and Transfer to Thimphu", "richText": "<div id=\\"collapse-1\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-1\\">\\r\\n<div id=\\"collapse-1\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-1\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nA warm welcome by the Bhutanese guide upon reaching the Paro International Airport. A short stop at a restaurant/cafe for lunch/coffee. After that, enjoy a scenic drive to Thimphu. Rest for a while at a hotel. Then, the guide takes you to visit Jungshi Handmade Paper Factory. The Daphne tree and the Dekap tree’s barks are used to produce a traditional handmade paper called “Deh-so”. Experience the process of traditional handmade paper making. One can also purchase handmade items as a souvenir at the factory’s small shop. A side tour to the busiest Centenary Farmer’s Market. This domestic market is happening on the weekend. A great place to learn about the Bhutanese ingredients and interact with locals if one wishes to. One can also purchase organic items. Later on, visit the nearby Voluntary Artist Studio popular as VAST. The art galleries abundant with modern and contemporary artworks are a perfect place for art lovers. Travelers can purchase artwork and money goes to charity. Enjoy the nightlife and try delicious Bhutanese cuisine. Spend a night at a hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 2, "meal": "", "title": "Thimphu Sightseeing", "richText": "<div id=\\"collapse-2\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-2\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nHave breakfast and let’s get ready to explore this beautiful capital Thimphu. A visit to Kuensel Phodrang to view the largest statue of the Great Buddha in Bhutan. Enjoy the good view of the Thimphu valley from there. After that, a tour of the National Memorial Chorten was built in honor of the third Druk Gyalpo. The Tibetan-style architecture of golden spires and bells is impressive and holds great cultural significance. An interesting tour of the Bhutan Postal Museum. An amazing collection of varieties of stamps in different shapes and also learn about Bhutanese history. Customize stamps with your photos and take them as a souvenir. Then, a visit to the Buddhist monastery and fortress Tashichho Dzong-“Fortress of Auspicious Doctrine”. Popularly known as Thimphu Dzong, it is famous for its history, unique architecture, and calm atmosphere. At last, end the trip by visiting the National Folk Heritage Museum. The Bhutanese culture is greatly shown through documentaries or educational programs. The displaying of seasonal artifacts is the highlight of this museum. Rest, relax and spend a night at a hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 3, "meal": "", "title": "Thimphu to Punakha", "richText": "After breakfast, drive to Punakha. On the way, stop at Dochu-La-Pass and witness the snow-capped mountains of Bhutan. The beautiful landscape, and vegetation while descending the Pass. Visit the 108 memorial Druk Wangyal Chortens constructed in respect of Bhutanese soldiers killed in a war.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom there, head towards Punakha. Stop at the “Fertility Temple of Bhutan”-Chimi Lhakhang. Many childless couples seek blessings of the Divine Madman even from around the world. Upon reaching Punakha, rest for a while at a hotel. A time to visit the second oldest Punakha dzong in Bhutan. This palace of bliss is constructed without using any nails. Participate in the Punakha festival if you are here around mid-Feb. Complete the tour by visiting Khamsum Yulley Namgyal Chorten. The iconic landmark was constructed to bring peace to the world. Admire the lovely images of the deities of mandalas Vajrakilaya. In the evening, visit nearby local places or markets. Spend a night at a hotel.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 4, "meal": "", "title": "Punakha to Wangdue and Phobjikha valley stay", "richText": "After breakfast, drive to Wangdue. A tour to Wangdue Phodrang Dzong. A historic importance dzong consists of 14 temples and has three doorways and three courtyards. Witness the stunning interior inside the dzong and one can also see Mahakala carved on a stone slab. From there, a visit to the temple of Sha Radap. Locals referred to it as Rada Lhakhang. Locals worship as guardian deities and it is accustomed to bringing newborns to seek the blessings and for the naming ceremony. Usually, the name of a baby begins with Rada. Wangdue is a doorway to the Phobjika valley. Have lunch and a 2-hour drive to the Phobjika valley.\\r\\n\\r\\nPhobjika is a beautiful glacial valley in Bhutan. It is also called Gangtey because of the Gangtey Monastery. The valley is rich in a variety of flora and fauna. It is a winter home for endangered and sacred black-necked cranes which symbolizes longevity. A popular trekking route and the breathtaking scenery, vegetation, and landscapes make this valley more attractive. A visit to the Gangtey Monastery, beautiful for its traditional architecture. The vital monastery of the Nyingmapa school of Buddhism is situated on a forested hill. Admire the mesmerizing view of the Phobjika valley from the hilltop. Interact with locals if one wishes to and spend a night at a hotel.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 5, "meal": "", "title": "Travel to Bumthang", "richText": "An exciting 5-hour trip to Bumthang witnessing beautiful scenery on the way. Take a rest for a while upon reaching a hotel. Get ready to visit Jakar Dzong. It is well-known as the “Castle of the white bird”. It is also called Yuelay Namgyal Dzong. A victorious place that acted as a defensive house during the war in Bhutan. Visit the nearby markets after exploring the dzong. Try out some Bhutanese cuisine too. Spend a night at a hotel.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 6, "meal": "", "title": "Sightseeing in Bumthang", "richText": "Let’s explore the lovely district of Bumthang. Tour around Kurjey Lhakhang. Historically significant as the relics of the first three kings of Bhutan rests here. Thus, it is named after the body print (kurjey) of Guru Padmasambhava. A large tree behind the temple is believed to be related to Guru.\\r\\n\\r\\nFurther, visit the Tamshing Lhakhang also called as “Temple of Good Message”. A remarkable temple and monastery that has a direct link with the Bhutanese saints. Get fascinated with traditional religious paintings. A great center of Bhutanese holy masked dance.\\r\\n\\r\\nComplete the trip by exploring the Konchogsum Lhakhang also named Tsilung. It holds great historic importance and the good blending of ancient culture and modern art is the best part. Return to a hotel after an exciting trip. Stay overnight at a hotel.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 7, "meal": "", "title": "Sightseeing Bumthang", "richText": "Have breakfast and let’s continue to sightsee the remaining places. Visit the first place of Bhutan “Wangdichholing Palace” which wasn’t mainly a fortress.It was used as a monastic school but now renovation has helped it to convert into a museum. Also, see five colossal water-powered prayer wheels inside chortens.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom here, tour an ancient Jambay Lhakhang which was constructed to calm down the demons. The three steps symbolizing three ages are the main attraction inside the main Lhakhang. It indicates the past, present, and a new age of the historic Shakyamuni Buddha. Witness the future Buddha with his feet on an elephant, ancient murals portraying 1000 Buddhas, Kalachakra Temple, a pile of mani stones, and stone chortens. An ancient belief is that there is a lake under the Lhakhang which consists of hidden holy texts and artifacts concealed by Guru Rinpoche.\\r\\n\\r\\nA visit to the Buddhist monastery Ngang Lhakhang popularly known as Swan temple. Admire the beautiful religious architecture, Guru Rinpoche’s statue with his two consorts, and the protective three deities of long-life Amitayus, Tara, and Usnishavijaya. Stay overnight at a hotel.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 8, "meal": "", "title": "Travel to Paro", "richText": "Have your breakfast and get ready for a long 9-hour road trip to Paro. Admire the beautiful scenery en route to Paro and check into the hotel upon arrival. Enjoy dinner and take much-needed rest after such a long travel. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\nAlternatively, take a domestic flight from Bumthang to Paro. Upon arrival, rest at a hotel for a while. Leave the hotel to visit the oldest Jowo temple in Kyichu Lhakhang. This temple holds great importance in Bhutanese history as it was constructed to stop female giants who were troubling to spread Buddhism across Tibet. The original statue of Jowo Shakyamuni and a statue of Chenrezig can be seen too. From here, an hour drive to reach Chele La Pass. At the highest pass of Bhutan, one can get a glimpse of mesmerizing mountain ranges. Every photographer delight to capture splendid natural scenery including Bhutan’s most sacred peak Mt. Jumolhari, and the surrounding peak overlooking the lovely Paro and Haa valleys. Witness the rock paintings of Guru Rinpoche with his two consorts. Spend a night at a hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter the tour of the pass, return to your hotel for the night’s stay.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 9, "meal": "", "title": "Tiger’s Nest Monastery Hike", "richText": "<div id=\\"collapse-9\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-9\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nAn adventurous day to travel to Bhutan’s most iconic Tiger’s Nest Monastery. A lovely place where one can get a good glimpse of the Paro valley as it is situated on the Cliffside. This monastery is one finest specimens of Bhutanese architecture holding spiritual and cultural significance. Mediate in this peaceful cave for one’s mind and soul calmness. One can interact with monks to learn more about the folklore related to this cave. On returning, stop halfway at a cafe for lunch/coffee. Descend down to reach the next destination Drukgyel Dzong. This ancient ruin is Bhutan’s beautiful archaeological site. This dzong was built solely for protection purposes and the nation’s sovereignty is highly connected with it. The best example of masonry crafts on the walls can be seen. Also, witness the cylindrical tower building Chu-dzong. After an amazing tour, return to a hotel to enjoy dinner. Spend a night at a hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 10, "meal": "", "title": "Sightseeing in Paro", "richText": "Today is remaining sightseeing in Paro and the first destination is the National Museum of Bhutan. The paintings, art pieces, animal masks, and bronze statues are the finest collections displayed here. The galleries have an enormous collection and are the best place for history and art lovers.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom here, travel to visit Paro Dzong. The formal name is Rinpung Dzong meaning “Fortress on a Heap of Jewels”. Famous for its finest Bhutanese architecture one can see the gold, black and ochre-painted carved wood. The variation on the Bhutanese mandala and a “Thondrol” (a huge thangka) where religious pictures of Guru Rinpoche are painted or embroidered are major highlights.\\r\\n\\r\\nAccomplish the tour by touring Dzongdrakha Goemba. A unique place combined with four chapels is also stated as “Mini Taktsang”. Jongsarbu Lhakhang, Tshering Lhakhang, Guru Lhakhang, and Lhamey are four main chapels. Besides, one can witness a whole year of fruit-bearing magical orange trees in the courtyard. Other attractions are a huge white Chorten, a hidden chamber of Guru Lhakhang, and a permanent Shakyamuni Buddha statue. Return to hotel and arrange backpack for next day’s departure. Spend a night there.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 11, "meal": "", "title": "Departure from Paro", "richText": "An end to a remarkable 11-day tour making some sweet memories. Along with the Bhutanese guide, drive to the Paro International Airport. The guide bids farewell and you depart to the preferred destinations with the hope of visiting this heavenly nation again.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Tachogang-Lhakhang-Bridge-Paro.jpg", "title": "Tachogang-Lhakhang-Bridge-Paro", "altText": "Tachogang-Lhakhang-Bridge, Bhutan", "caption": "Tachogang-Lhakhang-Bridge, Bhutan", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["4462", "4464", "4434", "4414", "4325", "4239", "3894", "4447", "3868", "4015", "4035", "3949", "4033", "3950"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "ws_block_attractions": "Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle", "ws_block_best_season": "Any Season", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-white", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": "Overview", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc651ee1073", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_block_transportation": "Private AC Vehicle", "ws_trip_galleries_title": "Photo/Visual Gallery", "_ws_block_transportation": "field_63eeee74072de", "_ws_trip_galleries_title": "field_63ec89128acaa", "starter_kit_padding_type": "p-medium", "ws_trip_block_highlights": "", "ws_trip_information_list": 11, "_starter_kit_padding_type": "field_5f8584c998bc2", "_ws_trip_block_highlights": "field_63ec73a6a0d8f", "_ws_trip_information_list": "field_63ec94565c587", "starter_kit_section_title": "Day by Day Activities", "_starter_kit_section_title": "field_63ec948c94a16", "starter_kit_enable_section": "1", "_starter_kit_enable_section": "field_63edeb1c7635c", "starter_kit_section_padding": "", "ws_trip_include_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Accommodation in approved hotels</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>US$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>USD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fee</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Breakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (Restaurant)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>English speaking Bhutan licensed guide</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Entrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bottled drinking water throughout the journeys</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_starter_kit_section_padding": "field_5f3e0f86a2634", "_ws_trip_include_description": "field_63edd6a337cd0", "ws_trip_overview_description": "<a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-tour-9-days/\\">Bhutan</a> is best known as the Kingdom of Happiness. Bhutan Tour with Bumthang Valley 11 days offers you breathtaking scenery, beautiful landscapes, natural resources, stunning mountain peaks, cultural heritage, and a rich belief in Buddhism. A perfect gateway to relaxation and a holiday destination and lose oneself in tranquility and spirituality from the hustle-bustle of daily life.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe most traveled destinations such as Thimphu, Wangdue, Punakha, <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumthang_District\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Bumthang</a>, and Paro are the complete package of artistically beautiful and iconic landmarks. Tourists are very satisfied and pleased after exploring these landmarks.\\r\\n\\r\\nBuddhism and Bhutanese culture are interrelated. Buddhism is a way of living life and their practices can be seen in their warm behavior. The nation is not only rich in its arts, tradition, and culture but also its free services of health and education to the natives. Come and let’s join to discover in-depth this dreamlike spiritual Bhutan in this 11-day tour to rejuvenate and make unforgettable memories.", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "", "_ws_trip_fact_short_description": "field_63ec73a69d305", "ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "01", "ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "02", "ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "03", "ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "04", "ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "05", "ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days": "06", "ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days": "07", "ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days": "08", "ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days": "09", "ws_trip_information_list_9_di_days": "10", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_9_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_information_list_10_di_days": "11", "_ws_trip_information_list_10_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_food": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "Arrival at Paro Airport and Transfer to Thimphu", "ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "Thimphu Sightseeing", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "Thimphu to Punakha ", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "Punakha to Wangdue and Phobjikha valley stay", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title": "Travel to Bumthang", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title": "Sightseeing in Bumthang", "ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_title": "Sightseeing Bumthang", "ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_title": "Travel to Paro", "ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title": "Tiger’s Nest Monastery Hike", "ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_title": "Sightseeing in Paro", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_title": "Departure from Paro", "_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "<div id=\\"collapse-1\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-1\\">\\r\\n<div id=\\"collapse-1\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-1\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nA warm welcome by the Bhutanese guide upon reaching the Paro International Airport. A short stop at a restaurant/cafe for lunch/coffee. After that, enjoy a scenic drive to Thimphu. Rest for a while at a hotel. Then, the guide takes you to visit Jungshi Handmade Paper Factory. The Daphne tree and the Dekap tree’s barks are used to produce a traditional handmade paper called “Deh-so”. Experience the process of traditional handmade paper making. One can also purchase handmade items as a souvenir at the factory’s small shop. A side tour to the busiest Centenary Farmer’s Market. This domestic market is happening on the weekend. A great place to learn about the Bhutanese ingredients and interact with locals if one wishes to. One can also purchase organic items. Later on, visit the nearby Voluntary Artist Studio popular as VAST. The art galleries abundant with modern and contemporary artworks are a perfect place for art lovers. Travelers can purchase artwork and money goes to charity. Enjoy the nightlife and try delicious Bhutanese cuisine. Spend a night at a hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "<div id=\\"collapse-2\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-2\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nHave breakfast and let’s get ready to explore this beautiful capital Thimphu. A visit to Kuensel Phodrang to view the largest statue of the Great Buddha in Bhutan. Enjoy the good view of the Thimphu valley from there. After that, a tour of the National Memorial Chorten was built in honor of the third Druk Gyalpo. The Tibetan-style architecture of golden spires and bells is impressive and holds great cultural significance. An interesting tour of the Bhutan Postal Museum. An amazing collection of varieties of stamps in different shapes and also learn about Bhutanese history. Customize stamps with your photos and take them as a souvenir. Then, a visit to the Buddhist monastery and fortress Tashichho Dzong-“Fortress of Auspicious Doctrine”. Popularly known as Thimphu Dzong, it is famous for its history, unique architecture, and calm atmosphere. At last, end the trip by visiting the National Folk Heritage Museum. The Bhutanese culture is greatly shown through documentaries or educational programs. The displaying of seasonal artifacts is the highlight of this museum. Rest, relax and spend a night at a hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "After breakfast, drive to Punakha. On the way, stop at Dochu-La-Pass and witness the snow-capped mountains of Bhutan. The beautiful landscape, and vegetation while descending the Pass. Visit the 108 memorial Druk Wangyal Chortens constructed in respect of Bhutanese soldiers killed in a war.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom there, head towards Punakha. Stop at the “Fertility Temple of Bhutan”-Chimi Lhakhang. Many childless couples seek blessings of the Divine Madman even from around the world. Upon reaching Punakha, rest for a while at a hotel. A time to visit the second oldest Punakha dzong in Bhutan. This palace of bliss is constructed without using any nails. Participate in the Punakha festival if you are here around mid-Feb. Complete the tour by visiting Khamsum Yulley Namgyal Chorten. The iconic landmark was constructed to bring peace to the world. Admire the lovely images of the deities of mandalas Vajrakilaya. In the evening, visit nearby local places or markets. Spend a night at a hotel.", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "After breakfast, drive to Wangdue. A tour to Wangdue Phodrang Dzong. A historic importance dzong consists of 14 temples and has three doorways and three courtyards. Witness the stunning interior inside the dzong and one can also see Mahakala carved on a stone slab. From there, a visit to the temple of Sha Radap. Locals referred to it as Rada Lhakhang. Locals worship as guardian deities and it is accustomed to bringing newborns to seek the blessings and for the naming ceremony. Usually, the name of a baby begins with Rada. Wangdue is a doorway to the Phobjika valley. Have lunch and a 2-hour drive to the Phobjika valley.\\r\\n\\r\\nPhobjika is a beautiful glacial valley in Bhutan. It is also called Gangtey because of the Gangtey Monastery. The valley is rich in a variety of flora and fauna. It is a winter home for endangered and sacred black-necked cranes which symbolizes longevity. A popular trekking route and the breathtaking scenery, vegetation, and landscapes make this valley more attractive. A visit to the Gangtey Monastery, beautiful for its traditional architecture. The vital monastery of the Nyingmapa school of Buddhism is situated on a forested hill. Admire the mesmerizing view of the Phobjika valley from the hilltop. Interact with locals if one wishes to and spend a night at a hotel.", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description": "An exciting 5-hour trip to Bumthang witnessing beautiful scenery on the way. Take a rest for a while upon reaching a hotel. Get ready to visit Jakar Dzong. It is well-known as the “Castle of the white bird”. It is also called Yuelay Namgyal Dzong. A victorious place that acted as a defensive house during the war in Bhutan. Visit the nearby markets after exploring the dzong. Try out some Bhutanese cuisine too. Spend a night at a hotel.", "ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description": "Let’s explore the lovely district of Bumthang. Tour around Kurjey Lhakhang. Historically significant as the relics of the first three kings of Bhutan rests here. Thus, it is named after the body print (kurjey) of Guru Padmasambhava. A large tree behind the temple is believed to be related to Guru.\\r\\n\\r\\nFurther, visit the Tamshing Lhakhang also called as “Temple of Good Message”. A remarkable temple and monastery that has a direct link with the Bhutanese saints. Get fascinated with traditional religious paintings. A great center of Bhutanese holy masked dance.\\r\\n\\r\\nComplete the trip by exploring the Konchogsum Lhakhang also named Tsilung. It holds great historic importance and the good blending of ancient culture and modern art is the best part. Return to a hotel after an exciting trip. Stay overnight at a hotel.", "ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_description": "Have breakfast and let’s continue to sightsee the remaining places. Visit the first place of Bhutan “Wangdichholing Palace” which wasn’t mainly a fortress.It was used as a monastic school but now renovation has helped it to convert into a museum. Also, see five colossal water-powered prayer wheels inside chortens.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom here, tour an ancient Jambay Lhakhang which was constructed to calm down the demons. The three steps symbolizing three ages are the main attraction inside the main Lhakhang. It indicates the past, present, and a new age of the historic Shakyamuni Buddha. Witness the future Buddha with his feet on an elephant, ancient murals portraying 1000 Buddhas, Kalachakra Temple, a pile of mani stones, and stone chortens. An ancient belief is that there is a lake under the Lhakhang which consists of hidden holy texts and artifacts concealed by Guru Rinpoche.\\r\\n\\r\\nA visit to the Buddhist monastery Ngang Lhakhang popularly known as Swan temple. Admire the beautiful religious architecture, Guru Rinpoche’s statue with his two consorts, and the protective three deities of long-life Amitayus, Tara, and Usnishavijaya. Stay overnight at a hotel.", "ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description": "Have your breakfast and get ready for a long 9-hour road trip to Paro. Admire the beautiful scenery en route to Paro and check into the hotel upon arrival. Enjoy dinner and take much-needed rest after such a long travel. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\nAlternatively, take a domestic flight from Bumthang to Paro. Upon arrival, rest at a hotel for a while. Leave the hotel to visit the oldest Jowo temple in Kyichu Lhakhang. This temple holds great importance in Bhutanese history as it was constructed to stop female giants who were troubling to spread Buddhism across Tibet. The original statue of Jowo Shakyamuni and a statue of Chenrezig can be seen too. From here, an hour drive to reach Chele La Pass. At the highest pass of Bhutan, one can get a glimpse of mesmerizing mountain ranges. Every photographer delight to capture splendid natural scenery including Bhutan’s most sacred peak Mt. Jumolhari, and the surrounding peak overlooking the lovely Paro and Haa valleys. Witness the rock paintings of Guru Rinpoche with his two consorts. Spend a night at a hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter the tour of the pass, return to your hotel for the night’s stay.", "ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description": "<div id=\\"collapse-9\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-9\\">\\r\\n\\r\\nAn adventurous day to travel to Bhutan’s most iconic Tiger’s Nest Monastery. A lovely place where one can get a good glimpse of the Paro valley as it is situated on the Cliffside. This monastery is one finest specimens of Bhutanese architecture holding spiritual and cultural significance. Mediate in this peaceful cave for one’s mind and soul calmness. One can interact with monks to learn more about the folklore related to this cave. On returning, stop halfway at a cafe for lunch/coffee. Descend down to reach the next destination Drukgyel Dzong. This ancient ruin is Bhutan’s beautiful archaeological site. This dzong was built solely for protection purposes and the nation’s sovereignty is highly connected with it. The best example of masonry crafts on the walls can be seen. Also, witness the cylindrical tower building Chu-dzong. After an amazing tour, return to a hotel to enjoy dinner. Spend a night at a hotel.\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_description": "Today is remaining sightseeing in Paro and the first destination is the National Museum of Bhutan. The paintings, art pieces, animal masks, and bronze statues are the finest collections displayed here. The galleries have an enormous collection and are the best place for history and art lovers.\\r\\n\\r\\nFrom here, travel to visit Paro Dzong. The formal name is Rinpung Dzong meaning “Fortress on a Heap of Jewels”. Famous for its finest Bhutanese architecture one can see the gold, black and ochre-painted carved wood. The variation on the Bhutanese mandala and a “Thondrol” (a huge thangka) where religious pictures of Guru Rinpoche are painted or embroidered are major highlights.\\r\\n\\r\\nAccomplish the tour by touring Dzongdrakha Goemba. A unique place combined with four chapels is also stated as “Mini Taktsang”. Jongsarbu Lhakhang, Tshering Lhakhang, Guru Lhakhang, and Lhamey are four main chapels. Besides, one can witness a whole year of fruit-bearing magical orange trees in the courtyard. Other attractions are a huge white Chorten, a hidden chamber of Guru Lhakhang, and a permanent Shakyamuni Buddha statue. Return to hotel and arrange backpack for next day’s departure. Spend a night there.", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_description": "An end to a remarkable 11-day tour making some sweet memories. Along with the Bhutanese guide, drive to the Paro International Airport. The guide bids farewell and you depart to the preferred destinations with the hope of visiting this heavenly nation again.", "_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6"}, "categoryId": null, "meta_title": "Bhutan Tour with Bumthang Valley  | Everest Vacation", "blogContent": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-tour-9-days/\\\\u0022\\\\u003eBhutan\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e is best known as the Kingdom of Happiness. Bhutan Tour with Bumthang Valley 11 days offers you breathtaking scenery, beautiful landscapes, natural resources, stunning mountain peaks, cultural heritage, and a rich belief in Buddhism. A perfect gateway to relaxation and a holiday destination and lose oneself in tranquility and spirituality from the hustle-bustle of daily life.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe most traveled destinations such as Thimphu, Wangdue, Punakha, \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumthang_District\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eBumthang\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e, and Paro are the complete package of artistically beautiful and iconic landmarks. Tourists are very satisfied and pleased after exploring these landmarks.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nBuddhism and Bhutanese culture are interrelated. Buddhism is a way of living life and their practices can be seen in their warm behavior. The nation is not only rich in its arts, tradition, and culture but also its free services of health and education to the natives. Come and let’s join to discover in-depth this dreamlike spiritual Bhutan in this 11-day tour to rejuvenate and make unforgettable memories.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4462\\",\\"4464\\",\\"4434\\",\\"4414\\",\\"4325\\",\\"4239\\",\\"3894\\",\\"4447\\",\\"3868\\",\\"4015\\",\\"4035\\",\\"3949\\",\\"4033\\",\\"3950\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Arrival at Paro Airport and Transfer to Thimphu\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-1\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-1\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-1\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-1\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nA warm welcome by the Bhutanese guide upon reaching the Paro International Airport. A short stop at a restaurant/cafe for lunch/coffee. After that, enjoy a scenic drive to Thimphu. Rest for a while at a hotel. Then, the guide takes you to visit Jungshi Handmade Paper Factory. The Daphne tree and the Dekap tree’s barks are used to produce a traditional handmade paper called “Deh-so”. Experience the process of traditional handmade paper making. One can also purchase handmade items as a souvenir at the factory’s small shop. A side tour to the busiest Centenary Farmer’s Market. This domestic market is happening on the weekend. A great place to learn about the Bhutanese ingredients and interact with locals if one wishes to. One can also purchase organic items. Later on, visit the nearby Voluntary Artist Studio popular as VAST. The art galleries abundant with modern and contemporary artworks are a perfect place for art lovers. Travelers can purchase artwork and money goes to charity. Enjoy the nightlife and try delicious Bhutanese cuisine. Spend a night at a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Thimphu Sightseeing\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-2\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-2\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nHave breakfast and let’s get ready to explore this beautiful capital Thimphu. A visit to Kuensel Phodrang to view the largest statue of the Great Buddha in Bhutan. Enjoy the good view of the Thimphu valley from there. After that, a tour of the National Memorial Chorten was built in honor of the third Druk Gyalpo. The Tibetan-style architecture of golden spires and bells is impressive and holds great cultural significance. An interesting tour of the Bhutan Postal Museum. An amazing collection of varieties of stamps in different shapes and also learn about Bhutanese history. Customize stamps with your photos and take them as a souvenir. Then, a visit to the Buddhist monastery and fortress Tashichho Dzong-“Fortress of Auspicious Doctrine”. Popularly known as Thimphu Dzong, it is famous for its history, unique architecture, and calm atmosphere. At last, end the trip by visiting the National Folk Heritage Museum. The Bhutanese culture is greatly shown through documentaries or educational programs. The displaying of seasonal artifacts is the highlight of this museum. Rest, relax and spend a night at a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Thimphu to Punakha \\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After breakfast, drive to Punakha. On the way, stop at Dochu-La-Pass and witness the snow-capped mountains of Bhutan. The beautiful landscape, and vegetation while descending the Pass. Visit the 108 memorial Druk Wangyal Chortens constructed in respect of Bhutanese soldiers killed in a war.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom there, head towards Punakha. Stop at the “Fertility Temple of Bhutan”-Chimi Lhakhang. Many childless couples seek blessings of the Divine Madman even from around the world. Upon reaching Punakha, rest for a while at a hotel. A time to visit the second oldest Punakha dzong in Bhutan. This palace of bliss is constructed without using any nails. Participate in the Punakha festival if you are here around mid-Feb. Complete the tour by visiting Khamsum Yulley Namgyal Chorten. The iconic landmark was constructed to bring peace to the world. Admire the lovely images of the deities of mandalas Vajrakilaya. In the evening, visit nearby local places or markets. Spend a night at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Punakha to Wangdue and Phobjikha valley stay\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After breakfast, drive to Wangdue. A tour to Wangdue Phodrang Dzong. A historic importance dzong consists of 14 temples and has three doorways and three courtyards. Witness the stunning interior inside the dzong and one can also see Mahakala carved on a stone slab. From there, a visit to the temple of Sha Radap. Locals referred to it as Rada Lhakhang. Locals worship as guardian deities and it is accustomed to bringing newborns to seek the blessings and for the naming ceremony. Usually, the name of a baby begins with Rada. Wangdue is a doorway to the Phobjika valley. Have lunch and a 2-hour drive to the Phobjika valley.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nPhobjika is a beautiful glacial valley in Bhutan. It is also called Gangtey because of the Gangtey Monastery. The valley is rich in a variety of flora and fauna. It is a winter home for endangered and sacred black-necked cranes which symbolizes longevity. A popular trekking route and the breathtaking scenery, vegetation, and landscapes make this valley more attractive. A visit to the Gangtey Monastery, beautiful for its traditional architecture. The vital monastery of the Nyingmapa school of Buddhism is situated on a forested hill. Admire the mesmerizing view of the Phobjika valley from the hilltop. Interact with locals if one wishes to and spend a night at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"05\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Travel to Bumthang\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"An exciting 5-hour trip to Bumthang witnessing beautiful scenery on the way. Take a rest for a while upon reaching a hotel. Get ready to visit Jakar Dzong. It is well-known as the “Castle of the white bird”. It is also called Yuelay Namgyal Dzong. A victorious place that acted as a defensive house during the war in Bhutan. Visit the nearby markets after exploring the dzong. Try out some Bhutanese cuisine too. Spend a night at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"06\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Sightseeing in Bumthang\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Let’s explore the lovely district of Bumthang. Tour around Kurjey Lhakhang. Historically significant as the relics of the first three kings of Bhutan rests here. Thus, it is named after the body print (kurjey) of Guru Padmasambhava. A large tree behind the temple is believed to be related to Guru.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFurther, visit the Tamshing Lhakhang also called as “Temple of Good Message”. A remarkable temple and monastery that has a direct link with the Bhutanese saints. Get fascinated with traditional religious paintings. A great center of Bhutanese holy masked dance.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nComplete the trip by exploring the Konchogsum Lhakhang also named Tsilung. It holds great historic importance and the good blending of ancient culture and modern art is the best part. Return to a hotel after an exciting trip. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days\\":\\"07\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Sightseeing Bumthang\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Have breakfast and let’s continue to sightsee the remaining places. Visit the first place of Bhutan “Wangdichholing Palace” which wasn’t mainly a fortress.It was used as a monastic school but now renovation has helped it to convert into a museum. Also, see five colossal water-powered prayer wheels inside chortens.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom here, tour an ancient Jambay Lhakhang which was constructed to calm down the demons. The three steps symbolizing three ages are the main attraction inside the main Lhakhang. It indicates the past, present, and a new age of the historic Shakyamuni Buddha. Witness the future Buddha with his feet on an elephant, ancient murals portraying 1000 Buddhas, Kalachakra Temple, a pile of mani stones, and stone chortens. An ancient belief is that there is a lake under the Lhakhang which consists of hidden holy texts and artifacts concealed by Guru Rinpoche.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nA visit to the Buddhist monastery Ngang Lhakhang popularly known as Swan temple. Admire the beautiful religious architecture, Guru Rinpoche’s statue with his two consorts, and the protective three deities of long-life Amitayus, Tara, and Usnishavijaya. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days\\":\\"08\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Travel to Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Have your breakfast and get ready for a long 9-hour road trip to Paro. Admire the beautiful scenery en route to Paro and check into the hotel upon arrival. Enjoy dinner and take much-needed rest after such a long travel. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAlternatively, take a domestic flight from Bumthang to Paro. Upon arrival, rest at a hotel for a while. Leave the hotel to visit the oldest Jowo temple in Kyichu Lhakhang. This temple holds great importance in Bhutanese history as it was constructed to stop female giants who were troubling to spread Buddhism across Tibet. The original statue of Jowo Shakyamuni and a statue of Chenrezig can be seen too. From here, an hour drive to reach Chele La Pass. At the highest pass of Bhutan, one can get a glimpse of mesmerizing mountain ranges. Every photographer delight to capture splendid natural scenery including Bhutan’s most sacred peak Mt. Jumolhari, and the surrounding peak overlooking the lovely Paro and Haa valleys. Witness the rock paintings of Guru Rinpoche with his two consorts. Spend a night at a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter the tour of the pass, return to your hotel for the night’s stay.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"09\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Tiger’s Nest Monastery Hike\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-9\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-9\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAn adventurous day to travel to Bhutan’s most iconic Tiger’s Nest Monastery. A lovely place where one can get a good glimpse of the Paro valley as it is situated on the Cliffside. This monastery is one finest specimens of Bhutanese architecture holding spiritual and cultural significance. Mediate in this peaceful cave for one’s mind and soul calmness. One can interact with monks to learn more about the folklore related to this cave. On returning, stop halfway at a cafe for lunch/coffee. Descend down to reach the next destination Drukgyel Dzong. This ancient ruin is Bhutan’s beautiful archaeological site. This dzong was built solely for protection purposes and the nation’s sovereignty is highly connected with it. The best example of masonry crafts on the walls can be seen. Also, witness the cylindrical tower building Chu-dzong. After an amazing tour, return to a hotel to enjoy dinner. Spend a night at a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_di_days\\":\\"10\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Sightseeing in Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Today is remaining sightseeing in Paro and the first destination is the National Museum of Bhutan. The paintings, art pieces, animal masks, and bronze statues are the finest collections displayed here. The galleries have an enormous collection and are the best place for history and art lovers.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom here, travel to visit Paro Dzong. The formal name is Rinpung Dzong meaning “Fortress on a Heap of Jewels”. Famous for its finest Bhutanese architecture one can see the gold, black and ochre-painted carved wood. The variation on the Bhutanese mandala and a “Thondrol” (a huge thangka) where religious pictures of Guru Rinpoche are painted or embroidered are major highlights.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAccomplish the tour by touring Dzongdrakha Goemba. A unique place combined with four chapels is also stated as “Mini Taktsang”. Jongsarbu Lhakhang, Tshering Lhakhang, Guru Lhakhang, and Lhamey are four main chapels. Besides, one can witness a whole year of fruit-bearing magical orange trees in the courtyard. Other attractions are a huge white Chorten, a hidden chamber of Guru Lhakhang, and a permanent Shakyamuni Buddha statue. Return to hotel and arrange backpack for next day’s departure. Spend a night there.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_di_days\\":\\"11\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Departure from Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"An end to a remarkable 11-day tour making some sweet memories. Along with the Bhutanese guide, drive to the Paro International Airport. The guide bids farewell and you depart to the preferred destinations with the hope of visiting this heavenly nation again.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":11,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAccommodation in approved hotels\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUS$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVisa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUSD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fee\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (Restaurant)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking Bhutan licensed guide\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEntrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBottled drinking water throughout the journeys\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-tour-9-days/\\\\u0022\\\\u003eBhutan\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e is best known as the Kingdom of Happiness. Bhutan Tour with Bumthang Valley 11 days offers you breathtaking scenery, beautiful landscapes, natural resources, stunning mountain peaks, cultural heritage, and a rich belief in Buddhism. A perfect gateway to relaxation and a holiday destination and lose oneself in tranquility and spirituality from the hustle-bustle of daily life.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe most traveled destinations such as Thimphu, Wangdue, Punakha, \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumthang_District\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eBumthang\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e, and Paro are the complete package of artistically beautiful and iconic landmarks. Tourists are very satisfied and pleased after exploring these landmarks.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nBuddhism and Bhutanese culture are interrelated. Buddhism is a way of living life and their practices can be seen in their warm behavior. The nation is not only rich in its arts, tradition, and culture but also its free services of health and education to the natives. Come and let’s join to discover in-depth this dreamlike spiritual Bhutan in this 11-day tour to rejuvenate and make unforgettable memories.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4462\\",\\"4464\\",\\"4434\\",\\"4414\\",\\"4325\\",\\"4239\\",\\"3894\\",\\"4447\\",\\"3868\\",\\"4015\\",\\"4035\\",\\"3949\\",\\"4033\\",\\"3950\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Arrival at Paro Airport and Transfer to Thimphu\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-1\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-1\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-1\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-1\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nA warm welcome by the Bhutanese guide upon reaching the Paro International Airport. A short stop at a restaurant/cafe for lunch/coffee. After that, enjoy a scenic drive to Thimphu. Rest for a while at a hotel. Then, the guide takes you to visit Jungshi Handmade Paper Factory. The Daphne tree and the Dekap tree’s barks are used to produce a traditional handmade paper called “Deh-so”. Experience the process of traditional handmade paper making. One can also purchase handmade items as a souvenir at the factory’s small shop. A side tour to the busiest Centenary Farmer’s Market. This domestic market is happening on the weekend. A great place to learn about the Bhutanese ingredients and interact with locals if one wishes to. One can also purchase organic items. Later on, visit the nearby Voluntary Artist Studio popular as VAST. The art galleries abundant with modern and contemporary artworks are a perfect place for art lovers. Travelers can purchase artwork and money goes to charity. Enjoy the nightlife and try delicious Bhutanese cuisine. Spend a night at a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Thimphu Sightseeing\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-2\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-2\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nHave breakfast and let’s get ready to explore this beautiful capital Thimphu. A visit to Kuensel Phodrang to view the largest statue of the Great Buddha in Bhutan. Enjoy the good view of the Thimphu valley from there. After that, a tour of the National Memorial Chorten was built in honor of the third Druk Gyalpo. The Tibetan-style architecture of golden spires and bells is impressive and holds great cultural significance. An interesting tour of the Bhutan Postal Museum. An amazing collection of varieties of stamps in different shapes and also learn about Bhutanese history. Customize stamps with your photos and take them as a souvenir. Then, a visit to the Buddhist monastery and fortress Tashichho Dzong-“Fortress of Auspicious Doctrine”. Popularly known as Thimphu Dzong, it is famous for its history, unique architecture, and calm atmosphere. At last, end the trip by visiting the National Folk Heritage Museum. The Bhutanese culture is greatly shown through documentaries or educational programs. The displaying of seasonal artifacts is the highlight of this museum. Rest, relax and spend a night at a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Thimphu to Punakha \\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After breakfast, drive to Punakha. On the way, stop at Dochu-La-Pass and witness the snow-capped mountains of Bhutan. The beautiful landscape, and vegetation while descending the Pass. Visit the 108 memorial Druk Wangyal Chortens constructed in respect of Bhutanese soldiers killed in a war.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom there, head towards Punakha. Stop at the “Fertility Temple of Bhutan”-Chimi Lhakhang. Many childless couples seek blessings of the Divine Madman even from around the world. Upon reaching Punakha, rest for a while at a hotel. A time to visit the second oldest Punakha dzong in Bhutan. This palace of bliss is constructed without using any nails. Participate in the Punakha festival if you are here around mid-Feb. Complete the tour by visiting Khamsum Yulley Namgyal Chorten. The iconic landmark was constructed to bring peace to the world. Admire the lovely images of the deities of mandalas Vajrakilaya. In the evening, visit nearby local places or markets. Spend a night at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Punakha to Wangdue and Phobjikha valley stay\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"After breakfast, drive to Wangdue. A tour to Wangdue Phodrang Dzong. A historic importance dzong consists of 14 temples and has three doorways and three courtyards. Witness the stunning interior inside the dzong and one can also see Mahakala carved on a stone slab. From there, a visit to the temple of Sha Radap. Locals referred to it as Rada Lhakhang. Locals worship as guardian deities and it is accustomed to bringing newborns to seek the blessings and for the naming ceremony. Usually, the name of a baby begins with Rada. Wangdue is a doorway to the Phobjika valley. Have lunch and a 2-hour drive to the Phobjika valley.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nPhobjika is a beautiful glacial valley in Bhutan. It is also called Gangtey because of the Gangtey Monastery. The valley is rich in a variety of flora and fauna. It is a winter home for endangered and sacred black-necked cranes which symbolizes longevity. A popular trekking route and the breathtaking scenery, vegetation, and landscapes make this valley more attractive. A visit to the Gangtey Monastery, beautiful for its traditional architecture. The vital monastery of the Nyingmapa school of Buddhism is situated on a forested hill. Admire the mesmerizing view of the Phobjika valley from the hilltop. Interact with locals if one wishes to and spend a night at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"05\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Travel to Bumthang\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"An exciting 5-hour trip to Bumthang witnessing beautiful scenery on the way. Take a rest for a while upon reaching a hotel. Get ready to visit Jakar Dzong. It is well-known as the “Castle of the white bird”. It is also called Yuelay Namgyal Dzong. A victorious place that acted as a defensive house during the war in Bhutan. Visit the nearby markets after exploring the dzong. Try out some Bhutanese cuisine too. Spend a night at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"06\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Sightseeing in Bumthang\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Let’s explore the lovely district of Bumthang. Tour around Kurjey Lhakhang. Historically significant as the relics of the first three kings of Bhutan rests here. Thus, it is named after the body print (kurjey) of Guru Padmasambhava. A large tree behind the temple is believed to be related to Guru.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFurther, visit the Tamshing Lhakhang also called as “Temple of Good Message”. A remarkable temple and monastery that has a direct link with the Bhutanese saints. Get fascinated with traditional religious paintings. A great center of Bhutanese holy masked dance.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nComplete the trip by exploring the Konchogsum Lhakhang also named Tsilung. It holds great historic importance and the good blending of ancient culture and modern art is the best part. Return to a hotel after an exciting trip. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_5_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days\\":\\"07\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Sightseeing Bumthang\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Have breakfast and let’s continue to sightsee the remaining places. Visit the first place of Bhutan “Wangdichholing Palace” which wasn’t mainly a fortress.It was used as a monastic school but now renovation has helped it to convert into a museum. Also, see five colossal water-powered prayer wheels inside chortens.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom here, tour an ancient Jambay Lhakhang which was constructed to calm down the demons. The three steps symbolizing three ages are the main attraction inside the main Lhakhang. It indicates the past, present, and a new age of the historic Shakyamuni Buddha. Witness the future Buddha with his feet on an elephant, ancient murals portraying 1000 Buddhas, Kalachakra Temple, a pile of mani stones, and stone chortens. An ancient belief is that there is a lake under the Lhakhang which consists of hidden holy texts and artifacts concealed by Guru Rinpoche.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nA visit to the Buddhist monastery Ngang Lhakhang popularly known as Swan temple. Admire the beautiful religious architecture, Guru Rinpoche’s statue with his two consorts, and the protective three deities of long-life Amitayus, Tara, and Usnishavijaya. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_6_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days\\":\\"08\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Travel to Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Have your breakfast and get ready for a long 9-hour road trip to Paro. Admire the beautiful scenery en route to Paro and check into the hotel upon arrival. Enjoy dinner and take much-needed rest after such a long travel. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAlternatively, take a domestic flight from Bumthang to Paro. Upon arrival, rest at a hotel for a while. Leave the hotel to visit the oldest Jowo temple in Kyichu Lhakhang. This temple holds great importance in Bhutanese history as it was constructed to stop female giants who were troubling to spread Buddhism across Tibet. The original statue of Jowo Shakyamuni and a statue of Chenrezig can be seen too. From here, an hour drive to reach Chele La Pass. At the highest pass of Bhutan, one can get a glimpse of mesmerizing mountain ranges. Every photographer delight to capture splendid natural scenery including Bhutan’s most sacred peak Mt. Jumolhari, and the surrounding peak overlooking the lovely Paro and Haa valleys. Witness the rock paintings of Guru Rinpoche with his two consorts. Spend a night at a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter the tour of the pass, return to your hotel for the night’s stay.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_7_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"09\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Tiger’s Nest Monastery Hike\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cdiv id=\\\\u0022collapse-9\\\\u0022 class=\\\\u0022panel-collapse collapse show\\\\u0022 role=\\\\u0022tabpanel\\\\u0022 aria-labelledby=\\\\u0022heading-9\\\\u0022\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAn adventurous day to travel to Bhutan’s most iconic Tiger’s Nest Monastery. A lovely place where one can get a good glimpse of the Paro valley as it is situated on the Cliffside. This monastery is one finest specimens of Bhutanese architecture holding spiritual and cultural significance. Mediate in this peaceful cave for one’s mind and soul calmness. One can interact with monks to learn more about the folklore related to this cave. On returning, stop halfway at a cafe for lunch/coffee. Descend down to reach the next destination Drukgyel Dzong. This ancient ruin is Bhutan’s beautiful archaeological site. This dzong was built solely for protection purposes and the nation’s sovereignty is highly connected with it. The best example of masonry crafts on the walls can be seen. Also, witness the cylindrical tower building Chu-dzong. After an amazing tour, return to a hotel to enjoy dinner. Spend a night at a hotel.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/div\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_8_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_di_days\\":\\"10\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Sightseeing in Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Today is remaining sightseeing in Paro and the first destination is the National Museum of Bhutan. The paintings, art pieces, animal masks, and bronze statues are the finest collections displayed here. The galleries have an enormous collection and are the best place for history and art lovers.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nFrom here, travel to visit Paro Dzong. The formal name is Rinpung Dzong meaning “Fortress on a Heap of Jewels”. Famous for its finest Bhutanese architecture one can see the gold, black and ochre-painted carved wood. The variation on the Bhutanese mandala and a “Thondrol” (a huge thangka) where religious pictures of Guru Rinpoche are painted or embroidered are major highlights.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAccomplish the tour by touring Dzongdrakha Goemba. A unique place combined with four chapels is also stated as “Mini Taktsang”. Jongsarbu Lhakhang, Tshering Lhakhang, Guru Lhakhang, and Lhamey are four main chapels. Besides, one can witness a whole year of fruit-bearing magical orange trees in the courtyard. Other attractions are a huge white Chorten, a hidden chamber of Guru Lhakhang, and a permanent Shakyamuni Buddha statue. Return to hotel and arrange backpack for next day’s departure. Spend a night there.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_9_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_di_days\\":\\"11\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Departure from Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"An end to a remarkable 11-day tour making some sweet memories. Along with the Bhutanese guide, drive to the Paro International Airport. The guide bids farewell and you depart to the preferred destinations with the hope of visiting this heavenly nation again.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":11,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAccommodation in approved hotels\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUS$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVisa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUSD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fee\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (Restaurant)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking Bhutan licensed guide\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEntrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBottled drinking water throughout the journeys\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Tachogang-Lhakhang-Bridge-Paro.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bhutan-airport.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/bhutan-tour-photo.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/prayer-flags-in-bhutan-tour.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/horse-in-bhutan.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/food-in-bhutan-rotated.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/with-bhutan-guide.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/DochuLa-Pass-Thimphu-bhutan.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/travel-to-punakha.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Bridge-of-Punakha-Dzong.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Punakha-Dzong-with-River2.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Taktsang-Monastery-Tigers-Nest.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Memorial-Chorten-Thimphu.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Memorial-Chorten-with-prayers.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=3509", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "3509", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2024-01-03 08:49:26", "post_date_gmt": "2024-01-03 08:49:26", "post_modified": "2024-02-13 02:11:50", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-02-13 02:11:50"}}, "customSections": [{"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["<a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-tour-9-days/\\">Bhutan</a> is best known as the Kingdom of Happiness. Bhutan Tour with Bumthang Valley 11 days offers you breathtaking scenery, beautiful landscapes, natural resources, stunning mountain peaks, cultural heritage, and a rich belief in Buddhism. A perfect gateway to relaxation and a holiday destination and lose oneself in tranquility and spirituality from the hustle-bustle of daily life.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe most traveled destinations such as Thimphu, Wangdue, Punakha, <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumthang_District\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Bumthang</a>, and Paro are the complete package of artistically beautiful and iconic landmarks. Tourists are very satisfied and pleased after exploring these landmarks.\\r\\n\\r\\nBuddhism and Bhutanese culture are interrelated. Buddhism is a way of living life and their practices can be seen in their warm behavior. The nation is not only rich in its arts, tradition, and culture but also its free services of health and education to the natives. Come and let’s join to discover in-depth this dreamlike spiritual Bhutan in this 11-day tour to rejuvenate and make unforgettable memories."], "description": "<a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-tour-9-days/\\">Bhutan</a> is best known as the Kingdom of Happiness. Bhutan Tour with Bumthang Valley 11 days offers you breathtaking scenery, beautiful landscapes, natural resources, stunning mountain peaks, cultural heritage, and a rich belief in Buddhism. A perfect gateway to relaxation and a holiday destination and lose oneself in tranquility and spirituality from the hustle-bustle of daily life.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe most traveled destinations such as Thimphu, Wangdue, Punakha, <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bumthang_District\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Bumthang</a>, and Paro are the complete package of artistically beautiful and iconic landmarks. Tourists are very satisfied and pleased after exploring these landmarks.\\r\\n\\r\\nBuddhism and Bhutanese culture are interrelated. Buddhism is a way of living life and their practices can be seen in their warm behavior. The nation is not only rich in its arts, tradition, and culture but also its free services of health and education to the natives. Come and let’s join to discover in-depth this dreamlike spiritual Bhutan in this 11-day tour to rejuvenate and make unforgettable memories."}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Accommodation in approved hotels", "US$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)", "Visa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary", "USD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fee", "Breakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (Restaurant)", "English speaking Bhutan licensed guide", "Transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary", "Entrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary", "Bottled drinking water throughout the journeys"], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Accommodation in approved hotels", "US$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)", "Visa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary", "USD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fee", "Breakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (Restaurant)", "English speaking Bhutan licensed guide", "Transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary", "Entrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary", "Bottled drinking water throughout the journeys"], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "Thimphu, Punakha, Pobhjikha, Bumthang Valley and Paro with Taktsang", "trip_type_level": "Private Tour", "meta_description": "Bhutan Tour with Bumthang Valley treats with breathtaking scenery, beautiful landscapes, stunning mountain peaks, and rich cultural heritage.", "trip_attractions": "Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": "Private AC Vehicle"}, "trip_transportations": "Private AC Vehicle", "trip_highlights_title": "What's included?"}	2024-01-03 08:49:26+00	2024-02-13 02:11:50+00
224	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "3 nights in Kathmandu, 8 nights in Bhutan with Bunthang Valley", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "12", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour"}, "meta": {"_edit_last": "5", "_edit_lock": "1723975844:5", "_dp_original": "3508", "_thumbnail_id": "400", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "3 nights in Kathmandu, 8 nights in Bhutan with Bunthang Valley", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "12", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "Nepal Bhutan Tour 11 nights 12 days", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Nepal Bhutan Tour 11 nights 12 days", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "44", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Visit iconic landmarks, immerse in their culture, enjoy the uniqueness of these magical nations during Nepal Bhutan Tour 11 nights 12 days.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "nepal-bhutan-tour-11-nights-12-days", "tags": [], "title": "Nepal Bhutan Tour 11 nights 12 days", "duration": "12 Days", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Nepal Bhutan Tour 11 nights 12 days (3 nights in Nepal and 8 nights in Bhutan)</strong></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Travel Route (Bhutan and then Nepal also possible), Flexible monuments to visit, Flexible number of nights in both countries.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We take care of your Visa to Bhutan and internal flights. A Nepal visa is easily available upon your arrival at Kathmandu (TIA) airport.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n&nbsp;\\r\\n\\r\\nThe <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-bhutan-tour-10-nights-11-days-2/\\">Nepal Bhutan Tour</a> 11 nights 12 days package designed by Everest Vacation is tremendous. Visit the Himalayan nations of Nepal and Bhutan. Visit iconic landmarks, immerse in their culture, and enjoy the uniqueness of these captivating destinations. In Nepal, explore the cultural city of Kathmandu, the oldest Changu Narayan temple, and architecturally marvelous Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Durbar Squares. A scenic cable car ride to the lovely Chandragiri Hill mesmerizes you with panoramic views of the Himalayan ranges.\\r\\n\\r\\nExplore the beautiful cities of Thimphu, Punakha, Trongsa, Jakar, <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phobjikha_Valley\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Phobjikha</a>, and Paro in Bhutan. All these amazing destinations have diverse offerings for visitors. Visit iconic landmarks such as Chhimi Lhakhang Temple, Memorial Chorten, ancient Dzongs, and Tiger’s Nest Monastery. The Phobjikha trail hike takes you closer to nature. The Bumthang Valley excursion is full of amazing surprises which we ensure will enthrall visitors. Get rewarded by the phenomenal mountain views from the Dochu La Pass."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Arrival in Kathmandu and Kathmandu Sightseeing", "richText": "<div id=\\"collapse-1\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-1\\">\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pickup from Kathmandu (TIA) airport</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Boudhanath ( A large Buddhist Stupa)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pashupatinath (Largest Hindu Temple having an open cremation area)</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you arrive lately in Kathmandu, we will manage the tour in next day (before flight to Bhutan)</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Kathmandu\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "driveTime": "Approx, 30 minutes drive from airport to hotel.", "elevation": "1400m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 2, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Bhaktapur, Changu Narayan and Swoyambhu Stupa (Monkey Temple)", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pickup from your hotel</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Swoyambhu Stupa/Monkey Temple</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bhaktapur Durbar Square</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Changu Narayan Temple</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Kathmandu", "driveTime": "Approx, 40 minutes drive to Bhaktapur", "elevation": "1406m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 3, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Chandragiri hills (2551 meters) by cable car and Patan Durbar Square Tour", "richText": "<ul><li>Place to visit / Tour<ul><li>Drive to Chandragiri Cable car station</li><li>Station to Chandragiri hills by cablecar</li><li>Chandragiri sightseeing for panoramic views of Kathmandu Valley and the Himalayan ranges from Annapurna to Everest</li><li>Back to station and drive back to Patan</li></ul></li></ul><p>Overnight at Kathmandu</p>", "driveTime": "Approx, 1 hour drive to Chandragiri cable car station from Kathamndu", "elevation": "2551m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 4, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Fly Kathmandu to Paro(Bhutan), drive to Thimphu and Thimphu sightseeing", "richText": "<ul><li>Drop to Kathmandu airport</li><li>Pickup from Paro airport</li><li>Drive to Thimphu</li><li>Place to visit / Tour<ul><li>Memorial Chorten (temple)</li><li>Changangkha Lhakhang</li><li>Statue of Buddha</li><li>Visit the fortress of Thimphu, Tashichho Dzong</li><li>Weekend market (Friday, Saturday, Sunday)</li></ul></li><li>If you arrive lately in Paro, we will manage the tour in next day morning.</li></ul><p>Overnight at Thimphu</p>", "driveTime": "Approx, 1 hour 30 minutes drive from Paro to Thimphu.", "elevation": "2200m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 5, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Drive to Punakha and Punakha Sightseeing", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive to Punakha crossing over Dochu La Pass (3100 mts)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Dochu La Pass (views of the highest mountain peaks &amp; walk around the 108 stupas)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike through the paddy field and old village to visit Chhimi Lhakhang, the temple of fertility.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Punakha Dzong</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Khamsum Yuley Lhakhang</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Punakha", "driveTime": "Approx, 2 hours 30 minutes drive from Thimphu to Punakha", "elevation": "1200m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 6, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Drive from Punakha to Trongsa", "richText": "<div id=\\"collapse-6\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-6\\">\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive to Trongsa crossing over Pele La Pass at 3,420 meters</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Cross over Pele La Pass at 3,420m which forms the part of Black mountain range</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Enroute could take a short break and go for short hike to the remote village of Rukubji/Chendibji</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Trongsa\\r\\n\\r\\n</div>", "driveTime": "Approx, 4 hours drive from Punakha to Trongsa", "elevation": "2200m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 7, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Drive from Trongsa to Jakar (Bumthang Valley)", "richText": "<ul><li>Place to visit / Tour<ul><li>Visit the majestic Trongsa Dzong (Fortress) , the home of the royals</li><li>Visit Ta Dzong, an ancient watchtower</li><li>Start driving for Jakar crossing over Yotong La pass at 3,400m</li><li>Stop in Chumi valley, the weaving place</li><li>Continue your drive for Jakar crossing over Kiki La pass 2870m</li><li>Arrive Bumthang (Jakar) Valley.</li></ul></li></ul><p>Overnight at Jakar</p>", "driveTime": "Approx, 2 hours drive from Trongsa to Jakar", "elevation": "2587m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 8, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Jakar Sightseeing", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit Jampay Lhakhang</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit Kurjey Lhakhang temple</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit Tamshing Lhakhang temple</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Swiss farm</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Jakar Dzong (if time permits)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Evening walk around Jakar town and try some local pancake and noodles</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Jakar", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "2587m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 9, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Drive from Jakar to Phobjikha and Village tour/hike at Pobhjikha", "richText": "<div id=\\"collapse-9\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-9\\"><div id=\\"collapse-9\\" class=\\"panel-collapse collapse show\\" role=\\"tabpanel\\" aria-labelledby=\\"heading-9\\"><ul><li>Drive to Phobjikha passing by Trongsa town and crossing over Pele La pass, 3420 meters</li><li>Place to visit/tour<ul><li>Phobjikha Nature trail hike (2.5 Hrs), which offers beautiful view of the valley. It starts from the valley and end with Gangtey Goempa</li><li>Visit Gangtey Goempa Temple</li><li>Crane Canter</li><li>An option to visit a village and a farmhouse for lunch/dinner</li></ul></li></ul><p>Overnight at Pobhjikha</p></div></div>", "driveTime": "Approx, 4 hours drive from Jakar to Phobjikha", "elevation": "3000m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 10, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Drive to Paro and Paro Sightseeing", "richText": "<ul><li>Drive to Paro after breakfast</li><li>Place to visit / tour<ul><li>Paro Dzong (Fortress)</li><li>Old Paro Town</li><li>Could get some opportunity to see the traditional game, Archery.</li></ul></li></ul><p>Overnight at Paro</p>", "driveTime": "Approx, 5 hours drive from Phobjikha to Paro", "elevation": "2200m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 11, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Hike to Taktsang Monastery and visit Kyichu Lakhang", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drive to base for the hike</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Place to visit / Tour\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike to Taktsang Monastery (Tiger’s Nest) – 3 hours uphill</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kyichu Lhakhang, one of the oldest temples in Bhutan</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\nOvernight at Paro", "driveTime": "Approx, 20 minutes drive from Paro town to base camp of hike", "elevation": "3120m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 12, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Final Departure / Tour end", "richText": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Drop you to Paro airport from your hotel</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Return with some magnificent memories and moments from Nepal and Bhutan trip.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flight available from Paro to Kathmandu, Bangkok, New Delhi, Kolkata, Bagdogra, Singapore, Dhaka etc.</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/Bhutan-experience.jpg", "title": "Bhutan experience", "altText": "Bhutan experience", "caption": "Bhutan experience", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["4821", "527", "613", "4052", "4897", "4440", "4914", "4435", "400", "4915", "4325", "4239", "4414", "4464"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "ws_block_attract