lkata, Bagdogra, Singapore, Dhaka etc.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_10_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":11,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cblockquote\\\\u003eWe are dedicated to providing quality service to our clients where safety is our topmost priority. We have not mentioned our costs as they depend on factors like trip customization, group sizes, travel season, trip duration, and types of accommodation, meals, transportation, and choice of various activities.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cem\\\\u003e(\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eNote:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e On your request, we can send you cost details. Feel free to contact us for further details.)\\\\u003c/em\\\\u003e\\\\u003c/blockquote\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBhutan Travel Permit and Visa\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBhutan Government sustainable development fee (SDF) USD 100 per person per night.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate vehicle with air conditioning\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003ePrivate cultural English-speaking tour guide (Other language guide also available upon your request with extra cost.)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAll meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) in Bhutan\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast in Nepal\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAll accommodation as per your choice (Luxury/5-star or 4-star hotel or 3-star hotel)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eMonuments entrance/admission fees\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGuide and driver’s meals and accommodation\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eService Charge (the planning, handling, operational and communication charges) \\\\u0026amp; government taxes.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHandle your flight ticket (Kathmandu/Bangkok/New Delhi/Kolkata/Singapore/Dhaka/Singapore to Paro(Bhutan))\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Outdoor Extra Activities\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"Not only historical, cultural, and natural tours embark on an adventurous journey through our outdoor extra activities. Some of our popular outdoor activities to carry out during this tour are as follows:\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHiking:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Short scenic hikes take you closer to nature and offer picturesque views\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eRiver rafting: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eThrilling White Water River rafting in Nepal and Bhutan on rapid rivers relishing scenic landscapes\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eParagliding: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eRelish amazing panoramic Himalayan views, scenic landscapes, and beautiful surroundings\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eZipline: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eExperience the longest and steepest zipline in Nepal and admire scenic surroundings (Currently no zip line in Bhutan)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eBungee jump: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eAdrenaline rush experience through bungee jumping in Nepal amidst beautiful surrounding scenery (Not permitted in Bhutan)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eYoga and meditation: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003ePractice Yoga and Meditation in serene places such as a monastery, yoga centers, or in the vicinity of nature\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eHelicopter tours: \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003eExciting helicopter tours to the iconic Everest Base Camp \\\\u0026amp; Annapurna Base Camp in Nepal and get close-up views of the Himalayas and admire its beauty in Bhutan\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Best time to visit\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eHigh season (Best Time):\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eMarch to May\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e with the blooming flowers covering the hillsides, warm temperatures, stable weather with low humidity and rainfall, clear skies with clear views, and lush greenery everywhere.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eSeptember to November \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003ewith mild temperatures, stable weather, clear skies, and phenomenal views.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eShoulder season (Good Time):\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDecember to February \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003ewith sunny day weather and slightly cold nights \\\\u0026amp; mornings, mild day temperatures, clear surrounding views, and fewer crowds which is perfect for visitors seeking a peaceful visit.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003ch3\\\\u003eLow or Off-season (Average Time):\\\\u003c/h3\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eJune to August \\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003ewith unstable weather and temperature, high humidity, light to heavy rainfall, mostly obstructed views, but lush greenery everywhere. High chances of flight cancelations and roadblocks due to floods \\\\u0026amp; landslides in some places.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Nepal-Bhutan Tour: Is It Right for You?\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eA perfect combination tour of history, culture, and nature\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSuitable for all age groups of travelers (Senior citizens to Kids)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAccompanied by experienced local guides\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eComfortable flat trails while sightseeing Heritage Sites\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTechnical Climbing is not involved during the trip\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHike through forested trails which is medium.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAn experienced guide accompanies you to ensure a comfortable Taktsang Monastery Hike. Pony rides to the halfway are also available.\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransfer via clean private vehicles that are comfortable during sightseeing tours\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Why Travel With Us?\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003e24/7 International Support\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eFlexible Private and Customize Trips\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSafety: Our Topmost Priority\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eSecure Online Payment\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBookings and Payments Flexibility\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eLifetime Deposit Guaranteed\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eGuaranteed Departures\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTravel with Locals to support locals\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eExperienced Team and Expert Guides\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eRespect Nature through Responsible Tourism\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eHappiness and Best Priced Assured\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/travel-to-punakha.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/boudhanath-stupa-1.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/bhaktapur-city-of-arts-e1706022904337.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/local-people-bungmati.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/swoyambhu-monkey-temple.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/phewa-lake-pokhara-1.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/saangkot-pokhara.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/bhaktapur-durbar-square.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/thimphu-buddha-statue.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/archary-game-bhutan.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/punakha-tour.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/Bhutan-experience.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/tiger-nest-monastery-paro.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=3512", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "3512", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2024-01-03 11:08:53", "post_date_gmt": "2024-01-03 11:08:53", "post_modified": "2024-08-18 10:06:17", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-08-18 10:06:17"}}, "customSections": [{"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Nepal Bhutan Tour 10 nights 11 days (5 nights in Nepal and 5 nights in Bhutan)</strong></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Travel Route (Bhutan and then Nepal also possible), Flexible monuments to visit, Flexible number of nights in both countries.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We take care of your Visa to Bhutan and internal flights. A Nepal visa is easily available upon your arrival at Kathmandu (TIA) airport.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n&nbsp;\\r\\n\\r\\nEverest Vacation has created a wonderful <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-bhutan-tour-7-nights-8-days/\\">Nepal Bhutan Tour</a> 10 nights 11 days package to explore these magical Himalayan nations. Visit the ancient temples in Kathmandu Valley including Durbar Squares. The tourist hub Pokhara amazes visitors with scenic mountain views, beautiful places, Phewa Lake boating, and Sarangkot hike for sunrise view. Walk a tour around the Thamel area and go shopping, which is a great way to wrap up the Nepal tour.\\r\\n\\r\\nFly to Bhutan and visit culturally and naturally beautiful places in <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paro_District\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Paro</a>, Punakha, Phobjikha, and Thimphu. Sightsee ancient Dzongs, the giant Great Buddha Dordenma, a lovely old Paro town, beautiful Punakha Dzong, Kyichu Lhakhang, and the popular Chhimi Lhakhang temple. Phobjikha remote village tour with a natural trail hike is a unique experience. Tiger’s Nest Monastery visit in Paro rewards visitors with deep spiritual insights. Create cherished memories of a lifetime during these Nepal-Bhutan tours."], "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Nepal Bhutan Tour 10 nights 11 days (5 nights in Nepal and 5 nights in Bhutan)</strong></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Travel Route (Bhutan and then Nepal also possible), Flexible monuments to visit, Flexible number of nights in both countries.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We take care of your Visa to Bhutan and internal flights. A Nepal visa is easily available upon your arrival at Kathmandu (TIA) airport.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n&nbsp;\\r\\n\\r\\nEverest Vacation has created a wonderful <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-bhutan-tour-7-nights-8-days/\\">Nepal Bhutan Tour</a> 10 nights 11 days package to explore these magical Himalayan nations. Visit the ancient temples in Kathmandu Valley including Durbar Squares. The tourist hub Pokhara amazes visitors with scenic mountain views, beautiful places, Phewa Lake boating, and Sarangkot hike for sunrise view. Walk a tour around the Thamel area and go shopping, which is a great way to wrap up the Nepal tour.\\r\\n\\r\\nFly to Bhutan and visit culturally and naturally beautiful places in <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paro_District\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Paro</a>, Punakha, Phobjikha, and Thimphu. Sightsee ancient Dzongs, the giant Great Buddha Dordenma, a lovely old Paro town, beautiful Punakha Dzong, Kyichu Lhakhang, and the popular Chhimi Lhakhang temple. Phobjikha remote village tour with a natural trail hike is a unique experience. Tiger’s Nest Monastery visit in Paro rewards visitors with deep spiritual insights. Create cherished memories of a lifetime during these Nepal-Bhutan tours."}, {"id": "overview-2", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Outdoor Extra Activities", "content": ["Not only historical, cultural, and natural tours embark on an adventurous journey through our outdoor extra activities. Some of our popular outdoor activities to carry out during this tour are as follows:\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Hiking:</strong> Short scenic hikes take you closer to nature and offer picturesque views\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>River rafting: </strong>Thrilling White Water River rafting in Nepal and Bhutan on rapid rivers relishing scenic landscapes\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Paragliding: </strong>Relish amazing panoramic Himalayan views, scenic landscapes, and beautiful surroundings\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Zipline: </strong>Experience the longest and steepest zipline in Nepal and admire scenic surroundings (Currently no zip line in Bhutan)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Bungee jump: </strong>Adrenaline rush experience through bungee jumping in Nepal amidst beautiful surrounding scenery (Not permitted in Bhutan)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Yoga and meditation: </strong>Practice Yoga and Meditation in serene places such as a monastery, yoga centers, or in the vicinity of nature\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Helicopter tours: </strong>Exciting helicopter tours to the iconic Everest Base Camp &amp; Annapurna Base Camp in Nepal and get close-up views of the Himalayas and admire its beauty in Bhutan"], "description": "Not only historical, cultural, and natural tours embark on an adventurous journey through our outdoor extra activities. Some of our popular outdoor activities to carry out during this tour are as follows:\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Hiking:</strong> Short scenic hikes take you closer to nature and offer picturesque views\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>River rafting: </strong>Thrilling White Water River rafting in Nepal and Bhutan on rapid rivers relishing scenic landscapes\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Paragliding: </strong>Relish amazing panoramic Himalayan views, scenic landscapes, and beautiful surroundings\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Zipline: </strong>Experience the longest and steepest zipline in Nepal and admire scenic surroundings (Currently no zip line in Bhutan)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Bungee jump: </strong>Adrenaline rush experience through bungee jumping in Nepal amidst beautiful surrounding scenery (Not permitted in Bhutan)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Yoga and meditation: </strong>Practice Yoga and Meditation in serene places such as a monastery, yoga centers, or in the vicinity of nature\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Helicopter tours: </strong>Exciting helicopter tours to the iconic Everest Base Camp &amp; Annapurna Base Camp in Nepal and get close-up views of the Himalayas and admire its beauty in Bhutan"}, {"id": "overview-3", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Best time to visit", "content": ["<h3>High season (Best Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>March to May</strong> with the blooming flowers covering the hillsides, warm temperatures, stable weather with low humidity and rainfall, clear skies with clear views, and lush greenery everywhere.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>September to November </strong>with mild temperatures, stable weather, clear skies, and phenomenal views.\\r\\n<h3>Shoulder season (Good Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>December to February </strong>with sunny day weather and slightly cold nights &amp; mornings, mild day temperatures, clear surrounding views, and fewer crowds which is perfect for visitors seeking a peaceful visit.\\r\\n<h3>Low or Off-season (Average Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>June to August </strong>with unstable weather and temperature, high humidity, light to heavy rainfall, mostly obstructed views, but lush greenery everywhere. High chances of flight cancelations and roadblocks due to floods &amp; landslides in some places."], "description": "<h3>High season (Best Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>March to May</strong> with the blooming flowers covering the hillsides, warm temperatures, stable weather with low humidity and rainfall, clear skies with clear views, and lush greenery everywhere.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>September to November </strong>with mild temperatures, stable weather, clear skies, and phenomenal views.\\r\\n<h3>Shoulder season (Good Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>December to February </strong>with sunny day weather and slightly cold nights &amp; mornings, mild day temperatures, clear surrounding views, and fewer crowds which is perfect for visitors seeking a peaceful visit.\\r\\n<h3>Low or Off-season (Average Time):</h3>\\r\\n<strong>June to August </strong>with unstable weather and temperature, high humidity, light to heavy rainfall, mostly obstructed views, but lush greenery everywhere. High chances of flight cancelations and roadblocks due to floods &amp; landslides in some places."}, {"id": "overview-4", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Nepal-Bhutan Tour: Is It Right for You?", "content": ["<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>A perfect combination tour of history, culture, and nature</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Suitable for all age groups of travelers (Senior citizens to Kids)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Accompanied by experienced local guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Comfortable flat trails while sightseeing Heritage Sites</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Technical Climbing is not involved during the trip</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike through forested trails which is medium.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>An experienced guide accompanies you to ensure a comfortable Taktsang Monastery Hike. Pony rides to the halfway are also available.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transfer via clean private vehicles that are comfortable during sightseeing tours</li>\\r\\n</ul>"], "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>A perfect combination tour of history, culture, and nature</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Suitable for all age groups of travelers (Senior citizens to Kids)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Accompanied by experienced local guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Comfortable flat trails while sightseeing Heritage Sites</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Technical Climbing is not involved during the trip</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike through forested trails which is medium.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>An experienced guide accompanies you to ensure a comfortable Taktsang Monastery Hike. Pony rides to the halfway are also available.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transfer via clean private vehicles that are comfortable during sightseeing tours</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, {"id": "overview-5", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Why Travel With Us?", "content": ["<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>24/7 International Support</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Private and Customize Trips</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Safety: Our Topmost Priority</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Secure Online Payment</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bookings and Payments Flexibility</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Lifetime Deposit Guaranteed</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Guaranteed Departures</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Travel with Locals to support locals</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Experienced Team and Expert Guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Respect Nature through Responsible Tourism</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Happiness and Best Priced Assured</li>\\r\\n</ul>"], "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>24/7 International Support</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Private and Customize Trips</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Safety: Our Topmost Priority</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Secure Online Payment</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bookings and Payments Flexibility</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Lifetime Deposit Guaranteed</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Guaranteed Departures</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Travel with Locals to support locals</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Experienced Team and Expert Guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Respect Nature through Responsible Tourism</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Happiness and Best Priced Assured</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "<blockquote>We are dedicated to providing quality service to our clients where safety is our topmost priority. We have not mentioned our costs as they depend on factors like trip customization, group sizes, travel season, trip duration, and types of accommodation, meals, transportation, and choice of various activities.\\r\\n<em>(<strong>Note:</strong> On your request, we can send you cost details. Feel free to contact us for further details.)</em></blockquote>", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Bhutan Travel Permit and Visa", "Bhutan Government sustainable development fee (SDF) USD 100 per person per night.", "Private vehicle with air conditioning", "Private cultural English-speaking tour guide (Other language guide also available upon your request with extra cost.)", "All meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) in Bhutan", "Breakfast in Nepal", "All accommodation as per your choice (Luxury/5-star or 4-star hotel or 3-star hotel)", "Monuments entrance/admission fees", "Guide and driver’s meals and accommodation", "Service Charge (the planning, handling, operational and communication charges) & government taxes.", "Handle your flight ticket (Kathmandu/Bangkok/New Delhi/Kolkata/Singapore/Dhaka/Singapore to Paro(Bhutan))"], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Bhutan Travel Permit and Visa", "Bhutan Government sustainable development fee (SDF) USD 100 per person per night.", "Private vehicle with air conditioning", "Private cultural English-speaking tour guide (Other language guide also available upon your request with extra cost.)", "All meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) in Bhutan", "Breakfast in Nepal", "All accommodation as per your choice (Luxury/5-star or 4-star hotel or 3-star hotel)", "Monuments entrance/admission fees", "Guide and driver’s meals and accommodation", "Service Charge (the planning, handling, operational and communication charges) & government taxes.", "Handle your flight ticket (Kathmandu/Bangkok/New Delhi/Kolkata/Singapore/Dhaka/Singapore to Paro(Bhutan))"], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "5 nights in Nepal with Pokhara, 5 nights in Bhutan with Pobhjikha", "trip_highlights": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kathmandu sightseeing including UNESCO World Heritage Sites (Durbar Squares, Boudhanath, Swayambhunath, Pashupatinath)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Phenomenal Sunrise View from Sarangkot</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pokhara Sightseeing (Lakeside View, Davis Fall, Phewa Lake Boating, etc.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit stunning landmarks such as Tashichho Dzong, Memorial Chorten, Great Buddha Dordenma, etc. in Thimphu.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>An option to visit a village and a farmhouse for lunch/dinner</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Overnight at Phobjikha</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Cherish the fabulous views of mountain ranges from Dochu La Pass</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Punakha Sightseeing (Chhimi Lakhang Temple, Punakha Dzong, Kham Sum Yuley Lhakhang)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit Paro Dzong (Fortress), Old Paro Town, and enjoy the traditional Archery game in Paro</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hike to the popular Tiger’s Nest Monastery</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "trip_type_level": "Private Tour", "meta_description": "Cherished memories of a lifetime during the Nepal Bhutan Tour 10 nights 11 days by exploring phenomenal cultural and natural landmarks.", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "", "best_season": "", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": ""}, "trip_highlights_title": "Including Kathmandu, Bhaktapur, Patan & Pokhara | Thimphu, Punakha, Pobhjikha & Paro with Taktsang Monastery Hike"}	2024-01-03 11:08:53+00	2024-08-18 11:06:17+01
226	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "1", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy"}, "meta": {"_edit_last": "5", "_edit_lock": "1706856822:5", "_dp_original": "806", "_thumbnail_id": "4541", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "1", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Bhutan Helicopter Tour", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "47", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Bhutan Helicopter Tour is the perfect way to enjoy the true beauty and experience the diverse geography of this wonderful mountainous nation.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Easy", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "bhutan-helicopter-tour", "tags": [], "title": "Bhutan Helicopter Tour", "duration": "1 Day", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "<strong>The Bhutan Helicopter Tour</strong> is the perfect way to enjoy the true beauty and experience the diverse geography of this wonderful mountainous nation. Helicopter tours here started over half a decade ago on the auspicious occasion of the 60th birthday of the fourth king of Bhutan, His Highness Jigme Singye Wangchuck. In this short time, there have been about a dozen or more fantastic trips all over the country worthy of your time each with different majestic qualities.\\r\\n<h3>Why choose Bhutan Helicopter tour over regular tours in Bhutan</h3>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>For discovering some fantastic destinations in Bhutan that were only reachable through long and hard trekking.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>To save time and effort of the lengthy journey on-road or bus with this alternative.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>From the helicopter tour you can admire the natural beauty of this nation better in a new way.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>A helicopter tour is an ideal way of capping your Bhutan holiday. It introduces a different chapter to your journey of this magical land</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Almost 40% of Bhutan is still not connected with proper roadways so, a Helicopter tour might be your only option to witness the hidden delights here.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>One of the main attractions of any helicopter tour here is the adventure and thrill of glancing at the Himalayas from the air.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you have never done a helicopter/flight tour, Helicopter tours of Bhutan are a great way of experiencing all first-hand.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>In some manner Helicopter tours are comparatively affordable to reach and explore the sites here in comparison to conventional tours.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Different Helicopter Tours Available for Travelers in Bhutan</h3>\\r\\nBhutan has some of the most amazing and underrated tours for travelers. There are many more to be added and selections will be from large as we head further down this decade. Right from the Paro International Airport, there are a few absolute must-do tours that you can enjoy on a vacation.\\r\\n\\r\\nApart from these, a few recent additions are here specializing in the natural and cultural beauty of Bhutan too. At the end of the day, you will be amazed at how much this small nation has within itself, and once might not just be enough. Having said that, here are our top picks that never fail to impress you during the Bhutan Helicopter tour that you can choose from.\\r\\n<h4>Discover Paro Taktsang Tour (30 minutes)</h4>\\r\\nDiscover Paro Tour is one of the short helicopter tours highlighting the first glance overview of Bhutan with Paro Valley at its center. Most tours in Bhutan start from landing in Paro but the city is less explored in comparison to other places. By land, it might take a few days and that might affect your itinerary. However, Paro is beautiful enough and you are set to miss a lot while you are in Bhutan if Paro is not included. This Discover Paro Taktsang tour is perfect for anyone with a couple of hours to spare at the start or end of their Bhutan Holiday.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Easy take-off with minimal time loss from the Paro International Airport.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Close view of the traditional houses, rice fields, and farmlands of Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pa Chhu River, hills, and Landscape views of Paro Valley.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Paro Taktsang Monastery, the iconic landmark of Bhutan alongside other beautiful heritage sites like Ta Dzong, Rinpung Dzong, Kyichu Lhakhang, and Drugyel Dzong</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Clear views of Mount Jomolhari and the sub-ranges from the sky.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Short and effective tour to introduce Bhutan to travelers.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>Mt. Jomolhari Helicopter Tour (an hour’s worth of snow-covered delight)</h4>\\r\\nMt. Jomolhari helicopter tour is one of the best helicopter tours in the Himalayas taking travelers close to the Jomolhari Peak (7320 m). The tour starts from the beautiful Paro Valley showcasing the natural and cultural attractions here first. Heading higher to the snow-covered peaks, the natural components take over the tour with some magnificent views and sceneries. A short stop at the Jangothang Base camp here will be memorable for anyone here. Choose the perfect alternative to the 11-day Jomolhari trek as the amazing Mt.Jomolhari Helicopter Tour.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flight close to the majestic Mount Jomolhari (7320 m), the second-highest mountain yet to be climbed in the world.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>A brief pitstop at the base camp of Jomolhari and the opportunity to take some pictures from close.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Trail experience and reach the primary destination of the popular Jomolhari trek in an hour and back.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Other interesting cultural and natural attractions of Paro valley including the Taktsang Monastery (Tigers Nest).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Wonderful mountain experience in the Eastern Himalayas. Also, some wonderful other peaks are visible in clear weather from this Helicopter tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>An hour’s worth of high-elevation Natural exploration in Bhutan with a proper adventure ride.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>Magnificent Round Himalayan Tour (2 hours of Helicopter ride near the major Mountains)</h4>\\r\\nNow for someone who wants to have a complete mountain experience in the Northern end of Bhutan, our two-hour round Himalayan tour fulfills your desire. Add everything starting from Paro to Mount Jumolhari for the first half of the tour. Extending further you can have a closer look at Jichu Drakey Mountain. It is often said to be the most picturesque mountain in Bhutan with a double summit. The return flight is even more interesting here, after the full mountain experience as you fly over the historic Lingzhi Yugyal Dzong.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Complete Himalayan Experience from Paro, and one of the best to choose for beginners.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Mount Jomolhari and Mount Jichu Drakey among several other fantastic snow-covered peaks throughout the tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flying over the beautiful Lingzhi Yugyal Dzong located at an elevation of 4150 meters. This fortress celebrates the victory of Bhutanese troops over Tibet in 1667.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ideal for anyone willing to know more about the landscapes and geography of Bhutan from a flight.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Natural sceneries are among the most beautiful that Bhutan has to offer with several bonus wonders.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Taktsang Monastery, Rinpung, and Ta Dzong as well as Kyichu Lakhang as the cultural standouts in the Round Himalayan Tour.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>Dagala Couple Tour (30 minutes highlighting Thimphu, mountains, and more)</h4>\\r\\nDagala is hands down among one of the most naturally-gifted places on Earth. Thousands of pristine crystal clear mountain lakes decorate the land hidden in mountains. A popular trekking destination to the South of Paro Valley, this piece of Shangri La is now accessible through a helicopter. Dagala Couple Helicopter Tour is a lovely and romantic tour for couples to explore the wonderful lakes of Dagala within a short flight. The mind-blowing sceneries, lakes, and mountain views together with some bits of Thimphu make the Dagala Couple Tour one of the best value Helicopter tours that Bhutan has offered.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Over a thousand small and big crystal clear lakes in the main destination of this tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>On the way to Dagala, close view of several small villages of Bhutan. It gives the perspective of the rural lifestyle in the Bhutanese highlands.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Stunning Mountains including Mt. Jumolhari, Mt. Jichu Drake, Mt. Tsherimgang, Mt. Masagang, and Tiger Mountain, with even Mount Kanchenjunga on clear weather.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Buddha Dordenma at Kuensel Phodrang and Talakha Gompa add some cultural touches to the tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>A panoramic view of Thimpu City and beyond from the Dagala Couple Helicopter Tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>One of the best natural experiences in Bhutan within 30 minutes is available through this Helicopter Tour.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>SnowMan Trek helicopter tour (3 hours covering about 30 days’ worth of trekking trail in Bhutan)</h4>\\r\\nSnowman trek is amongst the longest and most challenging treks in Bhutan. It takes anywhere from 25-30 days for a normal person to complete the tour. Our Snowman Trek Helicopter tour makes it possible within 3 hours to cover every major component of the trek and more. This Helicopter Tour takes you deep into the Himalayas and showcases some of the magical components of the wilderness here. For photographers, this helicopter tour is a must-do with some fantastic sceneries, mountains, and natural landmarks guaranteed at each moment here.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>A well-formulated helicopter tour covering the major components of the popular SnowMan trek in Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Within 3 hours you will go over the trail, challenges, settlements, and other adventures offered by the SnowMan trekking trail.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ideal for trekkers who have decided to do the trek. The SnowMan Trek helicopter tour will allow you to get familiar with the geography, altitude, and trail conditions you will cover in about a month.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Sublime views of Mt. Jumolhari, Mt. Jichu Drake, Mt. Tsherimgang, Mt. Masagang, and Tiger Mountain from close.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Laya, Lingzhi, and Lunana villages showcasing the culture and lifestyle of locals in rural Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Punakha Dzong, Gasa Tongmon Dzong, Lingzhi Yugyal Dzong, and Bumthang Valley are among the other main attractions of the SnowMan trek helicopter Tour.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>Hidden Lake Tour (35-minute tour to the Bumthang Valley and Hidden Lake of Gomthang)</h4>\\r\\nThe Hidden Lake tour is among the newest addition to the list of nature-based Helicopter tours in Bhutan. Starting from Bhumthang Airport this flight first displays the wonderful Bumthang valley before heading north towards Dhur Tsachu. Known for the hot springs and landscape views, from Dhur Tsachu the helicopter lands at the elusive hidden lake in the middle of nowhere here.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>A flight to the lovely hidden glacier lake near Bumthang with spiritual local beliefs.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Magnificent views of the mountains and landscape including Gangkhar Puensum (7570 m), the highest peak of Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bumthang and Chamkhar Valley Heli exploration with a birds-eye view of the major components here.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>A refreshing tour in one of the underrated destinations in Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Opportunity to see and experience a different side of Bhutan before and after the tour in Bumthang.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>Traditional Textile Heli Tour (50 minutes of culture and art-rich tour)</h4>\\r\\nTraditional Textile Heli tour is one of the best culture-based helicopter tours from Bumthang Airport in Bhutan. The art of weaving is closer to the Bhutanese locals than you can imagine. At any instant, after entering this country you can witness different unique articles of clothing and textiles made in local factories. This tour takes you over some wonderful destinations and monuments to the traditional Khoma Village. Known for its intricately patterned silk textile (hence the name) this village will give you a closer look at Bhutanese art, culture, and lifestyle.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Scenic flight from Bumthang to Lhuntse region over the beautiful Lhuntse Rinchentse Dzong near Kuri Chhu.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Wonderful view of natural wonders and landscape from start to finish of the tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>In Takila one can view the World’s Tallest Guru Nangsey Ziloen statue (157 feet).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>One can buy ‘Gho’ and ‘Kira’ for themselves which is the traditional dress of Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Interaction with the locals and understanding the Textile industry in Khoma Village.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>Merak- Sakteng Tour (about 2 hours ride to the easternmost tip of Bhutan)</h4>\\r\\nMerak- Sakteng Tour takes you to the easternmost ends of Bhutan through this two-hour-long round flight. Travelers here can glance at some of the untouched vegetation, geography, and nature in this tour. Similarly, the Sakteng Wildlife Sanctuary also offers amazing interaction opportunities with the wildlife and birds of East Bhutan. Merak and Sakteng villages here will be unique as the highlands lie close to the Indian border.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fantastic views of the landscape and beyond on the Trashigang Dzongkhag of Eastern Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Exotic flight over numerous beautiful valleys and riverbeds to reach Merak and Sakteng.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Wildlife and natural experience in the Sakteng Wildlife Sanctuary.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Village and lifestyle tours of the Sakteng and Merak villages here.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>Royal Manas Wildlife Tour (1.5 hours of the tour to five beautiful national parks in Bhutan)</h4>\\r\\nIf you are looking for a complete natural tour in Bhutan covering all the major national parks and sanctuaries in Bhutan, the Royal Manas Wildlife Tour is just for you. This tour is often considered the king of natural tours in Bhutan. Within a 90-minute flight, you can have an overall Bhutan tour centering on the Royal Manas Wildlife Park.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Royal Manas wildlife park tour connected by Jigme Singye Wangchuck NP (Northwest), Phibsoo Wildlife Sanctuary (Southwest), Phrumsengla NP (North), and Jomotshangkha Wildlife Sanctuary (southeast) through wildlife corridors.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Opportunities to encounter and witness different varieties of flora and fauna from this brief helicopter tour.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Combining normal tours with Bhutan Helicopter tour</h3>\\r\\nOne of the most common ways that people do these helicopter tours is by combining them with several other tours in Bhutan. Similarly, these can also be added separately in the Bhutan segment of any multi-country tour in Asia. Here are our top recommendations if you like to combine these amazing Bhutan Helicopter tours with your vacation in Asia.\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://asiaexperiences.com/nepal-tibet-bhutan-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Nepal Tibet Bhutan Tour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-tour/\\">Bhutan Short Tour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://asiaexperiences.com/luxury-trips-nepal-tibet-bhutan/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Luxury Nepal Tibet Bhutan trip</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://asiaexperiences.com/buddhist-pilgrimage-tour-nepal-tibet-bhutan-india/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Buddhist Pilgrimage Tour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-bhutan-tour/\\">Bhutan Nepal Combined Multi-Day Tour</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<h3>Why Choose Everest Vacation for Bhutan Helicopter Tour</h3>\\r\\nEverest Vacation is one of your options for selecting to do any helicopter tour in Bhutan. What makes us different is our tenacity to seek top-quality and safe tours for any travelers associated with us. Apart from the obvious here are a few reasons why you should consider us for your next Bhutan Helicopter tour:-\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>We operate our tours throughout Asia. It gives you the freedom to add other destinations to the Bhutan Helicopter Tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Booking and Payment are easy with us and we are flexible to provide services on your time.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Personal guides will be provided to you for any kind of tour specializing in the category of your vacation.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We provide the best value for your money with a high level of transparency and no hidden charges.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>You can ask or meet our exerts even before selecting the tour for a more complete experience.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We provide complete travel services helping you with ticketing, travel, permits, travel visas, and more.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Our traveler help services will help you with any problems and inquiries 24*7.</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, "taxonomy": {}, "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/heli-bhutan-e1665999804276-1536x937-1.jpg", "title": "heli-bhutan-e1665999804276-1536x937", "altText": "heli-bhutan-e1665999804276-1536x937", "caption": "heli-bhutan-e1665999804276-1536x937", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["802", "801", "799", "798", "744", "757", "797"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "ws_trip_faqs_lists": "", "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "_ws_trip_faqs_lists": "field_63ede38e351c7", "ws_block_attractions": "", "ws_block_best_season": "Any Season", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-light", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": " Overview", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc6695edb31", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_c