lear weather.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Buddha Dordenma at Kuensel Phodrang and Talakha Gompa add some cultural touches to the tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>A panoramic view of Thimpu City and beyond from the Dagala Couple Helicopter Tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>One of the best natural experiences in Bhutan within 30 minutes is available through this Helicopter Tour.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>SnowMan Trek helicopter tour (3 hours covering about 30 days’ worth of trekking trail in Bhutan)</h4>\\r\\nSnowman trek is amongst the longest and most challenging treks in Bhutan. It takes anywhere from 25-30 days for a normal person to complete the tour. Our Snowman Trek Helicopter tour makes it possible within 3 hours to cover every major component of the trek and more. This Helicopter Tour takes you deep into the Himalayas and showcases some of the magical components of the wilderness here. For photographers, this helicopter tour is a must-do with some fantastic sceneries, mountains, and natural landmarks guaranteed at each moment here.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>A well-formulated helicopter tour covering the major components of the popular SnowMan trek in Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Within 3 hours you will go over the trail, challenges, settlements, and other adventures offered by the SnowMan trekking trail.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Ideal for trekkers who have decided to do the trek. The SnowMan Trek helicopter tour will allow you to get familiar with the geography, altitude, and trail conditions you will cover in about a month.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Sublime views of Mt. Jumolhari, Mt. Jichu Drake, Mt. Tsherimgang, Mt. Masagang, and Tiger Mountain from close.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Laya, Lingzhi, and Lunana villages showcasing the culture and lifestyle of locals in rural Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Punakha Dzong, Gasa Tongmon Dzong, Lingzhi Yugyal Dzong, and Bumthang Valley are among the other main attractions of the SnowMan trek helicopter Tour.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>Hidden Lake Tour (35-minute tour to the Bumthang Valley and Hidden Lake of Gomthang)</h4>\\r\\nThe Hidden Lake tour is among the newest addition to the list of nature-based Helicopter tours in Bhutan. Starting from Bhumthang Airport this flight first displays the wonderful Bumthang valley before heading north towards Dhur Tsachu. Known for the hot springs and landscape views, from Dhur Tsachu the helicopter lands at the elusive hidden lake in the middle of nowhere here.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>A flight to the lovely hidden glacier lake near Bumthang with spiritual local beliefs.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Magnificent views of the mountains and landscape including Gangkhar Puensum (7570 m), the highest peak of Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bumthang and Chamkhar Valley Heli exploration with a birds-eye view of the major components here.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>A refreshing tour in one of the underrated destinations in Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Opportunity to see and experience a different side of Bhutan before and after the tour in Bumthang.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>Traditional Textile Heli Tour (50 minutes of culture and art-rich tour)</h4>\\r\\nTraditional Textile Heli tour is one of the best culture-based helicopter tours from Bumthang Airport in Bhutan. The art of weaving is closer to the Bhutanese locals than you can imagine. At any instant, after entering this country you can witness different unique articles of clothing and textiles made in local factories. This tour takes you over some wonderful destinations and monuments to the traditional Khoma Village. Known for its intricately patterned silk textile (hence the name) this village will give you a closer look at Bhutanese art, culture, and lifestyle.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Scenic flight from Bumthang to Lhuntse region over the beautiful Lhuntse Rinchentse Dzong near Kuri Chhu.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Wonderful view of natural wonders and landscape from start to finish of the tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>In Takila one can view the World’s Tallest Guru Nangsey Ziloen statue (157 feet).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>One can buy ‘Gho’ and ‘Kira’ for themselves which is the traditional dress of Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Interaction with the locals and understanding the Textile industry in Khoma Village.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>Merak- Sakteng Tour (about 2 hours ride to the easternmost tip of Bhutan)</h4>\\r\\nMerak- Sakteng Tour takes you to the easternmost ends of Bhutan through this two-hour-long round flight. Travelers here can glance at some of the untouched vegetation, geography, and nature in this tour. Similarly, the Sakteng Wildlife Sanctuary also offers amazing interaction opportunities with the wildlife and birds of East Bhutan. Merak and Sakteng villages here will be unique as the highlands lie close to the Indian border.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Fantastic views of the landscape and beyond on the Trashigang Dzongkhag of Eastern Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Exotic flight over numerous beautiful valleys and riverbeds to reach Merak and Sakteng.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Wildlife and natural experience in the Sakteng Wildlife Sanctuary.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Village and lifestyle tours of the Sakteng and Merak villages here.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h4>Royal Manas Wildlife Tour (1.5 hours of the tour to five beautiful national parks in Bhutan)</h4>\\r\\nIf you are looking for a complete natural tour in Bhutan covering all the major national parks and sanctuaries in Bhutan, the Royal Manas Wildlife Tour is just for you. This tour is often considered the king of natural tours in Bhutan. Within a 90-minute flight, you can have an overall Bhutan tour centering on the Royal Manas Wildlife Park.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Main Attractions</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Royal Manas wildlife park tour connected by Jigme Singye Wangchuck NP (Northwest), Phibsoo Wildlife Sanctuary (Southwest), Phrumsengla NP (North), and Jomotshangkha Wildlife Sanctuary (southeast) through wildlife corridors.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Opportunities to encounter and witness different varieties of flora and fauna from this brief helicopter tour.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<h3>Combining normal tours with Bhutan Helicopter tour</h3>\\r\\nOne of the most common ways that people do these helicopter tours is by combining them with several other tours in Bhutan. Similarly, these can also be added separately in the Bhutan segment of any multi-country tour in Asia. Here are our top recommendations if you like to combine these amazing Bhutan Helicopter tours with your vacation in Asia.\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://asiaexperiences.com/nepal-tibet-bhutan-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Nepal Tibet Bhutan Tour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-tour/\\">Bhutan Short Tour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://asiaexperiences.com/luxury-trips-nepal-tibet-bhutan/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Luxury Nepal Tibet Bhutan trip</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://asiaexperiences.com/buddhist-pilgrimage-tour-nepal-tibet-bhutan-india/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Buddhist Pilgrimage Tour</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-bhutan-tour/\\">Bhutan Nepal Combined Multi-Day Tour</a></li>\\r\\n</ol>\\r\\n<h3>Why Choose Everest Vacation for Bhutan Helicopter Tour</h3>\\r\\nEverest Vacation is one of your options for selecting to do any helicopter tour in Bhutan. What makes us different is our tenacity to seek top-quality and safe tours for any travelers associated with us. Apart from the obvious here are a few reasons why you should consider us for your next Bhutan Helicopter tour:-\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>We operate our tours throughout Asia. It gives you the freedom to add other destinations to the Bhutan Helicopter Tour.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Booking and Payment are easy with us and we are flexible to provide services on your time.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Personal guides will be provided to you for any kind of tour specializing in the category of your vacation.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We provide the best value for your money with a high level of transparency and no hidden charges.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>You can ask or meet our exerts even before selecting the tour for a more complete experience.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We provide complete travel services helping you with ticketing, travel, permits, travel visas, and more.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Our traveler help services will help you with any problems and inquiries 24*7.</li>\\r\\n</ul>"}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Car/van transportation to and from the domestic airport and hotel.", "Escorting guide for this flight.", "Private helicopter."], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Car/van transportation to and from the domestic airport and hotel.", "Escorting guide for this flight.", "Private helicopter."], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "Explore Bhutan Helicopter Tour with Everest Vacation.", "trip_highlights": "<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info first_para\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\"card-header facts\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\"row\\">\\r\\n<div class=\\"col-lg-12 info\\">Discover Paro Taktsang Tour, Mt. Jomolhari Helicopter Tour, Magnificent Round Himalayan Tour, Dagala Couple Tour, Snowman helicopter tour, Hidden Lake Tour, Merak- Sakteng Tour</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>", "trip_type_level": "Easy", "meta_description": "Bhutan Helicopter Tour is the perfect way to enjoy the true beauty and experience the diverse geography of this wonderful mountainous nation.", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "faq_section_title": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": "AC Luxury Car/Hiace"}, "trip_transportations": "AC Luxury Car/Hiace", "trip_highlights_title": "What's included?"}	2024-01-04 05:08:43+00	2024-02-02 06:53:41+00
227	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "230", "ws_short_desc": "", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "5", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Short and Easy"}, "meta": {"_edit_last": "5", "_edit_lock": "1707375743:5", "_dp_original": "882", "_thumbnail_id": "4324", "ws_sale_price": "230", "ws_short_desc": "", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "5", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "Ghorepani Poonhill Ghandruk Trek", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Ghorepani Poonhill Ghandruk Trek", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "47", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Ghorepani Poonhill Ghandruk trek in the Annapurna region attracts travelers with pleasant scenery and beautiful sunrise over snowy mountains.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Short and Easy", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "ghorepani-poonhill-ghandruk-trek", "tags": [], "title": "Ghorepani Poonhill Ghandruk Trek ", "duration": "5 Days", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "Everest Vacation has designed a pleasant 7 days Ghorepani Poonhill trek that is suitable for all age groups trekkers. This trek takes the trekkers to the beautiful Magar settlements in Ghorepani (2,874m). A short hike to Poon Hill for a sunrise view over snow-capped Annapurna Ranges, <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machapuchare\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Machhapuchhre</a>, and other peaks is mesmerizing. Traverse through lush forest admiring the surrounding beauty and mountains. This package is a perfect blend of natural beauty and cultural immersion in the beautiful Annapurna region.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 1:</strong> Drive to Nayapul. Trek to Ulleri.\\r\\n<strong>Day 2:</strong> Trek to Ghorepani. Explore around Ghorepani.\\r\\n<strong>Day 3:</strong> Early morning climb Poon Hill then Trek to the Tadapani\\r\\n<strong>Day 4:</strong> Trek to Ghandruk and explore the Gurung village and Cultural\\r\\n<strong>Day 5:</strong> Trek to Nayapul and Drive to Pokhara"}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Drive to Nayapul from Kathmandu or Pokhara and Trek to Tikhedunga – Ulleri (village)", "richText": "The starting point of the <strong>Annapurna short trek</strong> is Nayapul. If you are in Pokhara, it’s only a short drive of an hour to reach here. From Kathmandu, you will take a hill highway drive of 6-7 hours to reach Nayapul.\\r\\n\\r\\nSimilarly, from Kathmandu, you can also take a domestic flight and then take the drive to Nayapul. On the first day of the trek, we will have a shorter walking session passing by multiple hill settlements of the area. You can stop in one of the many teahouses on the way and try some local snacks. You will cross the suspension bridge over Tikedhunga Khola which then leads us to a steep trail to the village of Tikedhunga. Nearing the village of Ulleri, we can have some great views of <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Annapurna_Massif\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Mt. Annapurna south (7219m.) and Hiunchuli (6441m)</a>.\\r\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Ulleri.\\r\\n<em>(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)</em>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 2, "meal": "", "title": "Trek to Ghorepani. Explore around Ghorepani", "richText": "The trek from <strong>Ulleri to Ghorepani</strong> shows us the art of living, farming, and agriculture in the hills of Nepal. The trek is relaxed, and most of the time we will have a gradual ascend through different types of Forest. From this segment of our route, we can spot many wildflowers and beautiful birds found around here. We will pass by small settlements and rest there for a while enjoying the view of nature surrounding us. In a clear sky, you can view snow-capped mountains behind the green hills.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter trekking for about 7 hours, you will reach the <strong>Ghorepani village</strong> in the late afternoon. Ghorepani is one of the major villages of the Annapurna region. It is here that most of the trails linking to the other villages and the regions (including ABC and circuit) diverge. With a brief village tour here, we can witness a lot about the local lifestyle and culture.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at a lodge in Ghorepani.\\r\\n<em>(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)</em>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 3, "meal": "", "title": "Early morning climb Poon Hill then Trek to the Tadapani", "richText": "We will start our day early as our first goal today is to Hike up to Poon-Hill for the sunrise view. <strong>Poon hill</strong> is about an hour of walking from Ghorepani village. <strong>Poonhill</strong> is one of the best places to view the Annapurna range and the surrounding Himalayas in Nepal. The rays of the sun will treat us with majestic views of Annapurna South, Nilgiri, Dhaulagiri ranges, Tukuche peak, BahariShikhar, Hiuchuli, Annapurna I, II, III, IV, Lamjung Himal, Machhapuchhre (Fishtail), Mt.Manaslu ranges, and many other mountains. We will spend some time here and return to the Ghorepani village for breakfast.\\r\\n\\r\\nOur trek continues from here to the village of <strong>Tadapani</strong>. The first section of the trail is a bit steep and goes through the Deurali pass. This pass is almost a similar height to that of Poonhill, and we can get a <strong>beautiful landscape view touching the horizon from here</strong>. We will then descend gradually and pass multiple settlements to reach the village of Tadapani.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at a lodge in Tadapani.\\r\\n<em>(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)</em>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 4, "meal": "", "title": "Trek to Ghandruk and explore the Gurung village and Cultural", "richText": "We will have a comparatively shorter trek today giving us enough time to stop and admire the nature in the way. Our destination for today is the <a href=\\"http://ecs.com.np/features/ghandrukland-of-the-gurungs\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Gurung village of Ghandruk</a>. The trail descends gradually and passes through rhododendron forests to reach Ghandruk. Nearing the village we can spot terraced farmlands and Animal sheds.\\r\\n\\r\\n<a href=\\"https://wikitravel.org/en/Ghandruk\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"><strong>Ghandruk</strong></a> is about 3 hours of walk from Tadapani. The compact and close Gurung community is one of the most culturally rich settlements of the Annapurna region. After reaching the village, we can go for a brief visit around. The Gurung Museum here showcases some of the traditional art, culture, lifestyle, and attire of the people living in the village. We can try some of the local organic products alongside the mesmerizing view available from the village.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at a lodge in Ghandruk.\\r\\n<em>(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)</em>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 5, "meal": "", "title": "Trek to Nayapul and Drive to Pokhara or Kathmandu", "richText": "For the last stretch of our short Annapurna trek, we will walk past hilly settlements beside the Modi Khola to reach Nayapul with around a 5-hour hike. After reaching Nayapul, you can either drive to <strong>Pokhara </strong>or<strong> Kathmandu</strong> from here. With some great memories and majestic Himalayan scenery to bring back with you, this short trek highlighting the best bits of the Annapurna region terminates today. The Everest Vacation team will stay connected for your valuable suggestions and feedback.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/enjoyed-with-annapurna-range.jpeg", "title": "enjoyed with annapurna range", "altText": "enjoyed with annapurna range", "caption": "enjoyed with annapurna range", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": "", "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "ws_block_attractions": "Ghorepani , Poonhill", "ws_block_best_season": "All season", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-light", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "3210m", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": "Overview", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc6695edb31", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_block_transportation": "Private AC Vehicle", "ws_trip_galleries_title": "Photo/Visual Gallery", "_ws_block_transportation": "field_63eeee74072de", "_ws_trip_galleries_title": "field_63ec89128acaa", "starter_kit_padding_type": "p-medium", "ws_trip_block_highlights": "", "ws_trip_information_list": 1, "_starter_kit_padding_type": "field_5f8584c998bc2", "_ws_trip_block_highlights": "field_63ec73a6a0d8f", "_ws_trip_information_list": "field_63ec90a574f02", "starter_kit_section_title": "Day by Day Activities", "_starter_kit_section_title": "field_63ec948c94a16", "starter_kit_enable_section": "1", "_starter_kit_enable_section": "field_63edeb1c7635c", "starter_kit_section_padding": "", "ws_trip_include_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Internal Flight: Kathmandu to Lukla to Kathmandu for Everest Trek</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Private/Public vehicle from Kathmandu/Pokhara to Nayapul for Annapurna Trek</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Trekking Permit for your related trip</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Trekkers’ Information Management system (TIMS) card</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Professional English speaking guide with porter, 2 trekkers for 1 porter (1 porter carries 20-25 kilograms of luggage)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Salary, food, accommodation and Insurance &amp; equipment for guide &amp; porter.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>All meals three times a day (breakfast, lunch and dinner) during the trek</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Accommodation in teahouses (lodges) or Luxury Hotels for high-end travelers during the trek</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_starter_kit_section_padding": "field_5f3e0f86a2634", "_ws_trip_include_description": "field_63edd6a337cd0", "ws_trip_overview_description": "Everest Vacation has designed a pleasant 7 days Ghorepani Poonhill trek that is suitable for all age groups trekkers. This trek takes the trekkers to the beautiful Magar settlements in Ghorepani (2,874m). A short hike to Poon Hill for a sunrise view over snow-capped Annapurna Ranges, <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machapuchare\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Machhapuchhre</a>, and other peaks is mesmerizing. Traverse through lush forest admiring the surrounding beauty and mountains. This package is a perfect blend of natural beauty and cultural immersion in the beautiful Annapurna region.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Day 1:</strong> Drive to Nayapul. Trek to Ulleri.\\r\\n<strong>Day 2:</strong> Trek to Ghorepani. Explore around Ghorepani.\\r\\n<strong>Day 3:</strong> Early morning climb Poon Hill then Trek to the Tadapani\\r\\n<strong>Day 4:</strong> Trek to Ghandruk and explore the Gurung village and Cultural\\r\\n<strong>Day 5:</strong> Trek to Nayapul and Drive to Pokhara", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "", "_ws_trip_fact_short_description": "field_63ec73a69d305", "ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "01", "ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "02", "ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "03", "ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "04", "ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "05", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "Drive to Nayapul from Kathmandu or Pokhara and Trek to Tikhedunga – Ulleri (village)", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "Trek to Ghorepani. Explore around Ghorepani", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "Early morning climb Poon Hill then Trek to the Tadapani", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "Trek to Ghandruk and explore the Gurung village and Cultural", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title": "Trek to Nayapul and Drive to Pokhara or Kathmandu", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "Extended Tours", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_title": "field_63ec91180462f", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "The starting point of the <strong>Annapurna short trek</strong> is Nayapul. If you are in Pokhara, it’s only a short drive of an hour to reach here. From Kathmandu, you will take a hill highway drive of 6-7 hours to reach Nayapul.\\r\\n\\r\\nSimilarly, from Kathmandu, you can also take a domestic flight and then take the drive to Nayapul. On the first day of the trek, we will have a shorter walking session passing by multiple hill settlements of the area. You can stop in one of the many teahouses on the way and try some local snacks. You will cross the suspension bridge over Tikedhunga Khola which then leads us to a steep trail to the village of Tikedhunga. Nearing the village of Ulleri, we can have some great views of <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Annapurna_Massif\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Mt. Annapurna south (7219m.) and Hiunchuli (6441m)</a>.\\r\\nOvernight at a Lodge in Ulleri.\\r\\n<em>(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)</em>", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "The trek from <strong>Ulleri to Ghorepani</strong> shows us the art of living, farming, and agriculture in the hills of Nepal. The trek is relaxed, and most of the time we will have a gradual ascend through different types of Forest. From this segment of our route, we can spot many wildflowers and beautiful birds found around here. We will pass by small settlements and rest there for a while enjoying the view of nature surrounding us. In a clear sky, you can view snow-capped mountains behind the green hills.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter trekking for about 7 hours, you will reach the <strong>Ghorepani village</strong> in the late afternoon. Ghorepani is one of the major villages of the Annapurna region. It is here that most of the trails linking to the other villages and the regions (including ABC and circuit) diverge. With a brief village tour here, we can witness a lot about the local lifestyle and culture.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at a lodge in Ghorepani.\\r\\n<em>(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)</em>", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "We will start our day early as our first goal today is to Hike up to Poon-Hill for the sunrise view. <strong>Poon hill</strong> is about an hour of walking from Ghorepani village. <strong>Poonhill</strong> is one of the best places to view the Annapurna range and the surrounding Himalayas in Nepal. The rays of the sun will treat us with majestic views of Annapurna South, Nilgiri, Dhaulagiri ranges, Tukuche peak, BahariShikhar, Hiuchuli, Annapurna I, II, III, IV, Lamjung Himal, Machhapuchhre (Fishtail), Mt.Manaslu ranges, and many other mountains. We will spend some time here and return to the Ghorepani village for breakfast.\\r\\n\\r\\nOur trek continues from here to the village of <strong>Tadapani</strong>. The first section of the trail is a bit steep and goes through the Deurali pass. This pass is almost a similar height to that of Poonhill, and we can get a <strong>beautiful landscape view touching the horizon from here</strong>. We will then descend gradually and pass multiple settlements to reach the village of Tadapani.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at a lodge in Tadapani.\\r\\n<em>(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)</em>", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "We will have a comparatively shorter trek today giving us enough time to stop and admire the nature in the way. Our destination for today is the <a href=\\"http://ecs.com.np/features/ghandrukland-of-the-gurungs\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\">Gurung village of Ghandruk</a>. The trail descends gradually and passes through rhododendron forests to reach Ghandruk. Nearing the village we can spot terraced farmlands and Animal sheds.\\r\\n\\r\\n<a href=\\"https://wikitravel.org/en/Ghandruk\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener noreferrer\\"><strong>Ghandruk</strong></a> is about 3 hours of walk from Tadapani. The compact and close Gurung community is one of the most culturally rich settlements of the Annapurna region. After reaching the village, we can go for a brief visit around. The Gurung Museum here showcases some of the traditional art, culture, lifestyle, and attire of the people living in the village. We can try some of the local organic products alongside the mesmerizing view available from the village.\\r\\n\\r\\nOvernight at a lodge in Ghandruk.\\r\\n<em>(There are Luxury hotels for high-end travelers)</em>", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description": "For the last stretch of our short Annapurna trek, we will walk past hilly settlements beside the Modi Khola to reach Nayapul with around a 5-hour hike. After reaching Nayapul, you can either drive to <strong>Pokhara </strong>or<strong> Kathmandu</strong> from here. With some great memories and majestic Himalayan scenery to bring back with you, this short trek highlighting the best bits of the Annapurna region terminates today. The Everest Vacation team will stay connected for your valuable suggestions and feedback.", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/helicopter-tour-to-everest-base-camp/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Helicopter Tour to Everest Base Camp</a> - 4-5 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/mountain-flight-with-view-of-mt-everest/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Mountain Flight over Mt. Everest Area</a> - 1 hour</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-trekking/easy-hiking/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Short 1 Day Hiking around Kathmandu</a> - 4-6 hours</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu, Bhaktapur &amp; Patan Tour</a> - 2 days</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/4-days-kathmandu-nagarkot-hill-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Kathmandu Valley with Nagarkot Sunrise/Sunset Tour</a> - 4 days</li>\\r\\n</ol>", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_information_description": "field_63ec913e04630"}, "categoryId": null, "meta_title": "Ghorepani Poonhill Ghandruk Trek", "blogContent": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"3210m\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Ghorepani , Poonhill\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"All season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"Everest Vacation has designed a pleasant 7 days Ghorepani Poonhill trek that is suitable for all age groups trekkers. This trek takes the trekkers to the beautiful Magar settlements in Ghorepani (2,874m). A short hike to Poon Hill for a sunrise view over snow-capped Annapurna Ranges, \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machapuchare\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eMachhapuchhre\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e, and other peaks is mesmerizing. Traverse through lush forest admiring the surrounding beauty and mountains. This package is a perfect blend of natural beauty and cultural immersion in the beautiful Annapurna region.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 1:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Drive to Nayapul. Trek to Ulleri.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 2:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Trek to Ghorepani. Explore around Ghorepani.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 3:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Early morning climb Poon Hill then Trek to the Tadapani\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 4:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Trek to Ghandruk and explore the Gurung village and Cultural\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003cstrong\\\\u003eDay 5:\\\\u003c/strong\\\\u003e Trek to Nayapul and Drive to Pokhara\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63e