s avoid getting in this Eddie and whirlpool after a great time rafting completing on the bank of the river, after changing into dry clothes drive back to <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\">Kathmandu</a> after an exciting thrill of rafting in Trisuli River."], "description": "White Water Rafting in Nepal Himalayan glacial rivers with exciting floats through white waters forming enjoyable rapids, drops, and holes to make the adventure thrill with excitement in the world of water sports on <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trishuli_River\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Trisuli River</a> Rafting, the river is fed from the glaciers of Ganesh, Langtang and Jugal Himal range of mountains towards north central Himalayan region.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe adventure starts with 2-3 hours of drive to reach Trisuli River Rafting ‘put in point’ where our river guides will receive and then brief on safety procedure, and paddling technique and then board the inflatable raft putting on life jackets, and helmets for safety.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen float for a few hours through exciting rapids with a name like double-decker, monsoon, upset and surprise continue rafting with the last rapids of Bijili, S, and C bends with 2 types of whirlpools Tea Pot and Coffee Pot, where the rafters avoid getting in this Eddie and whirlpool after a great time rafting completing on the bank of the river, after changing into dry clothes drive back to <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/2-days-kathmandu-city-tour/\\">Kathmandu</a> after an exciting thrill of rafting in Trisuli River."}, {"id": "overview-2", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Bhote Kosi or Upper Sun Kosi River Rafting with Bungy Jumping", "content": ["Rafting in Nepal’s Himalayan glacial rivers with exciting floats through white waters forming enjoyable rapids, drops, and holes to make the adventure thrill with excitement in the world of water sports at <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhotekoshi_River\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Bhote Kosi River</a>. this is also known as Upper Sun Kosi, as this river joins further downstream at the main Sun Kosi River at Dolalghat village.\\r\\n\\r\\nBhote Kosi River Rafting, the river is fed from the glaciers of the massive Shisapangma Mountains which is wholly in Tibet, and from the glaciers of Jugal Himal and Bhairav Kund area towards the north central Himalayan region.\\r\\n\\r\\nAdventure starts with 2-3 hours of drive to reach Bhote Kosi ‘put in point’ near the border of Nepal and  Tibet. where our river guides will receive and then brief on safety procedures, and paddling techniques and then board the inflatable raft putting on life jackets, and helmets for safety.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen float for a few hours through exciting rapids, continue rafting with the last best rapids, and after a great time rafting completing on the bank of the river. After changing into dry clothes drive back to Last Resorts for another adventure and thrill of Bungy Jumping towards Bhote Kosi from the high bridge.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn Ultimate Bungy from ‘The Last Resort’ in Nepal the most spectacular Bungy Jump on this Planet. This remarkable 500 ft. /160m falls or drops into the Bhote Kosi River gorge near the Nepal/Tibet border, which is the longest Free-Fall in the world touching the tip surface of raging Bhote Kosi. After fun and thrill from rafting and Bungy jumping return to Kathmandu."], "description": "Rafting in Nepal’s Himalayan glacial rivers with exciting floats through white waters forming enjoyable rapids, drops, and holes to make the adventure thrill with excitement in the world of water sports at <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhotekoshi_River\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Bhote Kosi River</a>. this is also known as Upper Sun Kosi, as this river joins further downstream at the main Sun Kosi River at Dolalghat village.\\r\\n\\r\\nBhote Kosi River Rafting, the river is fed from the glaciers of the massive Shisapangma Mountains which is wholly in Tibet, and from the glaciers of Jugal Himal and Bhairav Kund area towards the north central Himalayan region.\\r\\n\\r\\nAdventure starts with 2-3 hours of drive to reach Bhote Kosi ‘put in point’ near the border of Nepal and  Tibet. where our river guides will receive and then brief on safety procedures, and paddling techniques and then board the inflatable raft putting on life jackets, and helmets for safety.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen float for a few hours through exciting rapids, continue rafting with the last best rapids, and after a great time rafting completing on the bank of the river. After changing into dry clothes drive back to Last Resorts for another adventure and thrill of Bungy Jumping towards Bhote Kosi from the high bridge.\\r\\n\\r\\nAn Ultimate Bungy from ‘The Last Resort’ in Nepal the most spectacular Bungy Jump on this Planet. This remarkable 500 ft. /160m falls or drops into the Bhote Kosi River gorge near the Nepal/Tibet border, which is the longest Free-Fall in the world touching the tip surface of raging Bhote Kosi. After fun and thrill from rafting and Bungy jumping return to Kathmandu."}, {"id": "overview-3", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Bhote Kosi or Upper Sun Kosi River Rafting", "content": ["Bhote Kosi or Upper Sun Kosi River Rafting in Nepal’s Himalayan glacial rivers with exciting floats through white waters forming enjoyable rapids, drops, and holes to make the adventure thrill with excitement in the world of water sports at Bhote Kosi River also known as Upper Sun Kosi, as this river joins further downstream at main <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunkoshi_River\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Sun Kosi</a> River at Dolalghat village.\\r\\n\\r\\nBhote Kosi River Rafting, the river is fed from the glaciers of the massive Shisapangma Mountains which are wholly in Tibet, and from the glaciers of Jugal Himal and Bhairav Kund area towards the north central Himalayan region.\\r\\n\\r\\nAdventure starts with 2-3 hours of drive to reach Bhote Kosi ‘put in point’ near the border of Nepal/ Tibet, where our river guides will receive and then brief on the safety procedure, and paddling technique and then board in the inflatable raft put on life jackets, helmets for safety.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen float for a few hours through exciting rapids, and continue rafting with the last best rapids, after a great time rafting on the bank of the river, after changing into dry clothes drive back to Kathmandu after an exciting thrill of rafting in Bhote Kosi River.\\r\\n\\r\\nDuring monsoon Rivers are very big and flooded. after September rivers are very regularly flowing and perfect for rafting. In winter low levels of water and it is not much fun to raft due to the cold water."], "description": "Bhote Kosi or Upper Sun Kosi River Rafting in Nepal’s Himalayan glacial rivers with exciting floats through white waters forming enjoyable rapids, drops, and holes to make the adventure thrill with excitement in the world of water sports at Bhote Kosi River also known as Upper Sun Kosi, as this river joins further downstream at main <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunkoshi_River\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Sun Kosi</a> River at Dolalghat village.\\r\\n\\r\\nBhote Kosi River Rafting, the river is fed from the glaciers of the massive Shisapangma Mountains which are wholly in Tibet, and from the glaciers of Jugal Himal and Bhairav Kund area towards the north central Himalayan region.\\r\\n\\r\\nAdventure starts with 2-3 hours of drive to reach Bhote Kosi ‘put in point’ near the border of Nepal/ Tibet, where our river guides will receive and then brief on the safety procedure, and paddling technique and then board in the inflatable raft put on life jackets, helmets for safety.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen float for a few hours through exciting rapids, and continue rafting with the last best rapids, after a great time rafting on the bank of the river, after changing into dry clothes drive back to Kathmandu after an exciting thrill of rafting in Bhote Kosi River.\\r\\n\\r\\nDuring monsoon Rivers are very big and flooded. after September rivers are very regularly flowing and perfect for rafting. In winter low levels of water and it is not much fun to raft due to the cold water."}, {"id": "overview-4", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Seti River a scenic and semi white water Rafting", "content": ["<strong>Seti River a scenic and semi white water Rafting in Nepal Himalayan is very famous.</strong> Glacial rivers with exciting floats through white waters form enjoyable rapids, drops, and holes to make the adventure thrill with excitement in the world of water sports at Seti.\\r\\n\\r\\n<a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seti_River\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Seti River</a> “the Milky River”, as this river starts with white color (from the chalk and limestone) originates from the glaciers of the massive range of Annapurna Himalaya including the majestic Machhapuchare peak (Fish Tail).  this river flows through Pokhara and joins further downstream making a wider Seti River at Damauli town.\\r\\n\\r\\nAdventure starts with 2 hours of drive to reach Damauli town from <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/cultural-scenic-tour-kathmandu-pokhara-chitwan-lumbini/\\">Pokhara city</a> to ‘put in point’ near at Mardi River. Our river guides will receive and then brief on safety procedure, and paddling technique and then board the inflatable raft putting on life jackets, and helmets for safety. Then float for a few hours through exciting rapids, and continue rafting with the last best rapids. After a great time rafting on the bank of the river, after changing into dry clothes drive back to Pokhara after the exciting thrill of rafting in the scenic Seti River."], "description": "<strong>Seti River a scenic and semi white water Rafting in Nepal Himalayan is very famous.</strong> Glacial rivers with exciting floats through white waters form enjoyable rapids, drops, and holes to make the adventure thrill with excitement in the world of water sports at Seti.\\r\\n\\r\\n<a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seti_River\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Seti River</a> “the Milky River”, as this river starts with white color (from the chalk and limestone) originates from the glaciers of the massive range of Annapurna Himalaya including the majestic Machhapuchare peak (Fish Tail).  this river flows through Pokhara and joins further downstream making a wider Seti River at Damauli town.\\r\\n\\r\\nAdventure starts with 2 hours of drive to reach Damauli town from <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/cultural-scenic-tour-kathmandu-pokhara-chitwan-lumbini/\\">Pokhara city</a> to ‘put in point’ near at Mardi River. Our river guides will receive and then brief on safety procedure, and paddling technique and then board the inflatable raft putting on life jackets, and helmets for safety. Then float for a few hours through exciting rapids, and continue rafting with the last best rapids. After a great time rafting on the bank of the river, after changing into dry clothes drive back to Pokhara after the exciting thrill of rafting in the scenic Seti River."}], "sub_description": "Explore River rafting with Everest Vacation.", "trip_highlights": "Experience the thrill of conquering Nepal’s mighty rivers with Everest Vacation’ River Rafting adventure. Discover and embark on a thrilling journey that combines adrenaline-pumping rapids, stunning scenery, and unforgettable memories. Whether you’re a seasoned rafter or a first-timer, this tour offers an exhilarating experience suitable for all skill levels. We provides detailed information about the different river rafting options available, allowing you to choose the one that best suits your preferences and abilities. Brace yourself for an adrenaline rush as you navigate through challenging rapids, witnessing the raw power of nature firsthand. Along the way, soak in the breathtaking landscapes, from lush forests to cascading waterfalls. Safety is a top priority, and experienced guides will accompany you throughout the journey, ensuring a fun and secure rafting adventure. Whether you’re seeking an adrenaline-fueled experience or simply want to immerse yourself in the beauty of Nepal’s rivers, this River Rafting tour promises an unforgettable adventure you won’t want to miss.", "trip_type_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "meta_description": "River rafting in Nepal is full of adventure with exciting floats through white waters forming enjoyable rapids, drops, and holes.", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": "Private AC Vehicle"}, "trip_transportations": "Private AC Vehicle"}	2023-12-29 07:17:24+00	2024-02-07 05:15:57+00
220	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "Thimphu, Punakha and Paro with Tiger's Nest Monastery", "ws_dulux_price": "", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "5", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour"}, "meta": {"_edit_last": "1", "_edit_lock": "1707790291:1", "_dp_original": "606", "_thumbnail_id": "4012", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "Thimphu, Punakha and Paro with Tiger's Nest Monastery", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_dulux_price": "", "_ws_dulux_price": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "5", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "Bhutan Tour 5 Days", "_yoast_wpseo_linkdex": "47", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Bhutan Tour 5 days is a short but unforgettable experience for a lifetime in a culturally rich nation alongside nature and greenery.", "child_select_quick_link": "a:4:{i:0;s:8:\\"overview\\";i:1;s:9:\\"itinerary\\";i:2;s:7:\\"reviews\\";i:3;s:4:\\"faqs\\";}", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "bhutan-tour-5-days", "tags": [], "title": "Bhutan Tour 5 Days", "duration": "5 Days", "overview": {"title": "Overview", "description": "The <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/7-days-bhutan-itinerary/\\">Bhutan</a> Tour 5 days is a short but unforgettable experience for a lifetime. You find yourself in a cultural nation rich in culture, tradition, arts, and architecture alongside greenery, beautiful landscapes, and the snowcapped Himalayas. Visit the traditional monasteries, fortresses, temples, and Chortens strong holding historic and cultural importance.\\r\\n\\r\\nYour journey begins in the historic town of Paro, including the cultural hubs of Thimphu and Punakha. Explore the oldest temple in Bhutan, the architecturally rich Paro Dzong, Taschichho Dzong, National Memorial Chorten, and the <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddha_Dordenma_statue\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Great Buddha Dordenma</a> all showcasing Bhutan’s rich history, art, and tradition. The high mountain pass Dochu La pass and scenic view on the way. Traditional art schools preserve and promote Bhutan’s art. The traditional Hot Stone Bath and hike to Tiger’s Nest are some major attractions included in our 5-day itinerary."}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Arrival in Paro and Get Transferred to Thimphu", "richText": "You are greeted by your Bhutanese guide after arrival at the Paro International Airport. Rest and relax a while at a restaurant or cafe enjoying your lunch or coffee. Firstly, visit the beautiful “Jowo” temple of Kyichu Lhakhang which is the oldest in Bhutan. It is taken as the holy jewel of Bhutan. Witness the real statue of Jowo Shakyamuni, a statue of Chenrezig, a painting of the King Gesar Ling on the wall, a statue of Guru Rinpoche, monk houses, prayer wheels, and two historically significant orange trees in the courtyard. A place is full of art and culture significant to all art lovers and historians.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf time permits, explore the beautiful Paro Dzong which is a classic example of Bhutanese architecture. The gorgeous architecture and photographic scenic views from dzong are worthy to visit this place. “Paro Tsechu” one of the biggest festivals is organized here every year. If you arrive at festival time, then get a chance to participate and enjoy it.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter exploring Paro, you are transferred to Thimphu in the evening. You take a rest and relax here in a hotel. Enjoy Bhutanese cuisine as nightlife here in Thimphu.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 2, "meal": "", "title": "Thimphu Sightseeing and Travel to Punakha", "richText": "Thimphu is the capital as well as the largest city of Bhutan. The traditional Bhutanese art, architecture, and culture hold major significance and can be seen well preserved here in Thimphu. You begin your trip today by traveling to the National Memorial Chorten built in the memory of the third king of Bhutan. Explore the Great Buddha Dordenma and a spectacular view of Thimphu valley from the top. Then, visit the National Library, behind it the National Folk Heritage Museum showcasing rural life. Also, visit the Zorig Chusum School of Traditional Arts. The 13 traditional arts of Bhutan are well-preserved here and appreciate the students refining their skills. Paintings, carpentry, wood carving, sculpture, casting, metalwork, bamboo carving, gold and silverwork, masonry, weaving, embroidery, leatherwork, and paper-making are these 13 traditional arts being transferred to the new generation to preserve and promote them.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe main highlight of the tour is visiting Tashichho Dzong (Thimpu Dzong). “The Fortress of the Glorious Religion” is the most beautiful Bhutanese dzong and seat of the government since 1968. The Utse or Central tower, thirty temples, chapels, and shrines are major attractions there. Later, you travel northeast to Punakha, the former capital of Bhutan. On the way, stop at beautiful Dochu La Pass (3,100m) for a refreshing tea/coffee. The pass offers a scenic view of the Great Himalayas. Likewise, witness the famous 108 memorial stupas. After lunch at your next stop, along with your guide keep driving to Punakha. Stay overnight at a hotel and enjoy your dinner.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 3, "meal": "", "title": "Punakha Dzong Sightseeing and Drive back to Paro", "richText": "You visit Punakha Dzong with your guide today. It is one of the most beautiful as well as vital dzong in Bhutanese history. The second oldest and second largest dzong in the nation was built without using any nails. It is a place where Bhutan’s national treasures are kept. The dzong is situated between Po and Mo Chu rivers and the access to the dzong is crossing Bazam Bridge. A big white stupa, a Bodhi tree, and the main temples inside the courtyards to the dzong are major attractions. Don’t miss the Punakha festival around mid-Feb if you arrive here at that time.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter exploring Punakha Dzong, drive back to Paro with your Bhutanese guide. Visit the National Museum of Bhutan which looks like a combination of the circular sun and crescent moon. The rich diversity of historical relics and culture from all over Bhutan through its collection of artworks is exhibited. Ancient and modern Thangkas and cultural masks are some remarkable collections to watch there. A gallery showcasing preserved carcasses of animals and birds depicts the biodiversity and wildlife of Bhutan. You feel connected with Bhutan’s history of arts and crafts.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen we drive to visit the historically important Drukgyel Dzong meaning “Victories Fortress.” You can see the ruins of huge walls, burnt wooden posts, beams, and watchtowers. Enjoy the spectacular view from the top of the hill. Stay overnight at a hotel.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 4, "meal": "", "title": "Trek to Taktsang Lhakhang (Tiger’s Nest)", "richText": "Today you commence your day by trekking to Taktsang Lhakhang. It is widely known as “Tiger’s Nest” and a famous landmark of Bhutan. To travel here is short-listed in every itinerary of Bhutan. It is a 2-hour hike full of beautiful scenery on the way, shady pine forests, many prayer flags, and a panoramic view of Paro valley. The Vajrayana Buddhist temple perched on the edge at 3120m is considered sacred in Bhutan. Guru Padmasambhava is believed to have flown on the back of a tigress and meditated in this cave for over 3 years to calm down the demons. You can also meditate for a while if you wish to. Hike down to Paro afterward.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter lunch, you may opt to soak yourself in a hot stone bath or enjoy exploring nearby.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}, {"day": 5, "meal": "", "title": "Departure from Paro", "richText": "It’s time to bid farewell to this beautiful nation after a delightful and memorable trip. Your guide departs you to the Paro International Airport.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Punakha-Dzong-2.jpg", "title": "Punakha-Dzong-2", "altText": "Punakha-Dzong", "caption": "Punakha-Dzong", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["4397", "4022", "4032", "4013", "4001", "3995", "3996", "3994", "3990", "3973", "3949", "3881", "3869", "584"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "ws_block_attractions": "Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle", "ws_block_best_season": "Any Season", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "What's included?", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-white", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": "Overview", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc651ee1073", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_block_transportation": "Private AC Vehicle", "ws_trip_galleries_title": "Photo/Visual Gallery", "_ws_block_transportation": "field_63eeee74072de", "_ws_trip_galleries_title": "field_63ec89128acaa", "starter_kit_padding_type": "p-medium", "ws_trip_block_highlights": "", "ws_trip_information_list": 5, "_starter_kit_padding_type": "field_5f8584c998bc2", "_ws_trip_block_highlights": "field_63ec73a6a0d8f", "_ws_trip_information_list": "field_63ec94565c587", "starter_kit_section_title": "Day by Day Activities", "_starter_kit_section_title": "field_63ec948c94a16", "starter_kit_enable_section": "1", "_starter_kit_enable_section": "field_63edeb1c7635c", "starter_kit_section_padding": "", "ws_trip_include_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Accommodation in approved hotels</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>US$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>USD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fees</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Breakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (at Restaurant)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>English speaking Bhutan licensed guide</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Entrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bottled drinking water throughout the journeys</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_starter_kit_section_padding": "field_5f3e0f86a2634", "_ws_trip_include_description": "field_63edd6a337cd0", "ws_trip_overview_description": "The <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/7-days-bhutan-itinerary/\\">Bhutan</a> Tour 5 days is a short but unforgettable experience for a lifetime. You find yourself in a cultural nation rich in culture, tradition, arts, and architecture alongside greenery, beautiful landscapes, and the snowcapped Himalayas. Visit the traditional monasteries, fortresses, temples, and Chortens strong holding historic and cultural importance.\\r\\n\\r\\nYour journey begins in the historic town of Paro, including the cultural hubs of Thimphu and Punakha. Explore the oldest temple in Bhutan, the architecturally rich Paro Dzong, Taschichho Dzong, National Memorial Chorten, and the <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddha_Dordenma_statue\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Great Buddha Dordenma</a> all showcasing Bhutan’s rich history, art, and tradition. The high mountain pass Dochu La pass and scenic view on the way. Traditional art schools preserve and promote Bhutan’s art. The traditional Hot Stone Bath and hike to Tiger’s Nest are some major attractions included in our 5-day itinerary.", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "", "_ws_trip_fact_short_description": "field_63ec73a69d305", "ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "01", "ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "02", "ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "03", "ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "04", "ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "05", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food": "field_63ec96f1878e1", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "Arrival in Paro and Get Transferred to Thimphu", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "Thimphu Sightseeing and Travel to Punakha", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "Punakha Dzong Sightseeing and Drive back to Paro", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "Trek to Taktsang Lhakhang (Tiger’s Nest)", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title": "Departure from Paro", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel": "field_63ec96e3878e0", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title": "field_63ec945663e31", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration": "field_63ec96a0878df", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation": "field_63ec967a59e99", "ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "You are greeted by your Bhutanese guide after arrival at the Paro International Airport. Rest and relax a while at a restaurant or cafe enjoying your lunch or coffee. Firstly, visit the beautiful “Jowo” temple of Kyichu Lhakhang which is the oldest in Bhutan. It is taken as the holy jewel of Bhutan. Witness the real statue of Jowo Shakyamuni, a statue of Chenrezig, a painting of the King Gesar Ling on the wall, a statue of Guru Rinpoche, monk houses, prayer wheels, and two historically significant orange trees in the courtyard. A place is full of art and culture significant to all art lovers and historians.\\r\\n\\r\\nIf time permits, explore the beautiful Paro Dzong which is a classic example of Bhutanese architecture. The gorgeous architecture and photographic scenic views from dzong are worthy to visit this place. “Paro Tsechu” one of the biggest festivals is organized here every year. If you arrive at festival time, then get a chance to participate and enjoy it.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter exploring Paro, you are transferred to Thimphu in the evening. You take a rest and relax here in a hotel. Enjoy Bhutanese cuisine as nightlife here in Thimphu.", "ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "Thimphu is the capital as well as the largest city of Bhutan. The traditional Bhutanese art, architecture, and culture hold major significance and can be seen well preserved here in Thimphu. You begin your trip today by traveling to the National Memorial Chorten built in the memory of the third king of Bhutan. Explore the Great Buddha Dordenma and a spectacular view of Thimphu valley from the top. Then, visit the National Library, behind it the National Folk Heritage Museum showcasing rural life. Also, visit the Zorig Chusum School of Traditional Arts. The 13 traditional arts of Bhutan are well-preserved here and appreciate the students refining their skills. Paintings, carpentry, wood carving, sculpture, casting, metalwork, bamboo carving, gold and silverwork, masonry, weaving, embroidery, leatherwork, and paper-making are these 13 traditional arts being transferred to the new generation to preserve and promote them.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe main highlight of the tour is visiting Tashichho Dzong (Thimpu Dzong). “The Fortress of the Glorious Religion” is the most beautiful Bhutanese dzong and seat of the government since 1968. The Utse or Central tower, thirty temples, chapels, and shrines are major attractions there. Later, you travel northeast to Punakha, the former capital of Bhutan. On the way, stop at beautiful Dochu La Pass (3,100m) for a refreshing tea/coffee. The pass offers a scenic view of the Great Himalayas. Likewise, witness the famous 108 memorial stupas. After lunch at your next stop, along with your guide keep driving to Punakha. Stay overnight at a hotel and enjoy your dinner.", "ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "You visit Punakha Dzong with your guide today. It is one of the most beautiful as well as vital dzong in Bhutanese history. The second oldest and second largest dzong in the nation was built without using any nails. It is a place where Bhutan’s national treasures are kept. The dzong is situated between Po and Mo Chu rivers and the access to the dzong is crossing Bazam Bridge. A big white stupa, a Bodhi tree, and the main temples inside the courtyards to the dzong are major attractions. Don’t miss the Punakha festival around mid-Feb if you arrive here at that time.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter exploring Punakha Dzong, drive back to Paro with your Bhutanese guide. Visit the National Museum of Bhutan which looks like a combination of the circular sun and crescent moon. The rich diversity of historical relics and culture from all over Bhutan through its collection of artworks is exhibited. Ancient and modern Thangkas and cultural masks are some remarkable collections to watch there. A gallery showcasing preserved carcasses of animals and birds depicts the biodiversity and wildlife of Bhutan. You feel connected with Bhutan’s history of arts and crafts.\\r\\n\\r\\nThen we drive to visit the historically important Drukgyel Dzong meaning “Victories Fortress.” You can see the ruins of huge walls, burnt wooden posts, beams, and watchtowers. Enjoy the spectacular view from the top of the hill. Stay overnight at a hotel.", "ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "Today you commence your day by trekking to Taktsang Lhakhang. It is widely known as “Tiger’s Nest” and a famous landmark of Bhutan. To travel here is short-listed in every itinerary of Bhutan. It is a 2-hour hike full of beautiful scenery on the way, shady pine forests, many prayer flags, and a panoramic view of Paro valley. The Vajrayana Buddhist temple perched on the edge at 3120m is considered sacred in Bhutan. Guru Padmasambhava is believed to have flown on the back of a tigress and meditated in this cave for over 3 years to calm down the demons. You can also meditate for a while if you wish to. Hike down to Paro afterward.\\r\\n\\r\\nAfter lunch, you may opt to soak yourself in a hot stone bath or enjoy exploring nearby.", "ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description": "It’s time to bid farewell to this beautiful nation after a delightful and memorable trip. Your guide departs you to the Paro International Airport.", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description": "field_63ec9456679f6"}, "categoryId": null, "meta_title": "Bhutan Tour 5 Days | Everest Vacation", "blogContent": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_6