l Chorten, and the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddha_Dordenma_statue\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eGreat Buddha Dordenma\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e all showcasing Bhutan’s rich history, art, and tradition. The high mountain pass Dochu La pass and scenic view on the way. Traditional art schools preserve and promote Bhutan’s art. The traditional Hot Stone Bath and hike to Tiger’s Nest are some major attractions included in our 5-day itinerary.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4397\\",\\"4022\\",\\"4032\\",\\"4013\\",\\"4001\\",\\"3995\\",\\"3996\\",\\"3994\\",\\"3990\\",\\"3973\\",\\"3949\\",\\"3881\\",\\"3869\\",\\"584\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Arrival in Paro and Get Transferred to Thimphu\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"You are greeted by your Bhutanese guide after arrival at the Paro International Airport. Rest and relax a while at a restaurant or cafe enjoying your lunch or coffee. Firstly, visit the beautiful “Jowo” temple of Kyichu Lhakhang which is the oldest in Bhutan. It is taken as the holy jewel of Bhutan. Witness the real statue of Jowo Shakyamuni, a statue of Chenrezig, a painting of the King Gesar Ling on the wall, a statue of Guru Rinpoche, monk houses, prayer wheels, and two historically significant orange trees in the courtyard. A place is full of art and culture significant to all art lovers and historians.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIf time permits, explore the beautiful Paro Dzong which is a classic example of Bhutanese architecture. The gorgeous architecture and photographic scenic views from dzong are worthy to visit this place. “Paro Tsechu” one of the biggest festivals is organized here every year. If you arrive at festival time, then get a chance to participate and enjoy it.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter exploring Paro, you are transferred to Thimphu in the evening. You take a rest and relax here in a hotel. Enjoy Bhutanese cuisine as nightlife here in Thimphu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Thimphu Sightseeing and Travel to Punakha\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Thimphu is the capital as well as the largest city of Bhutan. The traditional Bhutanese art, architecture, and culture hold major significance and can be seen well preserved here in Thimphu. You begin your trip today by traveling to the National Memorial Chorten built in the memory of the third king of Bhutan. Explore the Great Buddha Dordenma and a spectacular view of Thimphu valley from the top. Then, visit the National Library, behind it the National Folk Heritage Museum showcasing rural life. Also, visit the Zorig Chusum School of Traditional Arts. The 13 traditional arts of Bhutan are well-preserved here and appreciate the students refining their skills. Paintings, carpentry, wood carving, sculpture, casting, metalwork, bamboo carving, gold and silverwork, masonry, weaving, embroidery, leatherwork, and paper-making are these 13 traditional arts being transferred to the new generation to preserve and promote them.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe main highlight of the tour is visiting Tashichho Dzong (Thimpu Dzong). “The Fortress of the Glorious Religion” is the most beautiful Bhutanese dzong and seat of the government since 1968. The Utse or Central tower, thirty temples, chapels, and shrines are major attractions there. Later, you travel northeast to Punakha, the former capital of Bhutan. On the way, stop at beautiful Dochu La Pass (3,100m) for a refreshing tea/coffee. The pass offers a scenic view of the Great Himalayas. Likewise, witness the famous 108 memorial stupas. After lunch at your next stop, along with your guide keep driving to Punakha. Stay overnight at a hotel and enjoy your dinner.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Punakha Dzong Sightseeing and Drive back to Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"You visit Punakha Dzong with your guide today. It is one of the most beautiful as well as vital dzong in Bhutanese history. The second oldest and second largest dzong in the nation was built without using any nails. It is a place where Bhutan’s national treasures are kept. The dzong is situated between Po and Mo Chu rivers and the access to the dzong is crossing Bazam Bridge. A big white stupa, a Bodhi tree, and the main temples inside the courtyards to the dzong are major attractions. Don’t miss the Punakha festival around mid-Feb if you arrive here at that time.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter exploring Punakha Dzong, drive back to Paro with your Bhutanese guide. Visit the National Museum of Bhutan which looks like a combination of the circular sun and crescent moon. The rich diversity of historical relics and culture from all over Bhutan through its collection of artworks is exhibited. Ancient and modern Thangkas and cultural masks are some remarkable collections to watch there. A gallery showcasing preserved carcasses of animals and birds depicts the biodiversity and wildlife of Bhutan. You feel connected with Bhutan’s history of arts and crafts.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThen we drive to visit the historically important Drukgyel Dzong meaning “Victories Fortress.” You can see the ruins of huge walls, burnt wooden posts, beams, and watchtowers. Enjoy the spectacular view from the top of the hill. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Taktsang Lhakhang (Tiger’s Nest)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Today you commence your day by trekking to Taktsang Lhakhang. It is widely known as “Tiger’s Nest” and a famous landmark of Bhutan. To travel here is short-listed in every itinerary of Bhutan. It is a 2-hour hike full of beautiful scenery on the way, shady pine forests, many prayer flags, and a panoramic view of Paro valley. The Vajrayana Buddhist temple perched on the edge at 3120m is considered sacred in Bhutan. Guru Padmasambhava is believed to have flown on the back of a tigress and meditated in this cave for over 3 years to calm down the demons. You can also meditate for a while if you wish to. Hike down to Paro afterward.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter lunch, you may opt to soak yourself in a hot stone bath or enjoy exploring nearby.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"05\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Departure from Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"It’s time to bid farewell to this beautiful nation after a delightful and memorable trip. Your guide departs you to the Paro International Airport.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAccommodation in approved hotels\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUS$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVisa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUSD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fees\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (at Restaurant)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking Bhutan licensed guide\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEntrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBottled drinking water throughout the journeys\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "descriptions": "<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-trip-fact {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-trip-fact\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec73a6998bb\\",\\"ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_fact_short_description\\":\\"field_63ec73a69d305\\",\\"ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_block_highlights\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a0d8f\\",\\"ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_trip_grading\\":\\"field_63ec73a6a4716\\",\\"ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_max_elevation\\":\\"field_63eeee07072d9\\",\\"ws_block_attractions\\":\\"Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle\\",\\"_ws_block_attractions\\":\\"field_63eeee1f072da\\",\\"ws_block_best_season\\":\\"Any Season\\",\\"_ws_block_best_season\\":\\"field_63eeee37072db\\",\\"ws_block_meals\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_meals\\":\\"field_63eeee4e072dc\\",\\"ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_accommodation\\":\\"field_63eeee62072dd\\",\\"ws_block_transportation\\":\\"Private AC Vehicle\\",\\"_ws_block_transportation\\":\\"field_63eeee74072de\\",\\"ws_block_start_end\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_start_end\\":\\"field_63eeee8b072df\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-overview {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-overview\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec8086435ad\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-light\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4e9c19160\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"Overview\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_title\\":\\"field_63ec808647048\\",\\"ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"The \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://everestnepaltours.com/7-days-bhutan-itinerary/\\\\u0022\\\\u003eBhutan\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e Tour 5 days is a short but unforgettable experience for a lifetime. You find yourself in a cultural nation rich in culture, tradition, arts, and architecture alongside greenery, beautiful landscapes, and the snowcapped Himalayas. Visit the traditional monasteries, fortresses, temples, and Chortens strong holding historic and cultural importance.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nYour journey begins in the historic town of Paro, including the cultural hubs of Thimphu and Punakha. Explore the oldest temple in Bhutan, the architecturally rich Paro Dzong, Taschichho Dzong, National Memorial Chorten, and the \\\\u003ca href=\\\\u0022https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddha_Dordenma_statue\\\\u0022 target=\\\\u0022_blank\\\\u0022 rel=\\\\u0022noopener\\\\u0022\\\\u003eGreat Buddha Dordenma\\\\u003c/a\\\\u003e all showcasing Bhutan’s rich history, art, and tradition. The high mountain pass Dochu La pass and scenic view on the way. Traditional art schools preserve and promote Bhutan’s art. The traditional Hot Stone Bath and hike to Tiger’s Nest are some major attractions included in our 5-day itinerary.\\",\\"_ws_trip_overview_description\\":\\"field_63ec83089dd8e\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-galleries {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-galleries\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec891287214\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc4c3116dd8\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"Photo/Visual Gallery\\",\\"_ws_trip_galleries_title\\":\\"field_63ec89128acaa\\",\\"ws_trip_galleries\\":[\\"4397\\",\\"4022\\",\\"4032\\",\\"4013\\",\\"4001\\",\\"3995\\",\\"3996\\",\\"3994\\",\\"3990\\",\\"3973\\",\\"3949\\",\\"3881\\",\\"3869\\",\\"584\\"],\\"_ws_trip_galleries\\":\\"field_63ec89128e6ea\\",\\"ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_block_video_widgets\\":\\"field_63eef38026ee6\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-detailed-itineray\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ec9456589bf\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc666fbd79e\\",\\"starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"Day by Day Activities\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_title\\":\\"field_63ec948c94a16\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"01\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Arrival in Paro and Get Transferred to Thimphu\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"You are greeted by your Bhutanese guide after arrival at the Paro International Airport. Rest and relax a while at a restaurant or cafe enjoying your lunch or coffee. Firstly, visit the beautiful “Jowo” temple of Kyichu Lhakhang which is the oldest in Bhutan. It is taken as the holy jewel of Bhutan. Witness the real statue of Jowo Shakyamuni, a statue of Chenrezig, a painting of the King Gesar Ling on the wall, a statue of Guru Rinpoche, monk houses, prayer wheels, and two historically significant orange trees in the courtyard. A place is full of art and culture significant to all art lovers and historians.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nIf time permits, explore the beautiful Paro Dzong which is a classic example of Bhutanese architecture. The gorgeous architecture and photographic scenic views from dzong are worthy to visit this place. “Paro Tsechu” one of the biggest festivals is organized here every year. If you arrive at festival time, then get a chance to participate and enjoy it.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter exploring Paro, you are transferred to Thimphu in the evening. You take a rest and relax here in a hotel. Enjoy Bhutanese cuisine as nightlife here in Thimphu.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_0_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"02\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Thimphu Sightseeing and Travel to Punakha\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Thimphu is the capital as well as the largest city of Bhutan. The traditional Bhutanese art, architecture, and culture hold major significance and can be seen well preserved here in Thimphu. You begin your trip today by traveling to the National Memorial Chorten built in the memory of the third king of Bhutan. Explore the Great Buddha Dordenma and a spectacular view of Thimphu valley from the top. Then, visit the National Library, behind it the National Folk Heritage Museum showcasing rural life. Also, visit the Zorig Chusum School of Traditional Arts. The 13 traditional arts of Bhutan are well-preserved here and appreciate the students refining their skills. Paintings, carpentry, wood carving, sculpture, casting, metalwork, bamboo carving, gold and silverwork, masonry, weaving, embroidery, leatherwork, and paper-making are these 13 traditional arts being transferred to the new generation to preserve and promote them.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThe main highlight of the tour is visiting Tashichho Dzong (Thimpu Dzong). “The Fortress of the Glorious Religion” is the most beautiful Bhutanese dzong and seat of the government since 1968. The Utse or Central tower, thirty temples, chapels, and shrines are major attractions there. Later, you travel northeast to Punakha, the former capital of Bhutan. On the way, stop at beautiful Dochu La Pass (3,100m) for a refreshing tea/coffee. The pass offers a scenic view of the Great Himalayas. Likewise, witness the famous 108 memorial stupas. After lunch at your next stop, along with your guide keep driving to Punakha. Stay overnight at a hotel and enjoy your dinner.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_1_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"03\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Punakha Dzong Sightseeing and Drive back to Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"You visit Punakha Dzong with your guide today. It is one of the most beautiful as well as vital dzong in Bhutanese history. The second oldest and second largest dzong in the nation was built without using any nails. It is a place where Bhutan’s national treasures are kept. The dzong is situated between Po and Mo Chu rivers and the access to the dzong is crossing Bazam Bridge. A big white stupa, a Bodhi tree, and the main temples inside the courtyards to the dzong are major attractions. Don’t miss the Punakha festival around mid-Feb if you arrive here at that time.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter exploring Punakha Dzong, drive back to Paro with your Bhutanese guide. Visit the National Museum of Bhutan which looks like a combination of the circular sun and crescent moon. The rich diversity of historical relics and culture from all over Bhutan through its collection of artworks is exhibited. Ancient and modern Thangkas and cultural masks are some remarkable collections to watch there. A gallery showcasing preserved carcasses of animals and birds depicts the biodiversity and wildlife of Bhutan. You feel connected with Bhutan’s history of arts and crafts.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nThen we drive to visit the historically important Drukgyel Dzong meaning “Victories Fortress.” You can see the ruins of huge walls, burnt wooden posts, beams, and watchtowers. Enjoy the spectacular view from the top of the hill. Stay overnight at a hotel.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_2_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"04\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Trek to Taktsang Lhakhang (Tiger’s Nest)\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"Today you commence your day by trekking to Taktsang Lhakhang. It is widely known as “Tiger’s Nest” and a famous landmark of Bhutan. To travel here is short-listed in every itinerary of Bhutan. It is a 2-hour hike full of beautiful scenery on the way, shady pine forests, many prayer flags, and a panoramic view of Paro valley. The Vajrayana Buddhist temple perched on the edge at 3120m is considered sacred in Bhutan. Guru Padmasambhava is believed to have flown on the back of a tigress and meditated in this cave for over 3 years to calm down the demons. You can also meditate for a while if you wish to. Hike down to Paro afterward.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAfter lunch, you may opt to soak yourself in a hot stone bath or enjoy exploring nearby.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_3_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"05\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days\\":\\"field_63ec958b8c799\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"Departure from Paro\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_title\\":\\"field_63ec945663e31\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_Elevation\\":\\"field_63ec967a59e99\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_duration\\":\\"field_63ec96a0878df\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_hotel\\":\\"field_63ec96e3878e0\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_food\\":\\"field_63ec96f1878e1\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"It’s time to bid farewell to this beautiful nation after a delightful and memorable trip. Your guide departs you to the Paro International Airport.\\",\\"_ws_trip_information_list_4_ws_itinerary_description\\":\\"field_63ec9456679f6\\",\\"ws_trip_information_list\\":5,\\"_ws_trip_information_list\\":\\"field_63ec94565c587\\",\\"ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_title\\":\\"field_63ec94c094a17\\",\\"ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"\\",\\"_ws_flash_message_text\\":\\"field_63ec950194a18\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-include-exclude {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-include-exclude\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edd6a330794\\",\\"starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"bg-white\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_bg\\":\\"field_63fc651ee1073\\",\\"ws_select_content_type\\":\\"ws-included\\",\\"_ws_select_content_type\\":\\"field_63edd755e9729\\",\\"ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"What's included?\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_title\\":\\"field_63edd6a334286\\",\\"ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"\\\\u003cul\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eAccommodation in approved hotels\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUS$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eVisa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eUSD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fees\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBreakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (at Restaurant)\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEnglish speaking Bhutan licensed guide\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eTransfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eEntrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n \\\\t\\\\u003cli\\\\u003eBottled drinking water throughout the journeys\\\\u003c/li\\\\u003e\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003c/ul\\\\u003e\\",\\"_ws_trip_include_description\\":\\"field_63edd6a337cd0\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-testimonial-lists\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\",\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63ba53af63ade\\",\\"starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"Traveler's Reviews\\",\\"_starter_kit_testimonial_title\\":\\"field_63ba53af6b053\\",\\"review_number_of_post\\":\\"-1\\",\\"_review_number_of_post\\":\\"field_63ba542aa9a32\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->\\n\\n<!-- wp:acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry {\\"name\\":\\"acf/starter-kit-quick-enquiry\\",\\"data\\":{\\"starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"1\\",\\"_starter_kit_enable_section\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7635c\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"Ask to Expert about this trip\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_title\\":\\"field_63edeb1c7d769\\",\\"ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"Fill the form below for your interest.\\\\r\\\\n\\",\\"_ws_quick_enquiry_desc\\":\\"field_63edeb1c811ab\\",\\"ws_gf_id\\":\\"4\\",\\"_ws_gf_id\\":\\"field_63edec7318284\\",\\"starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"\\",\\"_starter_kit_section_padding\\":\\"field_5f3e0f86a2634\\",\\"starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"p-medium\\",\\"_starter_kit_padding_type\\":\\"field_5f8584c998bc2\\"},\\"mode\\":\\"edit\\"} /-->", "imageGallary": ["https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Punakha-Dzong-2.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/dochulapass.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Semtokha-dzong-thimphu.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Tachogang-Lhakhang-Bridge1-scaled.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Punakha-Dzong-with-bridge.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/piya-sheldon.jpeg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Paro-River.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Paro-Valley-with-villages.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Paro-Airport-Landing.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Paro-Airport1.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/National-Memorial-Chhorten-Thimphu.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Memorial-Chorten-Thimphu.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Craft-Bazaar-1.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Buddha-Dordenma.jpg", "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Memorial-Chorten-with-prayers-500x375-1.jpg"], "importSource": {"guid": "https://wildstonesolution.com/demo/ev/?post_type=trip&#038;p=3505", "system": "wordpress", "parentId": 0, "postType": "trip", "wpPostId": "3505", "wpSiteUrl": "https://everestnepaltours.com", "postStatus": "publish", "tablePrefix": "wev_", "wpContentDir": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content", "sourceTimestamps": {"post_date": "2024-01-03 07:55:03", "post_date_gmt": "2024-01-03 07:55:03", "post_modified": "2024-02-13 02:10:47", "post_modified_gmt": "2024-02-13 02:10:47"}}, "customSections": [{"id": "overview-1", "type": "paragraph", "title": "Overview", "content": ["The <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/7-days-bhutan-itinerary/\\">Bhutan</a> Tour 5 days is a short but unforgettable experience for a lifetime. You find yourself in a cultural nation rich in culture, tradition, arts, and architecture alongside greenery, beautiful landscapes, and the snowcapped Himalayas. Visit the traditional monasteries, fortresses, temples, and Chortens strong holding historic and cultural importance.\\r\\n\\r\\nYour journey begins in the historic town of Paro, including the cultural hubs of Thimphu and Punakha. Explore the oldest temple in Bhutan, the architecturally rich Paro Dzong, Taschichho Dzong, National Memorial Chorten, and the <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddha_Dordenma_statue\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Great Buddha Dordenma</a> all showcasing Bhutan’s rich history, art, and tradition. The high mountain pass Dochu La pass and scenic view on the way. Traditional art schools preserve and promote Bhutan’s art. The traditional Hot Stone Bath and hike to Tiger’s Nest are some major attractions included in our 5-day itinerary."], "description": "The <a href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/7-days-bhutan-itinerary/\\">Bhutan</a> Tour 5 days is a short but unforgettable experience for a lifetime. You find yourself in a cultural nation rich in culture, tradition, arts, and architecture alongside greenery, beautiful landscapes, and the snowcapped Himalayas. Visit the traditional monasteries, fortresses, temples, and Chortens strong holding historic and cultural importance.\\r\\n\\r\\nYour journey begins in the historic town of Paro, including the cultural hubs of Thimphu and Punakha. Explore the oldest temple in Bhutan, the architecturally rich Paro Dzong, Taschichho Dzong, National Memorial Chorten, and the <a href=\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buddha_Dordenma_statue\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">Great Buddha Dordenma</a> all showcasing Bhutan’s rich history, art, and tradition. The high mountain pass Dochu La pass and scenic view on the way. Traditional art schools preserve and promote Bhutan’s art. The traditional Hot Stone Bath and hike to Tiger’s Nest are some major attractions included in our 5-day itinerary."}, {"id": "included-list", "note": "", "type": "list", "title": "Cost Include", "content": ["Accommodation in approved hotels", "US$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)", "Visa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary", "USD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fees", "Breakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (at Restaurant)", "English speaking Bhutan licensed guide", "Transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary", "Entrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary", "Bottled drinking water throughout the journeys"], "description": ""}], "cost_inclusions": {"permits": ["Accommodation in approved hotels", "US$ 40 per person visa fees (single entry only)", "Visa arrangement for your stay in Bhutan as per the itinerary", "USD 100 per person per night Sustainable Development Fees", "Breakfast and Diner in hotels, Lunch will be in outside of hotel (at Restaurant)", "English speaking Bhutan licensed guide", "Transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary", "Entrance, museums and park fees indicated in the itinerary", "Bottled drinking water throughout the journeys"], "services": []}, "itinerary_title": "Day by Day Activities", "sub_description": "Thimphu, Punakha and Paro with Tiger's Nest Monastery", "trip_type_level": "Private Tour", "meta_description": "Bhutan Tour 5 days is a short but unforgettable experience for a lifetime in a culturally rich nation alongside nature and greenery.", "trip_attractions": "Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle", "trip_best_season": "Any Season", "related_trip_facts": {"meals": "", "start_end": "", "attractions": "Buddhist Stupas, local History of and culture ,Local lifestyle", "best_season": "Any Season", "accommodation": "", "max_elevation": "", "transportation": "Private AC Vehicle"}, "trip_transportations": "Private AC Vehicle", "trip_highlights_title": "What's included?"}	2024-01-03 07:55:03+00	2024-02-13 02:10:47+00
272	{"acf": {"ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "With addition Namtso Lake, Rongbuk Monastery (EBC), Pokhara, Chitwan National Park", "ws_regular_price": "", "ws_number_of_days": "15", "child_select_quick_link": "", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour"}, "meta": {"_edit_last": "1", "_edit_lock": "1728209107:1", "_thumbnail_id": "4873", "ws_sale_price": "", "ws_short_desc": "With addition Namtso Lake, Rongbuk Monastery (EBC), Pokhara, Chitwan National Park", "_ws_sale_price": "field_63ec6cbabf59a", "_ws_short_desc": "field_64bcfed7ea657", "ws_regular_price": "", "_ws_regular_price": "field_63ec6b81bf599", "ws_number_of_days": "15", "_ws_number_of_days": "field_63ec6d011465f", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "2 weeks Nepal and Tibet Tour with Lakes, Mountain views & Safari", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "2 weeks Tibet and Nepal tour is a great combined package which offers in these distinct and culturally rich destinations in the Himalayas.", "child_select_quick_link": "", "_child_select_quick_link": "field_643ed174633ee", "ws_trips_difficulty_level": "Private Tour", "_ws_trips_difficulty_level": "field_63ec7097385a5", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_activity": "", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_destination": "", "_yoast_wpseo_wordproof_timestamp": "", "_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes": "1"}, "slug": "2-weeks-tibet-and-nepal-tour", "tags": [], "title": "2 Weeks Tibet and Nepal Tour", "duration": "15 Days", "overview": {"title": "Outdoor Extra Activities", "description": "Not only historical, cultural, and natural tours embark on an adventurous journey through our outdoor extra activities. Some of our popular outdoor activities to carry out during this tour are as follows:\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Hiking:</strong> Short scenic hikes take you closer to nature and offer picturesque views\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>River rafting: </strong>Thrilling White Water River rafting in Nepal  on rapid rivers relishing scenic landscapes\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Paragliding: </strong>Relish amazing panoramic Himalayan views, scenic landscapes, and beautiful surroundings\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Zipline: </strong>Experience the longest and steepest zipline in Nepal and admire scenic surroundings\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Bungee jump: </strong>Adrenaline rush experience through bungee jumping in Nepal amidst beautiful surrounding scenery\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Yoga and meditation: </strong>Practice Yoga and Meditation in serene places such as a monastery, yoga centers, or in the vicinity of nature\\r\\n\\r\\n&nbsp;"}, "taxonomy": {}, "itinerary": [{"day": 1, "meal": "", "title": "Arrive at Gonggar airport. Transfer to Lhasa", "richText": "The flights to <strong>Gonggar Airport, Lhasa</strong> are easily available from various mainland cities (Shanghai, Beijing, Chengdu, etc.,) in China. Arrive at Gonggar Airport where the professional guide welcomes you. Then, transfers you to hotels in Lhasa via a private vehicle. Enjoy a scenic ride 1.5-2 hour ride. Upon arriving at the hotel, rest and relax. The elevation of Lhasa is high, so we suggest you acclimatize properly and adjust to the surroundings. Wear comfortable warm clothes, keep yourself hydrated, and eat healthy but light.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "3656m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 2, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Sightseeing in Lhasa (Potala Palace, Jokhang Temple, and Barkhor Bazaar)", "richText": "The second day in Lhasa commences with sightseeing of <strong>UNESCO-listed World Heritage Sites </strong>after breakfast. Make sure to wear appropriate clothes while visiting these sites. Explore the majestic landmarks of the grand <strong>Potala Palace</strong> and its aesthetic architecture. The most popular <strong>Buddhist temple of Jokhang</strong> is a spiritual center for Tibetans. Jokhang temple with its bronze roof, statues of golden deer, and the gold statue of Jowo Rinpoche is mesmerizing. <strong>Barkhor Street</strong> in the vicinity is popular for buying Tibetan original goods and crafts.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Optional:</strong> In the evening, attend the <strong>Tibetan Family Kitchen class</strong> between 4:30 pm to 8 pm. Here, shop the groceries, prepare Tibetan authentic dishes, dine, and enjoy with family and friends. <em>(After tour, we will take a group to the Tibetan Family Kitchen class. Dinner and Tibetan Traditional clothes with Tibetan family)</em>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "3656m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 3, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Sightseeing of Drepung, Sera Monasteries & Norbulingka Palace", "richText": "The third day in Lhasa starts with a tour of the UNESCO-listed World Heritage sites of <strong>Norbulingka Palace</strong>. The Palace which was built in 1755 is a perfect blend of Tibetan and Western cultures. Next, head to <strong>Drepung Monastery</strong> which was founded in 1416. It is one of the three largest monasteries of the Gelug School of Tibetan Buddhism. In the evening, visit <strong>Sera Monastery</strong> which holds scriptures written with golden powder. Debate sessions between 3-5 pm in the courtyard are the major highlights.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Optional:</strong> After dinner, attend <strong>Princess Wencheng Live Drama</strong> which is a grand show displaying the historical and cultural ties between the Tubo and Tang dynasties. The drama, music, and dances with modern choreography performed by 700 performers wearing traditional customs are magical and not to be missed. In the end, you can take pictures with the actors playing the princess and the King. <em>(After Dinner take the group to see The Big live drama Princess Wencheng)</em>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "3656m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 4, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Drive to Shigatse via Lake Yamdrok Lake and Gyantse Visit Kumbum Monastery, Pelkor Chöde Monastery, and drive to Shigatse", "richText": "Drive to Shigatse after breakfast from Lhasa. Pass Gampala Pass (4,790m) and explore the beautiful clear blue freshwater <strong>Yamdrok Lake. </strong>It is one of the largest of the Great Three Sacred Lakes in Tibet. Then, pass Simila Pass (4,200m) and head to Gyantse. En route get a sight of the huge <strong>Karola Glacier</strong>.\\r\\n\\r\\nVisit the Buddhist <strong>Pelkor Chöde Monastery </strong>famous for its <strong>multi-storied Kumbum</strong>, which is one of the largest such structures in Tibet. Take a tour of the <strong>Kumbum Monastery,</strong> popular for its infinite tiny chapels, intricate murals, and architectural style. Continue to drive to Shigatse.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "5039m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 5, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Visit Tashilhunpo Monastery, and drive to Shegar", "richText": "After breakfast, visit <strong>15<sup>th</sup> century</strong> <strong>Tashilhunpo Monastery</strong> which is one of the largest monasteries in Tibet. It houses one of the largest statues of the <strong>Maitreya Buddha</strong>. Then, drive to Shegar <strong>(New Tingri)</strong> and transfer to the 3-star hotel having basic but comfortable facilities. Take proper acclimatization rest as the following day, you are traveling to <strong>Rongbuk/</strong> <strong>Everest Base Camp</strong> at an elevation of 5200 meters above sea level.\\r\\n\\r\\n<em><strong>Note:</strong> We recommend to say at Shegar because Rongbuk has only one guesthouse, and only tents are a means of accommodation with an outside toilet.</em>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "4348m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 6, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Early morning drive to Rongbuk (Everest base camp), and drive back to Shigatse.", "richText": "Early morning drive to Rongbuk to witness the amazing sunrise views over snow-covered mountains. <strong>Rongbuk Monastery</strong> is one of the world’s highest-elevation monasteries at an elevation of 5,009 m. Tibetans called <strong>Everest as Mt. Qomolangma</strong>. From Rongbuk, relish the <strong>northern glory of Royal Mt. Everest</strong> and other surroundings. We advise travelers to walk slowly due to the gaining of high elevation. Also, make sure to wear warm clothes. After an awesome exploration, drive back to Shigatse.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "5200m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 7, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Drive to Namtso Lake (Damxung Town)", "richText": "After breakfast, drive to Damxung Town near Namtso Lake. Enjoy the scenic ride and reach Damxung town after some hours. Namtso is a town with limited facilities and Damxung town has a better accommodation facility. Transfer to the hotel, take a rest, and adjust to the surroundings.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "4300m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 8, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Drive Namtso Lake to Lhasa", "richText": "In the morning, head to the second-largest salt <strong>Namtso Lake</strong> in China. Adore the stunning view of <strong>Mt. Nyainqêntanglha </strong>from the vicinity of this crystal clear lake. Tibetans consider this lake holy and you can witness numerous pilgrims here. After a short tour, drive back to Lhasa.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "4718m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 9, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Drive to the airport and fly to Kathmandu, Short tour of Kathmandu (Pashupati & Boudha Stupa)", "richText": "Drive to the airport for the next tour destination, Nepal. Upon arriving at the Kathmandu airport, our tour guide welcomes you. Take a short tour of two wonderful UNESCO-listed World Heritage Sites: <strong>Pashupatinath</strong> and <strong>Boudhanath</strong>. Pashupatinath is one of the major Hindu temples in Nepal that is dedicated to Lord Shiva. From there, move to Boudhanath, which is one of the biggest Buddhist stupas in Nepal. The aura of these places is enchanting.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "1400m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 10, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Kathmandu sightseeing (Swoyambhunath, Bhaktapur Durbar Square, and Changunarayan", "richText": "Start the day with sightseeing at World Heritage-listed destinations. In the morning, drive to the hilltop <strong>Swayambhunath Stupa</strong> also popular as <strong>‘Monkey Temple’</strong>. Admire the stunning valley views and mountains from the top. Afterward, drive to an architecturally impressive<strong> Bhaktapur Durbar Square. </strong>This ancient town has numerous historic and cultural attractions which are artistically phenomenal. Have some snacks or lunch and drive to <strong>Changu Narayan temple</strong>, one of the oldest heritage sites of Nepal. The wood and stone carvings are very impressive. Attend the art-rich session here.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "1400m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 11, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Fly to Pokhara and Pokhara sightseeing (Boating, Cave, Davis Falls; Optional paragliding, Hot air balloon, etc.)", "richText": "Take a short scenic flight to Pokhara. The tourist hub Pokhara is packed with amazing destinations for sightseeing such as Davis Falls, Seti Gorge, Mountain Museum, Gupteshower Cave, Lakeside, and Boating on Phewa Lake. There are also optional adventure activities like Paragliding, Hot Air Balloon ride, etc.\\r\\n\\r\\n<em><strong>Note:</strong> Travelers who enjoy nature can choose a tourist bus ride to enjoy the scenic views. Which takes about 6-7 hours.</em>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "822m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 12, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Sarangkot Sunrise tour and drive/fly to Chitwan", "richText": "Wake up early to witness the marvelous sunrise views over snowy mountains from the <strong>Sarangkot</strong> viewpoint. Adore the breathtaking views of mountains like Annapurna, Dhaulagiri, Machhapuchhre, etc. Back to the hotel for breakfast.\\r\\n\\r\\nWe recommend at least one highway drive to get a sight of natural sceneries. Take a scenic ride to Chitwan which takes 4-5 hours admiring the terraced fields, hillsides, mountains, and small villages. Transfer to the resort upon arriving for an overnight stay.\\r\\n\\r\\n<em><strong>Note:</strong> Travelers can choose to fly if they don’t prefer to travel by road.</em>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "1600m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 13, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner", "title": "Chitwan National Park Tour with Jungle Safari", "richText": "<strong>Chitwan National Park</strong> is the first national park of Nepal that is also listed as a World Heritage Site. <strong>Jungle Safari </strong>commences as your preference<strong> either by Jeep or Elephant, and walking</strong>. It is a fun activity for travelers to carry in the vicinity of diverse flora and fauna. Start the Safari in the morning and get glimpses of wild animals such as deer, one-horned Rhinoceros, Gharial, etc., diverse species of birds, and plants. If lucky get a chance to get a sight of the Royal Bengal Tiger. Sit at the bank of the river and spend some quality relishing the sunset views. After completing the Safari, explore the traditional Tharu village in the surroundings and learn something about their culture and lifestyle.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "415m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 14, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Fly back to Kathmandu, Tour around Thamel and Ason Market", "richText": "In the morning, enjoy bird-watching where you witness varied species of birds. Drive to the airport and fly back to Kathmandu. Take a rest at the hotel. The day is free to spend on your own. Take a tour around the vibrant <strong>local</strong> <strong>Ason market and Thamel markets</strong> and do shopping if you prefer.\\r\\n\\r\\n<em><strong>Note:</strong> If you have an evening/night departing flight, our team will drop you off at the airport.</em>", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "1400m", "accommodation": "3star to Luxury hotels"}, {"day": 15, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Final Departure from Kathmandu to your home / next destination", "richText": "An amazing and adventurous 2-weeks Tibet and Nepal tour comes to an end. Our team will see you off to the airport for final departure to your home or next destination with the hope of serving you again.", "driveTime": "", "elevation": "", "accommodation": ""}], "mainImage": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Namtso-Lake-Tibet.jpg", "title": "Namtso-Lake-Tibet", "altText": "Namtso Lake, Tibet", "caption": "Namtso Lake, Tibet", "variants": {}}, "acf_blocks": {"ws_gf_id": "4", "_ws_gf_id": "field_63edec7318284", "ws_block_meals": "", "_ws_block_meals": "field_63eeee4e072dc", "ws_trip_galleries": ["4433", "4422", "4437", "4859", "4873", "4234", "4854", "4461", "4858", "4330", "4314", "525", "4341", "4282", "732", "4026", "4328", "4302", "735", "731"], "_ws_trip_galleries": "field_63ec89128e6ea", "ws_block_start_end": "", "_ws_block_start_end": "field_63eeee8b072df", "ws_block_attractions": "", "ws_block_best_season": "", "_ws_block_attractions": "field_63eeee1f072da", "_ws_block_best_season": "field_63eeee37072db", "review_number_of_post": "-1", "ws_block_trip_grading": "", "ws_flash_message_text": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "Fill the form below for your interest.\\r\\n", "ws_trip_include_title": "Cost Inclusion ", "_review_number_of_post": "field_63ba542aa9a32", "_ws_block_trip_grading": "field_63ec73a6a4716", "_ws_flash_message_text": "field_63ec950194a18", "_ws_quick_enquiry_desc": "field_63edeb1c811ab", "_ws_trip_include_title": "field_63edd6a334286", "starter_kit_section_bg": "bg-white", "ws_block_accommodation": "", "ws_block_max_elevation": "", "ws_block_video_widgets": "", "ws_flash_message_title": "", "ws_quick_enquiry_title": "Ask to Expert about this trip", "ws_select_content_type": "ws-included", "ws_trip_overview_title": "Why Travel With Us?", "_starter_kit_section_bg": "field_63fc6695edb31", "_ws_block_accommodation": "field_63eeee62072dd", "_ws_block_max_elevation": "field_63eeee07072d9", "_ws_block_video_widgets": "field_63eef38026ee6", "_ws_flash_message_title": "field_63ec94c094a17", "_ws_quick_enquiry_title": "field_63edeb1c7d769", "_ws_select_content_type": "field_63edd755e9729", "_ws_trip_overview_title": "field_63ec808647048", "ws_block_transportation": "", "ws_trip_galleries_title": "Photo Gallery ", "_ws_block_transportation": "field_63eeee74072de", "_ws_trip_galleries_title": "field_63ec89128acaa", "starter_kit_padding_type": "p-medium", "ws_trip_block_highlights": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>UNESCO-listed royal museum Potala Palace includes 1,000 rooms, 10,000 shrines, and approx. 200,000 statues</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Holy Barkhor Street popular for the Kora ritual and for buying Tibetan original goods</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Spiritual Buddhist Sacred Jokhang Temple</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit the holy Sera Monastery famous for debate sessions (between 3-5 pm)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Norbulingka Palace with its unique Tibetan architecture popular for the Yogurt festival (Sho Dun)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit the fresh water sacred Yamdrok Tso Lake</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Shigatse &amp; Gyantse Sightseeing (Tashilhunpo Monastery, Shigatse Dzong, Sakya Monastery, etc.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Visit the largest salt lake Namtso</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>One of the highest-elevated Monastery in the world-Rongbuk Monastery</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Iconic Northern Everest Base Camp and view of the north face of Mt. Everest</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kathmandu sightseeing including UNESCO World Heritage Sites (Durbar Squares, Boudhanath,  Pashupatinath)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Chitwan Sightseeing (Jungle Safari, Tharu Village Tour, Canoeing, Sunset View)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Phenomenal Sunrise View from Sarangkot, Pokhara</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Pokhara Sightseeing (Lakeside View, Davis Fall, Phewa Lake Boating, etc.)</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "ws_trip_information_list": 8, "_starter_kit_padding_type": "field_5f8584c998bc2", "_ws_trip_block_highlights": "field_63ec73a6a0d8f", "_ws_trip_information_list": "field_63ec90a574f02", "starter_kit_section_title": "Suggested Itinerary ", "_starter_kit_section_title": "field_63ec948c94a16", "starter_kit_enable_section": "1", "_starter_kit_enable_section": "field_63edeb1c7635c", "starter_kit_section_padding": "", "ws_trip_include_description": "<blockquote>We are dedicated to providing quality service to our clients where safety is our topmost priority. We have not mentioned our costs as they depend on factors like trip customization, group sizes, travel season, trip duration, and types of accommodation, meals, transportation, and choice of various activities.\\r\\n<em>(<strong>Note:</strong> On your request, we can send you cost details. Feel free to contact us for further details.)</em></blockquote>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Tibet Travel Permit</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Tibet visa if you want to apply from Kathmandu, Nepal</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Private vehicle with air conditioning</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Private English-speaking Tibetan guide for Tibet and English-speaking Nepalese guide for Nepal (Other language guide also available upon your request with extra cost.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Breakfast in Tibet and Nepal</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>All meals (Breakfast, Lunch &amp; Dinner) at Chitwan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>All accommodation as per your choice (Luxury/5-star or 4-star hotel or 3-star hotel)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Monuments entrance/admission fees</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Guide and driver’s meals and accommodation</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Service Charge (the planning, handling, operational and communication charges) &amp; government taxes.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Handle your flight or train tickets (Kathmandu/Beijing/Chengdu/Kunming to Lhasa(Tibet) or vice-versa)</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_starter_kit_section_padding": "field_5f3e0f86a2634", "_ws_trip_include_description": "field_63edd6a337cd0", "ws_trip_overview_description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>24/7 International Support</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Flexible Private and Customize Trips</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Safety: Our Topmost Priority</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Secure Online Payment</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bookings and Payments Flexibility</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Lifetime Deposit Guaranteed</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Guaranteed Departures</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Travel with Locals to support locals</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Experienced Team and Expert Guides</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Respect Nature through Responsible Tourism</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Happiness and Best Priced Assured</li>\\r\\n</ul>", "_ws_trip_overview_description": "field_63ec83089dd8e", "starter_kit_testimonial_title": "Traveler's Reviews", "_starter_kit_testimonial_title": "field_63ba53af6b053", "ws_trip_fact_short_description": "Tour Highlights", "_ws_trip_fact_short_description": "field_63ec73a69d305", "ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "01", "ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "02", "ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "03", "ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "04", "ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "05", "ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days": "06", "ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days": "07", "ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days": "08", "ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days": "09", "ws_trip_information_list_9_di_days": "10", "_ws_trip_information_list_0_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_1_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_2_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_3_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_4_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_5_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_6_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_7_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_8_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "_ws_trip_information_list_9_di_days": "field_63ec958b8c799", "ws_trip_information_list_10_di_days": "11", "ws_trip_information_list_11_di_days": "12", "ws_trip_information_list_12_di_days": "13", "ws_