a384c7cb-c116-42e7-a597-99ae2386e440	96152bd4-0a9e-47e0-b812-c578e7bcfa2f	repeatableTextImage	2	t	{"items": [{"id": "49442d42-ea47-4230-88c8-4ef221446227", "image": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Namtso-Lake-Tibet.jpg", "title": "Tibet and Bhutan Tour", "background": "white", "description": "<strong>The combined tours of magical destinations Bhutan and Tibet treat visitors with their cultural and natural diversity.</strong> Buddhism is highly practiced in these destinations and several monuments, and cultural monasteries are prime attractions. The spiritual significance is high in both destinations and visitors can feel peaceful while exploring these destinations. The unique heritage, remote landscapes, towering snow-covered mountains including Everest, serene lakes, vast grasslands, and the indomitable spirit of its people in Tibet make it an attractive and unmissed destination. Likewise, stunning Himalayan ranges, cultural heritages, impressive architectural landmarks, green valleys, and friendly and ever-smiling Bhutanese make Bhutan a top destination among visitors.", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "76e459d8-1afc-4ea6-a9f7-875aefa99828", "image": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "title": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "altText": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "caption": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "variants": {}, "localPath": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "attachmentId": 627}, "title": "", "background": "white", "description": "<strong>Tibet</strong> is popular as <strong>‘The Roof of the World’</strong> while <strong>Bhutan</strong> is renowned as the <strong>‘Land of Thunder Dragon’. </strong>Ancient fortresses and monasteries, fascinating architecture, unique traditional festivals, cultural richness, and cultural dresses add value to these destinations. Potala Palace, Drepung Monastery, Norbulingka Palace, Yamdruk Lake, Rongbuk Monastery, etc. are major attractions in Tibet. Bhutan is also rich in its monuments and landmarks like Tiger’s Nest Monastery, Chhimi Lhakhang Temple, Dzongs, Buddha Dordenma Statue, etc. Visitors must try unique and authentic delicious foods in both destinations. They are the identity of these destinations. With good scenic views, try some yummy meals and capture them in your tour memories of the combined Bhutan and Tibet tours. Visitors have the flexibility to choose an overland or flight tour as their preference. Connect with us for an unforgettable Bhutan and Tibet tours.\\r\\n\\r\\n<img class=\\"alignnone wp-image-5715 size-full\\" src=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/overland-tour-to-tibet-mountain-ranges-including-Everest.jpg\\" alt=\\"overland-tour-to-tibet,-mountain-ranges-including-Everest\\" width=\\"1500\\" height=\\"712\\" />\\r\\n<h2>Limitations for Tibet and Bhutan combined tour</h2>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Both Tibet and Bhutan have no direct connectivity by air or land. So the only option is travel via a third country like Nepal.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>There are no direct international flights to Lhasa (Tibet) except from Kathmandu (Nepal). However, numerous daily flights to Lhasa (Tibet) are available from China's mainland Chengdu/Beijing/Shanghai/other cities) while only three weekly flights (Mon, Wed, Fri) is available from Kathmandu (Nepal).</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>An overland tour to <strong>Tibet is possible via the Kathmandu-Kerung border</strong> and <strong>Bhutan is possible via Phuentsoling, Samdrup Jongkhar, and Gelephu (India)</strong>.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Prepare to drive 5-7 hours per day if you choose an overland tour option from Kathmandu to Lhasa or vice-versa.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>The Tibet overland tour via Kathmandu (or direct flight from Kathmandu to Lhasa) requires to stay in Kathmandu for a minimum of 4 days to get a <strong>Tibet Group Visa</strong> from Chinese embassy of Kathmandu. To collect a Tibet Group Visa, you must submit the original passport to the China visa center until one gets a visa. In that case, you do not need a China visa (<em>if you already have one, they will cancel it and provide a Tibet group visa</em>). During your 4-day stay in Kathmandu, explore this beautiful and cultural city.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>China Visa, Tibet Travel Permit, and train/flight ticket</strong> are essential if you are traveling to Tibet from China mainland (Chengdu/Beijing/Shanghai/other cities). It is mandatory to stay 1 night in China mainland to collect a hard copy of a travel permit from your hotel which will be sent to you by our representative. (<em>We can hand over your travel permit at the airport with extra cost if you have a same-day connecting flight to Lhasa, Tibet.</em>)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bhutan has limited direct flights to only 5 nations: Nepal, India, Bangladesh, Thailand, and Singapore<strong>. Druk Air</strong> and <strong>Bhutan Airlines</strong> are the only two national carriers of Bhutan and do not allow other airlines to land in Bhutan.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>There are no connecting flights from worldwide in Bhutan. Hence, Self transfer required. <em>You need to pick up your luggage from the nearest airport of Bhutan, and check it in again for your flight to Bhutan. Direct flight available to Bhutan from Nepal, India, Singapore, Thailand &amp; Bangladesh.</em></li>\\r\\n</ul>", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "062d5f34-f362-4258-8fda-595a45b1a460", "image": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "title": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "altText": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "caption": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "variants": {}, "localPath": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "attachmentId": 627}, "title": "Suggested Tour Packages", "background": "white", "description": "<blockquote><strong>What are China's mainland cities for Tibet tour?</strong>\\r\\nChengdu, Beijing, Chongqing, Xian, Xining, Kunming, Shanghai, Mian Yang, Zhengzhou, Shi Quan He, Wuhan, Wanxian, Luzhou, Bangda, Changsha, Diqing, Golmud, etc.</blockquote>\\r\\nWe have several<strong> Bhutan and Tibet tour packages</strong> with various durations (3-15 days) that are perfectly flexible and customizable to your choices of accommodations and monuments/landmarks visit. You just need to provide us <strong>with your preferred travel time, available duration, number of travelers, preferred hotels, interested monuments, travel days in each destination, etc</strong>. With the provided information, we will prepare a suitable itinerary that mostly aligns with your choices and calculate the total cost. <strong>It is best to travel between April to November in both destinations </strong>as these months offer phenomenal views with stable weather and temperature. Both <strong>Bhutan and Tibet tours are expensive </strong>due to the <strong>high transportation costs in Tibet </strong>and<strong> government SDF fee</strong> (USD 100 per person per night)<strong> in Bhutan. </strong>We only operate private tours for the personalized service which means there is no group joining. <strong>Suggested Tibet and Bhutan tour packages are as follows with travel routes and place to visits:</strong>", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "04e39a72-fb0d-4289-93de-deb486e0aab7", "image": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/potala-palace-lhasa.jpg", "title": "1. Tibet and Bhutan Tour package", "background": "white", "description": "<strong>Route: Fly to Lhasa from the city of China, Lhasa to Kathmandu </strong>(By flight or drive)<strong>, Kathmandu to Paro (Bhutan), Paro to next destination</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Tibet Tour duration: 04-10 days (Lhasa city tour, Yamdrok Lake, Tsedang, Gyantse, Shigatse, Rongbuk Monastery (Everest Base Camp), Shakya Monastery, Namtso Lake, Drak Yerpa with Ganden Monastery etc.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bhutan Tour duration: 03-10 (Paro with Taktsang Monastery, Thimphu, Punakha, Phobjikha/Gangtey, Trongsa, Bumthang Valley, etc.)</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<a class=\\"btn btn-success mt-2\\" href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/tibet-bhutan-tour-package/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">11 Days Sample Itinerary</a><a class=\\"btn btn-primary mt-2 ms-2\\" href=\\"#Enquiry\\">Ask to expert to customize trip</a>", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "8822add2-70f5-4afe-a58a-6b84e120dd9c", "image": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/sunrise-at-tourist-base.jpg", "title": "2. Tibet and Bhutan Tour with Everest Base Camp (By Overland)", "background": "white", "description": "<strong>Route: Fly from China mainland to Lhasa, Lhasa to Everest Base Camp</strong> (Rongbuk Monastery)<strong> to Kathmandu by drive, Kathmandu to Paro, Paro to next destination</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Tibet Tour duration: 07-15 days (Lhasa city tour, Yamdrok Lake, Gyantse, Shigatse, Rongbuk Monastery (Everest Base Camp), Shakya Monastery, Namtso Lake, Drak Yerpa with Ganden Monastery, Tsedang etc.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bhutan Tour duration: 03-10 (Paro with Taktsang Monastery, Thimphu, Punakha, Phobjikha/Gangtey, Trongsa, Bumthang Valley, etc.)</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<a class=\\"btn btn-success mt-2\\" href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/tibet-with-everest-base-camp-and-bhutan-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">13 Days Sample Itinerary</a><a class=\\"btn btn-primary mt-2 ms-2\\" href=\\"#Enquiry\\">Ask to expert to customize trip</a>", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "de7d0f28-7177-4894-951a-80f16898bed4", "image": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Taktsang-Monastery-Tigers-Nest.jpg", "title": "3. Bhutan and Tibet Tour Package (By Flight)", "background": "white", "description": "<strong>Route: Fly from Bangkok/Kathmandu/New Delhi to Bhutan, Bhutan to Kathmandu (Nepal), Kathmandu to Chengdu, Chengdu to Lhasa, Lhasa to next destination via China mainland</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bhutan Tour duration: 03-10 (Paro with Taktsang Monastery, Thimphu, Punakha, Phobjikha/Gangtey, Trongsa, Bumthang Valley, etc.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Tibet Tour duration: 04-10 days (Tsedang, Samya Monastery, Lhasa city tour, Yamdrok Lake, Tsedang, Gyantse, Shigatse, Rongbuk Monastery (Everest Base Camp), Shakya Monastery, Namtso Lake, Drak Yerpa with Ganden Monastery etc.)</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<a class=\\"btn btn-success mt-2\\" href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/bhutan-and-tibet-combined-tour-package/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">15 Days Sample Itinerary</a><a class=\\"btn btn-primary mt-2 ms-2\\" href=\\"#Enquiry\\">Ask to expert to customize trip</a>", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "0bd70b2a-838a-4b5d-8161-930a430db978", "image": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/kathmandu-durbar-square.jpg", "title": "4. Bhutan, Nepal, and Tibet Tour Package (By Flight)", "background": "white", "description": "<strong>Route: Fly to Kathmandu</strong><em> (Connecting flight available from worldwide),</em><strong> Apply for Tibet group visa and Kathmandu Tour, after getting Tibet visa, Kathmandu to Bhutan flight, Bhutan to Kathmandu, Kathmandu to Lhasa </strong>(by flight/drive)<strong>, Lhasa to next destination</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Nepal Tour duration: 04-10 (Tibet group visa apply, Kathmandu, Patan, Bhaktapur, Nagarkot, Panauti, Pokhara, Chitwan National Park, Lumbini, helicopter or mountain flight to Everest etc.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bhutan Tour duration: 03-10 (Paro with Taktsang Monastery, Thimphu, Punakha, Phobjikha/Gangtey, Trongsa, Bumthang Valley, etc.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Tibet Tour duration: 04-10 days (Lhasa city tour, Yamdrok Lake, Tsedang, Gyantse, Shigatse, Rongbuk Monastery (Everest Base Camp), Shakya Monastery, Namtso Lake, Drak Yerpa with Ganden Monastery etc.)</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<a class=\\"btn btn-success mt-2\\" href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-bhutan-tibet-tour-package/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">20 Days Sample Itinerary</a><a class=\\"btn btn-primary mt-2 ms-2\\" href=\\"#Enquiry\\">Ask to expert to customize trip</a>", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "261d5eec-bd60-406f-a2b6-448c034c884d", "image": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/boudhanath-stupa-1.jpg", "title": "5. Bhutan, Nepal, and Tibet Tour Package (By Overland)", "background": "white", "description": "<strong>Route: Fly to Kathmandu</strong><em>(Connecting flight available from worldwide),</em> <strong> Kathmandu to Paro(Bhutan), Paro to Kathmandu, Apply for Tibet group visa and Kathmandu Tour, after getting Tibet visa, drive from Kathmandu to Rongbuk Monastery (Everest base camp) to Lhasa, and flight from Lhasa to next destination</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Bhutan Tour duration: 03-10 (Paro with Taktsang Monastery, Thimphu, Punakha, Phobjikha/Gangtey, Trongsa, Bumthang Valley, etc.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Nepal Tour duration: 04-10 (Tibet group visa apply, Kathmandu, Patan, Bhaktapur, Nagarkot, Panauti, Pokhara, Chitwan National Park, Lumbini, helicopter or mountain flight to Everest etc.)</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Tibet Tour duration: 07-10 days (Lhasa city tour, Yamdrok Lake, Tsedang, Gyantse, Shigatse, Rongbuk Monastery (Everest Base Camp), Shakya Monastery, Namtso Lake, Drak Yerpa with Ganden Monastery etc.)</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<a class=\\"btn btn-success mt-2\\" href=\\"https://everestnepaltours.com/nepal-bhutan-tibet-overland-ebc-tour/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">18 Days Sample Itinerary</a><a class=\\"btn btn-primary mt-2 ms-2\\" href=\\"#Enquiry\\">Ask to expert to customize trip</a>", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "18244531-3bc7-44f7-bed6-c3e937223ebb", "image": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/flight-to-lhasa-tibet.jpg", "title": "Best starting point for Tibet Bhutan Tour only", "background": "white", "description": "<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li><strong>Arrive in Mainland China (Chengdu/Beijing/Kunming/etc.), then fly to Tibet. After completing the Tibet tour, fly/drive to Kathmandu (Nepal) and take a flight to Bhutan the next day.</strong></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Arrive in Kathmandu (Nepal), and take a flight to Bhutan the next day. After completing the Bhutan tour return to Kathmandu. Then, fly/drive to Lhasa (Tibet). Consider the following things before flying to Lhasa, Tibet.\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you already have a China visa, you will fly to Chengdu and then to Lhasa (Tibet) on the same/next day.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you have no China visa, you must apply for a Tibet group visa at the China visa center in Kathmandu (it takes 4 days) and take a direct flight/drive to Lhasa (Tibet).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Arrive in Bangkok or India, then take a direct flight to Bhutan. After that, fly to Kathmandu, and take a flight/drive to Lhasa (Tibet). Consider the following things before flying to Lhasa, Tibet.\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you already have a China visa, you will fly to Chengdu and then to Lhasa (Tibet) on the same/next day.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you have no China visa, you must apply for a Tibet group visa at the China visa center in Kathmandu (it takes 4 days) and take a direct flight/drive to Lhasa (Tibet).</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n</li>\\r\\n</ol>", "imageCaption": "We offer short tours for Chengdu, Beijing, Xining, and various mainland cities in China for those planning to reach Tibet via the Chinese mainland. It's essential to bring your China visa from your home. We will provide you required Tibet travel permit to fly or take a train to Lhasa (Tibet) from any city in China where you land.", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "bacfd3f8-df11-4799-8869-777547763844", "image": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/flight-to-kathmandu-nepal.jpg", "title": "Available options to go to Tibet from Kathmandu (Nepal)", "background": "white", "description": "There are mainly 3 options to go to Tibet from Kathmandu (Nepal) and are as follows:\\r\\n<ol>\\r\\n \\t<li>You can take a direct 1.5-hour flight from Kathmandu to Lhasa (Tibet) for which you must get a Tibet Group Visa from Kathmandu. It takes 4 days to complete the Visa process.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>If you choose an overland tour, it requires at least 4 days of driving (daily 6-8 hours) from Kathmandu to Lhasa (Tibet). An overland tour is a great way to explore and visit Rongbuk Monastery (Everest Base Camp) with a great Mt. Everest view, Shigatse, Gyantse, Yamdrok Lake, etc. Collecting a Tibet Group visa from Kathmandu is essential.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Firstly, fly to Chengdu/Beijing/Other Chinese mainland cities from your home city or your current destination. It is essential to bring a China visa from your country. Stay 1-night there and collect your Tibet Travel Permit. Next day, take a flight or train ride to Lhasa (Tibet) as your preference.</li>\\r\\n</ol>", "imageCaption": "We offer short tours in Kathmandu and surrounding while applying your Tibet visa in China embassy of Kathmandu. We offer helicopter tours to Mt. Everest, world heritage sites in Kathmandu, Pokhara, Chitwan National Park etc.", "imagePosition": "left-50"}, {"id": "92e08959-a896-46a1-a07f-764f76900633", "image": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "title": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "altText": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "caption": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "variants": {}, "localPath": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "attachmentId": 627}, "title": "List of recommended luxury hotels in each city", "background": "white", "description": "<strong>Tibet:</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>St. Regis, Lhasa: <a href=\\"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/lxaxr-the-st-regis-lhasa-resort/overview/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.marriott.com/lhasa-resort/</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Shangri La Hotel, Lhasa: <a href=\\"https://www.shangri-la.com/en/lhasa/shangrila/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.shangri-la.com/lhasa/</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hilton Shigatse: <a href=\\"https://www.hilton.com/en/hotels/rkzrchi-hilton-shigatse/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.hilton.com/shigatse/</a></li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<strong>Bhutan:</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hotel Pemako (Taj Tashi), Thimphu: <a href=\\"https://www.pemakohotels.com/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.pemakohotels.com/</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>TermaLinca Resort, Thimphu: <a href=\\"https://termalinca.com/about/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://termalinca.com/about/</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>COMO Uma Paro: <a href=\\"https://www.comohotels.com/bhutan/como-uma-paro\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://comohotels.com/uma-paro</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Le Meridian, Paro: <a href=\\"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/pbhpr-le-meridien-paro-riverfront/overview/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://marriott.com/paro-riverfront</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>COMO Uma Punakha: <a href=\\"https://www.comohotels.com/bhutan/como-uma-punakha\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://comohotels.com/uma-punakha</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Densa Resort, Punakha: <a href=\\"https://dhensa.com/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://dhensa.com/</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Gangtey Lodge, Pobhjikha: <a href=\\"https://gangteylodge.com/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://gangteylodge.com/</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Amankora Bumthang Lodge: <a href=\\"https://www.aman.com/resorts/amankora/accommodation/lodges/bumthang-lodge\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://aman.com/bumthang-lodge</a></li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n<strong>Nepal:</strong>\\r\\n<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Dwarikas’ Hotel, Kathmandu: <a href=\\"https://www.dwarikas.com/home/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.dwarikas.com/home/</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Hyatt Regency Kathmandu: <a href=\\"https://www.hyatt.com/en-US/hotel/nepal/hyatt-regency-kathmandu/kathm\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.hyatt.com/kathm</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>BaberMahal Re-visited, Kathmandu: <a href=\\"https://www.babermahal.com/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://www.babermahal.com/</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Kavya Resort, Nagarkot: <a href=\\"https://kavyaresorts.com/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://kavyaresorts.com/</a></li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Dusit Thani Himalayan Resort, Dhulikhel: <a href=\\"https://www.dusit.com/dusitthani-himalayannepal/\\" target=\\"_blank\\" rel=\\"noopener\\">https://dusit.com/nepal/</a></li>\\r\\n</ul>", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "577e2423-ee46-453c-addd-841e904d1fd2", "image": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "title": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "altText": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "caption": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "variants": {}, "localPath": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "attachmentId": 627}, "title": "3 Major Monasteries in Tibet: Rongbuk Monastery vs Ganden Monastery vs Samye Monastery", "background": "white", "description": "<h3>Rongbuk Monastery</h3>\\r\\nRongbuk Monastery, at an elevation of 5,009 m, is one of the highest-situated monastery. It was built in 1902 AD by Lama Ngawang Tenzin. The monastery practices the Nyingma tradition of Tibetan Buddhism. One of the best places to get a view of the Northern face of the world’s highest Mt. Everest. It serves as an important spiritual center for meditation and Buddhist teachings, which displays its great cultural and religious significance. The monastery, with its traditional architecture, houses sacred relics, thangkas, statues, and ancient scriptures.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance (from Lhasa):</strong> Approx. 691 km\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Travel Time Taken (from Lhasa):</strong> 2 days (11 to 12 hours drive)\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Activities:</strong> The Sunrise and Sunset views, Cultural and Monastery Exploration, Sightseeing Historical Sites, interacting with monks and nuns, Mt. Everest and surroundings photography\\r\\n<h3>Ganden Monastery</h3>\\r\\nGanden Monastery is a major Tibetan Buddhist site located on Wangbur Mountain at an altitude of 4,300 m. It was established in 1409 AD by Je Tsongkhapa. It is officially known as Gaden Namgyal Ling Monastery. One of the Great Three Gelugpa monasteries, renowned for its cultural and religious importance. The monastery features traditional Tibetan Buddhist architecture with a large central temple. It serves as a major pilgrimage destination and a hub for Gelug teachings. At present, it operates as an important religious site for monks, pilgrims, and visitors.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance (from Lhasa):</strong> Approx. 60 km\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Travel Time Taken (from Lhasa):</strong> 2 hours drive\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Activities:</strong> The Ganden Kora, Cultural and Monastery Exploration, Sightseeing Historical Sites (Drak Yerpa Caves, Yangpachen Monastery), Interact with local nomads, Take photographs\\r\\n<h3>Samye Monastery</h3>\\r\\nSamye Monastery is Tibet's first Buddhist monastery, founded between 775-779 AD. It is situated in the Yarlung River Valley near Tsedang at an elevation of 3,580 m. The official name is Samyé Migyur Lhundrup Tsug La Khang, meaning the \\"Inconceivable Unchanging and Spontaneously Perfected Temple.” The monastery is a chief center for the Nyingma tradition of Tibetan Buddhism. The unique mandala layout of the monastery blends perfectly with Tibetan and Indian architectural styles. It houses sacred relics, statues of Guru Rinpoche and Buddha, ancient texts, and vibrant thangkas and murals.\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Distance (from Lhasa):</strong> Approx. 124 km\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Travel Time Taken (from Lhasa):</strong> 2 hours drive\\r\\n\\r\\n<strong>Activities:</strong> The Kora, Cultural and Monastery Exploration, Sightseeing Historical Sites (Tibet’s first Yumbulagang Palace, Chimpu Meditation Caves), Visit nomadic settlements, Take photographs\\r\\n\\r\\n&nbsp;", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "7fd664ac-406f-4bf1-8a44-67aaf767c252", "image": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "title": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "altText": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "caption": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "variants": {}, "localPath": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "attachmentId": 627}, "title": "Recommended Private Tour instead of Group Joining Tour", "background": "white", "description": "There are several advantages of Private Tours over a Group Tour. A private tour offers a more personalized and flexible itinerary. You will have the great opportunity to explore the places of your interest as well as more comfort and more privacy. You will get accompanied by an expert &amp; dedicated guide who will take care of all the logistics and an experienced driver who knows the remote region and its high-altitude destination very well, especially in Tibet.", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}, {"id": "1f5682f8-2dae-4eba-98fc-f732b1dd36bd", "image": {"url": "https://everestnepaltours.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "title": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "altText": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "caption": "Antique handicrafts in Kathmandu", "variants": {}, "localPath": "/Users/pasangrumba/Documents/Work/JavaScript_Projects/everestnepaltours_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/antique-handicrafts-in-kathmandu.jpg", "attachmentId": 627}, "title": "What makes Everest Vacation different?", "background": "white", "description": "<ul>\\r\\n \\t<li>Over a decade-long experience in planning and organizing tours in Asia.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We are a dedicated team of professionals always seeking more ways to improve the quality of our services.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We do update our itinerary regularly for the best traveling experiences that you can enjoy.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Our guides are mostly local with good knowledge of local dialect and culture.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>Our tours are customizable and flexible perfect to fulfill your travel needs.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We provide the best value for money with our services.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>With us, you have to worry no more about visas, permits, transport, and all the other necessities until the end of your vacation.</li>\\r\\n \\t<li>We are modern by practice but traditional by heart meaning ‘Athithi Devo Bhawa’ is still implemented for our clients.</li>\\r\\n</ul>\\r\\n&nbsp;\\r\\n\\r\\n<aside class=\\"col-md-12 col-lg-3\\"></aside>", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "right-50"}]}	2026-02-25 21:33:11.267313+00	2026-02-25 21:33:11.267313+00
d8911f71-df2d-4933-8500-8cd2d8a0c3ab	96152bd4-0a9e-47e0-b812-c578e7bcfa2f	bookingForm	3	t	{"showBookingForm": true}	2026-02-25 21:33:11.267313+00	2026-02-25 21:33:11.267313+00
99c7a45b-f24d-466f-a60a-0c0b9fda0847	08147271-4972-4b55-8990-d4bfdaad773f	repeatableTextImage	1	t	{"items": [{"id": "f9e44ef2-d737-4c07-8b50-f8ae29698e86", "image": "", "title": "Book with Confidence", "background": "white", "description": "<h3 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Flexibility Plans and Easy Safe Booking</h3>\\nTraveling is fun but planning a trip to new destinations is a big challenge. Everything must be considered wisely to experience a smooth and memorable tour. Hence, Everest Vacation is here with&nbsp;<strong>Flexibility Plans and Easy Safe Bookings</strong>&nbsp;to provide a safe and memorable trip experience.\\n\\nWe strictly follow industry standards and safety laws set by both provincial and federal governments. We make sure to follow safety rules outlined by the&nbsp;<a href=\\"https://wttc.org/initiatives/crisis-preparedness-management-recovery/safetravels-global-protocols-stamp\\" data-type=\\"link\\" data-id=\\"https://wttc.org/initiatives/crisis-preparedness-management-recovery/safetravels-global-protocols-stamp\\">WTTC’s Safe Travels Protocols</a>.\\n<h4 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Flexible Bookings</h4>\\nThere is a flexible booking option with trip customization that best fits you. You can choose based on your preferences, budget, and schedule. For flexible bookings, consider the following things:\\n\\n<strong>Advance Notice:</strong>&nbsp;For any changes, communicate at least 15 days before the trip start date.\\n\\n<strong>Destination Change Limitation:</strong>&nbsp;After all the complete arrangements of logistics, destination changes are not allowed.\\n\\n<strong>Modification Options:</strong>&nbsp;You can’t change the destination but you can adjust the trip by changing the number of days, adding side trips, and more.\\n\\n<strong>Payment Flexibility:</strong>&nbsp;Confirm your trip with just 20% of the total payment and required to pay the balance amount before 60 days of arrival date.\\n<h4 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">No charges for Trips Rescheduling</h4>\\nWe take no charges for trip rescheduling 30 days before the arrival date. Charges may apply within 30 days for the necessary arrangements made.\\n<h4 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Lifetime Deposits</h4>\\nOnce you make a booking with us, your money will be safe with us at Lifetime Deposits. In case of tour cancellations or rescheduling for any reason, that money can be further used for future trip(s).\\n<h4 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Guaranteed Refund</h4>\\nWe will arrange an alternative tour, in case the trip is canceled due to some reasons. However, if you prefer, our cancellation policy ensures a guaranteed refund of the amount.\\n<h4 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Guaranteed Departures</h4>\\nWe assure guaranteed departures on every trip booked with us. In the event of trip cancellations due to unforeseen circumstances, you have the flexibility to choose a new destination within the same country as an alternative option.\\n<h4 class=\\"wp-block-heading\\">Guaranteed best price</h4>\\nWe are the local travel operator registered in our country. We guarantee the best and most reasonable prices for a smooth and memorable trip as we are not required to pay commission fees to mediators.", "imageCaption": "", "imagePosition": "left-50"}]}	2026-02-25 21:33:10.799252+00	2026-02-25 21:41:37.203+00
\.


