7031d7ff-14db-4493-9593-c99f028af185	Mountain Biking Tour	mountain-biking-tour	<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Mountain Biking Tour In Nepal Himalayas</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Mountain biking tour is one of the main adventure and leisure sports in Nepal Himalaya after trekking, rafting and mountaineering &nbsp;the best way to see Nepal rural life with beautiful landscapes and snow capped mountains, as there are many routes for mountain biking where the dirt and tar (pitched) road has reached several mid hills of Nepal Himalaya area.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Starting from Kathmandu valley itself ride around the valley rim on the least visited area by main line tourists, observe the medieval and local life as it was since many centuries, the farm fields, traditional typical Nepali villages with old culture and customs in the harmony of natural surrounding with high Himalayan mountains backdrop.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Mountain biking in Nepal with various destinations from a day bike around Kathmandu valley rim visiting &nbsp;famous areas of Nagarkot, Dhulikhel and many others to capture the mountain panorama with sunrise and sunset in the comfort of nice lodges, hotels and resorts.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Biking can be done from scenic Pokhara valley to Kathmandu on the off the main road on single and double track taking more than a week, at present biking from Muktinath to Pokhara in the Kaligandaki river valley, around Annapurna with stunning views of Dhaulagiri and Annapurna with more than 12 days of biking trip with high pass of Thorang-la 5,416 meters.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>On long routes biking expeditions we provide camping gear and vehicle support with expert camping and bike guides to show you the wonders of Himalaya.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->	t	Mountain Biking Tour | Everest Vacation	Mountain Biking Tour In Nepal Himalayas Mountain biking tour is one of the main adventure and leisure sports in Nepal Himalaya after trekking, rafting and mountaineering the best way to see Nepal rural life with beautiful landscapes and snow capped mountains, as there are many routes for mountain biking where the dirt 	\N	2024-01-19 07:49:14+00	2024-01-19 07:49:15+00	0
a890d2ca-de2f-47cf-9795-4dad17f8b8cb	Meditation Yoga	meditation-yoga	<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In Kathmandu and most places around Nepal, especially in high country of Himalaya with Buddhist old educational monasteries for learning of&nbsp;Meditation yoga as well, one can learn or practice meditation in and around monasteries area such as Kopan, and white Gompa around Kathmandu valley, or at Bouddhanath as well after getting instructions and lesson from higher level monks and priests.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For Meditation yoga classes as Nepal being a religious country blending well with Hinduism and Buddhism in peaceful harmony, around Kathmandu there various Yoga institute and schools, where one can enlist in.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Meditation yoga the martial art form of physical exercise originated from Hinduism religions and gurus, where it was taught only in certain Gurukul, this art form to stay physical and mentally healthy during one life time.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The practice on breathing, body movement, nervous and muscle system and to purify one’s mind as well.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This ancient art Yoga can be done where ever and when ever indoors or outdoors where there is lawn or a grassy field to practice the Meditation yoga at comfort.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>kopan monastry is best for this courses in Kathmandu, we need to book in advance. there are some other places like Nagi Gompa, Nagarjun hill, shivapuri, Namobuddha monatry for self classes centers. please contact us few months before the trip.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>cost Includes during Meditation yoga</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>– Guru, transportation, accommodation, all fees</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>cost excludes during&nbsp;<strong>Meditation yoga</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>-foods, flights</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->	t	Meditation Yoga | Everest Vacation	In Kathmandu and most places around Nepal, especially in high country of Himalaya with Buddhist old educational monasteries for learning of Meditation yoga as well, one can learn or practice meditation in and around monasteries area such as Kopan, and white Gompa around Kathmandu valley, or at Bouddhanath as well after	\N	2024-01-19 07:51:45+00	2024-01-19 07:51:46+00	0
efab8000-ce22-4353-b68e-d940a05b677c	Communication	communication	<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->\n<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Communication-Internet, wifi, and cell phones available in many places, Dial code +977</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>STD and ISTD are widely found in all parts of Nepal in towns and cities and as well in villages.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Internet services are found in all parts of Nepal where there are electric power facilities in most of the towns and cities with Wi-Fi services.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In tourist areas hotels, restaurants free Wi-Fi services, a telephone call can be made from towns and cities and from your own hotel rooms after dialing the code 977 and adding respective numbers overseas.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For Sat and cell phone networks are easily linked, but in some mid hills and valley gorges, the service of cell / sat phone can be weak or nil due to blockage of hills and mountains.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>There are many Cell companies, where one can buy a SIM card at a reasonable cost after showing your ID and passports.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->	t	Communication | Everest Vacation	Communication-Internet, wifi, and cell phones available in many places, Dial code +977 STD and ISTD are widely found in all parts of Nepal in towns and cities and as well in villages. Internet services are found in all parts of Nepal where there are electric power facilities in most of the towns and cities with Wi-Fi s	\N	2024-01-19 08:03:32+00	2024-01-19 08:03:34+00	0
97e9f2d6-28d5-4a00-b16a-e07ebe4dcc24	Nepal Visa Information	nepal-visa-information	<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>All foreign nationals except Indian nationals need a visa to enter Nepal.</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>To obtain a visa on arrival, you will need to fill out an arrival card and a visa application form, and pay the visa fee.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Issued to foreigners travelling to Nepal as an entry visa (On-Arrival Visa) at the port of entry</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Issued as an entry visa by Diplomatic Missions abroad</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Tourist visa is extended not exceeding total 150 days of stay in a single visa year (Jan-Dec)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Visa fees:</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Entry Tourist Visa</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>15 Days – USD 30<br>30 Days – USD 50<br>90 Days – USD 125</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Visa Extension</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>3 USD per Day(minimum 15 days)<br>5 USD per day as late fine in the case of delay<br>Additional 25 USD for a Multiple re-entry facility</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Foreigners can apply from the online portal</strong><br>https://nepaliport.immigration.gov.np/</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->\n<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Required documents for visa application:</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The required documents for a visa application are:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Passport: Your passport must be valid for at least 6 months from the date of your arrival in Nepal.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Visa application form: You can download the visa application form from the website of the Department of Immigration.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Arrival card: You will be given an arrival card when you enter Nepal.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Photo: You will need to provide a recent passport-sized photo.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Visa fee.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->\n<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Where you can apply Visa-on-arrival?</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Tribhuvan International Airport (TIA)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Immigration Office Mohana (Kailali)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Immigration Office Jamunah (Banke)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Immigration Office Hilsa (Humla)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Immigration Office Birgunj (Parsa)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Immigration Office Kakarbhitta (Mechi)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Immigration Office Kodari (Sindupalchowk)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Immigration Office Gaddachauki (Kanchanpur)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Immigration Office Rasuwagadi (Rasuwa)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Immigration Office Belahiya (Bhairahawa)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Immigration Office Pokhara</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Immigration Office Biratnagar (Morang)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Gautam Buddha International Airport (GBIA)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item -->\n\n<!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Pokhara International Airport (PIA)</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->	t	Nepal Visa Information | Everest Vacation	All foreign nationals except Indian nationals need a visa to enter Nepal. To obtain a visa on arrival, you will need to fill out an arrival card and a visa application form, and pay the visa fee. Issued to foreigners travelling to Nepal as an entry visa (On-Arrival Visa) at the port of entry Issued as an entry visa by 	\N	2024-01-19 07:57:56+00	2024-01-19 07:57:57+00	0
3767c748-bb36-425c-b531-027233ea1082	Shopping in Nepal	shopping-nepal	<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Nepal is famous for its handicrafts since many past centuries, handicrafts and other artworks are interwoven with culture, traditions and way of life of Nepali peoples.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In Kathmandu one can find unique intricate wooden carving and handicrafts, visit the handicrafts workshop and observe the artists on works and can buy from its showrooms many types of handicrafts from small medium to larger ones. Handicrafts range from wood works, metals and stones with furniture’s, decorating items, carets or rugs is another important work of arts and skill found in high Himalayan area’s of Nepal, in Kathmandu visit the famous Tibetan refugees settlement with carpet and other handicraft factory for quality carpets and other handmade goods, carpets ranging from 80 knots to 500 knots per sq inch, with natural, vegetable dye or chemical colors as per the budget and choice of quality.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Huge exports of carpets to European countries and some in Far East countriesare in demand including wooden and metal handicrafts, the other main exports is Pashmina shawls (from the wool of mountain goats) all carpets are mostly made from Yaks and Sheep wools.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->	t	Shopping in Nepal | Everest Vacation	Nepal is famous for its handicrafts since many past centuries, handicrafts and other artworks are interwoven with culture, traditions and way of life of Nepali peoples. In Kathmandu one can find unique intricate wooden carving and handicrafts, visit the handicrafts workshop and observe the artists on works and can buy 	\N	2024-01-19 08:01:59+00	2024-01-28 02:06:57+00	0
\.


